  ('usfs', '5628', 'Spring Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.784490, -111.275160, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'A campground by Hebgen Lake on the Hebgen Lake District.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=5628', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5630', 'Swan Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.371990, -111.163600, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground in the Gallatin canyon on the Bozeman District. Information: Rocky Mountain Recreation Company (661) 702-1420 info@rockymountainrec.com', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=5630', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5631', 'Timber Camp Campground', 'campground', 45.094220, -110.605600, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'A campground in the West Absaroka Mountains on the Gardiner District.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=5631', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5632', 'Tom Miner Campground', 'campground', 45.129380, -111.062530, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground in the Gallatin Mountains on the Gardiner District.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=5632', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5633', 'West Boulder Campground', 'campground', 45.548230, -110.306850, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'A campground in the west boulder area on the Yellowstone District. Next to trailhead into Absaroka Beartooth Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=5633', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56409', 'Blue Mountain Byway West Interpretive Site', 'scenic_drive', 45.786152, -120.038574, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'day use site', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56409', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56411', 'Bull Prairie Lake Campground', 'campground', 44.973577, -119.663582, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Bull Prairie has been a gem to the local community and is considered a beautiful woodsy place to enjoy a vacation, host family reunions or social events, and to extensively recreate. This moderate-sized campground is located adjacent to a 28- acre lake, Bull Prairie Lake (stocked annually with trout). There are family-friendly and wheelchair accessible paved paths along the lake that are designed for people who enjoy morning jogs, bicycle rides, picnicking, and leisure. While this campground offers potable water, there is no longer any garbage service, so please pack out all garbage and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56411', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56417', 'Coalmine Hill Campground', 'campground', 45.166321, -119.333840, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Coalmine Hill is just off the paved Blue Mountain Scenic Byway (also called the Western Route). The Campground serves as access to the Bald Mountain, Hells Half Acre, and Willow Creek trails, offering a 7.5 mile-long loop experience for hikers and equestrians. Once inside the campground''s large parking area, there is an information board on the northeast side. Past the information board runs the Bald Mountain hiking trail leading to Gibson Cave, which is 1.25 miles from the parking lot. The cave is really a shallow overhanging shelter with an interpretive sign describing its history.Once…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56417', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56427', 'Fairview Campground', 'campground', 44.955764, -119.711217, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Fairview Camp is drive-through loop off State Highway 207 offering five campsites and an accessible vault toilet. Two campsites directly across from the toilet are fully accessible. A free-flowing water fountain provides potable water from May to October. Remnants from a wildfire in the late 1980s can be seen along the egdes of this small campground. There is no garbage service, so please pack out all garbage and dispose of it at home. The campground is used primarily for hunting and OHV riding--its trailhead accesses 80 miles of OHV roads and trails on the Heppner Ranger District. Also,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56427', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56443', 'Penland Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.117182, -119.318803, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Fall asleep to the sound of crickets and frogs chirping and croaking and wake up to Blue Gill and Rainbow Trout jumping at the bit. This campground is set on the shore of Penland Lake, which also abuts private land and land owned by Oregon Department of Fish and Wildlife (ODFW). Penland is popular on summer weekends and offers access to fishing, boating, and swimming opportunities. There are seven campsites and two vault toilets on the National Forest portion of the campground, with more campsites located on the adjacent ODFW property. There is also a boat ramp, fishing dock, and benches…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56443', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56447', 'Stahl Canyon Overlook', 'scenic_drive', 45.008255, -119.898618, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'The overlook, located on Forest Service Road 21, offers a panoramic view of the canyon and beyond to the northwest. Big game use this canyon as a travelway, and raptors are often seen soaring overhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56447', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56467', 'Bear Wallow Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.184809, -118.752138, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This campground offers a pleasant experience among the pines adjacent to State Highway 244. It features 8 campsties, including 1 accessible site and 2 accessible vault toilets. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please dispose of your garbage at home. Attractions in this area include hunting, bird watching, photo opportunities, and a 1/4-mile-long, accessible interpretive trail detailing the life cycle of steelhead salmon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56467', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56475', 'Big Creek Meadows Campground', 'campground', 45.009000, -118.618889, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Big Creek Campground is small and increasingly popular with OHV recreationists, located just off the Blue Mountain Scenic Byway . It also provides access into the North Fork John Day Wilderness and there is ample parking for truck and stock trailers at the trailhead. It is set in a riparian area, so surrounding areas can be quite wet well into June. It features 3 campsites and an accessible vault toilet. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack out all garbage and dispose of it at home. Trail access: This campground contains a trailhead into the North Fork John Day…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56475', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56515', 'Divide Well Campground', 'campground', 45.102598, -119.142470, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Divide Well Campground is a remote site with a rustic look. It is situated in an meadow with scattered ponderosa pine and denser fir along the campground edges. Divide Well is a popular spot for elk hunters, but little used through the rest of the season. It features 11 campsties and two accessible vault toilets. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack out all garbage and dispose of it at home. Nearby is the Potamus Point Interpretive Site , with breathtaking views, interesting geology, and a herd of re-introduced bighorn sheep. There are no developed trails on this side…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56515', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56517', 'Drift Fence Campground', 'campground', 45.071589, -118.876447, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Drift Fence Campground is situated along the paved Blue Mountain Scenic Byway and is traditionally a hunting camp. This is a small, rustic site and the short access road is in poor condiiton. The campground features 6 campsties and 2 vault toilets. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack all garbage out and dispose of it at home. The surrounding area offers hunting, wildlife and wildflower viewing opportunities, and photography. Fishing is available at several nearby stocked ponds including Twin Ponds where the annual Fishing Derby is held. If you like to drive, you can…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56517', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56519', 'Driftwood Campground', 'campground', 45.018175, -118.859137, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This lovely campground is situated on the banks of the Wild and Scenic North Fork John Day River. Driftwood features 6 campsties and 1 accessible toilet. There is a put-in site for rafting. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Attractions in this area include swimming, non-motorized boating, and fishing. Water levels are low in mid to late summer, which can impede use of boats. The campground provides good access for big game hunting. In addition, the Oriental Trailhead is about 8 miles west, providing access to both OHV and wilderness trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56519', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56531', 'Four Corners Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 45.178143, -118.607520, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This site features a large paved parking lot for the convenience of snowmobile users and cross country skiers. This open area has no marked or groomed trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56531', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56535', 'Frazier Campground & Trailhead', 'campground', 45.159598, -118.639647, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This campground serves as the northern gateway to the Winom-Frazier Off Highway Vehicle (OHV) trail system, with over 100 miles of trail to ride. It features 20 campsites and 4 accessible vault toilets. There is a large day-use picnic shelter near the campground entrance. Trailhead parking and an interpretive sign is located in the upper loop of the campground, near the Butcherknife Trail #3189 . There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. The nearby area offers hunting, OHV riding, sight-seeing, and photography. The Tower Fire Lookout is a little more than…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56535', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56551', 'Gold Dredge Campground', 'campground', 45.001855, -118.817966, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This is a peaceful campground set in an open Ponderosa pine stand along the Wild and Scenic North Fork John Day River. Gold Dredge features 7 campsties and 1 accessible vault toilet. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Attractions in this area include photography, swimming, non-motorized boating, and fishing. Water levels are low in mid to late summer, which can impede use of boats. The campground provides good access for big game hunting. In addition, the Oriental Trailhead is about 6 miles west, providing access to both OHV and wilderness trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56551', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56567', 'Lane Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.189864, -118.766271, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Lane Creek Campground is set among open, large, Ponderosa pine. It features 7 campsties and an accessible toilet. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. This campground offers hunting and photo opportunities. It is also near the Bear Wallow Interpretive Trail, a 1/4 mile trail that interprets the lifecycle of steelhead fish.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56567', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56595', 'North Fork John Day Campground', 'campground', 44.915371, -118.403858, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This campground sits along the Wild and Scenic North Fork John Day River at the junction of the Blue Mountain and Elkhorn Scenic Byways . It features 20 campsites, 3 accessible toilet facilities, and stock handling facilities. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. This campground serves as the eastern access point to North Fork John Day Wilderness via North Fork John Day River Trail #3022 . The area offers hunting, fishing, hiking, horseback riding, sight-seeing, and photography opportunities. In spring and fall you can see the salmon spawning.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56595', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56605', 'Olive Lake Campground', 'campground', 44.783448, -118.595175, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Nestled on the edge of a lake, high in the Blue Mountains of Eastern Oregon, this popular campground is only 8 miles west of the historic Fremont Powerhouse and 12 miles west of the old mining town of Granite. The campground features 28 campsites and 7 accessible toilet facilities. Other features include a 2-mile hiking trail around the lake with nearby access to wilderness and scenic area trails, a boat ramp and 2 docks. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Besides beautiful scenery, the lake offers many opportunities for wildlife…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56605', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56609', 'Oriental Campground', 'campground', 44.973660, -118.728521, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This fairly secluded campground is near the end of Forest Road 5506 along the Wild and Scenic North Fork John Day River . It features 8 campsites and 2 accessible toilets. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Large vehicles, trailers, and low clearance vehicles are not recommended due to poor access road and limited turnaround capability. This campground offers fishing, swimming, non-motorized boating, hiking, OHV riding, horseback riding, sight-seeing, and photography. Water levels are low in mid to late summer, which can impede use of boats. The…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56609', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5662', 'Dinner Station Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.429600, -112.902650, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Dinner Station Campground is a hillside campground covering 5 acres along Birch Creek that has 8 camping units, a day-use picnic area, ADA accessible toilets, and water. The campground is close to fishing areas as well as many trailheads. For this site, please limit trailer lengths to 16'' or less, do not exceed the 16-day camping limit, and keep in mind that there are not garbage services here, so pack it in and pack it out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5662', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5663', 'East Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.563100, -112.660600, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Get high on life at this small, high-elevation campground in the Montana mountains with 4 camping units. East Creek Campground offers first-come, first-served sites for tents or small trailers. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 16 feet.There is no cell phone service here so you can truly unplug and let the wilderness take all your cares away. Immerse yourself in the outdoors, and find your happy place here with minimal distractions. Campers often rave about the views from this site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5663', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5664', 'Grasshopper Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.451020, -113.123830, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'At an elevation of 6,900 feet, this campground is about 9 acres and has 24 designated campsites. The basic facilities include ADA-accessible restrooms, picnic area for day-use and potable drinking water are offered during the open season. Fishing and hiking may be enjoyed nearby. The campground is adjacent to Grasshopper Creek in a steep canyon. The maximum recommended trailer and truck length for the area is 25 feet. This is a pack it in, pack it out campsite with no garbage services. Please limit your stay to 16 days. Bear-resistant food storage boxes are available. There is a fee for the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5664', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5665', 'Price Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.479509, 113.083134, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Price Creek Campground is surrounded by lots of trees that provide great shade and is close to the Crystal Park Recreation Area. The 28 camping units here can accommodate both tents and trailers (maximum trailer length is 30 feet). Drinking water, toilets, and other amenities are offered within sites as well. There are no garbages in sites, so campers must pack out what they pack in. Bear-resistant food storage boxes are available and as with all sites, following the food storage order is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5665', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56655', 'Tollbridge Campground', 'campground', 44.996954, -118.935134, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This is a small campground just off Highway 395 along the confluence of Desolation Creek and the North Fork John Day River. Tollbridge features 5 campsties and an accessible toilet. There is also a sign interpreting the geology of the area. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Local attractions include hunting, fishing, swimming, non-motorized boating, and photography.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56655', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5666', 'Reservoir Lake Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.122050, -113.453430, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a nice high elevation lakeside campground. Reservoir Lake Campground and day use picnic area sits along the lake''s south shores. The campground and dau use areas have vault toilets, drinking water, and a boat ramp. Scenic trails are offered for hiking. Fishing, swimming, and boating are also among the activities to be enjoyed at the campground. There are 16 designated campsites, as well as accessible restrooms and drinking water. Average parking apron size: 15'' X 61''. Parking aprons are dirt. Interior road is narrow in places with trees close to roadway. Pets are allowed if on a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5666', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56665', 'Welch Creek Campground & Trailhead', 'campground', 44.877016, -118.778767, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Welch Creek Campground has long been a favorite gathering spot for family reunion camp-outs and group hunting trips. The campground''s open area and easy parking access make it ideal for such events. It features 6 campsties an accessible vault toilet, and 4 stall recreational stock corral. There is no potable water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. Local attractions include hunting, fishing, hiking, horseback riding, sight-seeing, photography and a trailhead for the Desolation OHV trail system. Olive Lake, where there is fishing, boating, and swimming is about 13 miles to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56665', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56671', 'Winom Campground & Trailhead', 'campground', 45.011997, -118.638548, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This campground is located along the paved Blue Mountain Scenic Byway southeast of Ukiah, OR. There are 10 campsites (3 of which are group sites) and 2 accessible toilets. Sites 3 and 4 have log picnic shelters. There is an interpretive sign near the information board and OHV loading dock. There is no water or garbage service, so please pack your garbage home. 2018 Winom-Frazier OHV Complex and Desolation OHV Trail System Map - June 3, 2019 (pdf file - 466kb) Trail access : The Tower Loop Trail #3040 connects with the campground providing access to the southern end of the Winom-Frazier OHV…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56671', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56675', 'Alder Thicket Campground', 'campground', 46.258651, -117.567374, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Welcome to the northern gateway into the Blues. This campground is located just off of Forest Service Road 40, which is just three miles into the Blue Mountains. Overgrown trees and tall Alder shrubbery will provide plenty of shade for Grouse, White- Tailed deer and yourself on hot summer days. Hiking trails are within five miles and the Clearwater Guard station is six miles from the Alder Thicket Campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56675', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56685', 'Big Springs Campground', 'campground', 46.231463, -117.543510, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Looking for a nice cool break from that summer heat? This campground is the coolest campground in the area during hot summer days. Hunting and hiking opportunities are in a close proximity of Big Springs. There are five trailer and five tent sites, one vault toilet and a few picnic tables available for day use.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56685', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56705', 'Cloverland Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.148190, -117.335207, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This sno-park is great for skiing and snowshoeing when the snow level cooperates. Cloverland Sno-Park in the winter, requires a Washington State sno park pass. The park is also open in the summer months for a rest stop, with a vault toilet provided. A map of the area can be found here.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56705', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5673', 'Boulder Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.648810, -113.063700, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Boulder Creek Campground is located along the Pioneer Mountain Scenic Byway. It is a high elevation campground that is heavily wooded. The road leading to this site is paved, and 3 of the 13 sites are pull-through sites that are easier for campers and trailers. The maximum recommended length for trailers at this site is 30''. Fire rings, picnic tables, vault toilets, and water are available at this site, however garbage services are not so pleasepack out what you pack in. The Wise River flows along the western border of this campground area, providing easy fishing access. This is a great…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5673', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56739', 'Forest Boundary Campground', 'campground', 46.292643, -117.557989, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Forest Boundary Campground has a fantastic view overlooking Scoggin''s Ridge with unbelievable sunsets. Neighboring this campground are Boundary Snow Park, Wooten State Wildlife Area and the Arbothknott Canyon. The ATV trailheads for the North and South trails are also located nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56739', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5674', 'Canyon Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.623550, -112.942170, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a small campground with 3 tent sites and a picnic area west of Melrose in the Pioneer Mountains. It''s a quiet campground located near Canyon Creek and the Wise River, which are great places to fish for brook, rainbow, and cutthroat trout. There are hiking trails nearby, meaning you''ll want to bring your hiking boots and a water supply and explore the scenic and rugged landscape. Trailer length should not exceed 14'' and water and garbage service are not available at this site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5674', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56741', 'Godman Campground/Trailhead', 'campground', 46.099718, -117.786291, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Godman Campground has several secret treasures. There are numerous recreation opportunities available at this campground such as hunting, fishing, bicycling, and hiking. This campground location offers good views and great sunsets. The nearby Godman Trailhead provides access to West Butte Trail #3138 which enters Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness . Please Leave-No-Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56741', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5675', 'Fourth of July Campground', 'campground', 45.661310, -113.060350, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Located along the Scenic Byway between the communities of Wise River and Polaris, MT, the Fourth of July Campground has 6 campsites, made of compacted gravel with paved interior access trails. Water from a hand pump, fire-rings, picnic tables, and ADA accessible restrooms are provided. However, there are no garbage services, so remember to pack it in, pack it out. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 30 feet. Pets are allowed if on a leash. There is a 16 day camping limit. This is a nicely outfitted campground in an idyllic setting, which is open and sunny.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5675', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5676', 'Little Joe Campground', 'campground', 45.557920, -113.092710, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Little Joe Campground is accessed via the Pioneer Mountains Scenic Byway, with awesome views of the surrounding mountain peaks, valleys, and forests. This is a small, quiet campground with 5 camping units, a picnic day-use area, ADA accessible vault toilet, and water. It does not have garbage services, so pack out what you pack in. Wise River runs nearby and provides easy access for fishing but there is not a boat ramp at this site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5676', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5677', 'Lodgepole Campground', 'campground', 45.643340, -113.077490, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Lodgepole Campground is located at an elevation of 6,400 feet between the road and a steep hill across from the Wise River. There are 10 campsites, ADA accessible restrooms, and water provided. Fishing, hiking, and swimming are all accessible near the campground. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 30 feet. Pets are allowed if on a leash. Please limit your stay to 16 days and pack out what you pack in, as garbage services are not available at this site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5677', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56781', 'Ladybug Campground', 'campground', 46.196713, -117.669780, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Along with our welcomed visitors, the ladybugs of the Coccunellidae family, we also welcome you to enjoy these brightly colored insects along with other opportunities this campground has to offer. Being in close proximity of the Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness , hunting, hiking, and bicycling are a few of the recreational opportunities that are at your fingertips. Please Leave-No-Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56781', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5679', 'Mono Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.534360, -113.078760, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This small 2-acre campground is nestled in a thick timbered area, with Mono Creek located across the road. Basic facilities are provided including vault toilets, a day-use picnic area, and drinking water for the 5 designated campsites. Scenic hiking trails are nearby. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 18 feet. Pets are allowed if on a leash. Please limit your stay to 16 days and pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5679', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56791', 'Midway Campground', 'campground', 46.166855, -117.763457, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'At Midway''s high elevation of 6,000 feet, snow pack levels are higher here than other campgrounds on the Pomeroy Ranger District of the Umatilla National Forest. Opportune hiking trails are connected to this campground for convenient accessibility. Please Leave-No-Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56791', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56795', 'Misery Spring Campground', 'campground', 46.120302, -117.485097, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Providing panoramic views from Ray Ridge into the W enaha-Tucannon Wilderness . Misery Spring Campground offers hunting and hiking recreational opportunities. Please Leave-No-Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56795', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5680', 'Pettengill Campground', 'campground', 45.683440, -113.055130, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground is named after an early homesteader, the "Wild Man of the Mountains" George Pettingill. His grave is nearby. He is widely admired in the area although he was somewhat of a hermit. The campground is located where the Wise River meets Pettengill Creek. The campground has 3 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 24 feet. There are ADA accessible toilets at this site. There is no water and no garbage service at this campground, so please pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5680', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56809', 'Panjab Campground', 'campground', 46.204182, -117.705821, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Panjab Campground offers opportunities for hunting, hiking, swimming and bicycling. Just beyond the campground is the trailhead for Rattlesnake Trail #3129 that accesses Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness. This campground is located along Tucannon Springs River; which is a favorite area for mushrooming, hiking, and just relaxing listening to nature. . No camping with stock at Panjab Campground. Stock facilities are available 3 miles up Forest Service Road 4713 at Panjab Trailhead . Please Leave-No-Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56809', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5681', 'Pintler Campground', 'campground', 45.839170, -113.433940, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The campground has 3 units, with a day use picnic area and toilets. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 20 feet. There is no garbage service at this campground, so please pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5681', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56815', 'Pataha Campground', 'campground', 46.291569, -117.514913, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Pataha campground offers opportunities for hunting and fishing as well as other activities. Fish weirs have been installed to aid the passage of fish through a culvert in Pataha Creek. Keep in mind that this creek is stocked with fish every spring.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56815', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5682', 'Seymour Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.983180, -113.189230, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The campground has 17 units, with a maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 18 feet. The area is equipped with a day-use picnic area, toilets, water, and fishing access. Garbage services are not available for this site so please, pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5682', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56825', 'Ray Ridge Viewpoint', 'scenic_drive', 46.118773, -117.482658, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This viewpoint offers an unobstructed view of 95% of the Wenaha -Tucannon Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56825', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56829', 'Rose Springs Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.274471, -117.553167, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Rose Spring Sno-Park is a place where families and friends can head for the mountains during the winter months just to play in the snow. There are several areas, including this one, on the Umatilla National Forest that are popular for sledding and innertubing. A map of the area can be found here.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56829', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5683', 'Willow Campground', 'campground', 45.634490, -113.080110, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The campground has 5 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 20 feet. This campsite is equipped with ADA-accessible toilets, water, and fishing access. There is no garbage service at this site, so pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5683', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56857', 'Teal Spring Campground', 'campground', 46.190222, -117.572189, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Offering a spectacular view of the Tucannon drainage and the Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness, this small, but scenic campground is opportune for Off-Highway Vehicle (OHV) and day hiking enthusiasts.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56857', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5686', 'Miner Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.324070, -113.583880, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The campground is located in a lodgepole forest on relatively flat ground along the north side of the 54 acre Miner Lake. This campsite is equipped with a day-use picnic area, toilets, water, a boat launch area, and fishing access. The campground has 18 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 20 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5686', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5687', 'Mussigbrod Campground', 'campground', 45.788910, -113.609730, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground is located in a dense stand of lodgepole pine on the western shore of the 102-acre Mussigbrod Lake. This campsite is equipped with ADA-accessible toilets, a boat launch area, and fishing access. The campground has 10 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 30 feet. There is no garbage service at this campground, so please pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5687', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56877', 'Tucannon Campground', 'campground', 46.243093, -117.688669, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Located along the Tucannon River and bordering the Wooten State Wildlife area, the Tucannon Campground has several ponds nearby, managed by the Washington Department of Wildlife. These ponds are stocked with trout, offering excellent fishing opportunities for the entire family. This campground is heavily used from the opening weekend of fishing season, in early spring, through the fall hunting seasons. Tucannon is open for camping year around and is easily accessed by paved roads directly leading to the campground. Please call the Pomeroy Ranger District for current conditions. A fee of $8.00…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56877', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5688', 'North Van Houten Campground', 'campground', 45.248030, -113.476420, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a small high elevation campground surrounded by lodgepole pine near Van Houten Lake. This campsite is equipped with ADA-accessible toilets, a boat launch area, and fishing access. The campground has 7 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 20 feet. There is not water available and garbage services are not available, so please pack it in, pack it out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5688', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5689', 'South Van Houten Campground', 'campground', 45.244510, -113.475500, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground is located across the lake from North Van Houten Campground and surrounded by lodgepole pine. This campsite is equipped with ADA-accessible toilets, water, and fishing access. There is no garbage service at this site, so please pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5689', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5690', 'Steel Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.603415, -113.336572, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Steel Creek Campground is located in a stand of lodgepole pine and Douglas fir, with Steel Creek flowing through the area. The campsite is equipped with ADA-accessible toilets, water, and fishing access. The campground has 7 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5690', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56905', 'Wickiup Campground', 'campground', 46.136263, -117.437110, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Located near the Triple Ridge area surrounded by The Jones, Huckleberry, and Hogback ridges; Wickiup Campground offers great hiking opportunities (within five miles), hunting, and views. Cold water springs are available 100 yards below the campground and fishing can be found at Ranger Creek (within 5 miles).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56905', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5691', 'Twin Lakes Campground', 'campground', 45.414180, -113.688500, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Twin Lakes Campground contains 21 sites scattered in the trees along the shores of the adjacent lakes. The area provides good fishing opportunities and nice views of the peaks of the Beaverhead Mountains. This campsite is equipped with a day-use picnic area, ADA-accessible toilets, water, a boat launch area, and fishing access. The campground has 21 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 25 feet. There is no garbage service at this campground, so please pack out what you pack in.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5691', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56919', 'Sturdevant Springs', 'scenic_drive', 45.177833, -119.075845, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This site offers groomed cross-country ski trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56919', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56921', 'Table Rock Lookout', 'scenic_drive', 44.715686, -119.303181, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Table Rock offers spectacular and unmatched views of the surrounding terrain. To the west is the Mill Creek Watershed, municipal water source for the City of Walla Walla, Washington, and eastward lies the Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness. On the narrow ridgeline separating these two rugged areas is the Kendall Skyline Road (Forest Service Road 64).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56921', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56929', 'Andies Prairie Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 45.702268, -118.034490, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'So you want to play in the snow! Andies Prairie is the only designated sledding and winter camping area in the Blue Mountains. This sledding area is located in a rock pit which has been shaped to provide sledding runs. Motorized vehicles are not allowed in the sledding or snow camping area from December 1 through April 1. Your safety is everyone''s concern. It is up to you to make sure you have a safe and satisfying sledding and camping experience. Please follow the safety tips, information and rules that are mentioned in this brochure and posted on information boards located just off the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56929', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5696', 'Beaverdam Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.883180, -112.783870, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Beaverdam Campground and Picnic Area is located in the Fleecer Mountain Range, approximately 17 miles south of Butte, west of Interstate 15. The campground has 15 units that will accommodate trailers up to 50 feet. There are five pull-through sites with the remaining designed as back-in sites. Tent pads are available at most sites. Wood is generally able to be found within the campground area. The campground is located along Divide Creek providing opportunities for fishing and is also in close proximity to trails. Motorized trail opportunities include access to the Continental Divide National…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5696', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5697', 'Lowland Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 46.137730, -112.508580, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Lowland Campground and Picnic Area is located approximately 20 miles north of Butte, west of Interstate 15. The campground is located near Sheepshead Recreation Area, which provides fishing opportunities at Maney Lake and is in close proximity to the Continental Divide National Scenic Trail. The campground has 11 units that accommodate trailers up to 22 feet. The sites are back-in trailer sites. Tent pads are available at most sites. There are day-use picnic areas, the toilets are ADA accessible, and water is available along with garbage containers. Wood is generally able to be found within…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5697', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56973', 'Jubilee Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.833907, -117.965041, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'This high elevation, spruce fir surrounded campground is the largest and most popular campground on the Umatilla National Forest. Jubilee Lake is nestled among the trees and the lake provides a beautiful setting for day-use as well as camping. This site is known for good fishing and swimming and is a wonderful way to escape the summer heat. Jubilee Lake campground offers a variety of recreational actitivies for visitors of all abilities, including fishing and hiking trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56973', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '56999', 'Morning Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 45.775586, -118.082305, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Morning Creek Sno-Park is located off Highway 204. Popular with snowmobilers, snowshoers and Nordic skiers, the facility has two vault toilets. As a multi-use facility, the snowmobile trails are maintained in partnership with the local clubs, and the Sno-Park is plowed via an agreement with the Oregon Department of Transportation. A Sno-Park permit is required to use this facility from November through April and can be purchased through the state Department of Motor Vehicles or their vendors. For your safety use Sno-Park areas and do not park along the highway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=56999', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57001', 'Mottet Campground', 'campground', 45.868390, -117.960300, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Located just off the historic Kendall-Skyline Road, this high-level campground offers 6 campsites to choose from that are in close proximity to several wilderness trailheads. Spend your days hiking in the beautiful and scenic Wenaha-Tucannon Wilderness and your nights relaxing in this tranquil and secluded campground. Mottet even offers clear, cold, and delicious drinking water, straight from a mountain spring!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57001', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5703', 'Bear Creek Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.162600, -111.556460, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Bear Creek Campground is a nice summer or fall destination for those looking to camp, hike, or picnic. At an elevation of 6,350 feet, this campground contains 12 designated campsites. There is a group size limit within the wilderness boundary here of no more than 15 people and 20 head of stock, and stock are not allowed on the south side of the creek. No camping is authorized at the trailhead and certified weed-free hay is required. This campground has vault toilets and drinking water is available in spring/summer only. No garbage service is provided, so pack out what you pack in.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5703', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5704', 'Branham Lakes Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.517550, -111.989080, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The Branham Lakes Campground is a nice rustic campground on 3 acres. At almost 9,000 feet, this campground is one of the highest places you can drive to in Southwest Montana. There is a day-use picnic area here, ADA accessible toilet, water in spring/summer, as well as a boat launch and fishing access area. Although the road to get here is a dirt road that is rocky in places and may not be suitable for low-profile vehicles, and trailers are not recommended, the alpine meadows and views of the Tobacco Root mountains are worth the trek. The campground''s six sites rest along the lakeshore,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5704', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57053', 'Target Meadows Campground', 'campground', 45.805562, -118.077398, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Located around a scenic meadow and surrounded by majestic trees such as Engelmann spruce and Lodgepole pine, Target Meadows has a unique history. It was used by U.S. Army soldiers stationed at Ft. Walla Walla as a summer encampment and artillery range from the late 1880s through 1906. Visitors who explore the campground and surrounding area can even find grooves in trees left by the cavalry''s bullets. Located at the end of the road is the Burnt Cabin Trailhead (the trail is closed at the bridge due to instability). This trail will lead you down to the South Fork Walla Walla River Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57053', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5706', 'Cottonwood Campground', 'campground', 44.971460, -111.965520, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Cottonwood Campground is a relatively remote campground offering a nice relaxing campground that is ideal for the minimalistic or rustic adventurer. If you want to disconnect from the chaos and reconnect with nature, there is no cell service at this site so it is an excellent choice with 10 camping units, a maximum recommended trailer length of 28'', and ADA vault toilet. There are no garbage services at this site, so please pack it in, pack it out!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5706', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57061', 'Touchet Corral Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.093522, -117.846335, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Touchet Corral Sno-Park is located off Forest Service Road 64. Popular with snowmobilers, snowshoers and Nordic skiers, the facility has one double vault toilet. As a multi-use facility, the snowmobile trails are maintained in partnership with the local clubs. A Sno-Park permit is required from November through April and can be purchased through the state Department of Motor Vehicles or their vendors. For your safety use Sno-Park areas and do not park along Forest Service Road 64. A map of the area can be found here.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57061', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57067', 'Umatilla Forks Campground', 'campground', 45.723893, -118.187462, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Situated between the South Fork and the North Fork of the Umatilla River, this campground offers many more activities than just camping. Fishing (catch and release) and hiking in the North Fork Umatilla Wilderness are popular from early spring to late fall. With campsites nestled within a riparian area among an ample mix of conifers and deciduous trees and heavy vegetation that provides great privacy, you will think you are camping in the wilderness itself!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57067', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5708', 'Elk Lake Dispersed Camping and Picnic Area', 'campground', 44.669290, -111.631980, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Elk Lake dispersed camping and picnic area is surrounded by pristine wilderness and mountain lakes and streams. There are abundant wildlife viewing opportunities in the area, which is particularly popular with birders. Bears frequent the landscape here, so be sure to be bear aware and follow all regulations and best practices for food storage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5708', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57083', 'Woodland Campground', 'campground', 45.732595, -118.030200, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Located just off of Highway 204, Woodland Campground is conveniently located to picnic or camp. It offers both shady and sunny campsites that are easily accessible to set up for one night or several. Woodland Campground offers access to numerous hiking trails, including those located within the North Fork Umatilla Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57083', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57085', 'Woodland Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 45.733530, -118.031370, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Woodland Sno-Park is located off Highway 204. Popular with snowmobilers, snowshoers and Nordic skiers, the facility has one vault toilet. As a multi-use facility, the snowmobile trails are maintained in partnership with the local clubs, and the Sno-Park is plowed via an agreement with the Oregon Department of Transportation. Sno-Park permits are required in winter sports areas from November through April and can be purchased through the state Department of Motor Vehicles or their vendors. For your safety use Sno-Park areas and do not park along the highway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57085', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57087', 'Woodward Campground', 'campground', 45.776807, -118.099276, null, 'Umatilla National Forest', 'Nestled amongst trees such as Engelmann spruce and other conifers, this popular campground has ample shade and a hiking trail, not to mention it is close to the beautiful North Fork Umatilla Wilderness and the numerous trails and wildlife viewing it has to offer. Woodward Campground is situated on the edge of Langdon Lake, which is a private lake and therefore campers are unable to access it. However, some sites do offer a view of the water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umatilla/recarea/?recid=57087', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5709', 'Hilltop Campground', 'campground', 44.799590, -111.563210, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Hilltop Campground is a large site covering nearly 10 acres about an hour from Ennis. Located on top of the hill mid-way between Cliff and Wade Lakes, it''s about a 3/4 mile steep, winding drive from the Cliff Lake road. There are 18 sites that are all shaded and quiet, away from the crowds at the lakes. Vault toilet and water are available at this site, however there are no bear resistant food storages boxes available here. We recommend that trailer length does not exceed 22''.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5709', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5710', 'Madison River Campground', 'campground', 44.877190, -111.575710, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Madison Campground is a spacious campground covering nearly 7 acres located in southwestern Montana just beyond the banks of it''s namesake river. It is approximately 34 miles south of Ennis and about 45 miles west of Yellowstone National Park. The ten site campground borders a Douglas Fir covered hillside to the back, with the Madison River just across the road, on the front side. Each site is equipped with a picnic table and fire ring. Vault toilets and drinking water taps are located near each site, along the one-way road. Visitors enjoy fishing, sightseeing, and nearby hiking and ATV…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5710', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5711', 'Mill Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.485520, -112.079680, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Mill Creek Campground is a small campground not far from Sheridan, MT with 10 designated campsites. This site has a vault toilet and water. The maximum recommended trailer length for the campground is 22 feet. Food and refuse storage requirements are in effect and enforced at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5711', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5712', 'Potosi Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.573280, -111.904350, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a nice campground located on the east side of the Tobacco Root Mountains with South Willow Creek running through the middle. There are 15 designated campsites, a picnic day-use area, vault toilets, and drinking water at this site. There are no garbage services, so pack it in and pack it out. We recommend trailer length does not exceed 22''.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5712', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5713', 'Riverview Campground', 'campground', 44.884200, -111.576800, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This RV friendly campground sits on a bench above the Madison River with vistas of the Madison Range. Riverview Campground lies on a sagebrush and gross flat overlooking the Madison River and the Madison mountain range. There are 24 camp units, which are large enough for 30 foot trailer lengths and are each equipped with a fire ring and picnic table. There are three vault toilets and water is available at this campground. Cellular reception is also available. The Madison River, a world famous trout fishery, is about 1/4 mile from the campground. Fishing and boating is available at nearby…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5713', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57137', 'Antilon Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.975400, -120.164000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Antilon Lake camping area is great for large groups and accessible to small RV''s. Antilon Lake is open to fishing, and non-motorized or electric-motor boats. Not recommended for swimming. During the summer this camping area can be hot, dry and one of the first areas to close to campfires. Spring and Fall are much more pleasant. Can be very busy in spring. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57137', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5714', 'Wade Lake Campground and Picnic Areas', 'campground', 44.805320, -111.572020, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Wade Lake Campground is located in southwestern Montana on the shore of it''s scenic namesake lake. It is approximately 43 miles south of Ennis and 35 miles west of Yellowstone National Park. The 27 site campground includes one group site, and is situated in a dense Douglas Fir forest on the hillside above the lake. Each site is equipped with a picnic table and fire ring. Vault toilets and drinking water taps are provided in each of the two camping loops. There is an undeveloped natural-surface boat launch and the lake has a no-wake speed limit. Visitors enjoy fishing, small craft boating, and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5714', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57149', 'Cascade Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.198700, -120.549000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'The Cascade Creek campground is a hike-in campground located near the Lakeshore Trail #1247 between Prince Creek campground and Moore Point campground. There is no boat dock at this lakeside site but it offers two tent sites, 1 picnic table, 1 fire ring and 1 Wallowa toilet. There is not a bear proof communal food storage locker so you''ll need to bring some rope to hang your food. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57149', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5715', 'West Fork Madison Campground', 'campground', 44.883440, -111.579750, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a small campsite with 7 designated sites directly adjacent to West Fork of the Madison River with tent camping only. The campsite does not include room for trialers. Vault toilets, water, and fishing access are available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5715', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57163', 'Corral Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.045588, -120.439196, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a floating dock with a six boat capacity. There are 4 tent sites, 2 picnic tables, 2 fire rings and 1 toilet available. Good protection from down-lake winds. Accessible year-round. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57163', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5717', 'Clover Meadows Dispersed Camping and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.037500, -111.835556, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Dispersed camping and picnic area that is flat and open with well-maintained trails to enjoy a hike on. There is no water or garbage services at this site, but if rustic and simple tent camping is what you''re after, this is a beautiful option with a day-use picnic area and vault toilet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5717', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57175', 'Deer Point Campground', 'campground', 48.026112, -120.312617, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a floating dock with an eight boat capacity. There are five tent sites available, five picnic tables, five fire rings, and two toilets. Deer Point campground provides protection from down-lake winds but no protection from up-lake winds. Accessible year-round. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57175', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57183', 'Domke Falls Campground', 'campground', 48.164200, -120.544000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a floating dock with a six boat capacity. Accessible year-round. There are four tent sites, three fire rings, four tables, and one toilet available. These sites are located right on the shore of Lake Chelan, with a short trail to view Domke Falls. There is no access to Domke Lake, Domke Lake National Recreation Trail #1280 nor Domke Mountain Lookout Trail #1280.1 from Domke Falls. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57183', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57187', 'Domke Lake, Stuart Camp, Hatchery Campgrounds', 'campground', 48.183000, -120.590000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This is three small hike in campgrounds surrounding Domke Lake offering a total of eight tent only sites for DAY USE ONLY . Domke Lake, Stuart Camp, and Hatchery Camp are CLOSED FOR OVERNIGHT CAMPING due to post fire hazards caused by the 2015 Wolverine fire. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57187', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57213', 'Graham Harbor Campground', 'campground', 48.081800, -120.489000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a floating dock with a ten boat capacity and is accessible year-round. There are five sites, seven tables, six fire rings, two toilets and a shelter. Graham Harbor is a good shelter from down-lake winds however it does not provide any protection from up-lake winds. A &frac14;-mile trail connects to Graham Harbor Creek Campground . Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57213', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57215', 'Graham Harbor Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.084850, -120.492573, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'No protection from winds but well shaded site. There are four sites, four tables, four fire rings, and one vault toilet. &frac14;-mile trail connects to Graham Harbor Campground . Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57217', 'Grouse Mountain Campground', 'campground', 47.988997, -120.311151, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This drive to campground offers four tent sites with fire rings, picnic tables and two pit toilets. Remember to bring water, and to take your garbage with you when you leave. There are a number of hiking opportunities in the vicinity of these sites: Devils Backbone trail , Pot Peak trail and Angle Peak trail Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57217', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57221', 'Handy Springs Campground', 'campground', 47.978880, -120.412277, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground offers one tent-only site. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57221', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57225', 'Holden Ballpark Campground', 'campground', 48.200500, -120.792000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Holden Ballpark Campground is located one mile outside of Holden Village. A simple open field nestled in the Railroad Creek drainage the Holden Ballpark provides a gateway for hikers to explore Glacier Peak Wilderness area. This campground can be starting point or ending point to many of the hiking trails available around Holden. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57225', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57245', 'Junior Point Campground', 'campground', 47.994329, -120.400505, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground offers five tent-only sites, campfire rings, and picnic tables. Located at 6600 ft. this camping area provides wonderful views and a number of hiking trails close by. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57245', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57257', 'Lucerne Campground', 'campground', 48.201600, -120.589000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground adjacent to a Forest Service Guard Station offers a dock and boat basin with an eleven boat capacity. A &frac14;-mile trail connects to Refrigerator Harbor Campground & road to Holden Village. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57257', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5726', 'Basin Canyon Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.855500, -112.547900, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'The Basin Canyon Campground is a small undeveloped campground near the Boulder River. There are two camping units at this campground. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 16 feet. There are day use picnic areas and toilets. There is some interesting geology in the area as well with Indian Head Rock nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5726', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5727', 'Delmoe Lake Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.986667, -112.356111, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Delmoe Lake Campground and Picnic area is located 15 miles from Whitehall and Butte in the Whitetail-Pipestone area, a popular destination for OHV riding. The lake is a manmade reservoir controlled by the Pipestone Water Users for irrigation near Whitehall. The campground has 25 sites for trailer and tent camping. Maximum trailer length is 32 feet. Wood is generally able to be found within the campground area. Water and restrooms are available along with garbage containers. The picnic area has tables and a boat launch primarily for fishing activities. The lake level will fluctuate during the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5727', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57275', 'Mitchell Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.969869, -120.192579, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a picnic shelter and a dock with a 17 boat capacity. There are seven campsites (7 tables, and fire rings) available and two toilets. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57275', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57285', 'Moore Point Campground', 'campground', 48.234823, -120.616566, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'SPECIAL NOTICE: Crews from the Forest Service and the Washington Conservation Corps will pull and hand-spray Crupina, a noxious weed, in this area through the month of May. The crews will be camping at Moore Point campground. The campground will be open to the public during these dates. However, available camping sites will be limited and the campground will be more crowded. This boat-in campground offers a picnic shelter and a fixed dock with a three boat capacity. There are four tent sites with a lot of room for additional dispersed camping, four picnic tables, four fire rings and two vault…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57285', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5730', 'Pigeon Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.800360, -112.396500, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Pigeon Creek Campground is located on the eastside of the Highland Mountain Range, approximately 20 miles east of Butte, MT. The campground has 6 units that will accommodate tents only. The road leading to the campground is narrow with sharp turns and is not suitable for trailer traffic.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5730', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5731', 'Toll Mountain Campground', 'campground', 45.845670, -112.366600, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Toll Mountain campground is located on the eastside of the Highland Mountain Range, approximately 20 miles east of Butte. The campground has 5 units that will accommodate trailers up to 22 feet and a group picnic area. The campground is close to a creek and offers a quiet forest setting for weekend getaways.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5731', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57317', 'Prince Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.145283, -120.494829, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'SPECIAL NOTICE: Crews from the Forest Service and the Washington Conservation Corps pull and hand-spray Crupina, a noxious weed, in this area during April. The crews camp at Prince Creek Campground. The campground will be open to the public, however available camping sites will be limited and the campground will be more crowded during this time. This boat-in campground is located on the shores of Lake Chelan and borders Lake Chelan-Sawtooth Wilderness. The area offers a floating dock with a three boat capacity. Prince Creek offers six tent sites, five fire rings, five tables, and three…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57317', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5732', 'Whitehouse Campground', 'campground', 46.258950, -112.478770, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Whitehouse Campground is located in the Boulder River drainage, approximately 20 miles north of Butte. The campground has 5 units that will accommodate trailers up to 22 feet and a picnic day use area with ADA accessible toilets. Water is available and the campground is adjacent to the Boulder River, which offers opportunities for fishing. The area has additional dispersed camping just to the east of the campground. The campground is popular during the late spring, summer, and fall for camping as well as hunting and OHV riding opportunities. Access to the Continental Divide National Scenic…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5732', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57325', 'Refrigerator Harbor Campground', 'campground', 48.199321, -120.587392, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This boat-in campground offers a dock with a three boat capacity. There is one shelter, four tent sites, four tables, four fire rings, and two toilets. This site is accessible year-round. Good protection from down lake winds but no protection from up-lake winds. Located close to the old Lucerne Ranger Station. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57325', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57331', 'Safety Harbor Campground [CLOSED]', 'campground', 48.048628, -120.377672, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Campground is closed due to 2017 Uno Peak Fire above the campground. Potential for catastrophic flash floods is high. This boat-in campground offers a floating dock with a six boat capacity. There are four tent sites, two fire rings, two tables, and one vault toilet. This site has year round access and is a good shelter from both up and down lake winds. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map Kayaking and Canoeing Lake Chelan', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57331', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57337', 'Snowberry Bowl Campground', 'campground', 47.959421, -120.289673, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested drive to campground is nicely tucked in the 25 Mile Creek Drainage away from the busy town of Chelan but close to the Lake and recreational activities. There are seven single tent sites and two small group / small RV sites, all of which have fire rings and tables. The RV sites can accomodate up to ''25 vehicle or trailer. No hook-ups available. A group shelter containing four picnic tables may be accessed via barrier-free trails from both double campsites, but the group shelter is available to all campers on a first come basis. There is a water spigot to fill water bottles but…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57337', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57343', 'South Navarre Campground', 'campground', 48.107746, -120.339574, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', '35 miles from Chelan, mostly on dirt roads, this campground is for those looking to get away from it all. There are four campsites with three pit toilets. From this site there are a number of motorized trail bike, mountain bike, hiking and stock trails available, such as Safety Harbor Creek , Summer Blossom and Summit Trail Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57343', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5737', 'Cable Mountain Campground', 'campground', 46.221898, -113.246813, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Cable Mountain Campground is located on 5 wooded acres just three miles away from Georgetown Lake. This campsite has 11 camping units nestled along the North Fork of Flint Creek and offers plenty of shade. The site has an ADA-accessible toilet and water available. The recommended trailer length is no longer than 22 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5737', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5738', 'Copper Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.066134, -113.543507, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Copper Creek Campground is located in the Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest in southwest Montana. At an elevation of 5,500 feet, the campground covers an area of 2 acres. It is a small campground offering 8 campsites on the Middle Fork of Rock Creek, which is great fishery. Water and restrooms (handicap accessible) are provided. Pets are welcome as long as they are kept on a leash. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet. Please limit your stay to 16 days within a 30 day period.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5738', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57381', 'Windy Camp Campground', 'campground', 47.901407, -120.331698, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This remote campground offers two tent-only sites, picnic tables, fire rings and one toilet. Trailers not advised. Lake Chelan Boat-in and Drive-to Campground Guide and Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57381', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5739', 'Crystal Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.232727, -113.746149, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Crystal Creek is a small campground near Mud Lake with three camping units, a toilet, and fishing access. There are no garbage services so please pack it in, pack it out. The recommended trailer length is no greater than 16 feet. There is no fee for this campsite.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5739', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57399', 'Beverly Campground', 'campground', 47.377222, -120.881042, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Beverly campground is located along the North Fork of the Teanaway River. There are 14 tent/picnic sites available first come/first served. There is no potable water source and all trash must be packed out. Elevation 3200''', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57399', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5740', 'East Fork Group Picnic Area', 'campground', 46.133294, -113.384298, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This wooded picnic area is located near Rock Creek next to the East Fork Reservoir. The area has 8 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5740', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5741', 'Flint Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.233850, -113.302170, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Flint Creek Campground is 3 miles west of Georgetown Lake and has 10 camping units. This site is open year round and is popular with anglers. ADA accessible restrooms are available. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet. Please limit your stay to 16 days.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5741', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5742', 'Lodgepole Campground', 'campground', 46.210716, -113.273307, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a large campground with 31 reservable sites at Georgetown Lake, ADA-accessible toilets, water, a boat launch and fishing access across the road at Red Bridge and garbage services. We recommend trailer lengths do not exceed 32 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5742', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57425', 'Cabin Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.296673, -121.288859, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Non-motorized Sno-Park offering 21 miles of groomed cross-country ski trails. Approximately 200 parking spaces. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57425', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5743', 'Orofino Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 46.259424, -112.608868, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground covers 3 acres in southwest Montana and is located approximately 13 miles southeast of Deerlodge on FS Road #82. Pavilion use is first come, first serve and reservations are not needed for this site. There are 10 camping units available, with a recommendation that trailers do not exceed 22 feet. A picnic day use area is also available at this site, along with toilet. Garbage services are not available for this site, so please, pack out what you pack in and do not exceed the 16 day camping limit.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5743', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5744', 'Philipsburg Bay Campground', 'campground', 46.206390, -113.290000, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Philipsburg Bay Campground is adjacent to Georgetown Lake. The 68 camping units provide ideal access to fishing, boating, and water skiing. It is located in the Pintler Ranger District of the Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest, the largest national forest in Montana. Surrounded by mountains of outstanding beauty, the location is perfect for visitors who enjoy mountains, water sports, or relaxing and taking in the spectacular view. Natural Features: The campground overlooks the Anaconda-Pintler Wilderness. Georgetown Lake is a large mountain lake spanning close to 3,000 acres at an elevation…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5744', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57443', 'Cle Elum River Campground', 'campground', 47.351055, -121.104394, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located at the head of Lake Cle Elum along the Cle Elum River, this campground offers 14 trailer/tent sites and a reservable group site with a capacity of 100 people. Click here for bear warning link', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57443', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5745', 'Piney Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 46.195573, -113.302198, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'Piney Campground is adjacent to Georgetown Lake and has 48 camping units that provide ideal access to fishing, boating, and water skiing. Surrounded by mountains of outstanding beauty, the location is perfect for visitors who enjoy mountains, water sports, or relaxing and taking in the spectacular view. This campsite is equipped with a day-use picnic area, ADA-accessible toilets, water, a boat launch area, fishing access, and garbage services.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5745', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57459', 'Crystal Springs Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.306266, -121.316993, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Crystal Springs is a shared-use Sno-Park managed by WA State Parks. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website . The gravel pit near the Sno-Park is closed to sledding and snow play activity.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57459', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5746', 'Racetrack Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 46.280529, -112.937396, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground has restrooms, water, and a group picnic area. Racetrack Creek flows through the south edge of the campground and the terrain of this campground offers a private experience surrounded by nature. The campground has 13 units. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet. Please limit your stay to 16 days.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5746', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5747', 'Spillway Campground', 'campground', 46.126971, -113.383231, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground is located on the northwestern shore of East Fork Reservoir. The reservoir covers 500 acres with timbered hillsides all around. At the far end of the reservoir you may access the Anaconda Pintler Wilderness. At an elevation of 6,500 feet, Spillway Campground encompasses 3 acres. It is a nicely developed Forest Service campground with 13 campsites in lodgepole timber. Some sites are along the shore and some slightly back on the hillside. Restrooms and water are available and pets are welcome at the campground as long as they''re kept on a leash. The maximum recommended trailer…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5747', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5748', 'Spring Hill Campground', 'campground', 46.170720, -113.165065, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This is a nice campground in a lodgepole pine forest in southwestern Montana with 15 camping units, a day-use picnic area, ADA-accessible toilets, water, and garbage services. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5748', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5749', 'Stony Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.348556, -113.607432, null, 'Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest', 'This campground is located 19 miles west of Philipsburg off the Rock Creek Road (Forest Road 102) and contains 11 sites. The area is known for its high, rugged and beautiful mountain scenery, as well as the variety of wildlife that makes its home there, including bighorn sheep, elk, moose, deer, mountain lions, and bears. Fishing is available in Rock Creek and Stony Creek and anglers may find plentiful brook, brown, and rainbow trout. Much of the stream is protected from bull or westslope cutthroat trout fishing to improve the fishery. It is illegal to target bull trout; if caught they must…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bdnf/recarea/?recid=5749', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57507', 'Fish Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.521654, -121.072553, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground offers 5 walk-in tent-only sites near a small lake and the Cle Elum River. There is no fee and no services. Pack out your trash.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57507', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57515', 'French Cabin Creek Recreation Area', 'campground', 47.354401, -121.114600, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This dispersed camping area is located along the west bank of the Cle Elum River north of Cle Elum Lake and is accessed by Forest Service Road 4308.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57515', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57519', 'French Cabin Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.356394, -121.109122, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'French Cabin offers 12 miles of groomed snowmobile trails. Approximately 25 parking spaces. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57519', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57573', 'Icewater Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.113910, -120.902531, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located on Taneum Creek, this campground offers 15 campsites. The campground accesses North Fork Taneum Trail # 1377 and has a beginners motorcycle loop trail that originates in the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57573', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57595', 'Kachess Campground', 'campground', 47.356220, -121.246487, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Kachess Campground is a pleasant 5-1/2 mile drive from Interstate 90, Exit 62. The 92 acre Forest Service facility is located on the northwest shore of Kachess Lake with Little Kachess Lake to the immediate north. Set in dense old-growth evergreens and surrounded by high mountains, Kachess Campground has over 100 campsites and one group campsite (by reservation only). It is an excellent location for family camping. There are two boat launches and a picnic area. These water access points accommodate cartoppers and trailer boats and there is parking for vehicles & trailers. The south boat…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57595', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57643', 'Manastash Camp / Trailhead', 'campground', 47.034500, -120.954000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground offers 14 individual trailer/tent sites and an improved dispersed camping area for groups. Elevation 4200''', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57643', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57673', 'Mineral Springs Campground', 'campground', 47.290203, -120.699224, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along Highway 97, this campground offers 7 trailer/tent sites and a group site with a 50 person capacity. The namesake springs which were located near the present day campground smelled strongly of sulphur and dried up over 60 years ago.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57673', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57705', 'Owhi Campground', 'campground', 47.424400, -121.170000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This walk-in campground on Cooper Lake offers 22 tent-only sites. Elevation 2800'' [Click image for information]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57705', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5771', 'Lower Penstemon Campground', 'campground', 42.196513, -114.283857, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Lower Penstemon Campground is located 27 miles south of Hansen, ID on Rock Creek Road/County Rd. G3. The campground is located next to the Fourth Fork of Rock Creek (the main fork). There are 7 single family/individual sites in the campground. Camping fees are $8.00 per night. Sites can be reserved through Recreation.gov. Individual sites reserved through Recreation.gov will be posted. Sites that are not reserved are available on a first-come first-serve basis. Be sure a site is not reserved before you occupy. First-come first-serve customers must pay within 1/2 hour of occupying the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5771', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5772', 'Upper Penstemon Campground', 'campground', 42.194313, -114.285863, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Upper Penstemon Campground is located at the base of Magic Mountain Ski Area. This is a fee campground composed of 8 individual units and 1 group unit. Fee envelopes and a collection box are provided near the entrance and reservations are recommended. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June and September. Sites are handicapped accessible and campground amenities include a baseball diamond, horseshoe pits, and handicapped accessible toilets. The campground is well suited for motor homes, trailers, and tent camping. This area is popular in summer for trout fishing,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5772', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5773', 'Schipper Campground', 'campground', 42.322614, -114.267859, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'CLOSED DUE TO FIRE DAMAGE Schipper Campground is a developed, fee campground composed of 5 individual units adjacent to Birch Creek. It is an accessible day use area and is a convenient retreat for visitor''s from nearby Twin Falls, ID. The campground is suitable for tents and includes limited space for motor homes and trailers. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between April and October due. Campground amenities include handicapped accessible toilets, however no water is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5773', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5775', 'Diamondfield Jack Campground', 'campground', 42.171084, -114.277332, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Diamondfield Jack Campground and Picnic Area is located at the end of a paved road in Rock Creek. The campground is suitable for motor homes, trailers, and tent camping. This area is accessible year around. Campground amenities include drinking water, wheelchair accessible toilets, picnic tables, warming shelter, parking area, and fire rings. It is a winter play area from December through March. Pike Mountain and Eagle Trails (#239 and #243) are easy multi-use trails nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5775', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57755', 'Red Mountain Campground', 'campground', 47.365881, -121.102032, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground, located along Cle Elum River on Salmon La Sac road, offers 10 single campsites. [Click image for information]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57755', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5776', 'Father and Sons Campground', 'campground', 42.162700, -114.185734, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'CLOSED DUE TO FIRE DAMAGE Father and Sons Campground and Picnic Area is a developed campground located near Cottonwood Ridge. The campground is composed of 12 individual units and 1 group units that can accommodate a total of 100 people. The campground is suitable for trailer and tent camping. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June and September. Campground amenities include toilets. The area is attractive for exploration on an ATV or a mountain bike. Fishing opportunities can be found nearby at Big Cottonwood Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5776', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57765', 'Reecer Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.158839, -120.613478, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Reecer Creek offers 70 miles of groomed snowmobile trails. Approximately 75 parking spaces. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57765', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57767', 'Riders Camp', 'campground', 47.028930, -120.936732, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'INFORMATION POSTER Elevation 4,200 feet', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57767', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57777', 'Salmon La Sac Campground', 'campground', 47.403564, -121.098554, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This popular campground is located between the Cle Elum and Cooper Rivers, and offers 69 sites for both tent and RV camping. Some sites are pull through for larger vehicles. Prime location for hiking, fishing, swimming, and mountain biking in summer and early fall. [Click image for information]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57777', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57779', 'Salmon La Sac Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.392582, -121.092298, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Shared-use Sno-Park offering 38 miles of groomed snowmobile trails and 4 miles of groomed cross-country ski/snowshoe trails. Access to adjoining Red Mountain and Howson Creek voluntary non-motorized areas. Approximately 100 parking spaces. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57779', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5780', 'Harrington Fork Picnic Area', 'campground', 42.299269, -114.253278, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'CLOSED DUE TO FIRE DAMAGE Harrington Fork Picnic Area is accessible for a season that varies usually between April and October. The picnic area is fully accessible. Amenities include hand pumps and handicapped accessible toilets. No overnight camping is allowed. The Harrington Fork Trail (#006) is immediately accessible to the picnic area and it is a moderate terrain ten mile multi-use trail. Anglers can take advantage of the Harrington Fork Rock Creek that runs near the picnic area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5780', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5782', 'Pettit Campground', 'campground', 42.182669, -114.282166, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Pettit Campground and Picnic Area is composed of 8 individual units. The area is suitable for motor homes, trailers and tent camping. This is a fee campground. Fee envelopes and a collection box are provided near the campground entrance. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June and September. Campground amenities include toilets. A campground host manages the campground and visits the area weekly. No water is available at this site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5782', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5783', 'Bear Gulch Campground', 'campground', 42.227868, -114.378708, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Bear Gulch Campground is a developed campground composed of 8 individual units and 1 group unit near the Shoshone Wildlife Pond. The area is suitable for trailer and tent camping. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between May and October. Campground amenities include toilets and the facilities are handicapped accessible. A short trail from the campground goes to the pond which is fenced to provide habitat for bird and wildlife species; fishing is available in the creek and pond. For equestrians, there is a barrier-free stock loading ramp and corral near the campground.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5783', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57837', 'Swauk Campground', 'campground', 47.328127, -120.661841, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'A beautiful campground nestled in a grove of large Ponderosa Pine and western Larch trees. The campground offers 19 single campsites, 2 double campsites, and a picnic shelter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57837', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5784', 'Bostetter Campground', 'campground', 42.165809, -114.170110, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'CLOSED DUE TO FIRE DAMAGE Bostetter Campground is composed of 10 individual units and 1 group unit. It is located in a stand of Lodgepole pine and stretches along Cottonwood Creek with one site tucked up above in some Aspen trees. The campground is pack it in and pack it out. The area is suitable for trailer and tent camping. Anglers can take advantage of a nearby stream. Campground amenities toilets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5784', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5785', 'Third Fork Campground', 'campground', 42.253208, -114.249362, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'CLOSED DUE TO FIRE DAMAGE Third Fork Trailhead Picnic and Campground area is composed of 5 individual units and an accessible vault toilet. This area is suitable for motor homes and trailers and best suited for day use. Barrier free stock loading is available. Amenities include toilets and an accessible transfer station. Third Fork Trail (#004) is an easy multi-use trail that accesses an extensive trail system including Wahlstrom Hollow (#38) and Rim View Trails (#235), the latter a hiking/horse trail over moderate terrain. Rim View Trail is 9.5 miles long and runs from Buckskin Ridge to the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5785', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57859', 'Taneum Campground', 'campground', 47.108600, -120.856000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along Tanuem Creek near the site of a former CCC camp. The picnic shelter was built by the CCC''s. Ponderosa Pine and Douglas Fir shade the area. Camp ground is walk in only in June. Once snow melt ends and water levels in Taneum Creek slow to summer lows, access into the campground requires driving through Taneum Creek on a cement ford.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57859', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57861', 'Taneum Junction Campground', 'campground', 47.111900, -120.933000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground has a 15 vehicle and 75 person capacity. This is an improved dispersed camping area suitable for groups or individual camps which serves as a trailhead for single track trails open to both motorized and non-motorized use.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57861', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57867', 'Taneum Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.108329, -120.855967, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Taneum Sno-Park accesses 78 miles of groomed snowmobile trails. Approximately 25 parking spaces. More information can be found on the Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57867', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5788', 'Thompson Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.327908, -113.621212, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Thompson Flat Campground is a developed, fee picnic area and campground located near Lake Cleveland composed of 25 units; 21 units are individual units and 4 double units; 8 of these units are reservable through www.recreation.gov , and there are 3 group units. Group A can accommodate 40 people, Group B can accommodate 64 people and Group C can accommodate 56 people. Fee envelopes and a collection box are provided near the campground entrance. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between July and October. Reservations are available and recommended for both group sites.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5788', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5789', 'Lake Cleveland Campground - West Side', 'campground', 42.319094, -113.651841, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Lake Cleveland Campground is a very popular summer recreational facility. Located next to its namesake, the campground is divided into the East Side and West Side loops. Very popular with residents of local communities, the campground is often full every weekend from early July to Labor Day. Natural Features: At an elevation of 8,300 feet, the campground facility is located in an alpine lake basin below Mt. Harrison which has an elevation of 9,240 feet. Late season snowdrifts often block access to the campground until early to mid-July. The campground is near the timberline and alpine…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5789', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57919', 'Wish Poosh Campground', 'campground', 47.280032, -121.085246, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Wish Poosh is located in a mixed conifer forest on the south east shore of Cle Elum Lake. The campground offers 34 campsites suitable for RVs or tents. [Click image for information]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57919', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5792', 'Independence Lakes Campground', 'campground', 42.218269, -113.674353, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Independence Lake Campground and Picnic Area is a non-fee campground and picnic area where reservations are not required. There are 5 single sites. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between July through October. Sites are handicapped accessible. Campground amenities include 9 tables and grills, toilets, and livestock facilities. No drinking water or trash service is available. Nearby Independence Lakes Trail (NFS Trail 7035) is 3.1 miles to the Lake. Only non-motorized travel is authorized. The first mile is rocky, however the remainder is a reasonable grade with…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5792', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5794', 'Twin Lakes Campground (Albion Division)', 'campground', 42.317202, -113.625097, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Please contact the Minidoka Ranger District for updated information at 208-678-0430. Twin Lakes Picnic and Campground is a fee, non-reservation campground that can accommodate 100 visitors. The area is suitable for tent camping. The area is accessible for a season that varies usually between July through October. Amenities include toilets, fire rings, and tables, and three horse corrals. Water is not available. The campground provides access to the Skyline (# 513). The Skyline Trail is 26.2 miles in length. The trail begins at the back of the campground and ends at the City of Rocks National…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5794', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57945', 'Cottonwood Campground - Entiat Ranger District', 'campground', 48.021929, -120.644065, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', '25 campsites along the Entiat River at 3,100 feet elevation. Water, vault toilets & garbage service. Maximum trailer length 28 feet. 38 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57945', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5795', 'Bennett Springs Campground', 'campground', 42.326149, -113.602207, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Bennett Springs Campground is a primitive, non-fee, non-reservation campground located in the Albion Mountains. It is composed of 6 campsites that can accommodate up to 8 visitors per campsite. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June through October and campground amenities include chemical toilets. Fishing is available in the creek. Drinking water is not available. The campground is well suited for tent camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5795', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57965', 'Entiat Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.905700, -120.475900, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57965', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '57973', 'Fox Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.926045, -120.511235, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', '16 campsites along the Entiat River at 2,000 feet elevation. Water, vault toilets & garbage service. Maximum trailer length 28 feet. 27 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=57973', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58001', 'Lake Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.935528, -120.515084, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', '18 campsites along the Entiat River at 2,200 feet elevation. 9 of the sites are available for reservation at recreation.gov Water, vault toilets & garbage service. Maximum trailer length 25 feet. 28 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58001', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5803', 'Sublett Campground', 'campground', 42.327646, -113.002564, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Sublett Campground is a developed campground located two miles from Sublett Reservoir. This is a non-fee, non-reservation campground and picnic area. The campground is composed of 9 individual units that can accommodate up to 40 visitors. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June through November. Campground amenities include toilets, 9 tables and grills, RV sites, livestock facilities, and a boat ramp. The campground is well suited for tent and trailer camping. The campground is a pack in/pack out area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5803', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58033', 'North Fork Campground', 'campground', 47.987768, -120.580006, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Group site at 2,500 feet elevation. Maximum trailer length 25 feet. 33 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A. Vault toilet. Bring drinking water, toilet paper and pack out all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58033', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5804', 'Mill Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.430015, -113.013825, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Mill Flat Campground is a developed campground composed of 7 individual units located in an open setting within a canyon. This is a non-fee campground and picnic area where reservations are not required. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June through October. Campground amenities include restrooms. The campground is well suited for trailer and tent camping. Visitors can fish for trout in the stream and explore the mountains canyon by canyon on the extensive trail system.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5804', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58043', 'Pine Flats Campground', 'campground', 47.757641, -120.421926, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', '6 campsites near the Mad River at 1,600 feet elevation. Water, vault toilets & garbage service. Maximum trailer length is 28 feet. 14 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A. Individual sites and one group site. Group site: Maximum 40 people and 20 vehicles. Water, campfire rings, picnic area, garbage service, and vault toilets. No electricity. 28'' max trailer length.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58043', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58065', 'Silver Falls Campground', 'campground', 47.959259, -120.535911, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground has two loops and 31 trailer/tent sites at 2,400 feet elevation. Water, vault toilets & garbage service. Maximum trailer length 28 feet. 30 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A. Group Site: 1 site. 35'' max trailer length. $125/night plus $10 reservation fee. Reservations required, see below. Maximum 60 people & maximum 30 vehicles. Water, picnic tables, campfire rings, accessible toilets, garbage service and picnic shelter with a fireplace. No electricity.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58065', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5807', 'Clear Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.952848, -113.319767, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Clear Creek Campground is a non-fee campground and picnic area composed of 12 individual units and reservations are not required. This area is accessible for a season that varies usually between June through October. Campground amenities include toilets and the campground is well suited for tent and RV camping. Sites are handicapped accessible. Bull Flat (#001) and Lake Fork (#004) trails are popular with horseback riders, and hikers.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5807', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58073', 'Spruce Grove Campground', 'campground', 47.994833, -120.594230, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'DAY USE ONLY -- NO CAMPING -- Due to hazard trees 2 sites along the Entiat River at 2,900 feet elevation. Trailers not recommended. 34 miles up the Entiat River Road from Highway 97A. Vault toilet. No amenities. Bring drinking water, toilet paper and pack out all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58073', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58097', 'American Forks Campground', 'campground', 46.977020, -121.167121, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'OPEN FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 15th. American Forks Campground is located about 40 miles west of Naches, Washington, near the American River and Bumping River in the eastern Cascade Mountains. Natural Features: The Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest is defined by its diverse landscapes, boasting high glaciated alpine peaks, lush valleys of old growth forest, and rugged shrub-steppe country. The American Forks Campground is nestled in an old-growth forest of Douglas fir, western hemlock, and a cedar under story with grassy areas, ferns, and mosses. With the William O.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58097', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5812', 'Sawmill Campground', 'campground', 43.666507, -114.162879, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Sawmill Campground has 3 small, tight campsites; each with a fire ring and a picnic table. Sites to pitch a tent are small and limited by aspen within the campground. Parking is limited. Large RVs and trailers are not recommended. A single-unit, ADA-accessible SST vault toilet is found at the campground. Individual campsites are not considered ADA-accessible. An excellent site for a small picnic near a creek. Aspen trees shade the campsites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5812', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5813', 'Federal Gulch Campground and Trailhead', 'campground', 43.669307, -114.152876, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Federal Gulch Campground is a non-fee, non-reservation campground located on the East Fork of the Wood River. The campground is composed of 3 campsites on the East Fork of the Wood River. The trailhead provides access to Federal Gulch Tr. No. 169, which connects to the remote and seldom-visited Little Wood River country. The campground is generally accessible May through October. Campground amenities include a vault toilet is located in the campground, and each site has a fire ring and picnic table. Stock is permitted in designated areas and hitching rails are provided.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5813', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58135', 'Boulder Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.571437, -120.170040, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This Sno-Park offers groomed snowmobile trails and has 10 parking spaces. This Sno-Park gives access to East Chewuch Road (forest road #5010), Boulder Creek Road to Conconully and north onto forest road #39.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58135', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5814', 'Copper Creek/Garfield Campground', 'campground', 43.607500, -113.928900, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Copper Creek/Garfield Campground is a primitive, non-fee, non-reservation campground composed of 8 campsites in a canyon carved by Copper Creek. This area is accessible from May through October. Fishing is available in area streams. This trail extends north into the Challis National Forest. Campground amenities include a vault toilet, picnic tables, fire rings, and hitching posts for stock.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5814', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58141', 'Bumping Lake Campground', 'campground', 46.861304, -121.296370, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. This campground has an upper section and a lower section and offers barrier-free sites. It is located on the south shore of Bumping Lake with a boat launch located at the lower campground. The campground is operated by Rockey Mountain Concessionaire. None of the lakes, rivers, and ponds have designated swimming areas, thus swimmers will be sharing the water with boats and water craft. Please wear lifejackets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58141', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5815', 'Deer Creek Trailhead', 'campground', 43.528704, -114.502886, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Deer Creek Trailhead provides access to Deer Creek Tr. No. 158 and Kinsey Creek Tr. No. 319. The trailhead is located at the end of Deer Creek Rd. No. 097, and features a vault toilet and interpretive sign. The site is lightly used but provides access to one of the only 50" OHV trails on the Ketchum Ranger District.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5815', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58157', 'Cedar Springs Campground', 'campground', 46.970274, -121.166117, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. This campground is located along the Bumping River, just off Highway 410, and offers 2 multi-family sites as well as 14 single sites. Potable water on site and great hiking areas around American ridge. Only a few miles from Bumping Lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58157', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58173', 'Clear Lake North Campground', 'campground', 46.633163, -121.267549, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located below Clear Lake dam between Clear Lake and Rimrock Lake. 33 sites. There''s also a boat launch here. Water is available at nearby Clear Lake South Campground . Managed by White Pass Ski Resort. Fish Your National Forests: This site can be accessed by passenger car. Fish available include: Trout, Native Trout. Types of fishing available include: Shore, Motorized boat, Float tube, Fly, Spin, Bait. Fishing pier and boat launch available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58173', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58177', 'Clear Lake South Campground', 'campground', 46.628703, -121.268270, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closed for season This campground is located below Clear Lake Dam, just beyond Clear Lake North Campground . 22 sites. Managed by White Pass Ski Resort.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58177', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5818', 'Boundary Campground and Picnic Area', 'campground', 43.721508, -114.325880, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Boundary Campground is a developed, fee, non-reservation campground composed of 9 campsites located on Trail Creek approximately 2 miles northeast of the Sun Valley Resort Village. The 4-unit Boundary Picnic Area is adjacent to the campground and shares a vault toilet and hand pump for drinking water with it. The campground and picnic area are open the Friday before Memorial Day to September 30 annually. Amenities include drinking water from a hand pump; 2 vault toilets; refuse service; and a fire ring, grill stand, and picnic table in each site. Campsites also have a designated location to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5818', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58189', 'Cottonwood Campground - Naches RD', 'campground', 46.907371, -121.025623, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR WINTER SEASON. This campground is located along the Naches River, just off Highway 410. 16 sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58189', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58191', 'Cougar Flat Campground', 'campground', 46.916984, -121.234349, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. This campground has 12 sites and is a great location for hiking, fishing, hunting, horseback riding and mountain biking in summer and early fall. Nearby Bumping Lake offers visitors opportunities for boating, swimming and fishing. The campground is adjacent to William O Douglas Wilderness . Notice: a few sites within Cougar Flats are closed for the season due to hazard trees. if your reservation has been affected by this please call Recreation.gov at (877) 444-6777 Several trails are nearby making tis campground a perfect spot for a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58191', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58205', 'Crow Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.016520, -121.140529, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'OPEN FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 30th. This 15-site campground is located near the Little Naches River and is popular with motorcycle riders.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58205', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58215', 'Deep Creek Trailhead - Naches RD', 'campground', 46.752400, -121.361000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Deep Creek Trailhead has a stock/horse loading ramp and trailhead parking spots. It provides access to Twin Sisters Trail #980 , Indian Creek Trail #1105 , and William O. Douglas Wilderness .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5822', 'East Fork Baker Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.746303, -114.561567, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'East Fork Baker Creek Campground is a primitive non-fee, non-reservation campground composed of 7 campsites located by the East Fork of Baker Creek. This area is accessible from June through November. Campground amenities include a vault toilet and fire rings. Fishing is available in Baker Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5822', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58231', 'Dog Lake Campground', 'campground', 46.654572, -121.360359, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closed for the season on Oct 8, 2023. This campground is located on the southern shores of Dog Lake. Turning radius on interior campground roads is limited. Managed by White Pass Ski Resort.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58231', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58273', 'Halfway Flat Campground', 'campground', 46.980480, -121.095820, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closing for 2024 season on September 30th. Halfway Flat Campground is located about 30 miles west of Naches, Washington in the eastern Cascade Mountains. Natural Features: The Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest is defined by its diverse landscapes, boasting high, glaciated alpine peaks, lush valleys of old growth forest, and rugged shrub-steppe country. The Halfway Flat Campground is nestled in an old-growth forest of Douglas fir, western hemlock, and a cedar under story with grassy areas, ferns and mosses. With the William O. Douglas and Norse Peak Wilderness areas nearby, the location is…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58273', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58279', 'Hause Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.676023, -121.076376, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR WILDFIRE DANGER This campground is located along the Tieton River below Rimrock Lake Dam, just off U.S. Highway 12. Note: There is no water available, and no flush toilets. Sani-can toilets available. Bring your own water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58279', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58281', 'Hell''s Crossing Campground', 'campground', 46.965700, -121.264000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR SEASON. Re-opening spring of 2025 Located on the American River, this campground offers single sites and multi-family sites. Water is available at the west end only. Some sites are tent only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58281', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58293', 'Indian Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.644600, -121.243000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED for the season This campground is located on Rimrock Lake, near Clear Lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58293', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58311', 'Kaner Flat Campground', 'campground', 47.011000, -121.130000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'OPEN FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 30th. Located near the Little Naches River this campground offers an RV loop in a popular motorcycle area. Kaner Flat Campground has 49 sites. The site is paved with single and double camp units and equipped with picnic tables, campfire rings and vault toilets. Nearby Boulder Cave National Recreation Trail is one of the most popular places in the Naches District. Visitors can walk the accessible trail along the river or explore Boulder Cave. Interpretive signs along the trail explain the geology, plants, animals and fire history of the area.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58311', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58337', 'Little Naches Campground', 'campground', 46.990120, -121.098180, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'OPEN FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. Little Naches Campground sits along the bank of the Little Naches River. There are 17 sites, including back in sites with parking spurs ranging from 20-50 feet long and a multifamily site. The interior campground roads and parking spurs are hard-packed but not paved.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58337', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58343', 'Lodgepole Campground', 'campground', 46.914973, -121.384609, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Lodgepole Campground offers outdoor enthusiasts the opportunity to hike, fish, ski, raft and enjoy a multitude of outdoor recreational activities throughout the year. Beautiful rivers and streams, high elevation lakes, reservoirs, and small ponds provide an endless number of fishing opportunities for the experienced and beginning angler. The American River, adjacent to the campground, supports a variety of trout including rainbow, brook, and cutthroat. Lodgepole Campground offers several standard sites, accomodating both tent and RV camping. Picnic tables, vault toilets and drinking water are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58343', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58361', 'Longmire Meadow', 'campground', 47.027370, -121.153150, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closing for 2024 season on September 30th. Developed/Dispersed Camping, Vault Toilet. Water nearby at Kaner Flat Campground . Popular OHV staging area with motorcycle trails nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58361', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58383', 'Milk Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.982148, -121.092758, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Easy access off HWY 410 near the town of Cliffdell. Parking to accommodate 10 vehicles, Information board, Sani-can. See Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58383', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58409', 'Nile Feeding Area Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.849399, -121.006794, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This sno-park offers plenty of parking and 21 miles of groomed trails and great riding for all riders and family outings. Great area to view wildlife See Washington State Parks Winter Recreation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58409', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58437', 'Peninsula Campground', 'campground', 46.637110, -121.137740, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Dispersed camping area for RVs or tents. Located on the eastern shore of Rimrock Lake. Vault toilets and a boat launch.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58437', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58445', 'Pine Grass Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 46.622060, -121.292302, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This sno-park offers parking for 15 vehicles. Camping opportunities and a sani-can toilet, picnic tables, and fire rings. See Washington State SnoPark website', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58445', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5845', 'Caribou Campground', 'campground', 43.814793, -114.425106, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Caribou Campground is composed of 7 campsites which are first-come, first-serve, and is situated in a pine overstory near the Sawtooth National Recreation Area Visitor Center. Popular trail heads in the area include North Fork, West Fork, East Fork, and Murdock Creek. The trails in Northfork Canyon lead to Murdock Creek, Amber Lakes, Window Lake and into the Hemingway-Boulder Wilderness Area with views of Ryan Peak, Kent Peak, Glassford peak and Silver Peak in the Hemingway-Boulder mountains all of which are over 11,000 feet in elevation.. This is a terrific area for fishing in the Big Wood…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5845', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58455', 'Pleasant Valley Campground', 'campground', 46.944430, -121.328320, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'OPEN FOR SEASON. Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. Pleasant Valley Campground is smaller than other campgrounds in the area, offers about a dozen standard sites, accommodating both tent and RV camping. Picnic tables, vault toilets and drinking water are available. The American River, adjacent to the campground, supports a variety of trout including rainbow, brook, and cutthroat. The river also offers a scenic backdrop for swimmers braving its cold, refreshing waters. Nearby Mount Rainier National Park offers fantastic glimpses of glaciers, subalpine ecology and volcanic landscapes.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58455', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5846', 'Wood River Campground', 'campground', 43.793409, -114.457925, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Wood River Campground is composed of 30 campsites including 1 double-site and a picnic area which are all first-come, first-serve. Wood River Group Overnight Area is located inside the Wood River Campground, can accommodate up to 150 people, and may be reserved by visiting www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. The campground setting is heavily forested and divided by the Big Wood River. Trails in Northfork Canyon lead to the Amber Lakes, Window Lake, and into the Hemingway-Boulder Wilderness Area. This campground is located on the banks of the beautiful Big Wood River at an…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5846', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5850', 'Easley Campground (Wood River Valley Area)', 'campground', 43.780456, -114.537141, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Easley Campground is situated in groves of cottonwood and aspen and is composed of 10 campsites including 2 double-sites which can be reserved at www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. Easley Campground is located along the beautiful Big Wood River at an elevation of 6,800 feet, conveniently close to Ketchum only 14 miles south. Visitors enjoy fishing, hiking and soaking at Easley Hot Springs. A forest of Douglas fir, ponderosa pine, lodgepole pine and aspen offers plentiful shade in the campground. Colorful summer wildflowers are abundant and willows dot the banks of the river. The…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5850', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5851', 'Murdock Campground', 'campground', 43.805288, -114.420560, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Murdock Campground is composed of 11 campsites located in a pine overstory 2 miles north of the Sawtooth National Recreation Headquarters in the North Fork Canyon. The sites are all first-come, first-serve. This area is terrific for fishing in the Big Wood River and Murdock Creek. Hiking is wonderful in this area with the North Fork, West Fork, and East Fork trail heads leading up into the Hemingway-Boulder Wilderness Area. Wildlife viewing is superb along with the views of Ryan Peak, Kent Peak, Glassford peak and Silver Peak in the Hemingway-Boulder mountains all of which are over 11,000…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5851', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5852', 'North Fork Campground', 'campground', 43.787721, -114.425752, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'North Fork Campground is composed of 28 campsites including 3 double-sites located at the beginning of the 18.6 mile Harriman Trail. 26 of the 28 sites are currently available for reservation online or by phone. The campground is on the edge of the Big Wood River in a primarily aspen and cottonwood environment. Trails in North Fork Canyon lead to Amber Lakes, Window Lake and into the Hemingway-Boulder Wilderness Area and there is trail access from the campground to the Harriman trail. Fishing is available in the Big Wood River and surrounding creeks and the wildlife viewing is excellent.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5852', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58529', 'Sawmill Flat Campground', 'campground', 46.974610, -121.095890, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closing for 2024 season on October 7th. Located along the Naches River, this campground offers a Civilian Conservation Corps Shelter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58529', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58543', 'Soda Springs Campground', 'campground', 46.925900, -121.216000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR SEASON. Located on the Bumping River, this campground offers 2 Civilian Conservation Corps shelters and trailhead access.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58543', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58547', 'South Fork Bay Campground', 'campground', 46.627184, -121.131923, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closing for 2024 season on September 30th. Dispersed camping located near Rimrock Lake with RV and tent sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58547', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58613', 'White Pass Lake (Leech Lake) Campground', 'campground', 46.644965, -121.384205, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closing for season Oct. 30th 2023 Located on the northeastern shores of Leech Lake, this site also offers trailhead access to the Pacific Crest Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58613', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58625', 'Willows Campground', 'campground', 46.672761, -121.039212, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR WILDFIRE DANGER Willows campground is located along the Tieton River approximately 31 miles west of Yakima, Washington. Nearby hiking trails include: Little Wildcat Trail , Ironstone Mountain Trail and Grey Rock Trail. Whitewater paddling on the Tieton River is a great adventure, as well as fly and cast fishing. There are 16 sites, including back-in sites with parking spurs ranging from 20-35 feet long. The interior campground roads and parking spurs are hard packed but not paved.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58625', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58627', 'Windy Point Campground', 'campground', 46.693879, -120.907932, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED FOR WILDFIRE DANGER This campground is located along the Tieton River. Hiking is a popular activity that surrounds this 15 single family site campground. A few of the trails include Frost Mountain Lookout Trail, Keenan Meadows Trail and the Grey Rock Trail. The Tieton River offers whitewater paddling, great fishing and numerous water sports. Campground sits along the bank of the Tieton River. The site is a popular parking and take-out site for river rafters. There are 14 sites, including back in sites with parking spurs ranging from 21-37 feet long. The interior campground roads and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58627', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58637', 'Alpine Meadows Campground', 'campground', 48.046500, -120.834000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located along the Chiwawa River, 21 miles from Fish Lake. 8 campsites are located in a valley floor. Sites are occupied on a first come first served basis.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58637', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58639', 'Atkinson Flat Campground', 'campground', 48.002500, -120.819000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located along the Chiwawa River, 20 miles from Fish Lake. There are a total of 11 campsites along the floor of a large glacial carved valley. Sites are occupied on a first come first served basis.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58639', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58667', 'Bridge Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.563719, -120.783069, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located near the confluence of Bridge Creek and Icicle Creek, this campground is 9 miles from Leavenworth. There are 6 single sites that are not reservable, and 1 group site that can be reserved. This campground is close to many trails and trailheads.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58667', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58689', 'Chatter Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.606961, -120.886293, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This heavily-used campground is located about 16 miles up Icicle Creek Road/ Forest Road 7600, at the confluence of Icicle Creek and Chatter Creek. The campground consists of 12 single sites which cannot be reserved in advance, and one group site which must be reserved in advance at recreation.gov . Vault toilets, garbage service, and a small group shelter with a fireplace are maintained. The campground is close to the trailheads for many popular hiking trails. There is a nightly fee per vehicle parked in each site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58689', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58713', 'Chiwawa Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.818900, -120.698000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'See info and map link below. Lake Wenatchee and Entiat Valley Groomed Snowmobile Routes - Info and Map [PDF: 1.8 mb, 3 pages]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58713', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58731', 'Eightmile Campground', 'campground', 47.551579, -120.763789, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'A popular campground located along Icicle Creek, 8 miles from Leavenworth. Some campsites can now be reserved through recreation.gov . 60% of the sites are now reservation sites and 40% are first come, first serve. Reservations cannot be made less than three days in advance of the date of arrival. There is also a Group Site that can be reserved (reservations required).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58731', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58745', 'Finner Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.951393, -120.768842, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along Finner Creek, near the Chiwawa River, 17 miles from Lake Wenatchee, this campground offers trailhead access.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58745', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58747', 'Fish Lake Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 47.840000, -120.693000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This Sno-Park offers access to groomed snowmobile trails. See info and map link below. Lake Wenatchee and Entiat Valley Groomed Snowmobile Routes - Info and Map [PDF: 1.8 mb, 3 pages]', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58747', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5875', 'Lake View Campground', 'campground', 44.249550, -115.054974, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Lake View Campground is composed of 6 campsites including 1 double site, situated in a lodgepole pine overstory on Stanley Lake. All sites are first-come, first-serve. There is a boat ramp near this campsite and Stanley Lake offers excellent swimming, boating, waterskiing, canoeing, kayaking and fishing for rainbow, cutthroat, brook and bull trout. There are several hiking trails in the area including Stanley Lake trail head, Elk Mountain trail head and Lady Face Falls is nearby. Beautiful McGowan peak with an elevation of 9,860 is visible to the south.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5875', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58777', 'Glacier View Campground', 'campground', 47.823292, -120.810024, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located on the south shore of Lake Wenatchee. This campground also offers 16 walk-in sites located on the lakeshore.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58777', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58779', 'Goose Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.840515, -120.649167, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along Goose Creek, near the Chiwawa River, this site offers access to motorcycle trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58779', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5878', 'Iron Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.197951, -115.011179, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Iron Creek Campground is composed of 9 campsites alongside Iron Creek located in a lodgepole pine overstory to the south-west of Stanley. All sites are first-come, first-serve. Iron Creek trailhead and Alpine Way trail are located nearby for access into several lakes and creeks including Alpine lake, Sawtooth lake, Goat lake, Trail Creek lakes and the McGown lakes th the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness. This area is wonderful for hiking, fishing, wildlife viewing and enjoying the beauty of the Sawtooth Wilderness. Numerous mountain peaks including McGown Peak, Williams Peak, Thompson Peak,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5878', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58781', 'Grasshopper Meadows Campground', 'campground', 47.940500, -120.926000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along the White River, 10 miles from Lake Wenatchee, this campground offers river access.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58781', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5880', 'Trap Creek Campground - Hwy 21', 'campground', 44.319128, -115.095861, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Trap creek campground is a small campground offering one group site that consists of three smaller sites. The group site can accommodate up to 40 people. If the group site is not reserved, the individual sites are available on a first-come, first-serve basis. Reservations can be made by visiting www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. Summer wildflowers are plentiful and a mixed stand of pines shade the area with Trap Creek flowing nearby. Numerous sparkling lakes and streams, including the Salmon River dot the area, making for great rainbow and native westslope cutthroat trout…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5880', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58815', 'Ida Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.607606, -120.849235, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is concessionaire operated. It is located at the confluence of Ida Creek and Icicle Creek, 13 miles from Leavenworth, and is wheelchair accessible.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58815', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5882', 'Grandjean Campground', 'campground', 44.149034, -115.152367, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Grandjean Campground is composed of 31 campsites near the border of the Sawtooth Wilderness and the Boise National Forest. All sites are first-come, first-serve. It is situated in an old growth ponderosa pine forest. The Idaho Centennial Trail heads south along the Payette River, ultimately reaching a lush alpine paradise filled with alpine lakes. Once in the lake area, you can complete the loop back to Grandjean. Sawtooth Lodge is one mile away. Natural hot springs are 1.5 mile away. Horse trips are operated out of the Sawtooth Lodge and there are 10 sites for horse campers. This is a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5882', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58839', 'Johnny Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.599141, -120.816869, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located near the confluence of Johnny Creek and Icicle Creek in a forested setting, this first come first served campground is 12 miles from Leavenworth. There are two campgrounds -- an Upper Campground above Icicle Road and a Lower Campground close to Icicle Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58839', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5884', 'Elk Creek Campground - Hwy 21', 'campground', 44.265800, -114.723600, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Elk Creek Campground is composed of 3 campsites, located in a lodgepole pine understory, This small campground offers one group site that consists of three smaller sites. The group site can accommodate up to 40 people. If the group site is not reserved, the individual sites are available on a first-come, first-served basis. Reservations can be made by visiting www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. Expansive and scenic Elk Meadow is near the campground, providing a great location for bird watching and wildlife viewing. Numerous sparkling lakes and streams, including the Salmon River,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5884', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58843', 'Lake Creek Campground - Little Wenatchee River', 'campground', 47.876007, -121.014385, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Closed due to Irving Peak fire Located along the Little Wenatchee River, 11 miles from Lake Wenatchee.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5889', 'Buckhorn', 'campground', 44.162487, -114.886628, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'This is a great recreation area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5889', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58901', 'Napeequa Crossing Campground', 'campground', 47.919821, -120.894450, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along the White River, 7 miles from Lake Wenatchee, this site offers river access and trail access to Twin Lakes.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58901', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58905', 'Nason Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.799600, -120.716000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located near the southeastern end of Lake Wenatchee and is situated on both sides of Nason Creek. Electrical outlets are available in the restrooms. Some campsites can now be reserved through www.recreation.gov . 60% of the sites are now reservation sites and 40% are first come, first serve. Reservations must be made at least three days in advance of the date of arrival.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58905', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58917', 'Nineteenmile Campground', 'campground', 48.019500, -120.828000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along the Chiwawa River, 22 miles from Lake Wenatchee, this campground offers river access.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58917', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58935', 'Phelps Creek Campground/Horse Camp', 'campground', 48.069700, -120.849000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located near the confluence of Phelps Creek and the Chiwawa River, about 23 miles from Fish Lake, there are 7 tent sites and 6 equestrian sites at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58935', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58945', 'Rainy Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.851100, -120.963561, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located 10 miles away from Lake Wenatchee, this small campground provides access to Rainy Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58945', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58953', 'Riverbend Campground', 'campground', 47.965417, -120.786083, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This small campground is located along the Chiwawa River, 18 miles from Lake Wenatchee. River access is available at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58953', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58955', 'Rock Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.970100, -120.791000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located along Rock Creek, near where Rock Creek meets the Chiwawa River. 20 miles up the Chiwawa River from Lake Wenatchee, the campground offers trailhead access to Rock Creek and Estes Butte Trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58955', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58963', 'Rock Island Campground', 'campground', 47.608224, -120.916774, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground situated on both sides of Icicle Creek is located 17 miles up the Icicle Creek Road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58963', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5897', 'Salmon River Campground', 'campground', 44.250400, -114.869500, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'The Salmon River Campground has 2 sections, riverside and the north side of Hwy 75. It is composed of 30 campsites including 1 double-site. The campground is situated amongst lodgepole pines and sagebrush. All sites are first-come, first-serve. The campground allows easy access to numerous hot springs in the area. The town of Stanley is very close, visitors can take an afternoon to visit the fascinating Stanley Museum, which reveals the rich history of the area. This is an excellent site for fishing and hiking as Casiono Creek trailhead is close, leading you to either Little Casino Creek or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5897', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '58975', 'Schaefer Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.974400, -120.802000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along the Chiwawa River, 21 miles from Lake Wenatchee, river access is available at the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=58975', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5898', 'Casino Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.256390, -114.855278, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Casino Creek Campground is composed of 19 sites including 2 double-sites along the Salmon River. Sites 18 & 19 are for tent camping only and sites 12, 13 and 14 accommodate livestock tethered to hitching rails. Casino Creek trailhead is located within the campground leading to trails along Big Casino Creek and Little Casino Creek which lead to the Casino Lakes in the White Cloud Mountains to the east and the Sawtooth Mountains to the west. This area is terrific for fishing and hiking along the beautiful Salmon river and surrounding creeks. All sites are first-come, first-serve.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5898', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5899', 'Riverside Campground', 'campground', 44.266900, -114.849100, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Riverside Campground is composed of 17 campsites bordering the Salmon River located in a lodgepole pine forest. All sites are first-come, first-serve. Casino Creek trailhead leads to the isolated and pristine Casino Lakes and then into the beautiful White Cloud Mountains. This is an excellent area for fishing, hiking and backpacking. To maintain stream bank integrity sites 1 8 are available from mid-May through mid-September. Sites 10 17 are available from mid-May through August 15. This campground is 1 of 4 in the general area which include Salmon River campground, Casino Creek campground,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5899', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5900', 'Mormon Bend Campground', 'campground', 44.261600, -114.841100, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Mormon Bend Campground is composed of 15 campsites including 1 double-site bordering the Salmon River. All sites are first-come, first-serve. It is situated in a lodgepole pine forest along with sagebrush and some open meadows. Visitors can fish for trout and steelhead in the Salmon River and surrounding creeks. This campground is opened early in the season to accommodate steelhead fishermen. A designated put-in for float boaters is located within the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5900', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5901', 'Lower O''Brien Campground', 'campground', 44.257340, -114.694525, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Lower O''Brien Campground is composed of 10 campsites including 1 double-site on the Salmon River located in a lodgepole pine forest. All sites are first-come, first-serve. The Warm Springs Creek Trail is nearby. Visitors can fish for steelhead and trout or soak in the fabulous Sunbeam Hot Springs which maintains a temperature of 169 degrees fahrenheit. You can adjust the temperature by moving rocks to allow river water to flow in. A boat ramp at Yankee Fork is available for floating the river, which has 14 miles of Class III and IV rapids. An interesting trip is to explore the mining history…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5901', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5902', 'Upper O''Brien Campground', 'campground', 44.259222, -114.698283, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'The Upper O''Brien Campground is composed of 9 campsites including 1 double-site under lodgepole pines along the Salmon River. All sites are first-come, first-serve. Visitors can fish for steelhead and trout or soak in the fabulous Sunbeam Hot Springs which maintains a temperature of 169 degrees fahrenheit. You can adjust the temperature by moving rocks to allow river water to flow in. A boat ramp at Yankee Fork is available for floating the river, which has 14 miles of Class III and IV rapids. An interesting trip is to explore the mining history of the area by touring the Land of the Yankee…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5902', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5903', 'Whiskey Flats Campground', 'campground', 44.254864, -114.552384, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Whiskey Flats is a small campground comprised of 4 single-sites. All sites are first-come, first-serve. It is a popular fishing campground located along the Salmon River where there is excellent steelhead and trout fishing. Hiking and backpacking are popular in this area between the Salmon-Challis National Forest and the White Clouds Wilderness Area. There are several creeks to explore and try your luck fishing in. Torreys Hole boat launch is just to the west along Hwy 75 and a forest service road leads you south into the White Clouds Wilderness Area along Slate Creek through Sheephead Creek,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5903', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5904', 'Holman Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.248400, -114.530000, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Holman Creek Campground is composed of 10 campsites including 1 double-site near the Salmon River east of Stanley. Visitors will find excellent fishing for trout and steelhead in the Salmon River along with excellent rafting. The campground sits at the base of a tree-covered rock slope. Holman Creek runs through the campground. All sites are first-come, first-serve. The Yankee Fork Work Center and Clayton Museum are to the east along Hwy 75. Enjoy the beautiful scenery of the Salmon River between the White Clouds Wilderness area and the Salmon Challis National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5904', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59041', 'Tumwater Campground', 'campground', 47.678100, -120.732000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'TUMWATER CAMPGROUND CLOSED In 2014 Tumwater Campground was closed due to risk of debris flows and flooding resulting from conditions created by the Chiwaukum Fire. Tumwater Campground was already suffering from aging infrastructure at that time. In the intervening years of closure the campground sewage treatment system was determined to be inoperable and in need of replacement, hazard trees in the area accumulated, and other infrastructure passed the point of serviceability. The Forest would like to redesign and repair Tumwater Campground to return it to service while also performing stream…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59041', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59065', 'White River Falls Campground', 'campground', 47.952700, -120.940000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located along the White River, 11 miles from Lake Wenatchee, this campground does not have a trailer turnaround. It is located near a waterfall. Please use caution on rocks.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59065', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59081', 'Eightmile Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.599540, -120.167140, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Open, easily visible Sno-Park parking area on the right side of the road, suitable for trailers. Gives access to groomed snowmobile routes up Chewuch River, up 8 Mile Creek and to Sweetgrass Butte. The Sno-Park has a plowed parking area and has a vault toilet. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59081', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59087', 'Ballard Campground', 'campground', 48.660504, -120.542314, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along the West Fork Methow River gives access to nearby hiking trails: Robinson Creek Trail 478 and Lost River/ Monument Creek Trail 484 entering the Pasayten Wilderness and the West Fork Methow Trail 480 .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59087', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59105', 'Black Canyon Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.067260, -120.021420, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Black Canyon Sno-Park gives access to groomed snowmobile trails to Chelan Ridge and Parrish Peak, Cooper Mountain, Oss Peak, and Ski Peak areas with many scenic views. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59105', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59107', 'Black Pine Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.313700, -120.273000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Majestic landscape views. Boat launch, fishing, two floating docks. Interpretive accessible trail. Wildlife viewing. Picnic area for up to 12 people (Picnic area: $5 or NW Forest Pass / America the Beautiful Pass). Maximum length of site is 30 feet. Camp Hosts on site during the summer months.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59107', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59123', 'Buck Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.606060, -120.202590, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Small, quiet forested campground. Boat landing, adequate for small crafts. Successful fishing early in the year. Lake stocked. Mountain biking opportunites. Maximum length of site is 25 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59123', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59131', 'Camp Four Campground', 'campground', 48.715233, -120.125314, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along the Chewuch River on paved road #51, 18 miles north of Winthrop. Hiking and driving opportunities nearby. Some sites maximum length of site is 16 feet. Trailers not recommended.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59131', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59145', 'Chewuch Campground', 'campground', 48.673900, -120.136920, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Small, remote campgroud surrounded by Ponderosa Pine. Walking and bicycle opportunities. Some sites have maximum lenght of 35 feet. This campground is located along the Chewuch River 15 miles north of Winthrop, Washington.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59145', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5917', 'Redfish Lake Recreation Complex', 'campground', 44.119600, -114.929300, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Redfish Lake is at the headwaters of the Salmon River, whose waters flow north to meet the Snake River and continue to the Columbia River and the Pacific Ocean. As late as the 1950''s, more than 4,000 sockeye salmon made the annual 900-mile (1,440-km) pilgrimage from the ocean to their spawning grounds in the Sawtooth Valley. However, in recent years only between 2-20 have returned each year. In an effort to save the endangered fish, whose bright red color gave Redfish Lake its name, the National Marine Fisheries Service established a local hatchery. Since 1999, the lake has been stocked with…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5917', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59203', 'Early Winters Campground', 'campground', 48.597586, -120.446244, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground, along Early Winters Creek, is located near the confluence of Early Winters Creek and the Methow River. There are two trails nearby, within 4 miles of this campground: Cedar Creek Trail 476 and Driveway Butte Trail 481.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59203', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59227', 'Falls Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.635240, -120.155580, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along the Chewuch River. with swimming opportunities in summer after high water subsides. A paved, 1/4 mile trail to scenic Falls Creek waterfalls is across the road from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59227', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59239', 'Flat Campground', 'campground', 48.614520, -120.195020, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along Eightmile Creek. Easy access for trailers. On paved forest road #5130.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59239', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59241', 'Foggy Dew Campground', 'campground', 48.205660, -120.196040, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located at the confluence of the North Fork Gold Creek and Foggy Dew Creek. Nearby trails allow hiking and mountain biking, there is also access to a motorbike use area. Sawtooth Backcountry multiple use trail brochure with map showing which trails are open to hikers, horses, mountain bikes and motorcycles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59241', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59255', 'Goat Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.581770, -120.373760, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Forested Goat Creek Sno-Park gives access to many scenic areas on groomed snowmobile routes to Goat Peak area, Blackpine Basin area, Goat Creek to Banker Pass to Cub Pass and Sweetgrass Butte area. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59255', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5926', 'Outlet Campground', 'campground', 44.141042, -114.911481, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Outlet Campground on Redfish Lake is composed of 19 sites, including 7 double-sites and all sites accept reservation which can be made at www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. The campground is situated in a lodgepole pine forest. The Redfish Lake Visitor Center offers area information and interpretive programs along with equestrian stables, a dump station, and boat rentals. There is a boat ramp at Sandy Beach boat launch, on the east shore of the lake. Take a short tour on the interpretive Fishhook Nature Trail or a longer walk west into the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness to battle…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5926', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59263', 'Hart''s Pass Campground', 'campground', 48.720360, -120.669600, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Great views. Alpine meadows. This forested campground is located in the Hart''s Pass Area, near the Pacific Crest National Scenic Trail. No trailers allowed on Forest Road 5400 to Hart''s Pass (very narrow road).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59263', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59273', 'Honeymoon Campground', 'campground', 48.696400, -120.264170, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested, small quaint camp located along Eightmile Creek is named after honeymoon spot of past forest ranger and wife. Maximum length of campsite is 22 feet. Beautiful but challenging Copper Glance Trail #519 is nearby, travel about 4 miles north of campground on Eightmile Road 5130 and look on left side of road for an old road closed to vehicles, this is the beginning of the trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59273', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5928', 'Sunny Gulch Campground', 'campground', 44.175191, -114.910587, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Sunny Gulch Campground is composed of 45 campsites including 8 double-sites situated in a lodgepole pine overstory. 10 of the sites accept reservations including 1 of the double-sites, and the Sunny Gulch Pavillion & Picnic Area. Reservations can be made at www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. All other campsites are first-come, first-serve. There is excellent fishing in the Salmon River which includes rainbow trout, westslope cutthroat trout and occasional hybrid cutbow and bull trout. A day use area for picnicking and fishing is located near the campground entrance. This…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5928', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59281', 'Klipchuck Campground', 'campground', 48.597360, -120.513000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located near Early Winters Creek, has majestic trees with a stream and good hiking opportunites nearby. Units combinable to accommodate groups.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59281', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5930', 'Glacier View Campground', 'campground', 44.146965, -114.915319, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Glacier View Campground is composed of 64 campsites including 9 double-sites on the north shore of Redfish Lake. The campsites accept reservations which can be made by going to www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. North Shore Picnic Area is across the road and can be reserved for groups. The campground is situated in a lodgepole pine forest. The Redfish Visitor Center offers area information and interpretive programs. There is a boat ramp at Sandy Beach boat launch on the east shore of the lake. Take a short tour on the interpretive Fishhook Nature Trail or a longer walk west into…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5930', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59303', 'Lone Fir Campground', 'campground', 48.581300, -120.624000, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground, surrounded by nearby mountains, is located along Early Winters Creek on Highway 20. This campground has beautiful mountain views, access to Lone Fir Trail 535 and is near Cuttthroat Creek Trail 483 . Good overnight spot for bicyclists. Next campground westbound is located at Diablo Lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59303', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5931', 'Point Campground', 'campground', 44.139966, -114.925545, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Point Campground is composed of 17 campsites on the west side of Redfish Lake. This campground is consistently rated as one of the top campsites in the country. Sites 1 - 8 are for walk-in tent camping only. Motorhomes and trailers are not allowed at this campground. Reservations can be made by visiting www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. This campsite is situated in a lodgepole pine forest. The visitor Center offers area information and interpretive programs. The campground features a sandy beach and a day use area for picnicking and great fishing for trout is in the lake. Take a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5931', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59317', 'Loup Loup Campground', 'campground', 48.394890, -119.902100, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located on Frazer Creek. Good location for large groups. Beautiful Western Larch trees. Acess to mountain bike trails and scenic drives.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59317', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5932', 'Chinook Bay Campground', 'campground', 44.164037, -114.904499, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Chinook Bay Campground is composed of 13 campsites on the north side of Little Redfish Lake on Little Redfish Creek and is situated in a lodgepole pine overstory. All sites are first-come, first-serve. Kayaking, canoeing, wading, hiking, biking, and floating are popular activities. Redfish Lake offers interpretive trails, a visitor center, interpretive programs, equestrian stables, boat rentals, and a dump station. Several trailheads are in the surrounding area including Alpine Way and Redfish trail which lead into the Sawtooth Wilderness, and Boundary Creek trail which leads into the White…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5932', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59329', 'Meadows Campground', 'campground', 48.709240, -120.674090, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Great views. Alpine meadows. Access to Pacific Crest National Scenic Trail. This campground is located in the Hart''s Pass Area. No trailers allowed on Forest Road 5400 (very narrow road). Guard station at Hart''s Pass.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59329', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5933', 'Mountain View Campground', 'campground', 44.161685, -114.904765, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'This campground is located on the east side of Little Redfish Lake. There are six campsites which are all first-come, first-serve. Enjoy fishing, canoeing, kayaking, swimming and camping alongside Little Redfish Lake. Several trailheads are in the surrounding area including Alpine Way and Redfish which lead into the Sawtooth Wilderness, and Boundary Creek trail which leads into the White Clouds Wilderness. Photography of the beautiful Sawtooth and White Clouds Wilderness areas and surrounding lakes and mountains is very popular here. Redfish Lake Visitor Center offers informational and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5933', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5934', 'Mt. Heyburn Campground', 'campground', 44.134624, -114.915471, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Mt. Heyburn Campground is composed of 19 campsites on the east side of Redfish Lake and all sites are first-come, first-serve. The campground is situated in a lodgepole pine forest. The Visitor Center offers area information and interpretive programs. There is a boat ramp at Sandy Beach boat launch, on the eastern shore of the lake. Take a short tour on the interpretive Fishhook Nature Trail or a longer walk west into the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness to battle wild cutthroat in the alpine lakes. A section of the Idaho Centennial Trail passes near the area. Equestrian stables, a dump station,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5934', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59347', 'Mystery Campground', 'campground', 48.401960, -120.471700, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Small Group Site. This small, quiet, forested campground is located along the Twisp River about 12.5 miles west of Twisp. Enjoy hiking on nearby trails, bicycling on quiet forest roads or mountain biking on nearby Twisp River Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59347', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5935', 'Sockeye Campground', 'campground', 44.132097, -114.917344, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Sockeye Campground is composed of 23 secluded campsites including 6 double-sites on the shore of Redfish Lake. All sites are first-come, first-serve. The campground is situated in a lodgepole pine forest. The Visitor Center offers area information and interpretive programs. There is a boat ramp at Sandy Beach boat launch, on the east shore of the lake. Take a short tour on the interpretive Fishhook Nature Trail or a longer walk west into the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness to battle wild cutthroat trout in the alpine lakes. A section of the Idaho Centennial Trail passes near the area.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5935', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59351', 'Nice Campground', 'campground', 48.632580, -120.221800, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'CLOSED due to Wildfire Damage Small Group Site . This forested campground is located along Eightmile Creek, near a beaver pond. This small campground is good for small group camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59351', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59359', 'North Summit Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.390690, -119.889090, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'North Summit Sno-Park See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59359', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5936', 'Redfish Inlet Campground', 'campground', 44.099309, -114.953075, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Redfish Lake Inlet is accessible either through water access: shuttle boat, kayak, canoe or hiking in. The campground consists of 4 sites and is first-come, first-serve. This site has trash removal and toilets but no potable water. It is located at the very southern end of Redfish lake by the Redfish Inlet trailhead. Enjoy hiking Redfish trail along Mt. Heyburn, Braxon Peak, Grand Mogul and Decker Peak near the Bench lakes and Saddle back lakes in the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness area. Enjoy hiking, swimming, fishing and kayaking from this unique location.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5936', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59381', 'Poplar Flat Campground', 'campground', 48.421260, -120.497540, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Forested campground with a community kitchen, access to Twisp River Trail, and other trailheads nearby. Good Group campground and a picnic area for up to 12 people. Wildlife viewing opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59381', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59399', 'River Bend Campground', 'campground', 48.652160, -120.555050, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along West Fork Methow River and gives access to nearby trails: West Fork Methow Trail , Robinson Creek Trail and Monument Creek /Lost River trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59399', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59413', 'Ruffed Grouse Campground', 'campground', 48.681240, -120.258830, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This forested campground is located along Eightmile Creek. Small campground is good for small group camping. Maximum length of site is 35 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59413', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5942', 'North Shore (Alturas) Campground', 'campground', 43.918383, -114.866915, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'The North Shore campground is composed of 10 single-sites and 4 double-sites on beautiful Alturas lake and is situated in a mixed conifer setting. All sites are first-come, first-serve. Spend sunny summer days fishing for trout, waterskiing, sailing, motorized boating, swimming, and picnicking by the lake. Cabin Creek trail head to the north or Alturas Lake Creek trail head to the west provide hiking trails into the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5942', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5943', 'Smokey Bear (Alturas) Campground', 'campground', 43.919784, -114.862662, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Smokey Bear Campground is composed of 8 single-sites and 3 double-sites on beautiful Alturas Lake situated in a mixed conifer setting. All sites are first-come, first-serve. A group picnic area is located on the east side of the campground. Trails at the end of Forest Road #205 lead to Alturas Lake Creek, Eureka Gulch and to Alpine Creek to the north in the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness. At this campground there is a boat ramp and boat trailer parking area. This is a superb place to spend sunny summer days fishing for trout, sailing, motorized boating, swimming, and picnicking by the lake. .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5943', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59433', 'South Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.438510, -120.529780, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'This campground is located near the confluence of South Creek and the Twisp River and gives access to several trailheads for day hikes. Enjoy bicycling and scenic drives. This campground gives access to the Twisp River Trail 440 and also gives access to the South Creek Trail 401 and nearby Scatter Creek Trail 427 , which both go into the Lake Chelan-Sawtooth Wilderness', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59433', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59439', 'South Fork Gold Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.156600, -120.149960, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'In winter months this Sno-park gives access to South Fork Gold Creek area groomed snowmobile trails. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59439', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5944', 'Alturas Inlet Campground', 'campground', 43.905101, -114.880403, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Alturas Inlet Campground, located on beautiful Alturas lake, is composed of 28 campsites including 8 double-sites. This site accepts reservations which can be made at www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. A day use beach and picnic area is located within walking distance of the campground on the north side of the lake. There is excellent canoeing, kayaking and fishing available on Alturas lake as well as Perkins Lake. Spend sunny summer days fishing for trout, sailing, motorized boating, swimming, and picnicking by the lake. No personal watercraft are allowed on Alturas lake or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5944', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5945', 'Chemeketan Campground - Salmon River Headwaters', 'campground', 43.849072, -114.752873, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Chemeketan is a marvelously secluded group area that can accommodate up to 150 people and accepts reservations which can be made by visiting www.recreation.gov or by calling (877)444-6777. It is located in a lodge pole pine forest near the Salmon river. At the base of Galena Summit on Hwy 75 take FS Rd 215 approximately 3 miles to the campground. Visitors can enjoy fishing for rainbow trout, westslope cutthroat trout, bull trout, occasional hybrid cutbow and steelhead in the Salmon River. You can explore the Idaho Centennial Trail or admiring the marvelous views. This campground is reached…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5945', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5946', 'Pettit Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.984452, -114.869270, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Pettit Lake Campground is located approximately two miles west of Hwy 75 on FS Rd 208. It is in a secluded area next to Pettit Lake nestled at the base of rolling hills and majestic peaks. Swimming, fishing, kayaking and canoeing are wonderful activities for Pettit lake. There are 9 single-sites and 3 double-sites which are all first-come, first-serve. Tin Cup trailhead leading into the beautiful Sawtooth Wilderness is located at the north end of the campground. There is a day use picnic area adjacent to the campground. Personal watercraft are not allowed on Pettit lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5946', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59473', 'Twisp River Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.351890, -120.353790, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Forested Sno-Park parking gives access to groomed snowmobile trails around Twisp River area from Dec. 1st to April 1st. When snow melts out, this parking area gives access to the Twisp River Trail #440 , going the length of Twisp River, 15 miles, to Gilbert Trailhead near North Creek. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59473', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5948', 'Alturas Tent Camping Area', 'campground', 43.925800, -114.849900, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'This tent camping area is accessible by hiking in, and consists of 4 single-sites and 2 double-sites on the east side of beautiful Alturas Lake. It is first-come, first-serve. Experience a quiet, serene, relaxing time in the heart of the Sawtooth National Recreation Area with the Sawtooth Mountains to the west, Smoky Mountains to the south and the Hemingway-Boulder Mountains to the east. Fishing is terrific in Alturas lake along with swimming, kayaking and canoeing. Capturing the scenic beauty, plants and wildlife through photography is ideal at this unique location. It includes flush…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5948', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59485', 'War Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.367610, -120.398300, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Located near the confluence of War Creek and the Twisp River, this forested campground has two sections. One section stretches along the seasonal War Creek and has long parking aprons that are well-suited to recreational vehicles. The sounds of Twisp River can be heard in the distance. There are a few sites in a small grassy meadow. Mature Douglas fir provide ample shade to most campsites. The other section is small and just off the roadway. It is best suited for smaller vehicles as well as tent campers. A thick middle and understory in both sections provide good privacy between some sites.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59485', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59513', 'Yellowjacket Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.652320, -120.498640, null, 'Okanogan-Wenatchee National Forest', 'Forested Yellowjacket Sno-Park gives access to snowmobile trails in Hart''s Pass and Blackpine Basin areas. These trails have scenic views. See MAP', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/okawen/recarea/?recid=59513', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59711', 'Lofton Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 42.262100, -120.818142, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Lofton Reservoir Campground is one of the three main points of interest in the Lofton Recreation Area. Located 45 minutes east of Bly, Oregon, this highly developed campground features 26 campsites. 24 of the campsites are RV sites. The road is paved all the way to Lofton Area Reservoir, ideal if you''re towing a trailer or boat. A camp host is on site throughout the summer months and provides visitor information. These spacious campsites accommodate trailers and feature grills, fire rings, picnic tables, and tent pads. There are four vault toilets, five group sites, and one ADA designated…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59711', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59715', 'Digit Point Campground', 'campground', 43.226734, -121.966545, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'For outdoor enthusiasts looking for a campground in a peaceful forest setting with great fishing and a variety of hiking opportunities, Digit Point Campground is the place. This scenic campground is located on the south shore of Miller Lake 35 minutes west of Chemult, Oregon. The location of the campground places many campsites on the lake shore with scenic views of the lake and Mt. Thiels en. A dense growth of mixed conifers including hemlock, white pine, white fir and sugar pine, provide ample shade. Osprey, eagles, loons and grebes are local residents. June and July are heavy mosquito…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59715', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59719', 'Scott Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.888029, -121.925932, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Scott Creek Campground is located 50 minutes southwest of Chemult, Oregon. This site lies off the beaten path and is an ideal camping destination if you want to relax in a serene and remote setting. A mix of conifers like lodgepole, ponderosa pines, and white firs shade the six campsites. You''ll find each site with a picnic table and fire ring. There is one vault toilet and an information board. Scott Creek flows peacefully through the north side of the campground and you may see a few small trout swimming in the creek. In the fall, this campground is popular amongst hunters. There is no…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59719', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5972', 'Bowns Campground', 'campground', 43.606801, -114.881898, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Bowns Campground, located 25 miles east of Featherville and 18 miles north of Fairfield, is a developed campground composed of 10 units along Big Smoky Creek. Two of the camp sites are double family units. Camping, fishing, hiking, and picnicking are popular activities. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings, drinking water (seasonally) and restrooms. Miller Creek Trail (#087) starts just south of the campground and is open to motorcycles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5972', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59721', 'Head of the River Campground', 'campground', 42.732438, -121.418448, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 50 minutes northeast of Chiloquin, OR, Head of the River Campground is a rustic forest camp situated at the headwaters of the Williamson River at the base of the hillside. The pure, spring-fed river flows by the rustic campground. There are five campsites and one vaulted toiled. Amenities include picnic tables and camp fire rings. June and July are heavy mosquito months, so bring bug spray. There are no official trails for hiking at Head of the River, but you can walk down to the bank. Fly-fishing opportunities abound nearby; check the State of Oregon fishing regulations for precise…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59721', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59723', 'Williamson River Campground', 'campground', 42.658572, -121.855084, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'The Williamson River Campground is conveniently located just off Highway 97 about five minutes north of Chiloquin, Oregon. There are 19 campsites with picnic tables, fire grates, three vault toilets, and two hand pumps round out the amenities at this campground. One campsite is ADA accessible. Ponderosa pines and sagebrush populate the landscape and contrast with the crystal clear Williamson River. Due to its close proximity to the highway, this is a popular campground. You can mountain bike on miles of Forest Service roads, go fishing, or explore day hikes opportunities. Situated next to the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59723', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59725', 'Aspen Point Campground @ Lake of the Woods', 'campground', 42.384117, -122.214336, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located approximately 40 minutes west of Klamath Falls Oregon, Aspen Point Campground offers many amenities. This scenic campground is located on the northeast shore of Lake of the Woods. It features 58 camp sites with a camp host. Within the total campsites, 50 are RV sites, eight double campsites, seven tent only campsites, and one group site. There are five restrooms (maintained May 1st though October 1st). Improvements at Aspen Point campground include durable aggregate around every picnic table and fire grate to diminish overall dust and dirt. Visitors can enjoy motorized and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59725', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59729', 'Odessa Picnic Site', 'campground', 42.429979, -122.061221, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located approximately 35 minutes west of Klamath Falls, Oregon, this picnic site features large ponderosa pines, Douglas firs, and an abundance of natural vegetation. Amenities include picnic tables, fire rings and one vault toilet. A steep boat ramp for small boats is available to access Klamath Lake through a water channel. There is no dock, so be prepared to wade in the water to board your boat. Odessa''s peaceful and secluded setting is situated on the Klamath Basin Birding Trail and affords many opportunities to view birdlife. June and July are heavy mosquito months, so bring bug spray.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59729', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5973', 'Pioneer Campground', 'campground', 43.490500, -114.831100, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Pioneer Campground, which is situated next to Soldier Mountain Ski Area, is a developed campground composed of 5 units on Soldier Creek. The campground can be reserved in its entirety for groups of up to 50 people. The amphitheater and adjacent picnic area can be used for group events. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings, drinking water and a restroom. The South Fork and North Fork of Soldier Creek trails begin along Forest Road 093 and join a major network of trails in the Soldier Mountains.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5973', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59731', 'Sunset Campground @ Lake of the Woods', 'campground', 42.365937, -122.201825, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes west of Klamath Falls, Oregon, Sunset Campground provides 64 camp sites and a camp host. These campsites include picnic tables, and fire rings. All 64 camp sites provide RV parking (although there are no hook-ups available) and two of the campsites are ADA accessible. There are three renovated restrooms, one for each loop, with electric flush toilets, running water, and automatic hand dryers. Nearby, the Lake of the Woods Resort offers dining options, boat rentals, and basic supplies. Sunset also has a day use area , tucked in next to the campground and ideal for boating.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59731', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59733', 'Can Springs Campground', 'campground', 42.380200, -120.168675, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located on hour northeast of Lakeview, Oregon, Can Springs births a bubbling creek that flows through this primitive forest camp with a riparian vegetation area bordering it. Large ponderosa pine trees help create a wonderful place to explore or relax in nature''s solitude. There are three campsites with picnic tables and fire rings. There is no potable water. Visitors need to pack plenty of water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59733', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59735', 'Cottonwood Recreation Area Campground', 'campground', 42.284155, -120.638411, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'The Cottonwood Recreation Area, located 45 minutes northwest of Lakeview, Oregon, is one of the busiest campgrounds in the southeast zone of the Fremont-Winema National Forest. Western white pine, white fir offer shade and aspens turn sunny gold every autumn. Abundant deer and even black bear can be sighted strolling through the campground. It''s essential to pack all food away in vehicles or hang it high. This campground features 22 campsite, six vault toilets, potable water, and a seasonal camp host. Each campgrounds has a picnic table and campfire ring. Additionally, there are four walk-in,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59735', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5974', 'Willow Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.606498, -115.143909, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Willow Creek Campground is a small site composed of 6 camping units. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings and a restroom. Campground was renovated in 2021 and has a new vault toilet, new site furniture and a new layout.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5974', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59741', 'Dog Lake Campground/Boating Site/Picnic Site', 'campground', 42.084530, -120.707723, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Dog Lake Campground is located approximately 55 minutes west of Lakeview, Oregon. The campground is a serene destination for those seeking to fish and relax in a lakeside setting. It offers 20 campsites and four vault toilets. Each campsite has a picnic table and campfire ring. Dog Lake Boating and Picnic Sites are across from the campground. Non-motorized boats and boats with electric motors are allowed at Dog Lake. There is a large parking area with adequate trailer turnaround, and one vault toilet. In addition to the boat ramp, you''ll find a fishing dock. Dog Lake attracts a multitude of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59741', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59743', 'Drews Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.119842, -120.580497, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 35 minutes southwest of Lakeview, Oregon, this small and secluded creekside campground is ideal for a family or group. A bridge crosses over Drews Creek to the campground. Three campsites feature picnic tables and fire rings. Conveniently, there is a day use area within the campground with five tables, two fire rings, and horseshoe pits. You''ll find one vault toilet for the campground and one for the day use area. Drews Creek offers peace and quiet under a majestic ponderosa pine canopy. Riparian vegetation dominates the land around Drews Creek. There is no potable water. Visitors…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59743', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59745', 'Mud Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.282742, -120.207180, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 35 minutes northeast of Lakeview, Oregon, Mud Creek campground is a quiet campground with seven spacious sites among ponderosa and lodgepole pines, as well as some aspens and cottonwood trees. Amenities include picnic tables and fire grates at each campsite, potable water, and one vault toilet. Recreational opportunities include fishing, bird watching, wildlife viewing, and wading in Mud Creek. Crane Mountain National Recreation Trail is two miles to the west, accessed at the Walker Trailhead for those interested in hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59745', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59749', 'Twin Springs Campground', 'campground', 42.157280, -120.212374, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes southeast of Lakeview, Oregon, Twin Springs campground offers three peaceful campsites at 6,300 feet elevation. Twin Springs gurgles up in the center of the forest camp amid tall ponderosa pine, white fir, and aspen trees. There is a lush riparian understory along the creek and bright wildflowers in the late spring and summer. Amenities at Twin Springs include picnic tables and fire grates, and one vault toilet. Visitors can enjoy bird watching, wildlife viewing (deer are common) and hiking on the Crane Mountain National Recreation Trail , located two miles west and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59749', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5975', 'Willow Creek Transfer Camp', 'campground', 43.625972, -115.134433, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Willow Creek Transfer Camp is composed of 4 large camping units. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings, a restroom, corrals, mangers and barrier free stock loading ramps. Campsites and restroom were renovated in 2021-2022. ADA loading ramp and horse facilities are currently under renovation. The Willow Creek Trail No. 019 (single track trail) is located on the north end of the campground and is open motorcycles but closed to ATVs and UTVs.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5975', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59751', 'Vee Lake Trailhead/Campground', 'campground', 42.422047, -120.162119, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Vee Lake Trailhead/Campground is a ending point for the southern segment Fremont National Recreation Trail in the North Warner Mountains. The trailhead is located one hour 15 minutes northeast of Lakeview, Oregon. The site overlooks Hart Mountain National Wildlife Refuge on the edge of the high desert. The trailhead offers two camping sites and one vault toilet that are maintained during the open season. The mixed forest features ponderosa pine, white fir, and some aspen stands. Vee Lake is stocked with rainbow trout, and there is a launch for electric motor boats and canoes. One unique…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59751', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59753', 'Willow Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.092966, -120.201922, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'The Willow Creek Campground offers secluded tent and trailer sites in a large ponderosa pine and aspen setting. The campsites are located on the banks of Willow Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59753', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59755', 'Campbell Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.564624, -120.752322, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'The Campbell Lake Campground offers camping, a picnic area and boat launch in a high mountain lake setting located one hour and 20 minutes southwest of Paisley, Oregon. There are 18 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings, three vault toilets, potable water, and garbage service from Memorial Day to Labor Day. Campbell Lake, lined with grassy and pebbly shores, is stocked with rainbow trout, making it ideal for fishing, swimming, and boating. There is also a boat ramp for non-motorized or electric motor boats. Additional picnic tables and another vault toilet are located in the day use…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59755', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59757', 'Clear Spring Campground', 'campground', 42.471379, -120.712714, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Clear Spring is located southwest of Paisley, Oregon and can be reached in approximately one hour. At an elevation of about 5400 feet, this campground is situated right along Dairy Creek. There is one picnic table and fire ring, and a variety of dispersed camping spaces. This camp is primarily used by hunters during hunting season. You can fish for rainbow trout in Dairy Creek. There is potable water, but no garbage service. Remember to pack it in, pack it out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59757', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59759', 'Dairy Point Campground', 'campground', 42.466928, -120.640954, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Dairy Point Campground is located one hour 20 minutes south of Paisley, OR. This site borders a riparian area along Dairy Creek and has a diverse mix of ponderosa pines, willows, and grasses. This campground offers hand-pumped potable water, one vault toilet, and five camping sites with picnic tables and fire grates. It''s a great location for destination camping, relaxing, and leisure. Please be respectful of surrounding private lands.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59759', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5976', 'Hunter Creek Transfer Camp', 'campground', 43.423767, -115.132042, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Located 20 miles northwest of Fairfield through Cow Creek Reservoir on Road No. 055, the campground offers 3 single camping units, and 1 multi-family unit. Corrals, mangers and barrier free stock loading ramps are available along with restrooms. No water is available. The trailhead for the North Fork Lime Creek Trail No. 044 is located at the north end of the campground and connects with the Virginia Gulch Trail No. 037.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5976', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59761', 'Deadhorse Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.561068, -120.774282, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Deadhorse Lake is located one hour 20 minutes south of Paisley, Oregon situated on Deadhorse Lake, a high-mountain lake with grassy and pebble beaches. The lake, elevation 7372 feet, spans 31 acres and is stocked with rainbow trout. There are nine tent and trailer sites, all with picnic tables and fire grills. It also features seven group campsites; some larger sites are located further from the lakeshore. There is also a hand pump for potable water. Deadhorse Lake, great for fishing, swimming, and boating (non-motorized or electric motors only), features a boat launch and separate day use…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59761', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59763', 'Happy Camp Campground', 'campground', 42.477206, -120.682822, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located approximately one hour from Paisley, Oregon, Happy Camp is a campground ideally located along peaceful Dairy Creek. The stream flows through the middle of the campground, offering fishing opportunities for rainbow trout. At an elevation of 5289, this campground features nine camping sites. All campsites include picnic tables and fire rings, but no garbage receptacles. * Remember to pack it in, pack it out. There is one vault toilet and water is available at Clear Springs Forest Camp , approximately 1.5 miles to the west on Forest Service Road 047. Besides fishing, hiking on the nearby…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59763', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59765', 'Jones Crossing Campground', 'campground', 42.607117, -120.600131, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 25 minutes south of Paisley, Oregon, Jones Crossing is a rustic and popular forest camp located right on the free-flowing Chewaucan River. Some juniper and ponderosa pines dot the camp, offering shade. There are eight spacious campsites each campsite features a picnic table and fire grate, and there is one vault toilet. There no potable water. Visitors need to pack plenty of water For recreation, campers can fish for rainbow or brook trout in the Chewaucan River. You may see or hear woodpeckers and songbirds make their presence known in this peaceful camp. There is also access to the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59765', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59767', 'Lee Thomas Campground', 'campground', 42.591336, -120.840028, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located one hour 30 minutes southwest of Paisley, Oregon, Lee Thomas Campground is located right on the banks of the North Fork of the Wild and Scenic Sprague River. Lodgepole pine trees, rock outcroppings, and riparian meadows characterize the landscape. All seven campsites are close enough to hear the river riffling by. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire grates, one vault toilet, and potable water. Just one mile east of the campground is the Lee Thomas Trailhead , which accesses Deadhorse Rim Trail #139 .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59767', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59769', 'Marsters Spring Campground', 'campground', 42.624378, -120.605602, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 20 minutes south of Paisley, Oregon, Marsters Spring is a rustic and peaceful campground along the banks of the Chewaucan River. The water level stays consistent on this river, providing good habitat for fish. Anglers can cast their line for catch-and-release bull trout. A creek flows amid sagebrush and through a mixed stand of alder, juniper and ponderosa pines. The Chewaucan Crossing trailhead is just one and a half miles up the road. You can either drive or walk along the river. Ten widely spaced campsites offer privacy. All sites have picnic tables and fire grates, and there are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59769', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5977', 'Bear Creek Transfer Camp', 'campground', 43.727218, -114.900558, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Bear Creek Transfer Camp is located 32 miles north of Fairfield. Travel over Fleck Summit on Road No. 012. Once at the summer home area, turn onto Road No. 079 and continue north past the Methodist Church Camp then turn left on to Road No. 889 and look for the entrance sign. The transfer camp offers 6 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings along with corrals and mangers with loading ramps and stock water available 150 yards to the north at Bear Creek. There is one vault toilet restroom available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5977', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59771', 'Sandhill Crossing Campground', 'campground', 42.594060, -120.880854, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes southwest of Paisley, OR, Sandhill Crossing campground is a remote and restful campground overlooking the North Fork of the Wild and Scenic Sprague River in a lodgepole pine and meadow setting. At 6,303 feet in elevation, Sandhill Crossing is a popular hunting camp in the fall. There is no fee to use this campground and amenities include potable water, one vault toilet, picnic tables and fire rings at all five campsites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59771', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59773', 'Eastbay Campground', 'campground', 42.944237, -121.063847, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes south of Silver Lake, Oregon, East Bay is a desirable campground located at the base of Hager Mountain on the scenic Thompson Reservoir. Enjoy gorgeous views of the mountain and shady campsites thanks to the ponderosa pines and aspens. Eighteen spacious campsites accommodate tent and RV camping. Amenities include picnic tables, fire rings, potable water, and three vault toilets. East Bay is a popular campground with hunters every fall. East Bay Campground has convenient access to the hiker trail that leads to the summit of Hager Mountain, about 4 miles one way. Besides…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59773', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59775', 'Lower Buck Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.069485, -121.246287, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Lower Buck Creek is located 35 minutes southwest of Silver Lake, Oregon. For back-country solitude, look no further than Lower Buck Creek. The small stream is surrounded by pastoral meadows and a mixed conifer forest. Lower Buck Creek''s elevation tips 5000 feet. Hunter groups and small family reunions are typical groups that enjoy this rustic forest camp. This campground has five camping sites, picnic tables, fire rings, and one vault toilet. Remember to park your vehicle a minimum of 200 feet from the creek. Lower Buck Creek is ideal for wildlife viewing (deer and elk), photography, and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59775', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59777', 'Silver Creek Marsh Campground', 'campground', 43.006469, -121.134981, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Silver Creek Marsh Campground is located 30 minutes south of Silver Lake, Oregon. The Silver Creek March Campground offers campsites at a popular fishing spot along Silver Creek in a beautiful forest setting. This spacious, timbered camp offers pastoral meadow and marsh views and great camping. There are 15 campsites with picnic tables, fire rings, two vault toilets, horse corrals, and potable water. You can enjoy bird watching, fishing, and hiking besides horseback riding. For horses, you''ll find large corrals with about six stalls that can accommodate 10-12 horses. There are also five…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59777', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59779', 'Thompson Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 42.961392, -121.092803, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes south of Silver Lake, Oregon, Thompson Reservoir Campground is a developed campground ideally situated on the three-square-mile reservoir with pretty vistas of nearby Hager Mountain. There are 19 campsites with picnic tables, fire rings. Other amenities include hand-pumped water, and three vault toilets. There is also one large group site. Tall ponderosa pines and a few aspen trees lord over the high mountain setting of Thompson Reservoir. Recreation opportunities include fishing, hiking, and exploring. The reservoir is stocked once a year with rainbow trout and there is a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59779', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59781', 'Upper Buck Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.053105, -121.266546, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Upper Buck Creek is your destination for rustic seclusion in a high mountain setting. Located 35 minutes southwest of Silver Lake, Oregon, ponderosa, lodgepole pine trees, aspen, and willows co-exist with open meadows and marsh land. This quiet forest camp is a great place to relax, fish, walk along the creek, and enjoy nature. Upper Buck Creek features five campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings, and two vault toilets. Remember to park your vehicle at least 200 feet from the creek. There are no garbage receptacles, so remember to pack it in, pack it out. There no potable water.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59781', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59793', 'Moss Meadows Horse Camp', 'campground', 42.480297, -120.484858, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Located 40 minutes south of Paisley, Oregon, this rustic horse camp affords pretty views of Steens Mountain and Mount Shasta. There is one vaulted toilet and four campsites, each with a picnic table and fire grate, and one hitching post. This is a good choice for a stop-over, as Moss Meadows has no corrals and no options for short trail rides. It''s about 20 miles from Moss Meadows to Currier Springs on the Fremont National Recreation Trail . Another option is to ride west from Moss Meadow along the road for about five miles to the Chewaucan River. You need to get permission to ride along the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59793', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5980', 'Chaparral Campground', 'campground', 43.614297, -115.202917, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Chaparral Campground is a non-reservation campground composed of 7 single sites and 3 double sites located on the South Fork of the Boise River. Campground amenities include 3 vault toilet restrooms, picnic tables and fire rings. Hiking, tubing, and fishing are popular activities. View Video', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5980', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5981', 'Abbott Campground', 'campground', 43.608697, -115.217917, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Abbott Campground is a primitive non-reservation campground composed of 7 units located on the South Fork of the Boise River. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings and restrooms. Tubing, and fishing are popular activities. There is a footbridge located on the west end of the camp area that crosses the river and accesses the Abbot Gulch area. View video of area', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5981', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5982', 'Five Points Campground', 'campground', 43.542101, -114.817900, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Five Points Campground is a primitive campground composed of 7 units located near Five Points Creek 17 miles north of Fairfield over Couch Summit. The newly renovated campground offers restrooms and is close to the popular Worswick hot springs. Potable water is not available at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5982', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5983', 'Canyon Transfer Camp', 'campground', 43.627901, -114.858902, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Canyon Campground is a non-reservation campground composed of 7 single units and 3 group sites on Big Smoky Creek. Campground amenities include picnic tables, fire rings, drinking water, restrooms, horse corrals and a stock loading station. The Big Smoky Trail #072 begins at the north end of the campground and leads to Skillern Hot Springs. Big Smoky trail is open to non-motorized travel and motorcycles. Numerous trails split off of the main Big Smoky Trail, some of them are only open to non-motorized travel. Please be sure to pick up a Motor Vehicle Use Map from the local Ranger Station.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5983', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59833', 'Annie Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 42.760706, -122.059227, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Annie Creek Sno-Park is located 43 miles northwest of Klamath Falls, Oregon, near the Crater Lake National Park boundary. Its proximity is rich with history, as Fort Klamath lies less than 10 miles from the Sno-Park. Fort Klamath was established as a military outpost on the Oregon Trail in 1863. Today, it''s listed on the U.S. National Register of Historic Places. If you want a break from recreating, it''s convenient to visit the Fort Klamath park and museum. Annie Creek offers more amenities than the average Sno-Park. As an official stop on the Oregon Volcanic Scenic Byway , you''ll find an…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59833', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5984', 'Baumgartner Campground', 'campground', 43.605699, -115.075905, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Baumgartner Campground is a group, fee, reservation campground composed of 39 camping units on the South Fork of the Boise River. It is one of two campgrounds on the District that has a campground host. There are 6 double family units, for up to 16 people each, and 1 multi-family group unit that can be reserved for up to 32 campers. Swimming, fishing, and picnicking are popular activities. An extensive trail system for OHV and motorcycles can be accessed from this campground, however OHVs are not allowed on the roads within the campground. An interpretive nature trail offers history on the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5984', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59841', 'Hadley Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 42.679500, -120.639790, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Hadley Sno-Park is located on Forest Service Road 3360 about 35 minutes west of Paisley, Oregon. Over 75 miles of trails branch off from this Sno-Park, providing an opportunity for snowmobilers to cruise through towering ponderosa and lodge pole pines using orange markers as guides. Thanks to its high elevation at 7,100 feet, winter adventurers can find snow from early November through May. The Sno-Park has a parking area with room for trailer turnaround, a vault toilet and disperse camping is allowed year round. The road to the Sno-Park is very windy and steep and maintained on an irregular…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59841', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5987', 'Bird Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.620398, -115.175915, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Bird Creek Campground is a primitive, non-reservation campground composed of 5 units on the South Fork of the Boise River. Tubing and fishing are popular activities. View Video', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5987', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '59885', 'Chewaucan Crossing Campground/Trailhead', 'campground', 42.615805, -120.606239, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'This highly used campground is ideally located right on the Chewaucan River, 20 minutes south of Paisley, Oregon. Chewaucan Crossing Trailhead, within the campground, accesses Fremont National Recreation Trail #160 a multi-use trail, and a challenging trek in both directions as hikers must climb out of the river canyon. You can hike, mountain bike, or horseback ride north to Yamsay Mountain or south to Cox Pass. A pedestrian bridge crosses the river and links to the trail. There are many fishing opportunities for rainbow and brook trout. The site is surrounded by a high desert, pine, and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=59885', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '5990', 'Big Hole', 'campground', 43.590700, -114.954906, null, 'Sawtooth National Forest', 'Big Hole is a day use site on the South Fork of the Boise River located 6 miles west (down river) from the Big Smoky Gaurd Station area on Road No.227. Popular for it''s swimming hole, the area provides access to fishing, parking and a restroom.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sawtooth/recarea/?recid=5990', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60217', 'Trapper Spring Forest Camp', 'campground', 43.280584, -121.342687, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'Trapper Spring Forest Camp offers rustic campsites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=60217', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60236', 'Skalkaho Snowpark', 'snow_area', 46.181763, -113.896474, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Skalkaho Snowpark offers a parking lot allowing snowmobilers and cross country skiers access to Skalkaho Pass which is closed to traffic through the winter months.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60236', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60242', 'Black Bear Campground', 'campground', 46.166389, -113.920556, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Located on the banks of Skalkaho Creek, Black Bear Campground hosts 6 sites with picnic tables, fire rings, and a vault toilet. There is no garbage service so Pack it in/Pack it out. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 50''.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60242', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60264', 'Lake Como Campground', 'campground', 46.068186, -114.235762, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'The campground, a.k.a. Lower Como, is a single loop through a stand of mixed pine and fir trees and one of three campgrounds in the Lake Como Recreation Area. It is located below Lake Como. The understory is grass with good privacy between campsites. Lake Como Lower Campground is paved and features a host site and ten 125'' pull through recreational vehicle (RV) sites (with electrical and water hookups) water, and garbage services. Three sites are handicap accessible, and there are 4 handicap accessible vault toilets located throughout the campground. This is bear country; practice safe food…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60264', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60270', 'Lost Horse Observation Point Observation Site', 'scenic_drive', 46.111376, -114.270760, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Lost Horse Observation site offers stunning views of Lost Horse Canyon. There are no facilities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60270', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60280', 'Schumaker Campground', 'campground', 46.150553, -114.496332, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Schumaker Campground sits on the edge of Twin Lakes near the Selway Bitterroot Wilderness. It features one host site, 16 campsites, two vault toilets and two handicap accessible sites. It is located near the Twin Lakes Trailhead. There are no motorized boats allowed on Twin Lakes. The road is narrow, rough, and fairly steep in some places. Please call the Darby Ranger Station for more information about road conditions. Maximum vehicle length 55''.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60280', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60290', 'Three Frogs Campground', 'campground', 46.066415, -114.248935, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Three Frogs Campground is a newly reconstructed campground and features 16 small trailer campsites and 4 walk-in tent sites. The campground offers accessible vault toilets, picnic tables, fire rings, water and garbage service, and gravel surfaced roads. Some campsites are also equipped with tent pads. Can accommodate trailers to 30'' lengths.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60290', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60306', 'Blodgett Campground', 'campground', 46.269922, -114.244263, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Blodgett Campground consists of 5 campsites, 1 walk-in site, plus 1 host site, complete with picnic tables, fire rings, and a vault toilet. There are two accessible campsites. The campground rests under the towering cliff faces of Blodgett Canyon which are very popular to rock climbers. Blodgett Canyon Picnic Area is across Blodgett Creek. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 45 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60306', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60312', 'Charles Waters Campground', 'campground', 46.575266, -114.140839, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'The Charles Waters campground is paved asphalt with 26 campsites plus one double site, including 4 pull-through, one bicycle site, and one horse site; there is also one accessible site with electric hook-up. The campground also has water; accessible vault toilets; open meadow for activities and can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 70 feet. Please note that the bicycle site and horse site are reserved for those users until 6 p.m. daily after which time if no one is occupying them then they are considered available on a first come first served basis. A campground host is available Memorial Day…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60312', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60320', 'Gold Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.397422, -113.902316, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', '4 campsites with extensive hiking, biking, motorcycle and horseback riding opportunities. Trails from the campground and from near the campground access the Skalkaho Wildlife Preserve, Gold Creek, and the Easthouse National Recreation Trail. Fishing in area creeks or the North Fork Bitterroot; hunting for deer and elk in season. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 25 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60320', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60342', 'Crazy Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.811603, -114.068814, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Crazy Creek Campground hosts 7 sites with picnic tables, fire rings, vault toilet and a well with hand pump for water. There is no garbage service so Pack it in/Pack it out. Campground can accommodate trailers under 26 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60342', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60352', 'Indian Trees Campground', 'campground', 45.755491, -113.954498, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'This paved, accessible campground has 16 sites with picnic tables, fire rings, vault toilets and camp host. Will accept trailers/RV''s up to 50''. It is conveniently located near Highway 93 and gets its name from the scarred ponderosa trees whose bark was long ago stripped in order to extract the cambium layer which was a food source.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60352', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60354', 'Jennings Camp Campground', 'campground', 45.896336, -113.819636, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'This campground is located on the banks of the East Fork of the Bitterroot river. It has 4 campsites with picnic tables, fire rings and an accessible vault toilet. Site will accept RV''s or trailers to 20''.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60354', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60362', 'Lost Trail Pass Snowpark Trailhead', 'snow_area', 45.694118, -113.947226, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'This trailhead is located on top of Lost Trail Pass. It offers parking for access to the Trail Creek Area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60362', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60364', 'Martin Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.932037, -113.722420, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'This campground is located at the junction of Moose and Martin Creek and consists of 7 campsites with picnic tables, fire rings, and a vault toilet. Will accept RV''s or trailers to 50''. It is also close to trailhead access to the Anaconda-Pintler Wilderness at the east end of Forest Roads #5771 and #724.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60364', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60378', 'Spring Gulch Campground', 'campground', 45.858585, -114.023208, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Located on the banks of the East Fork of the Bitterroot River, this campground is nestled in a grassy ponderosa pine area. It offers easy access from Highway 93 and hosts 10 sites, plus 1 bicycle site, with picnic tables, fire rings, and vault toilets. It also has a picnic area and handicapped accessible facilities to include a fishing pier on the river. Campground can accommodate trailers and RV''s to 50''. There are no hook-ups but water is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60378', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60384', 'Warm Springs Campground', 'campground', 45.842015, -114.040115, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Warm Springs Campground is nestled in a wooded area along Crazy Creek. It hosts 14 sites with picnic tables, fire rings, and vault toilets. There is no garbage service so Pack it in/Pack it out. Campground can accommodate trailers under 26 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60384', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60388', 'Alta Campground', 'campground', 45.624487, -114.302009, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Alta Campground features 15 campsites with 1 host site, potable water, garbage, vault toilets, and handicap accessible picnic tables. Site will accept RV''s or trailers to 30''. Alta campground is located along the West Fork of the Bitterroot River, a popular fishing river in the area. Large yellow-barked Ponderosa Pine tower above many of the campsites which along with fir, aspen and lodgepole pine provide shade for many of the campsites. Painted Rocks Lake is located less than 5 miles away by paved road. Wildlife in the area include, bald eagle, mule and whitetail deer, moose, and elk along…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60388', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60490', 'Deep Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.713970, -114.709029, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Deep Creek Campground features 3 campsites complete with picnic tables, fire rings, and a vault toilet. Site will accept RV''s or trailers to 30 feet. Stock can be kept in this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60490', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60570', 'Indian Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.789488, -114.763536, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Indian Creek Campground sits along the banks of the Selway River and consists of 2 sites, hitching rails and a vault toilet. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 25 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60570', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60608', 'Little West Fork Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 45.784579, -114.329026, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Little West Fork Trailhead offers adequate parking for cars and trailers. In the winter it is a popular snowmobile starting point and in the summer offers dispersed camping. Facilities include a wooden out house', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60608', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60616', 'Magruder Crossing Campground', 'campground', 45.735340, -114.758813, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Magruder Crossing Campground features 6 campsites on the Selway River, and a vault toilet. Site will accept RV''s or trailers to 30''. Stock can be kept in this campground. This was the crossing on a route established for commerce between Lewiston and Virginia City, MT during the gold rush. To the north of the campground, an earlier route, Southern Nez Perce Trail, crosses the road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60616', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60666', 'Paradise Campground', 'campground', 45.861263, -114.737718, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Paradise Campground is located near the Paradise Boating Site which is one of the most popular launching sites on the Selway River. The campground consists of 11 sites complete with picnic tables, and fire rings. Other facilities include 3 vault toilets, hitching rails, and feed bunks. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 25 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60666', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60700', 'Rombo Campground', 'campground', 45.765000, -114.280560, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Rombo Campground is located in a scenic area along the West Fork Bitterroot River in the mountains of southwestern Montana. The area is home to a variety of big game and wildlife, and provides access to a number of outdoor activities, including fishing, seasonal rafting and various trail opportunities. Natural Features: The campground is located along the West Fork of the Bitterroot River. Large yellow-barked ponderosa pine trees tower above many of the campsites, which along with fir, aspen and lodgepole pine, provide pleasant shade. The campground is situated at an elevation of 4,600 feet.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60700', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60716', 'Sam Billings Memorial Campground', 'campground', 45.825238, -114.248982, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Sam Billings Memorial Campground is located off of the West Fork Rd and consists of 12 campsites complete with picnic tables, and fire rings. There is also a large area ideal for group activities. Other facilites include vault toilets. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 30 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60716', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60752', 'Slate Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.698128, -114.283434, null, 'Bitterroot National Forest', 'Slate Creek Campground is located right near Painted Rocks lake and has 7 sites complete with picnic tables and fire rings, and a vault toilet. Campground can accommodate RV''s or trailers to 25 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/bitterroot/recarea/?recid=60752', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60825', 'Greenough Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.058078, -109.410865, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov Greenough Lake Campground is 12 miles south of Red Lodge, Montana, along the banks of the Main Fork of Rock Creek. Located just off the scenic Beartooth Highway , the area is popular for fishing, hiking, and scenic driving. Greenough Lake is 0.2 miles from the campground and offers canoeing, kayaking, and rainbow trout fishing.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60825', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60827', 'Limber Pine Campground', 'campground', 45.058257, -109.412369, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov Limber Pine Campground is south of Red Lodge, along the banks of the Main Fork of Rock Creek. It is near the base of the switchbacks of the Beartooth Scenic Highway . Mount Maurice Trail (#6) , Corral Creek Trail (#9) , Bear Track Trail (#8) , Lake Fork Trail (#2) , Parkside National Recreation Trail (#103) , Hell Roaring Plateau…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60827', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60829', 'Parkside Campground and Group Campsites', 'campground', 45.060609, -109.403751, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov Parkside Campground is south of Red Lodge, along the banks of the Main Fork of Rock Creek. It is near the base of the switchbacks of the Beartooth Scenic Highway . Mount Maurice Trail (#6), Corral Creek Trail (#9), Bear Track Trail (#8), Lake Fork Trail (#2), Parkside National Recreation Trail (#103), Hellroaring Plateau Trail…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60829', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60831', 'Rattin Campground', 'campground', 45.087816, -109.323349, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Rattin Campground is approximately six miles south of Red Lodge, along the banks of the Main Fork of Rock Creek. You access it from the East Side Rd off the Beartooth Highway . Mount Maurice Trail (#6), Corral Creek Trail (#9), Bear Track Trail (#8), Lake Fork Trail (#2), Parkside National Recreation Trail (#103), Hellroaring Plateau Trail (#11), Glacier Lake Trail (#3), Sheridan Campground , Greenough Lake Campground , Parkside Campground , Limber Pine Campground and M-K Campground are also located in the Man Fork Rock Creek drainage. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth Ranger…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60831', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60833', 'Sheridan Campground', 'campground', 45.100971, -109.307408, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Sheridan Campground is located approx. five miles south of Red Lodge on the banks of the Main Fork of Rock Creek. You access it from East Side Road, off the Beartooth Highway (US Hwy 212). Mount Maurice Trail (#6) Corral Creek Trail (#9), Bear Track Trail (#8), Lake Fork Trail (#2), Parkside National Recreation Trail (#103), Hellroaring Plateau Trail (#11), Glacier Lake Trail (#3), Greenough Lake Campground , Rattin Campground , Parkside Campground , Limber Pine Campground and M-K Campground are also located in the Man Fork Rock Creek drainage. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60833', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60835', 'Cascade Campground', 'campground', 45.173015, -109.450824, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov The Cascade Campground is located 10.4 miles up the West Fork Rock Creek Road, near Red Lodge, MT. The campground is located in an area that is scarred by the 2008 Cascade Fire. However, there are trees in the campground and it is an excellent location for wildflowers and wildlife sightings. Basin Lakes National Recreation Trail…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60835', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60837', 'Basin Campground', 'campground', 45.161768, -109.392903, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Basin Campground is nestled in the trees along the banks of the West Fork of Rock Creek. Basin Lakes National Recreation Trail (#61) is a short distance from the campground. Silver Run National Recreation Trail (#102) Timberline Trail (# 12), West Fork Trail (# 1), Camp Senia Trail (# 16),Wild Bill Lake Picnic Ground and National Recreation Trail and Cascade Campground are also located in the West Fork Rock Creek drainage. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth Ranger District campgrounds.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60837', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60839', 'Wickham Gulch Campground', 'campground', 45.580278, -104.071389, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A small campground with a day use picnic area, located on the Long Pines Unit, Sioux Ranger District. 6 miles northwest of Camp Crook, SD. Located near Capitol Rock National Natural Landmark.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60839', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60841', 'Lantis Spring Campground', 'campground', 45.632222, -104.176667, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground with camp sites, and day use picnic sites, located in the Long Pines Unit, Sioux Ranger District, about 5 miles north off the Tie Creek Road. Information: Sioux District Office Box 37, Main & First Camp Crook, SD 57724 (605) 797-4432', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60841', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60843', 'Reva Gap Campground', 'campground', 45.526389, -103.171944, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground located in the Slim Buttes Unit near the Castles National Natural Landmark, one of two on the Sioux Ranger District. The campground is directly off of HWY 20, 20 miles south and east of Buffalo. Spectacularly eroded steep-walled buttes.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60845', 'Ekalaka Park Campground', 'campground', 45.798611, -104.516111, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov Campground with 7 sites and two day use picnic sites near Ekalaka on the Ekalaka Hills Unit, Sioux Ranger District. The Ekalaka Hills consist of scenic cliff drop-offs and cliff-edge views over the surrounding prairie, from Ponderosa pine savanna uplands.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60845', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60847', 'Picnic Spring Campground', 'campground', 45.873611, -103.484167, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground located in the North Cave Hills Unit, Sioux Ranger District, 8 miles west and north of Ludlow, SD adjacent to beautiful woods and rocky, cliff-edged canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60847', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60851', 'Holiday Spring Campground', 'campground', 45.638611, -105.974167, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground on the Ashland Ranger District. Camp sites: 3 Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No Potable Water: No', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60851', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60853', 'Red Shale Campground', 'campground', 45.572500, -106.147778, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground on the Ashland Ranger District. Camp sites: 14 Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60853', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60855', 'Cow Creek Campground And Picnic Area', 'campground', 45.309167, -106.246944, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground on the Ashland Ranger District. Camp sites: 4 Picnic Site: 1 Potable Water: No Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60855', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60857', 'M-K Campground', 'campground', 45.038032, -109.429744, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'M-K is a free campground located 3 miles up the Main Fork Rock Creek Road #2421, not far from the Beartooth Highway. Mount Maurice Trail (#6) Corral Creek Trail (#9), Beartrack Trail (#8), Lake Fork Trail (#2), Parkside National Recreation Trail (#103), Hellroaring Plateau Trail (#11), Glacier Lake Trail (#3), Sheridan Campground , Rattin Campground , Parkside Campground , Limber Pine Campground and Greenough Lake Campground are also located in the Man Fork Rock Creek drainage. Reservations: No Reservations: This campground does not use a reservation system, it is managed on a first-come,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60857', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60859', 'Woodbine Campground', 'campground', 45.353313, -109.897844, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov Woodbine Campground is located along the Stillwater River. It is a short walk from the Stillwater Trail (#24) and Woodbine Falls Trail (#93). Fully paved campground with paved spurs at the end of the Stillwater River Road #2400. Old Nye Picnic Ground and Fishing Access are also located in the Stillwater River drainage. There is a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60859', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60861', 'Palisades Campground', 'campground', 45.171504, -109.308559, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Palisades Campground is a free campground, located at the end of Palisades Road #2010 near Red Lodge, just below Red Lodge Mountain Ski Resort and the palisades geological formation. The Willow Creek Trail (# 105) and the Palisades Trail (# 109) both leave from the western end of the campground. * Please be advised that dogs are allowed on Willow Creek year-round, but the Palisades Trail (#109), which intersects with the Willow Creek Trail a short distance up the trail, has restrictions on dogs. Due to wintering moose habitat, dogs are not allowed on the Palisades Trail between Dec. 1- July…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60861', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60863', 'Emerald Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.253398, -109.700292, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Emerald Lake is in the West Rosebud drainage and is nestled in the trees between Emerald Lake and West Rosebud Lake. West Rosebud Trail (#19), Pine Grove Campground , Emerald Lake Fishing Access and West Rosebud Lake Fishing Access are also located in the West Rosebud drainage. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth Ranger District campgrounds. For a road map of the area, with locations of campgrounds, please see our Motor Vehicle Use Map Reservations : No Reservation. This campground does not use a reservation system. First-come, first-served. Be aware that the campground is very…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60863', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60865', 'Pine Grove Campground', 'campground', 45.275863, -109.645533, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Pine Grove Campground is located in the West Rosebud drainage. It is in the trees, along the banks of West Rosebud Creek. Emerald Lake Campground , West Rosebud Trail (#19) , Emerald Lake Fishing Access and West Rosebud Lake Fishing Access are also located in the West Rosebud drainage. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth Ranger District campgrounds. For a road map of the area, with locations of campgrounds, please see our Motor Vehicle Use Map ( MVUM ). Reservations : No Reservations. This campground does not use a reservation system; it is managed on a first-come, first-served…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60865', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60867', 'East Rosebud Campground', 'campground', 45.199442, -109.634267, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'East Rosebud Campground is nestled in the trees, not far from East Rosebud Lake. East Rosebud is considered one of the more scenic drainages in the Beartooths and the campground is a short distance from the East Rosebud Trail (#15), Spread Creek Trail (#13), and Phantom Creek Trail (#17). Jimmy Joe Campground and Sand Dunes Picnic Ground also located in the East Rosebud drainage. *Please be advised that much of the area directly around East Rosebud Lake is private property. Fishing or boat access to the lake is limited. Please call the district office for more information. Camp sites: 14…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60867', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60869', 'Jimmy Joe Campground', 'campground', 45.231418, -109.602893, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Jimmy Joe Campground is a free campground on the banks of East Rosebud Creek in the East Rosebud drainage. East Rosebud is considered one of the more scenic drainages in the Beartooths . East Rosebud Trail (#15), Spread Creek Trail (#13), and Phantom Creek Trail (#17). East Rosebud Lake Campground and Sand Dunes Picnic Ground also located in the East Rosebud drainage. Camp sites: 10 Host : No Max Trailer Length : 30ft Accessible Facilities: Vault toilets Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No For a road map of the area, including campground locations, please see our Motor Vehicle Use Map ( MVUM ).…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60869', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60871', 'Sage Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.213877, -108.554629, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Sage Creek Campground is the only campground in the Pryor Mountains. It is located along the banks of Sage Creek. Big Ice Cave Picnic Ground , and the Bureau of Land Management Pryor Mountain Wild Horse Range are also located in the Pryor Mountains. Numerous motorized trails are located in the Pryor Mountains. Please check our Motor Vehicle Use Map ( MVUM ) for any area and road closures. There is a 16 day maximum stay in all Beartooth Ranger District campgrounds. *** There is not consistent potable water here. Call the district office to learn if there is water, or plan ahead and bring your…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60871', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60873', 'Initial Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.403817, -109.954952, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'This free campground is located on the West Fork Stillwater Road and is near the West Fork Stillwater Trail (#90). The campground is maintained from Memorial Day to Labor Day, but is opened the rest of the year without services. There is a 16 day stay limit for all Beartooth Ranger District campgrounds. For a road map of the area, which shows campground locations, please see our Motor Vehicle Use Map ( MVUM ) Camp sites: 6 Host: No Max Trailer Length : 20 ft Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No Reservations No Reservations. This campground does not use a reservation system, it is managed on a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60873', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '60947', 'Blacks Pond Campground', 'campground', 45.349167, -106.286250, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', '.usa-accordion__button { width: auto /* 100%*/; float: right;} .my-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }.child { padding: 5px; margin: 3px; } .right-align { margin-left: auto; } View this site on Recreation.gov Vea este sitio en Recreation.gov A campground on the Ashland Ranger District. Camp sites: 2 Potable Water: No Trash Pickup: No Firewood: No', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=60947', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6101', 'Hopewell Boat Access Campground', 'campground', 41.912500, -78.932778, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This small rustic campground is located on the east bank of the Allegheny Reservoir just north of Sugar Bay. It is accessible by boat (Allegheny Reservoir) or hiking trail ( North Country National Scenic Trail with connections to the Tracy Ridge Trail System ). The closest boat launch is Roper Hollow directly across the reservoir on the west bank and Kinzua Wolf Run Marina approximately 5 miles south near State Route 59 at the Morrison Bridge. Visitors should bring their own water as this campground does not provide a potable water source.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6101', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6102', 'Kiasutha Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.782454, -78.900182, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'The campground sits on a large creek off the Allegheny Reservoir, offering countless water activities. This area provides a large, grassy lawn with beach access, great for picnicking and swimming. A two-lane, concrete boat launch with a 130-foot courtesy dock is available for reservoir access to fishing, boating, water-skiing and more. Popular hiking trails nearby include the North Country National Scenic Trail and Morrison Hiking Trail. View/Print Site Brochure - pdf', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6102', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6103', 'Loleta Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.401944, -79.081111, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This area has been recently nominated and accepted onto the National Register of Historic Places. The area was once a bustling logging town, established in 1889, with over 600 inhabitants. The town had a large sawmill, shingle mill, broom handle factory and a rail connection for shipping products to Sheffield, PA. Once the timber supply was exhausted in 1913, the mills shut down and the town was deserted. The Federal Government purchased the site in 1925, adding it to the newly formed Allegheny National Forest. In the 1930s, the Forest Service (using CCC labor) reconstructed the mill pond,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6103', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6105', 'Minister Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.621389, -79.154444, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'The Allegheny''s smallest campground with six family campsites sits along the babbling waters of Minister Creek. The Minister Creek Trailhead is situated directly across SR 666 from the campground where the popular 6 mile loop Minister Creek Hiking Trail starts and ends at the trailhead. Minster Creek Hiking Trail connects to the North Country National Scenic Trail at its northern most point. View/Print Site Brochure - pdf', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6105', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6107', 'Handsome Lake Boat Access Campground', 'campground', 41.922500, -78.930833, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This small rustic campground is located on the east bank of the Allegheny Reservoir just north of Sugar Bay. It is accessible by boat ( Allegheny Reservoir ) or hiking trail ( North Country National Scenic Trail with connections to the Tracy Ridge Trail System ). The closest boat launch is Roper Hollow directly across the reservoir on the west bank and Kinzua Wolf Run Marina approximately 5 miles south near State Route 59 at the Morrison Bridge. Visitors should bring their own water as this campground does not provide a potable water source.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6107', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6108', 'Hearts Content Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.691745, -79.254117, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Walk among the 300 to 400-year-old white pines which tower Hearts Content, a 122-acre area containing old-growth forest. In 1977, Hearts Content was designated as a registered National Natural Landmark by the National Park Service. This designation indicates that the site possesses exceptional value as an illustration of the nation''s natural heritage and contributes to a better understanding of the environment. In an area which was mostly clear-cut in the 1800s, 20 acres of what is now Hearts Content was owned by Wheeler and Dusenbury Lumber Company from 1897 to 1922. Wheeler and Dusenbury…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6108', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6109', 'Dewdrop Campground', 'campground', 41.828164, -78.966638, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Dewdrop Campground is located along Longhouse National Scenic Byway. This 11-acre campground is nestled on the shoreline of Kinzua Bay, which extends southwest from the main body of the Allegheny Reservoir. Several campsites offer views of the water. View/Print Site Brochure - pdf', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6109', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6111', 'Pine Grove Boat Access Campground', 'campground', 41.874167, -78.946667, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This small rustic campground is located on the east bank of the Allegheny Reservoir just north of Kinzua Wolf Run Marina. It is accessible by boat via the Allegheny Reservoir. The closest boat launch is Kinzua Wolf Run Marina approximately 1 mile south near State Route 59 at the Morrison Bridge. The North Country National Scenic Trail passes by this campground. Visitors should bring their own water as this campground does not provide a potable water source.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6111', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6112', 'Red Bridge Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.779091, -78.886632, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Red Bridge is a popular recreation area located along Pennsylvania State Route 321, about 10 miles north of Kane. The campground offers RV and tent sites, as well as cabin rentals during open season. Select camp sites offer views of the Allegheny Reservoir. Nearby recreational opportunities include Red Bridge Bank Fishing, located immediately adjacent to the campground, Allegheny Reservoir, and Jakes Rocks Overlook and Mountain Bike Trail. Hikers can enjoy nearby trails such as the North Country National Scenic Trail, which crosses State Route 321 only 0.2 miles south of the campground, and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6112', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6115', 'Buckaloons Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.838889, -79.257222, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Buckaloons Recreation Area is located along the west bank of the ⁠ Allegheny Wild and Scenic River , offering a one-lane, concrete boat launch for water access. Buckaloons is a great launch point to explore the Allegheny Islands Wilderness, seven islands stretched between Buckaloons and Tionesta. These islands are popular for dispersed camping, exploration, and viewing scenery and wildlife. Buckaloons is surrounded by three flowing bodies of water including Irvine Run, Brokenstraw Creek, and the Allegheny River, making abundant opportunities for water activities. In addition to fishing,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6115', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6116', 'Hooks Brook Boat Access Campground', 'campground', 41.962222, -78.943056, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This rustic campground is located on the west bank of the Allegheny Reservoir just south of Webbs Ferry Boat Launch . It is accessible by boat via the Allegheny Reservoir. The closest boat launch is Webbs Ferry approximately 1 mile north (west bank) and Willow Bay also 1 mile north (east bank). Visitors should bring their own water as this campground does not provide a potable water source.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6116', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6119', 'Willow Bay Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.988209, -78.909242, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Willow Bay Recreation Area was built in the early 1960s by the U. S. Army Corps of Engineers. When completed, it was transferred to the USDA, Forest Service. Willow Bay Recreation Area is located 15 miles west of Bradford, PA, on State Route (SR) 346, just south of the New York State line. The area overlooks the south shore of Willow Bay, a small arm on the eastern side of the Allegheny Reservoir. There are four camping loops - Oak, Aspen, Hemlock and Deer Grove. Campsites in Hemlock and Deer Grove Loops overlook Willow Bay while sites in Oak and Aspen loops back onto Willow Creek. The North…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6119', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6120', 'Morrison Boat Access Campground', 'campground', 41.821944, -78.927778, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This rustic campground is located on the east bank of the Allegheny Reservoir just east of Elijah Run Boat Launch on Morrison Bay a branch off of Kinzua Bay of the Allegheny Reservoir. It is accessible by boat via the Allegheny Reservoir and/or the Morrison Hiking Trail . The closest boat launch is Elijah Run directly west of the campground (access from the Longhouse National Scenic Byway - Forest Road 262).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6120', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6133', 'Kelly Pines Campground', 'campground', 41.485420, -79.009080, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Kelly Pines Campground is an equestrian campground located along the Spring Creek Horse Trail. Natural Features: The location is spacious with forest vegetation alongside a stream. Recreation : The recreation area is connected to Spring Creek Horse Trail with miles of designated marked trails. View the Spring Creek Horse Trail map. Facilities : The campground includes four campsites each with four horse stalls, as well as a double occupancy campsite with two, four horse stalls. A double occupancy campsite with two, four horse stalls is also available for advanced reservations. For visitors…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6133', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6137', 'Tracy Ridge Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.943155, -78.867056, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'This campground sits on a ridge top three miles east of the Allegheny Reservoir just minutes south of the PA/NY state border. This 45-site campground provides spacious, tree-shaded campsites in an area that is heavily forested with oak. The campground contains one of the two trailheads for the Tracy Ridge Hiking Trail , with one loop circling the campground. The North Country National Scenic Trail , which connects to the Tracy Ridge Hiking Trail, also goes past the campground. View/Print Site Brochure - pdf', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=6137', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61482', 'Double Falls Campground', 'campground', 47.407127, -112.721871, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Campground Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61482', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61526', 'Crystal Lake Campground', 'campground', 46.793889, -109.511111, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Crystal Lake Campground is in the shadow of Mt. Harlow at an elevation of 5,700 feet. The 28 campsites are large and widely spaced, and recent removal of hazard trees has left each camp site with expansive views of the surrounding mountains. The largest slot can accommodate a maximum trailer length of 45 feet and is a suitable campground for large RVs. Crystal Lake Campground opens around June 2nd and closes in late October. Nearby trailheads lead to the Crystal Lake Loop Trail and a trail which leads to ice caves. In the summer, Crystal Lake is well-suited for canoeing. The lake is stocked…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61526', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61528', 'Dry Wolf Campground', 'campground', 46.979167, -110.518611, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Located in the heart of Charlie Russell Country, Dry Wolf Campground''s 25 campsites are along Dry Wolf Creek. Dry Wolf Campground is usually open from June through the middle of fall. The largest slot can accommodate a maximum trailer length of 45 feet. Bandbox Mountain surrounds the campground where marine fossils can be found. Campers can fish from the two platforms along Dry Wolf Creek near the campground. All campgrounds on the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest are first-come, first-served. Reservations are not available. Camping is limited to 16 consecutive days in one location. A…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61528', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61530', 'Judith Station Day Use Area', 'campground', 46.848333, -110.289722, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Judith Station Day Use Area is located in the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest, adjacent to the historic Judith Guard Station. Amenities include nearby fishing access, drinking water, and a restroom. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61530', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61532', 'Hay Canyon Campground', 'campground', 46.798889, -110.300278, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Hay Canyon Campground is located in the Lewis and Clark National Forest. There are 7 campsites near fishing access to the South Fork of the Judith River and scenic ATV trails. Restrooms are provided. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 30 feet. Please limit your stay to 16 days. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61532', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61540', 'Thain Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.475556, -110.585278, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Thain Creek Campground is the only campground in the Highwood Mountains. One of the 19 campsites can accommodate a maximum trailer length of 40 feet. The campground is usually open from May through the middle of fall. A nearby trailhead leads up to Windy Mountain and back on a 6 mile loop trail, offering scenic views of the surrounding plains and faraway mountains. Other hikes are along Briggs Creek or from the North Fork Highwood Creek Trailhead. Please heed seasonal trail closures, as all trails in the Highwoods close either September 1st or Oct 15th . All campgrounds on the Helena-Lewis…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61540', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61542', 'Kings Hill Campground', 'campground', 46.842222, -110.696667, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'At approximately an 8000-foot elevation, Kings Hill Campground is the highest developed campground in the Little Belt Mountains. The 18 campsites are situated near the top of Kings Hill Pass on US Highway 89. Kings Hill Campground generally opens in mid to late June and is the first to close in the fall around the end of September. The largest slot for a trailer is 35 feet in length. During fire season, nearby Porphyry Peak Lookout offers amazing views from the manned fire tower dating back to 1960. Visitors are welcome to go up into the Lookout if staff are available. A network of roads and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61542', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61544', 'Moose Creek Campground - Little Belt Mountains', 'campground', 46.835833, -110.875000, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Moose Creek Campground is a 9 mile drive down Forest Service Roads 119 and 204, away from the popular US Highway 89 corridor. The 6 campsites are nestled against Moose Creek, which offers the opportunity to fish. Moose Creek Campground can only accommodate a maximum trailer length of 20 feet and is not suitable for campers with large RVs. The campground is usually open from May through the middle of fall. A motorcycle trail runs west along Allan Creek to Allan Park about one mile north of the campground. All campgrounds on the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest are first-come,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61544', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61546', 'Many Pines Campground', 'campground', 46.898056, -110.690556, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Many Pines Campground is in a stand of Lodgepole Pine directly off US Highway 89 in the Little Belt Mountains. The 23 campsites are located along Belt Creek, which offers opportunity for fishing for trout. Please follow Cutthroat Trout mandatory catch and release rules. The campground is usually open late May through October. The largest slot for a trailer is 51 feet in length. Many Pines Campground is the most convenient for campers with large RVs along the US Highway 89 corridor. Approximately one mile to the north is the Memorial Falls trailhead, a popular day hike. All campgrounds on the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61546', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61548', 'Richardson Campground', 'campground', 46.540833, -110.730556, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Richardson Campground is located in the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest in the Castle Mountains. At an elevation of 5,500 feet, the campground encompasses 8 acres. It is located in a lodgepole pine forest on a hillside. There are 3 campsites provided with restrooms. Richardson Creek is located nearby, and scenic hiking trails are accessible from the campground. Pets are welcome. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 16 feet. All campgrounds on the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest are first-come, first-served. Reservations are not available. Camping is limited to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61548', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61550', 'Jumping Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.763889, -110.784722, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Jumping Creek Campground sits at an elevation of 5800 feet along US Highway 89 in the Little Belt Mountains 22 miles north of White Sulphur Springs. The 10 campsites are along Sheep Creek, which offers opportunity for fishing for brook and rainbow trout. The campground has multiple slots which can accommodate long trailers, up to a maximum length of 45 feet. Jumping Creek Campground is usually open late May through October. Nearby historic logging roads provide motorized access to the Smoky Mountain area. To the east on US Highway 89 is the trailhead to a scenic ATV trail which climbs Mizpah…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61550', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61552', 'Grasshopper Campground', 'campground', 46.543611, -110.748056, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Grasshopper Campground is the only developed campground in the Castle Mountains and a mere 11 miles from White Sulphur Springs. The 12 campsites sit above Grasshopper Creek on a scenic hillside. Grasshopper Campground usually closes in early December. Many hunters stay at Grasshopper Campground because it is one of the last campgrounds to close in the area. Hunters cannot hang game in the campground. The campground can only accommodate a maximum trailer length of 22 feet and is not suitable campers with large RVs. Above the campground is access to a motorcycle trail open from December 1st…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61552', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61554', 'Logging Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.101111, -111.008889, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Logging Creek Campground is in the northeastern region of the Little Belt Mountains. All 25 campsites are accessible. This quiet developed campground is approximately 15 miles from the popular US Highway 89 corridor. Logging Creek flows below scenic limestone cliffs and is prime trout fishing. Please follow Cutthroat Trout mandatory catch and release rules. The largest slot can accommodate a maximum trailer length of 54 feet, and the campground is suitable for campers with large RVs. Logging Creek is usually open from May through the middle of fall. The trailhead for Deep Creek National…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61554', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61556', 'Aspen Campground', 'campground', 46.992222, -110.768889, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Aspen Campground is located directly off Highway 89 in the Little Belt Mountains. The 6 campsites are in a canyon carved out by Belt Creek and are usually open Memorial Day weekend through the middle of fall. The largest slot can accommodate a maximum trailer length of 22 feet. Nearby Belt Creek provides excellent fishing opportunities for trout. Please follow Cutthroat Trout mandatory catch and release rules. The Belt Creek Ranger Station is just to the north of the campground, and trails to the east of the ranger station connect to an extensive trail system. All campgrounds on the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61556', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61558', 'Spring Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.586389, -110.466667, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Located only 4 miles from Highway 12, Spring Creek Campground is easily accessible. The 10 campsites are in a lush riparian zone along Spring Creek. Campers can wade in the creek, or fish Spring Creek Campground can only accommodate a maximum trailer length of 35 feet, and is not recommended for campers with large RVs. The campground is usually open from May through the middle of fall. An ATV trailhead in the campground connects to a non-motorized trail with sweeping views of the surrounding mountain ranges. All campgrounds on the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest are first-come,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61558', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61560', 'Home Gulch Campground', 'campground', 47.615833, -112.724444, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', '15 campsites along the North Fork of the Sun River. Good fishing for rainbow and westslope cutthroat trout. Hiking nearby on the Mortimer Gulch National Recreation Trail. Motorized and non-motorized boat access at the boat launch. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61560', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61562', 'West Fork Teton Campground', 'campground', 47.961111, -112.806667, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'West Fork Campground is located in the Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest. There are 6 tent sites and the basic facilities are provided. Trails for hiking and fishing access are nearby. Please limit your stay to 14 days. A small fee is required for the use of this campground. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61562', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61564', 'Elko Campground', 'campground', 47.924444, -112.763333, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', '3 sites near the Teton River. Fishing for brook trout in the river. Nearby winter sports area at Teton Pass offers downhill skiing and snowmobiling. When there''s no snow to play in, hike up Jones Creek, about 3 miles north from campground. The Jones Creek trailhead is about 0.5 mile east of the campground. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61564', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61566', 'Mill Falls Campground', 'campground', 47.858889, -112.772778, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', '4 campsites near the South Fork of the Teton River. Some fishing for brook, rainbow, and cutthroat, though all populations are low. Go 1 mile west to the end of the road to the South Fork trailhead, and hike in the short distance to pristine Our Lake, near the border of the Bob Marshall Wilderness. Our Lake is a fantastic place to see mountain goats year round, as well as the ever-entertaining pika and yellow-bellied marmot. Never approach or feed wildlife. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61566', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61568', 'Summit Campground', 'campground', 48.318889, -113.350556, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', '17 campsites high in the Front Range of the Rocky Mountains. A 3-mile spur trail connects the campground to the Continental Divide Scenic Trail, and on into the Bob Marshall Wilderness. Adjacent Memorial Square commemorates Theodore Roosevelt and the Blackfeet tribe with a miniature Washington Monument. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61568', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61570', 'Cave Mountain Campground', 'campground', 47.891389, -112.726944, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', '18 sites located 18 miles west of Choteau, Montana. Fishing and hiking access. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61570', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61572', 'Mortimer Gulch Campground', 'campground', 47.609722, -112.769722, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Mortimer Gulch campground is located close to Gibson Resevoir with 26 campsites available for use. Fishing for rainbow or cutthroat trout in the reservoir and in the North Fork of the Sun River is an excellent way to spend the weekend away during the summer months. It is highly recommended that a 4WD vehicle is used to reach the cement boat ramp (1/2 mile away). Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61572', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61574', 'Wood Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.427778, -112.793333, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Wood Lake Campground is located in the Lewis and Clark National Forest of North Central Montana. At an elevation of 5500 feet, the campground encompasses 2 acres. This small forest service campground has 9 campsites and provides restrooms and drinking water for campers. Fishing and swimming may be enjoyed at Wood Lake; however, motorboats are prohibited. Scenic hiking trails skirt the camp. The maximum recommended trailer length for the area is 22 feet. Please limit your stay to 14 days. You will be asked to pay a small fee for the use of this campground. Bears may frequent the area; keep all…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61574', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61576', 'Benchmark Campground', 'campground', 47.485833, -112.880833, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Benchmark Camping area is located approximately 30 miles west of Augusta, Montana. It has 25 campsites and available from Summer until Fall. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61576', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61578', 'South Fork Campground', 'campground', 47.501111, -112.888056, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Located 31 miles west of Augusta, the South Fork offers 7 campsites with opportunities to fish and hike. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61578', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61582', 'Jellison Place Campground', 'campground', 46.665680, -110.055240, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Campground Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61582', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61584', 'Daisy Dean Camp Campground', 'campground', 46.622778, -110.354722, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Campground Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61584', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '61586', 'Van Deriet Campground', 'campground', 47.475556, -112.866389, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Located 30 miles west of Augusta, Van Deriet offers 6 sites with a variety of amenities close to the airport. There is no vehicle access and is not handicapped accessible. This site is maintained with the help of the MT Aeronautic Division. Bears may frequent the area; keep all food out of sight in approved containers and remove all food from area after eating. Mandatory food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=61586', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6205', 'Iron Ridge Campground', 'campground', 38.614480, -82.624400, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'This newly renovated family campground is located on a ridge on the east side of Lake Vesuvius and accesses Lake Vesuvius Recreation Area facilities by a hiking trail. The campground has a total of 32 campsites (21 RV sites and 11 tent sites). There is water available at all sites and electricity at nearly half of the sites. Electric is available at all but 11 sites (sites 23-34). The campground can accommodate large RVsWhiskey Run Trail is 0.85 miles long and connects the Lake Shore Trail and Iron Ridge Campground. This loop trail starts at the campground across from site 29, goes down to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6205', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6206', 'Oak Hill Campground', 'campground', 38.613840, -82.633350, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'The new campground is beautifully designed with 27 RV (includes Pine Knob Loop ) sites and one group site ( Two Points Group Camp ). All campsites are fully accessible with water and electrical hook-ups. Two new flush restrooms with showers and one new vault restroom were installed. Campsites 2, 11, 19, 20, and 21 are not reservable. The sites have been designated for hosts or volunteers. This family campground is located on a ridge on the west side of Lake Vesuvius. There are 4 hiking trails that connect to different parts of this campground and boat dock. The Rock House, Black Oak, Old…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6206', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6207', 'Pine Knob Loop', 'campground', 38.618950, -82.632940, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'This family campground is located adjacent to Oak Hill Campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6207', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6214', 'Lamping Homestead Recreation Area', 'campground', 39.630700, -81.189000, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'In Monroe County, this area offers camping, picnicking, fishing, canoeing, and a scenic hiking trail. The site has six walk-in campsites, eight picnic sites, and a picnic shelter. There are two loop trails for hiking, one at 3&frac12; miles and the other at 1&frac12; miles. A 2-acre pond at the site is stocked with bluegill, bass, and catfish. This secluded recreation area was once the farmstead of the Lamping family. The family homesteaded this area in the 1800s.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6214', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6215', 'Leith Run Recreation Area', 'campground', 39.446300, -81.152100, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'The Leith Run Campground provides a beautiful location on the Ohio River, where grassy campsites and picnic areas make for a comfortable getaway in the Wayne National Forest. The campground is equipped with modern conveniences like flush toilets and electricity. This fully accessible facility offers a variety of recreation activities. There are now several no-mow zones and plantings of native shrubs to increase bird habitat and make the landscape more sustainable. Additional Resources Leith Run Recreation Area Brochure', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6216', 'Covered Bridge Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 39.483400, -81.276300, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'The National Forest Covered Bridge Scenic Byway ( Map ) follows State Route 26 from Marietta to Woodsfield, Ohio. For most of its length, it parallels the Little Muskingum River. The scenic byway traverses some of Ohio''s most beautiful countryside and many choose to stop along its route, to camp and savor the natural beauty of this area. There are four campgrounds along the byway. The Scenic Byway is a self-guided tour to interpret 35 miles of scenery and history along the Little Muskingum River. To guide you along the tour, look for the tour markers that will lead you to each of the ten…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6216', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6217', 'Lane Farm Campground', 'campground', 39.435800, -81.358800, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'Formerly the Lane family farm, this small campground is approximately 5 miles north of Marietta along the National Forest Covered Bridge Scenic Byway. The site has four campsites on the Little Muskingum.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6217', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6220', 'Ring Mill Campground', 'campground', 39.608200, -81.122400, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'This was once the site of a mill and farmstead. The mill is now gone, but the stone house of its original owner, built in 1846, is still located at the site. The house is on the National Register of Historic Places. It has three camp-sites and a picnic shelter, and is also a canoe access point and near the North Country Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6220', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6221', 'Burr Oak Cove Campground', 'campground', 39.550710, -82.057950, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'Burr Oak Cove Campground is a small densely wooded campground on the northwest tip of Burr Oak Reservoir in Athens County. The campground has 19 camping units, including walk-in sites which offer additional seclusion to the camper looking for solitude.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6221', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6239', 'Ohio River Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 39.425600, -81.190900, null, 'Wayne National Forest', 'This byway follows the Ohio River and traverses two of the units (Ironton and Marietta) of the Wayne National Forest. Some of the Forest provides a backdrop to the byway''s scenery, in other cases, loop trails off the byway offer visitors alternative routes to explore. A Forest campground along the byway, trails, and other amenities offer byway travelers an opportunity to explore the Wayne.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/wayne/recarea/?recid=6239', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6242', 'Johnson Creek Guard Station - Rental Cabin', 'campground', 44.924000, -115.480910, null, 'Boise National Forest', 'The Johnson Creek Guard Station cabin was built in 1922 and offers a charming mountain respite with modern conveniences. The cabin offers nearly everything needed for a pleasant and comfortable stay. Peak season for the cabin is typically early June through late September. It can be accessed by most vehicles via dirt and gravel roads, but trailers are not recommended. Natural Features: Johnson Creek Cabin sits in a pretty mountain meadow a stone''s throw from scenic Johnson Creek, a tributary of the East Fork of the South Fork Salmon River. Mountain slopes covered in dense pine forest surround…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/boise/recarea/?recid=6242', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62773', 'Sulphur Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.248027, -121.193939, null, 'Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest', 'This campground will remain closed for the forseeable future due to hazards remaining from fires. This campground offers a more primitive, quiet camping experience. Situated along Sulphur Creek and the Suiattle River, were every campsite can hear the rushing water. Activities in the area include fishing, hiking, and bicycle riding. This campground is mostly shaded by large old Douglas Fir trees. Relatively private sites and creek front sites are available. Popular with those seeking a quiet getaway this campground is an ideal base camp to access many area trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbs/recarea/?recid=62773', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62774', 'Buck Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.267500, -121.332680, null, 'Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest', 'This campground offers a more primitive, quiet camping experience. Situated along Buck Creek in old growth forest, were every campsite can hear the rushing water. Activities in the area include fishing, hiking, and bicycle riding. This campground is mostly shaded by large old Douglas Fir trees. Relatively private sites and creek front sites are available. Popular with those seeking a quiet getaway an ideal base camp to access many area trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbs/recarea/?recid=62774', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62822', 'Yaak River Campground', 'campground', 48.560500, -115.974240, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Yaak River Campground is located 7 miles northwest of Troy on Hwy 2. The campground has 44 sites, including one host site, with tables and firerings. Seven sites are pull-throughs most offering an average length of 32''. Amenities include potable water, vault toilets and access to two rivers. The campground is divided in half by the Yaak River, the camphosts are located on the east side of the campground along with a group area that can be rented for the day. To reserve the group area contact Recreation.gov or the Three Rivers Ranger District at 406-295-4693. Yaak River Campground Site Map', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=62822', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62835', 'Coulter Campground', 'campground', 46.513300, -111.542800, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Coulter Campground offers 5 boat-in campsites on the east side of Upper Holter Lake and adjacent to the Gates of the Mountains Wilderness. Approximately 1 mile north is a large day-use area (Meriwether Picnic Site) with wilderness access and boat docks. A scenic river trail provides access between the campground and picnic site. The campground, located within a scenic river canyon, provides excellent opportunities for wildlife viewing. Fish Your National Forests: Fish available include: Trout, Walleye; Types of fishing available include: Shore, Motorized boat, Spin, Bait;', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62835', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62837', 'Cromwell Dixon Campground', 'campground', 46.332600, -112.185500, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Cromwell Dixon Campground, located right on the Continental Divide, provides spectacular views of surrounding country encompassing meadows, timbered slopes, and far away mountains. Trailhead access to the Continental Divide National Scenic Trail is nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62837', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62839', 'Kading Campground', 'campground', 46.428889, -112.481389, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'This campground, off Forest Road #227, is located adjacent to the Little Blackfoot River. Kading campground is also located adjacent to the proposed Electric Peak Wilderness Area and provides wonderful opportunities to camp, hunt, fish and hike. A nearby trail heads south to Blackfoot Meadows. The trail continues south into the Beaverhead-Deerlodge National Forest, emerging near the Whitehouse Campground. A small public corral is located across the road from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62839', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62841', 'Moose Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.526111, -112.256111, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Moose Creek Campground is located southwest of Helena, Montana. Travel west of Helena on Highway 12 (about 8 miles) and turn south on Rimini Road #695. This 9 unit campground is located near other Forest Service features including: rental cabin, picnic area and environmental education trail. Also located within a short distance is access to the Continental Divide National Scenic Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62841', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62843', 'Park Lake Campground', 'campground', 46.442778, -112.168611, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Park Lake Campground is located approximately 20 miles southwest of Helena, Montana. The site provides an opportunity to camp near the placid, lovely Park Lake. You could enjoy fishing for cutthroat and grayling trout in this beautiful mountain lake, hand launch non-motorized boats or picnic along the lakeshore.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62845', 'Vigilante Campground', 'campground', 46.766944, -111.650556, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Vigilante Campground is located approximately 24 miles northeast of Helena in the Big Belt Mountains. To access the campground travel northeast of Helena on Highway #280, across the Missouri River to the small community of York. At York continue driving straight on Road #4 to the campground. This 7 acre campground provides access to the Hanging Valley National Recreation Trail and the scenic Trout Creek Canyon Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62845', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62849', 'Copper Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.078333, -112.619444, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'This campground is located northeast of Lincoln. Snowbank Lake is located across the road from the campground. The campground is only a short two mile drive from the Indian Meadows Trailhead and access into the Scapegoat Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62849', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '62853', 'Skidway Campground', 'campground', 46.354167, -111.098333, null, 'Helena-Lewis and Clark National Forest', 'Skidway Campground is located near the top of Deep Creek Canyon, off Highway #12. The campground location provides opportunities for nearby hiking and fishing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hlcnf/recarea/?recid=62853', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63404', 'Cedar Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.670748, -122.708283, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Situated on a river terrace and shaded by old-growth forest canopy, Cedar Creek Campground offers a glimpse into the best of South Oregon nature. Thanks to nearby trailheads and Brice Creek, the 10-site campground provides access to a diverse array of recreation opportunities, including hiking, mountain biking, photography, fishing, berry picking, and sunbathing. Facilities 9 campsites with picnic tables, fire pits, and tent pads 1 double campsite with picnic table, fire pit, and tent pad No drinking water 2 vault toilets Garbage disposal 3 grey water waste sumps You can view a map of Cedar…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63404', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63420', 'Lund Park Campground', 'campground', 43.650626, -122.679232, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Nestled in the cool, quiet forest beside crystal clear Brice Creek, Lund Park is the perfect place for slow mornings spent drinking coffee, days spent exploring Brice Creek Trail just across the footbridge on the western side of camp, and nights being lulled to sleep by the sound of water. Lund Park also has a rich history. The campground was once a stopover for miners traveling from Cottage Grove to the Bohemia Mining Area. During the early 1900s, Lund Park consisted of a post office, hotel, dam, power house and several other small buildings. Most of the structures were reclaimed by the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63420', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63422', 'Mineral Camp Campground', 'campground', 43.583234, -122.713654, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Mineral Camp is a small campground situated along Sharps Creek, surrounded stand of Douglas fir. Located at the base of the historic Hardscrabble Grade, Mineral Camp was once a stopover place for miners before they started up the long steep grade to the Bohemia Mining District. Facilities 3 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out No drinking water View a map of Mineral Camp Campground here .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63422', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63436', 'Rujada Campground', 'campground', 43.707551, -122.742335, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'An inviting, forested campground with access to Layng Creek and Swordfern Trail #1404 , Rujada Campground offers modern day amenities for an easy, stress-free getaway. Its flush toilets, running water, playground, and large day use picnic area means you will not feel too far from civilization, while the local undergrowth including wildflowers like pioneer violet and wild iris ensures that your campsite feels secluded. When you are ready to escape into the forest, 1.8-mile Swordfern Trail #1404 starts at the day use site and loops around the campground, taking you along the shore of Layng…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63436', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63460', 'Broken Arrow Campground', 'campground', 43.132810, -122.147200, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Set back from the shores of Diamond Lake in lodgepole pine forest, this is a quiet, idyllic playground for golden mantle ground squirrels. This picturesque spot boasts views of both Mount Bailey and Mount Thielsen. Broken Arrow Campground offers easy access to fishing, walking and biking trails, yet sees lighter use from anglers and paddlers during the summer months. Broken Arrow Campground is comfortable spot for families and groups. This sizeable campground can comfortably accommodate large groups. Interpretive programs are provided in the summer at the amphitheater at nearby Diamond Lake…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63460', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63466', 'Bunker Hill Campground', 'campground', 43.319223, -122.187839, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations can be made through Bunker Hill Campground, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov This diminutive campground clings to the northwest shore of Lemolo Lake beneath the heavily wooded Bunker Hill. Bald eagles often soar above the lodgepole pine forest. Bunker Hill Campground is popular with anglers looking for a more rustic experience, although anyone seeking secluded getaway will find it all here. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Vault toilet No drinking water Limited garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63466', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63474', 'Clearwater Falls Campground', 'campground', 43.247836, -122.233760, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Clearwater Falls Campground is located along the Rogue-Umpqua National Scenic Byway. The Clearwater River meanders through old growth Douglas fir forest, surrounded by picturesque moist green foliage. Clearwater Falls separates the campground into two sections with one section situated above the falls. Facilities 9 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 4 picnic sites with picnic tables and fire pits 3 vault toilets No drinking water No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63474', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63480', 'Diamond Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.159300, -122.133090, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations only. Reservations can be made at Diamond Lake, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov . Surrounded by conifer trees along the east shore of mile-high Diamond Lake, this campground offers social lakeshore camping and several more secluded inshore sites. Reservations are required. During the summer season, Diamond Lake is a very popular destination with up to 700,000 visitors a year. There are interpretative ranger activities on the weekends. Expect mosquitoes. There is an 11-mile paved hiking-biking trail around the Lake . Facilities 238 campsites with picnic tables and fire…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63480', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63486', 'Diamond Lake RV Park', 'campground', 43.139824, -122.133200, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Diamond Lake R.V. Park is north of Crater Lake and Klamath March National Wildlife Refuge and between the snowcapped peaks of Mt Thielsen and Mt. Bailey. This setting provides opportunities for fishing, hiking, berry picking, swimming, horseback riding, scenic drives, and picnicking. Boats are available through the Diamond Lake Resort. Nearby access to the Pacific Crest Trail as well as other forest trails in the area. Short excursions of less than one day can be made to many waterfalls and other fishing lakes, rivers and reservoirs. Diamond Lake R. V. Park, an equal opportunity service…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63486', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63492', 'East Lemolo Campground', 'campground', 43.310697, -122.162651, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations can be made at East Lemolo Campground, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov A cluster of clearings in the lodgepole pine forest along the southeast shore of Lemolo Lake, this informal camp is a favorite with fishermen and sandpipers alike. This campground offers direct and unobstructed access to the lake''s shoreline, and several campsites are only feet from the beach. Facilities 15 informal campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Vault toilet No drinking water Limited garbage disposal - Please pack it out Boat ramp', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63492', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63508', 'Inlet Campground', 'campground', 43.312114, -122.155350, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations can be made at Inlet Campground, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov This camp is hidden in the deep, green, quiet forest where the North Umpqua River rushes into Lemolo Lake. This campground is popular with families and outdoor enthusiasts. Facilities 13 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits 2 vault toilets No drinking Water Limited garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63508', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63510', 'Kelsay Valley Campground / Trailhead', 'campground', 43.318240, -122.096113, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations can be made through Kelsay Valley Horse Camp, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov This campground and trailhead is located along the Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River where it rushes through a lush high Cascade meadow. Spring arrives late in the high country and it is welcomed here with an explosion of colors. Purples, reds, yellows, greens, and white are arranged in a riotous bouquet. This site is designed to accommodate pack and saddle use as well as standard camping. This site provides access to Porcupine Connect Trail 1412A , which connects to the North Umpqua Trail 1414…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63510', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63570', 'Poole Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.310020, -122.200470, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Situated in a mixed stand of lodgepole pine, mountain hemlock and Shasta red fir, this campground hugs the west shore of Lemolo Lake, just south of the eponymous Poole Creek. Lemolo Lake is also the highest reservoir on the North Umpqua River. This campground is popular with a variety of outdoor enthusiasts, offering fishing opportunities throughout much of the year and wildlife viewing during all seasons. Facilities 60 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 group site Drinking water 6 vault toilets Boat ramp (standard amenity fee) Swimming beach Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63570', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63572', 'Poole Creek Group Campground', 'campground', 43.310075, -122.195194, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Reservations can be made on Poole Creek, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov This campground lies just south of the mouth of Poole Creek on the west shore of Lemolo Lake, the highest reservoir on the North Umpqua River. It is surrounded by lodgepole pine, mountain hemlock, and Shasta red fir forest. Facilities 1 group campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 100 people maximum at site #1 Drinking water Vault toilets Boat ramp (standard amenity fee) Swimming beach Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63572', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63618', 'Thielsen View Campground', 'campground', 43.169490, -122.168010, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Few other sites in the Umpqua National Forest offer so much concentrated natural splendor. Visitors can simultaneously bask in the shadow of Mount Bailey and get an unforgettable view of Mount Thielsen from across Diamond Lake. Like its sister site across the lake, Thielsen View Campground is a perennial favorite among anglers. Facilities 60 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Boat ramp Drinking water Vault toilets Garbage disposal Grey water waste sumps', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63618', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63630', 'Toketee Campground', 'campground', 43.272395, -122.407020, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'The Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River pauses at Toketee Lake, providing a home for a wide variety of wildlife. Here beaver and otter make their homes. Great blue heron and kingfishers are joined in fall and winter by ducks, geese, and bald eagle. This campground is popular for anglers and year-round visitors to the Umpqua National Forest. Toketee Lake is a reservoir because of a dam; expect to see change in water levels. Facilities 33 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Boat ramp No drinking water 2 vault toilets Limited garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63630', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63638', 'Toketee Lake Group Campground', 'campground', 43.272395, -122.407020, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'NOTICE 04/30/2014: The reservoir''s water level is 2-3 feet lower than usual as of April 30, 2014, due to PacifiCorp''s work on the 1951 Toketee Dam. This means that boats must be portaged to the water until further notice. Another alternative is to use boat ramps at Lemolo or Diamond lakes. The Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River pauses at Toketee Lake providing a home for a wide variety of wildlife. Here beaver and otter make their homes. Great blue heron and kingfishers are joined in fall and winter by ducks, geese, and bald eagle. This group site is a picturesque place for family gatherings.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63638', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63656', 'Whitehorse Falls Campground', 'campground', 43.246296, -122.304189, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Beneath a sheltering canopy of old growth Douglas-fir forest the Clearwater River tumbles into a tranquil pool. The cool, relaxing setting is one of many along the Rogue-Umpqua National Scenic Byway. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 2 picnic sites with picnic tables at day use site 2 vault toilets No drinking water No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63656', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63664', 'Apple Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.305703, -122.676923, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Camp right along the bank of the Wild and Scenic North Umpqua at this secluded spot located at the confluence of Apple and Panther Creeks. Deep pools and steady riffles offer anglers diverse fishing opportunities with easy access to wade-able areas. Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 double campsite with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal Grey water waste sump Campground host available', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63664', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63668', 'Bogus Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.324534, -122.800443, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'The Bogus Creek Campground is closed due to extensive damage from wildfires. The western-most campground in the Umpqua National Forest is also one of its most diverse in terms of recreational access. This 11-site campground balances seclusion and easy access to Roseburg, as well as a boat launch and direct access to the North Umpqua Trail. This campground is an ideal basecamp for entire days'' worth of adventure. Facilities 11 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 4 double campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Drinking water Flush toilets Vault toilet at raft launch Grey water waste…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63668', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63672', 'Boulder Flat Campground', 'campground', 43.303570, -122.526100, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Perched beside the Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River, Boulder Flat Campground is indeed proof that great things come in small packages. A developed raft launch at the east end provides easy access to some of the North Umpqua River''s best trout fishing, while nearby trailheads make this site popular among hikers and hunters exploring the Boulder Creek Wilderness via Boulder Creek Trail #1552 . This campground also provides access to Jesse Wright Segment of the North Umpqua National Recreation Trail #1414. Facilities 9 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water 2 vault…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63672', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63678', 'Canton Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.347770, -122.730496, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'This small campground is located along the banks of Steamboat Creek. A pavilion makes it an ideal destination for groups and day use. Canton Creek is located near Douglas Co Roads 38 and 23, both of which offer access to northern parts of the Umpqua National Forest. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Drinking water Covered picnic pavilion Flush toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63678', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63680', 'Coolwater Campground', 'campground', 43.232579, -122.871500, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Nestled in the Little River valley, Coolwater offers both a contemplative forest setting with easy access to outdoor recreation. Many visitors come to fish, swim, and spend a relaxing weekend entirely at camp. Others come to take advantage of Coolwater''s proximity to Grotto Falls and nearby Taft and Lookout mountains. Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Tent area No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63680', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63686', 'Eagle Rock Campground', 'campground', 43.295236, -122.554458, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Eagle Rock Campground, Umpqua National Forest - Recreation.gov Nestled in mixed conifers and adjacent to North Umpqua River, Eagle Rock is a quiet, shaded respite for camping, or as a base camp for a variety of recreation. Its namesake, an enormous rock formation, is a popular day hike destination, and also offers challenging routes for rock climbers. This site offers easy road access and sees lighter use than nearby Horseshoe Bend and Boulder Flat campgrounds.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63686', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63704', 'Hemlock Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.190205, -122.704400, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Hemlock Lake is a beautiful 28 acre man-made reservoir surrounded by stands of mixed conifers. This reservoir is 33 feet at its deepest point. It is stocked with trout which provides for good fishing from the banks or by boat. Facilities 9 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 double campsite with picnic tables and fire pits 3 tent campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 picnic site with grill Boat ramp at Hemlock Meadows, located 1/2 mile around the east arm of the lake No drinking water 2 vault toilets Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63704', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63708', 'Hemlock Meadows Campground', 'campground', 43.189557, -122.695721, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Hemlock Meadows provides unique combination of isolation and amenities, with ample access to nearby wilderness areas and scenic destinations. Four campsites form the south edge of Yellowjacket Glade, a roadless area known for its populations of elk, sooty grouse, black bear, and black-tailed deer. Hemlock Lake offers fishing and swimming, and visitors can use a boat launch with its own parking located at the edge of the campground. Note: there is no drinking water available at this campground. However, visitors may use the taps at nearby Hemlock Lake Campground. Facilities 4 dispersed…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63708', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63712', 'Horseshoe Bend Campground', 'campground', 43.288490, -122.627322, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Sheltered from traffic noise on Highway 138, Horseshoe Bend is situated on a bench adjacent to the Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River. An open stand of old-growth Douglas Fir and sugar pine creates privacy among the campsites and shelters Horseshoe Bend from traffic noise on Highway 138. The North Umpqua Trail #1414.04 Calf Segment is in close proximity to this campground, which also features a boat launch and group reservation facilities. Horseshoe Bend is popular with anglers, as well as whitewater adventures running some of the Wild and Scenic North Umpqua River''s most exhilarating…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63712', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63720', 'Island Campground', 'campground', 43.341340, -122.724197, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Located right off of Highway 138 is the small 7-site Island Campground. Enjoy the shade on a summer day and the sounds of the North Umpqua River. There are also many nearby trails to enjoy hiking or mountain biking. Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Grey water waste sump No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63720', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63724', 'Lake In The Woods Campground', 'campground', 43.216634, -122.721300, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Nestled in a mixed conifer Forest, Lake in the Woods is a 4 acre man-made lake that is 8 feet at its deepest point. The trail cabin located on the site was built in 1907. Facilities 8 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 2 double campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 tent campsite with picnic table and fire pit 1 picnic site with grill 4 flush toilets (1 vault toilet during the winter) No drinking water Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63724', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63746', 'Steamboat Falls Campground', 'campground', 43.375392, -122.652453, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'This campground offers excellent scenery. Although Steamboat Creek is closed to all fishing, summer visitors often see large steelhead trout attempting to jump the falls during their spawning runs. The campground is on the other side of Steamboat Creek from Steamboat Road. Towering fir trees shade the campsites, making it feel as if you are further away from the North Umpqua Highway. The trailhead for the 5.5-mile Mott segment of the North Umpqua Trail is about 6 miles southwest of the campground. Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 3 tent campsites with picnic tables and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63746', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63754', 'White Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.227613, -122.861850, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Campers can enjoy a sandy beach on Little River with shallow water. Facilities 3 walk in campsites with picnic tables and fire pits 1 campsite with picnic table and fire pit near parking lot No drinking water 2 vault toilets Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63754', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63760', 'Wolf Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.239548, -122.934600, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'This campground is located along Little River and provides access to fishing and swimming. Abundant wildflowers can be seen in the spring. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings 3 tent campsites with picnic tables and fire rings Drinking water (chlorinated) 2 flush toilets Grey water waste sumps Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63760', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63780', 'Boulder Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.053380, -122.776797, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Boulder Creek Campground is located along the South Umpqua River near the mouth of Boulder Creek. A mixed conifer forest offers shade and seclusion for campers. There may be poison oak at this location. There is no fishing at this location. Campground sits at 1,400 feet of elevation. Latitude: 43.053380 Longitude: -122.776797 Facilities 7 Campsites with picnic tables and fire pit Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63780', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63788', 'Camp Comfort Campground', 'campground', 43.105739, -122.596373, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Near the Upper South Umpqua, Camp Comfort is perfect for camping, swimming, picnicking, and hiking. Large old-growth cedar and fir trees provide shade to campers, while rhododendron are a burst of color in the spring. Camp Comfort serves as the trailhead for Camp Comfort Trail #1586 , a short but rewarding trail that leads to a rocky outcrop overlooking the beginning of the South Umpqua River. Deer Lick Falls Trail #1568 , another short trail that leads to a popular swimming hole in the spring and summer, is a quick two-miles up Road 28. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63788', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63804', 'Cover Campground', 'campground', 42.977444, -122.686906, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Shaded by a stand of Douglas fir, Cover Campground provides quick access to swimming spots and beautiful views on Jackson Creek. Come in the spring to see butterflies flock to the shores of the creek. Campground sits at 1,700 feet of elevation. Campground generally does not have snow cover in Winter. Latitude: 42.977444 Longitude: -122.686906 Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63804', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63816', 'Devil''s Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.816784, -123.026320, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Enjoy a beautiful drive through the picturesque Cow Creek drainage on your way to one of the most interesting campsites in Umpqua. Located under a bluff and surrounded by a forest of cedar, pine, and madrone, Devil''s Flat is a small campground with three campsites, a bevy of hiking opportunities, and a handful of historic landmarks. On the north side of the campground, you can see the stone ruins of an old water fixture built by the CCC Fire-Eaters in the 1930s. On the south side is the old Devil''s Flat Guard Station, where you''ll find a Ranger Cabin built in 1915 and a 1920s-era horse barn.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63816', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63822', 'Dumont Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.035986, -122.811807, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Dumont Creek Campground is located on the South Umpqua River just above the mouth of Dumont Creek. A short trail leads to a small, rocky beach on a section of river that''s perfect for wading. With just three campsites, you won''t have to worry about the neighbors (unless you count the wildlife, that is). Campground sits at 1,300 feet of elevation. Latitude: 43.035986 Longitude: -122.811807 Facilities 3 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No Drinking Water Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63822', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63858', 'South Umpqua Falls Campground', 'campground', 43.055849, -122.688400, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Like a little taste of Yosemite tucked away in the Umpqua Valley, South Umpqua Falls Campground is an open meadow campground surrounded by timber. With 20 campsites, 3 vault toilets, and grey water waste sumps so you can easily dispose of dirty water, this campground has the space and amenities needed for family and group camping. Across the road is the picturesque South Umpqua Falls Picnic Area, where you can see the South Umpqua River cascade fifteen feet over a wide slab of bedrock, learn about Chinook salmon, and occasionally spot a bald eagle flying overhead. Campground sits at 1,600…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63858', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63860', 'Three C Rock Campground', 'campground', 42.964832, -122.887916, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Three C Rock Campground is named for a historic Civilian Conservation Corps camp built here in late 1930. Right on the South Umpqua River, it is a great spot for families to relax under a canopy of mixed conifers. This is the only spot along the South Umpqua River where fishing is permitted. Be advised there may be Poison Oak. Campground sits at 1,100 feet of elevation. Campground generally does not have snow cover in Winter. Latitude: 42.964832 Longitude: -122.887916 Facilities 8 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63860', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '63862', 'Threehorn Campground', 'campground', 42.802328, -122.868900, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Threehorn campground is located near the Rogue-Umpqua Divide off of the scenic road between Tiller and Trail. It is a higher elevation campground shaded by an open stand of large pine and fir. Campground sits at 2,600 feet of elevation. Campground may have snow cover and roads to this campground may be snow covered from late Fall to mid Spring. Please pack out all trash. Latitude: 42.802328 Longitude: -122.868900 Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=63862', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64056', 'Coal Mine Campground & Picnic Area', 'campground', 35.234030, -107.701970, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'The campground is located in a setting of pinon, juniper, gambel oak, and mature ponderosa pine trees, approximately 10 miles northeast of Grants. A loop road winds through the area providing access to the campsites and the 0.25 mile nature trail. A historic bridge built by the Job Corps in 1967-1968 provides entrance to the trail. The 11,301 feet peak of Mount Taylor, the highest point in northwest New Mexico, can be seen if you drive past the campground on State Highway 547 (FR239). Remember to pay attention to road conditions and your vehicle''s abilities before driving off of the main road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64056', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64058', 'Mills Canyon Rim Campground', 'campground', 36.071833, -104.349431, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Elevation of this campground is 5,760 feet and offers 6 camping units.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64058', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64062', 'Lobo Canyon Picnic ground', 'campground', 35.203670, -107.715030, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'The picnic ground is located 10 miles northeast of Grants at an elevation of approximately 7,437 feet. Ponderosa pine, pinon, and juniper trees provide shade and some privacy for visitors. There is a group picnic area that was built in the 1930''s by the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC). Remember to pay attention to road conditions and your vehicle''s abilities before driving off of the main road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64062', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64064', 'Ojo Redondo Campground', 'campground', 35.158544, -108.108508, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'This campground is located southwest of Mt. Sedgwick, the highest peak in the Zuni Mountains. It is situated in ponderosa pine, douglas fir, and aspen trees, with a scenic meadow adjacent to the campground. Be advised of road conditions due to elevation and precipitation.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64064', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64066', 'Quaking Aspen Campground', 'campground', 35.405809, -108.540170, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Quaking Aspen campground offers a respite from the heat in a setting of aspen and mature ponderosa pine trees. Approximately 6 miles south of Fort Wingate, this is the most recently renovated campground on the Mt. Taylor Ranger District. The area has a rich history of railroad logging and the original town of McGaffey was built in the vicinity of McGaffey Lake a few miles down the road. Pay attention to road conditions and your vehicle''s abilities before driving off of the main road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64066', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64068', 'Bear Trap Campground', 'campground', 33.883004, -107.514144, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Small (4 unit) campsite without water is popular nonetheless due to cool mountain setting and proximity to Withington Lookout 2 (steep) miles away', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64068', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64070', 'McGaffey Campground', 'campground', 35.370720, -108.522720, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'This campground is situated in what was once the historic railroad logging and sawmill town of McGaffey. McGaffey Campground was built in 1937 and lies west of the Continental Divide in the Zuni Mountains, at an elevation of approximately 8,000 feet. It is the largest of the Mt. Taylor Ranger District campgrounds and has a volunteer host on site. Mature ponderosa pine trees provide scenic settings and shade, while small hills provide some privacy. Follow the road past the entrance, staying to the right to access the Oso and Page overnight sites. Remember to pay attention to road conditions…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64070', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64072', 'Hughes Mill Campground', 'campground', 33.858061, -107.540717, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Popular campground at 8100'' has 2 sites and dispersed camping with trailhead for hiking seven tough miles to Mt. Withington Lookout', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64074', 'Luna Park Campground', 'campground', 33.495715, -107.414651, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Odd volcanic rock formations give moon-like appearance to this popular picnic spot which also has three campsites, but little shade and no water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64074', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64076', 'Water Canyon Campground', 'campground', 34.025466, -107.132365, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'This campground is located at an elevation of 6,800 feet in the Magdalena Mountains.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64076', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64078', 'Capilla Peak Campground', 'campground', 34.698976, -106.402297, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Great views of Manzano Mountains, Rio Grande and Estancia Valleys are part of the attraction of this popular 8-unit site at 9200 with access to Manzano Mountain Wilderness and Hawkwatch''s raptor counting station.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64078', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64084', 'New Canyon Campground', 'campground', 34.403160, -106.247350, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'West of the community of Manzano.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64084', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64086', 'Tajique Campground', 'campground', 34.777295, -106.310057, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Small (6 unit) site at 6800* near Tajique Creek No trailers; pronounced "Tah-HEE-key"', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64086', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64088', 'Springtime Campground', 'campground', 33.574721, -107.403957, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', '6 campsites with Adirondack shelters provide access to Apache Kid Wilderness and San Mateo Peak Lookout by hiking or horseback.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64088', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64090', 'Black Kettle Campground', 'campground', 35.745169, -99.714289, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Campground is located at an elevation of 2,100 feet and has 12 camping units.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64090', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64092', 'Lake Marvin Campground', 'campground', 35.886002, -100.180636, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Lake Marvin Campground has 12 camping units and is situated at an elevation of 2,000 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64092', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64094', 'Skipout Campground', 'campground', 35.635381, -99.880275, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'The elevation of Skipout Campground is 2,100 feet. Twelve camping units are available for public use.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64094', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64096', 'Spring Creek Campground', 'campground', 35.772781, -99.839506, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'This campground has 5 camping units located at an elevation of 2,300 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64096', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64098', 'East Bluff #1 Campground - Lake McClellan', 'campground', 35.212192, -100.864714, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'East Bluff #1 Campground offers picnicking and camping opportunities at Lake McClellan. Campsites on Lake McClellan. The lake, which is in the background, is currently dry. USDA Forest Service Photo.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64098', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64104', 'Lake McClellan Campground', 'campground', 35.211481, -100.874872, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'This campground is situated at an elevation of 3,500 feet. There are 60 camping units. The lake, which is in the background of the image, is currently dry.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64104', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64106', 'McDowell Campground', 'campground', 35.214589, -100.866569, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Campground has pullouts for campers. Opportunities include day use and overnight camping. Campsites on Lake McClellan. The lake, which is in the background, is currently dry. USDA Forest Service Photo.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64106', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64108', 'Mills Canyon Campground', 'campground', 36.048383, -104.376666, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Mills Canyon Campground is a beautiful, remote campground situated within the Canadian River Canyon at an elevation of 5,160 feet. There are 12 camping units available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64108', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64110', 'Red Canyon Campground', 'campground', 34.621818, -106.410955, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Lower Red Canyon Campground is open for the season. Upper Red Canyon is open for the season. Sites: 38 Elevation: 7,600 Large, well shaded campground (38 units + 11 picnic sites in the lower loop). This is a good way into Manzano Wilderness via Red and Spruce Canyon trails on foot or horseback. Corrals and parking for horse trailers. This site is open for day-use or overnight camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64110', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64112', 'Bosque Campground', 'campground', 34.762704, -106.403846, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Bosque Campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64112', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64128', 'Water Canyon Group Campground', 'campground', 34.026088, -107.136583, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'group campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64128', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6421', 'Antlers Campground', 'campground', 40.889044, -122.375507, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the upper Sacramento Arm, the campground sits on a bluff above the lake and although some sites are near the lakeshore, direct access to the water is very difficult. The campground area is flat and level, covered with oak and pine forest which provide shade and good screening between units. Each campsite contains a paved parking spur, a table, bear boxes, and one fire ring. Antlers boat ramp and Antlers amphitheatre are located nearby. The amphitheatre consists of a building and stage and an adjacent paved parking lot for 22 vehicles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6421', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6422', 'Bailey Cove Campground', 'campground', 40.800302, -122.319147, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Bailey Cove is a beautiful forested campground. Due to the nearby boatramp, this facility is very popular when the ramp is in the water (full to 50'' down). In addition to the boat ramp, there is also a day use area and hiking trail nearby. The boat ramp facility is very busy early in the season when the lake level is at its highest. Each site has a tent pad, picnic table, raised fire ring, bear boxes, and paved parking spur. Brick pavers have been used to provide added accessibility.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6422', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6423', 'Ellery Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.915843, -122.241631, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Ellery Creek is a beautiful, forested campground located on the McCloud Arm of Shasta Lake. When the lake is at its highest, to approximately 50 feet down, boats can be moored on the shore within sight of the campground making this a very popular place to camp. All sites have a picnic table, tent pads, fire rings, bear boxes, and paved parking spurs.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6423', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6424', 'Gregory Creek Group Campground', 'campground', 40.887973, -122.368149, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'The campground is a single loop and is moderately to thickly wooded with a mix of oak and pine trees that provide plenty of shade in the hot summers (80% + cover). The understory, which consists of manzanita, blackberries, poison oak, tree fern, wild grape and a variety of native grasses and forbs provide limited privacy between campsites. When the lake level is high, the bank is moderately sloped to provide access to the water. As the lake level drops, it exposes a step drop off to the water, especially on the side of the campground nearest Gregory Beach. There is a boat ramp nearby at…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6424', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6425', 'Hirz Bay Campground', 'campground', 40.866442, -122.249356, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Each campsite contains a paved parking spur, a table, bear boxes and one fire ring. This campground has a pay phone, an overflow parking area, access to Hirz Bay Trail, and is located near Hirz Bay boat ramp. Hirz Bay Group campgrounds #1 and #2 are in close proximity.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6425', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6426', 'Lakeshore East Campground', 'campground', 40.872236, -122.387538, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This campground is in close proxmity to Antlers and Sugarloaf boat ramps. Each site has a paved surface area, a picnic table, raised fire ring, and parking spur. There are two Yurts located at the Lakeshore East campground. What is a Yurt? The Yurt is a modern adaptation of the ancient shelter used by Central Asian nomads for centuries. Though generally classified as a tent, the yurt is much stronger and weather tight. Campground Host available during the reservation season.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6426', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6427', 'Lower Jones Valley Campground', 'campground', 40.727560, -122.228082, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This campground is located in a small canyon adjacent to the lake. The Jones Valley boat ramp and the Clickipudi Trail are located nearby. All sites have an paved parking spur, tent pad, raised campfire ring, bear boxes and a picnic table.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6427', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6428', 'Upper Jones Valley Campground', 'campground', 40.730078, -122.230025, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This facility is used on an "as needed basis" by the Shasta Recreation Company (Concessionaire to the Forest Service). There are 8 camping sites that can accommodate a trailer with an average max. size of 16''. All sites have a picnic table, campfire ring, and an unpaved parking spur.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6428', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6429', 'McCloud Bridge Campground', 'campground', 40.938333, -122.245000, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'All campsites have picnic tables, raised fire rings, tent pads, bear boxes, and paved parking spurs. The units have brick pavers to provide an accessible surface. Adjacent to the McCloud Bridge Day Use Area. McCloud Bridge is a very popular campground for easy lake access and is located on an old ranch site that is set among fruit trees, sweet peas and berries.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6429', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64294', 'Zuni Mt. Historic Auto Tour Interpretive Site', 'scenic_drive', 35.180526, -108.256192, null, 'Cibola National Forest and Grasslands', 'Self guided tour with 18 interpretive sites along Forest System roads in the Zuni Mountains.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/cibola/recarea/?recid=64294', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6434', 'Deadlun Campground', 'campground', 41.061844, -121.974884, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Deadlun Campground is located at Iron Canyon Reservoir, a beautiful 500 acre lake located in a mountainous area of the Shasta-Trinity National Forest at an elevation of 2,696 feet. With 15 miles of forested shoreline and surrounding natural environment, the reservoir is a pleasant destination for anglers, campers, hunters and 4 wheel drive enthusiasts. There are two developed campgrounds (Deadlun and the PG&E managed Hawkins Landing), many undeveloped camping spots, a boat ramp for small boats and a network of primitive roads and trails surrounding the reservoir. Nearby is the Pacific Crest…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6434', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6435', 'Madrone Campground', 'campground', 40.924456, -122.094430, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located east of Shasta Lake, these remote campsites offer the perfect spot to relax. Forested and shady, this is a perfect home base for your OHV adventures! Be aware, Fenders Ferry is a rough, unimproved dirt road. There is no lake access from this facility. This campground is very popular in the fall during hunting season. For more information and directions click this link', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6435', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6473', 'Ackerman Campground', 'campground', 40.786218, -122.770651, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the shores of Lewiston Lake, eight miles north of Lewiston on County Road 105, and 20 miles from Weaverville. This campground is on the waters edge, offers beautiful scenery, and is a favorite of fisherman. Each site is equipped with tables and grill/fire ring.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6473', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6474', 'Alpine View Campground', 'campground', 40.887065, -122.765816, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This campground is approximately 25 miles north of Weaverville and 8 miles south of Trinity Center, 2 miles off of Hwy 3, on Guy Covington Drive. This is a 54-unit family campground including several wheel-chair accessible campsites and three accessible restrooms. The campsites have paved social areas, roads, and spurs. Each campsite is furnished with a table and fireplace. Some of the campsites have bear-proof food lockers. This campground is very popular with the boating public, as the Bowerman boat ramp is located 1/4 mile down the road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6474', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6478', 'Captains Point Boat-In Campground', 'campground', 40.863083, -122.724452, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This is a boat access only facility with 3 campsites. There is a vault toilet and no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6478', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6479', 'Clark Springs Campground', 'campground', 40.857100, -122.813500, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located 17 miles from Weaverville, north on Hwy 3. This campground has 20 campsites with a table and a fireplace and most campsites have bear -proof food lockers. The campground is a single loop through cedar and other deciduous trees. There are four secluded walk-in tent sites next to a babbling brook. The campground accommodates mostly tent campers but has three spurs for trailers. While the campground tends to be rugged, the adjacent boat ramp and swimming area at Trinity Lake are attractive. Directly adjacent to the Clark Springs picnic area, swim beach and boat ramp.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6479', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6482', 'Cooper Gulch Campground', 'campground', 40.745926, -122.804285, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the shores of Lewiston Lake, approximately 4 miles north of Lewiston on County Road 105, and 17 miles from Weaverville. This campground is on the water''s edge and is a favorite for fisherman, and for launching kayaks or canoes. There are 5 paved campsites, furnished with a table and fireplace, paved wheelchair accessible trails and one vault restroom. There is a camp host at this facility. The Cooper Gulch day use area has 5 parking spaces for people to fish and/or to hike on the Baker Gulch Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6482', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64823', 'Big Eddy Campground', 'campground', 48.066110, -115.924630, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Big Eddy Campground is located approximately 6 miles of east of the Idaho border in Montana on Hwy 200. The campground has 5 sites with table and fire rings and will accommodate a 30'' RV. Amenities include vault toilets and a fully developed boat ramp with a dock. There is two day use sites, one with a covered shelter, two picnic tables and fire grills, near the boat ramp.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=64823', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64838', 'Ash Flat Campground', 'campground', 43.045400, -122.732160, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Tucked into a forest of mixed conifers and hardwoods, Ash Flat Campground provides shaded campsites for a relaxed getaway any time of the year. Beaches and beautiful downstream views courtesy of the South Umpqua River are just a few seconds away, so bring your bathing suits! Campground sits at 1,500 feet of elevation. Campground generally does not have snow cover in Winter. Latitude: 43.04540 Longitude: -122.73216 Facilities 4 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=64838', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6486', 'Hayward Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.874227, -122.767583, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located approximately 20 miles north of Weaverville, 2 miles off of Hwy 3 and is on the shores of Trinity Lake. Trinity Center is 9 miles north of Hayward Flat. Hayward Flat is easily one of the most popular campgrounds on Trinity Lake. It offers excellent lake access and plenty of shade. Sitting on one of the best arms of the lake for waterskiing, Hayward is favored by the watersports crowd.This is a 98 unit family campground with an amphitheatre and limited day-use parking. Each campsite has a paved spur, table, and fireplace. The campground road is paved. Most campsites have bear proof…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6486', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64866', 'Deer Flat Group Campground', 'campground', 43.292780, -122.686940, null, 'Umpqua National Forest', 'Located on the North Umpqua Wild and Scenic River adjacent to the Horseshoe Bend Campground with its own loop of camping spurs and restrooms. Facilities 1 group campsite with picnic tables, fire pit and grills 70 people maximum Drinking water Flush toilet Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/umpqua/recarea/?recid=64866', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6487', 'Jackass Springs Campground', 'campground', 40.961836, -122.660919, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located approximately 34 miles north of Weaverville on State Hwy 3, this campground offers 10 campsites that can accommodate up to a 32'' trailer. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6487', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6488', 'Mariners Roost Boat-In Campground', 'campground', 40.839805, -122.769745, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Mariners Roost is a boat access only campground located on the Stuart Fork Arm of Trinity Lake on the east side of the Mule Creek cove. The campground offers 7 campsites. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6488', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6489', 'Mary Smith Campground', 'campground', 40.731796, -122.807228, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Mary Smith campground is located off of County Road 105, two miles north of the town of Lewiston. This campground offers excellent fishing and tent camping. Mary Smith was picked as one of California''s prettiest lake campgrounds. Except for a large cluster of sites at campground entrance (sites 2-9), all campsites are walk-in and clustered in small groups. The campsites are tucked into a lush riparian environment of conifers and deciduous trees, a thick middlestory, and ample wildflowers. Privacy between campsites ranges from fair to outstanding. Each site has a view of the lake and Trinity…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6489', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64892', 'Highway 108 Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 38.267890, -119.992405, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'California State Highway 108 traverses over Sonora Pass in the Sierra Nevada mountain range at an elevation of 9,628 feet and is subject to winter closure at Highway 108 Sno-Park. This parking lot is for winter enthusiasts such as, snowmobilers accessing the legal over-snow vehicle use areas, and other users accessing the Highway 108 for winter recreation. Sno-Park permits are required for parking $15 a day, or $40 for a season pass. Passes can be purchased online or in person at the following locations: Rich and Sal''s Sport Shop, Strawberry Store and Pinecrest Market. The Highway 108…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=64892', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6490', 'Minersville Campground', 'campground', 40.851826, -122.811626, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the shores of Trinity Lake near the Bushytail campground. One of the more popular campgrounds on Trinity Lake in a stand of mixed conifers and deciduous trees. Excellent waterskiing is available on the arm. The first section of the campground is well developed with paved, level parking aprons and amenities. The second section is mostly walk-in, with good privacy between campsites, and more primitive with a wilderness feel. This section also features campsites next to the water''s edge. Most sites in both sections have views of Trinity Lake. There are six walk-in campsites (five…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6490', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64905', 'Chittenden Brook Campground', 'campground', 43.824070, -72.909310, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Centrally located between the Rochester and Middlebury Ranger Districts, the Chittenden Brook area offers many recreation opportunities for a variety of abilities. Trails meandering next to beautiful brooks and traveling through tall trees make this an attractive area for visitors. The area includes a 7.5 mile trail network designed for cross country ski and snowshoe use and open to summer hiking. The trail network serves as a connector to the Long Trail National Recreation Trail as well as the Brandon Gap Backcountry Recreation Area known for winter skiing and boarding. The area also…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64905', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64907', 'Moosalamoo Campground', 'campground', 43.918840, -73.027230, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Moosalamoo Campground is a small, remote campground located at the base of Mt. Moosalamoo, near Voter Brook. Located within the heart of the Moosalamoo National Recreation Area, the campground is located in close proximity to over 70 miles of trail managed for hiking, biking, cross-county skiing, horseback riding, and snowmobiling.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64907', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64909', 'Silver Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.897090, -73.050100, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Silver Lake Campground is a small, primitive campground located on Silver Lake. Silver Lake is only accessible by hiking 0.6 miles down the Goshen Trail or on the Service Road. Please note: drinking water access is currently closed to protect public health. There is no garbage service available, please carry out what you carry in. Hiking, mountain biking, horseback riding, cross-country skiing, snowshoeing, a snowmobiling opportunities are all available in the Silver Lake Area Trails .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64909', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64911', 'Greendale Campground', 'campground', 43.350640, -72.820850, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Greendale Campground is a small remote campground located along Greendale Brook in Weston, VT. There are 11 campsites available in a wooded setting. Each site has a picnic table, a fire ring with a grill, and a parking spur. Most sites can accommodate small campers as well as tents. There is also a vault toilet. The campground offers easy access to the Greendale Loop , a 4.0 mile hike through a mixed forest of northern hardwood and conifer trees with long stretches bordering scenic streams. This loop includes approximately 2 miles of walking along town maintained roads open to vehicular…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64911', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64915', 'Hapgood Pond Recreation Area', 'campground', 43.252790, -72.892070, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Hapgood Pond Recreation Area offers camping, fishing, swimming, picnicking, and hiking among the tranquil surroundings of Hapgood Pond. The pond itself is 12 acres in size and 12 feet at its deepest point. The recreation area offers a 28-site campground in a wooded setting, a 1 mile nature trail, and a day use area with a beach for swimming. No lifeguard is on duty; swim at your own risk.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64915', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64967', 'Grout Pond Recreation Area', 'campground', 43.045530, -72.954570, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Grout Pond Recreation Area is available for year-round recreation. The recreation area is a great destination for camping, hiking, canoeing, kayaking and fishing all based around the 80 acre Grout Pond. Over 10 miles of multipurpose non-motorized trails are available for enjoyment.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64967', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '64977', 'Little Rock Pond/Green Mountain Loop', 'campground', 43.401000, -72.957270, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'The Green Mountain Connector Trail, found across the road and slightly west of the parking lot, heads southwest for 0.6 miles to its junction with the Green Mountain Trail. Follow the blue blazes. From here the trail ascends, following old woods roads for the next mile and leads to the summit of Green Mountain at 2.5 miles. The trail continues along the ridgeline and passes several spur trails that lead to excellent views of the surrounding mountains and Little Rock Pond. Crossing ledges the trail descends steadily to its junction with the Little Rock Pond Loop Trail at the north end of the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=64977', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6500', 'Stoney Point Campground', 'campground', 40.848425, -122.858404, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Closed at this time. This campground is located 13 miles north of Weaverville on Highway 3 on the shores of the Stuart Fork arm of Trinity Lake. This tent-only campground hugs a shore of Trinity Lake. Cedar and Ponderosa pine provide shade. Manzanita, Mountain Mahogany, grass along with well separated walk-in campsites, give good privacy. Just off State Route 3, traffic noise can be heard throughout the campground. There are 22 walk-in tent campsites with tables and fireplaces. Drinking water, paved road and parking spaces. While there is a boat ramp at this campground, there is another at…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6500', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65003', 'Bingo', 'campground', 43.875356, -72.913700, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'General Forest Camping Recreational Opportunity Guide', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=65003', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6503', 'Tannery Gulch Campground', 'campground', 40.835485, -122.845152, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'The Tannery Gulch campground is located 12 miles north of Weaverville on Highway 3 and is on the shore of Trinity Lake nestled among tall pines, firs and oaks. Trout, bass and catfish can be caught along the shores of this campground.This attractive campground has four loops (A, B, C, and D) and a spur in a pleasant mix of conifers and deciduous trees next to Trinity Lake. Campsites in every loop except A have a view of lake. Although there are patches of middlestory, most campsites are close to each other making privacy minimal. All campsites have room for a tent, have a table and fireplace;…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6503', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6507', 'Tunnel Rock Campground', 'campground', 40.772396, -122.778414, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Tunnel Rock campground is located seven miles from Lewiston, north on County Road 105, and approximately 19 miles from Weaverville and offers fishing, camping, shade and beautiful scenery. This campground is across the road from the lake, about 250 feet from the water''s edge, near a popular fishing spot. Each site is equipped with a table and fireplace. Boat launching and rentals can be found 1 mile south at Pinecove boat ramp and Pinecove Marina. The marina has fishing supplies and some food items available. About 1-1/4 miles from Fairview boat ramp, Tunnel Rock offers easy access to both…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6507', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6511', 'Big Flat Campground (Klamath NF)', 'campground', 41.067300, -122.935200, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Big Flat Campground and trailhead are located on the north side of the Trinity Alps Wilderness. Managed by the Klamath National Forest, this trailhead is accessed via Coffee Creek Road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6511', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6512', 'Bridge Camp Campground', 'campground', 40.872876, -122.915360, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the North Fork of Stuart Fork Creek, five miles west on County Road 112 and 18 miles from Weaverville, this campground has 10 units with a average max. trailer size allowed of 20''. There are picnic table, fire rings, vault toilets, drinking water, one corral, an unsurfaced road and parking lot and two hitching rails. Camp is a tent/equestrian campground and trailhead for one of the most popular trails to the Trinity Alps Wilderness. The campground stretches out along Stewart''s Fork of Trinity River with some campsites at the water''s edge. The campground is adjacent Stuart''s Fork…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6512', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6513', 'Clear Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.930800, -122.585924, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Clear Creek campground is a small facility with only 6 campsites. It can accommodate up to a 22 foot trailer and offers picnic tables, fire rings and a vault toilet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6513', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6514', 'Eagle Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.152910, -122.668458, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located on the northside of Trinity Lake along State Highway 3 approximately five miles north of the Coffee Creek area. Surrounded by the Trinity River on one side and Eagle Creek on the other. It mostly attracts the tent camping population, but has several trailer length spurs. There are 7 sites with picnic table, fire rings and a vault toilet. The sites can accommodate a trailer up to 35 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6514', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6515', 'East Weaver Group Campground', 'campground', 40.773001, -122.920987, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'The East Weaver Group Campground is available by reservation only. It offers 10 sites, picnic tables, fire rings and a vault toilet. Located in the Weaverville area at the end of East Weaver Road, on the banks of East Weaver Creek, this is a rustic campground with plenty of trees. It is primarily a tent campground but small trailers can fit in 30% of the spurs. The road is paved and the spurs are dirt. Each campsite has a table and a stove/grill. Fuel, groceries, bait and restaurants can be found 1.5 miles away in Weaverville', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6515', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6516', 'Goldfield Campground', 'campground', 41.100008, -122.778634, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located off of State Hwy 3 on Coffee Creek Road. This campground offers picnic tables, fire rings and a vault toilet. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6516', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6517', 'Horse Flat Campground', 'campground', 41.166516, -122.691096, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located approximately 40 north on State Hwy 3 from Weaverville, this campground offers 10 units that can accommodate trailers up to 16 feet. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6517', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6518', 'Preacher Meadow Campground', 'campground', 40.963132, -122.730461, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Preacher Meadow campground is located one mile south of Trinity Center off of Highway 3 and approximately 30 miles from Weaverville. This quiet and serene campground attracts hikers as it is near the popular Swift Creek trailhead and many persons stay there before and after their hikes. The campground has two large unnamed loops meandering through mature cedar, ponderosa pine and some deciduous trees. The middle story is comprised mostly of deciduous trees providing fair privacy between campsites. The understory is grass and pine needles. Some parking aprons are overgrown. State Route. 3…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6518', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65180', 'Kyle Canyon Picnic Area', 'campground', 36.263000, -115.605900, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Kyle Canyon Picnic Area is set in the beautiful Spring Mountains National Recreation Area, just 23 miles from Las Vegas. Visitors enjoy hiking, horseback riding and scenic driving in this forested desert oasis.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65180', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6519', 'Rush Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.818751, -122.897261, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Rush Creek campground is located off of Highway 3, eight miles north of Weaverville. The campground stretches along Rush Creek among Douglas fir, oak and maple. The sound of Rush Creek can be heard throughout the campground. Most campsites are well separated providing good privacy. Fishing is good for brook trout. The campground road and spurs are unpaved. All campsites have fire rings and picnic tables. Some campsites have a Klamath Oven. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6519', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65190', 'McWilliams Campground', 'campground', 36.309000, -115.678000, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Near the Lee Canyon Ski Area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65190', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65198', 'Hilltop Campground', 'campground', 36.310100, -115.607400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Elevation 8,400 feet, 35 sites in timbered setting. Near the North Loop Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65198', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6520', 'Scott Mountain Campground', 'campground', 41.274608, -122.698132, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Scott Mountain campground offers 7 campsites and can accommodate up to a 15 foot trailer. There is no piped water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6520', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65200', 'Fletcher View Campground', 'campground', 36.262400, -115.617900, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Campground set in a timbered area that is open year around. This campground is near the Fletcher Canyon Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65200', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65202', 'Hope Valley Campground', 'campground', 38.729700, -119.928700, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Hope Valley Campground is located in its beautiful namesake valley at an elevation of 7,300 feet, surrounded by Jeffrey and lodgepole pines. The West Fork Carson River runs nearby, offering rainbow and cutthroat trout fishing. Numerous trails in the area provide excellent hiking and backpacking opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65202', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65204', 'Mt. Rose Campground', 'campground', 39.312200, -119.894000, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Mount Rose Campground is located at an elevation of 9,300 feet in an open conifer forest overlooking beautiful Lake Tahoe, just nine miles west. Popular activities include fishing, swimming, boating, and sightseeing. Hiking is also available on several area trails including Tahoe Meadows Trail, Tahoe Rim Trail, Mount Rose Wilderness Trail and Mount Rose Summit Trail. This campground contains single and double-family sites, as well as one triple-family site. Picnic tables and fire rings are provided, as are restrooms and potable water. Roads and parking spurs throughout the site are paved.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65204', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65206', 'Silver Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.587000, -119.783500, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Silver Creek Campground is located in a scenic fir and pine forest on the mountainside just above Noble Creek at an elevation of 6,800 feet. Popular activities include fishing nearby creeks and the East Fork Carson River, and hiking on the Pacific Crest Trail, which can be accessed just 3 miles west of the site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65206', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65208', 'Robinson Creek South/North Campground', 'campground', 38.187400, -119.321500, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Robinson Creek South Campground is located just 9 miles from Bridgeport, California next to Robinson Creek at an elevation of 7,000 feet. Massive Jeffrey pines tower over the site, offering partial shade. Lodgepole pines, sagebrush, and summer wildflowers dot the area. The creek offers good rainbow trout fishing and can be easily accessed within the site. Numerous hiking trails are in the vicinity, including the popular Robinson Creek Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65208', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65210', 'Trumbull Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.055200, -119.260400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Trumbull Lake Campground is set in a thick lodgepole pine forest on the banks of scenic Trumbull Lake. Aspens and summer wildflowers dot the landscape. The lake offers canoeing and fishing for rainbow, brown, and brook trout. The Virginia Lakes area is very close, offering additional canoeing and fishing, as well as hiking and horse trail access into the adjacent Hoover Wilderness Area and Yosemite National Park. This campground contains several single-family sites, a few double sites, and one triple site, all with picnic tables, fire rings with grills, and bear boxes. Vault toilets, potable…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65210', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65212', 'Honeymoon Flat Campground', 'campground', 38.202000, -119.322900, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The Honeymoon Flat Campground is nestled on Robinson Creek amidst aspens and Jeffrey pines. Robinson Creek has good fishing opportunities. Fishing and boating are available in nearby Twin Lakes. Interpretive programs are held in the amphitheater. Keep all your food in the bear-approved containers provided.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65212', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65214', 'Paha Campground', 'campground', 38.185700, -119.320800, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Paha Campground is located just 10 miles from Bridgeport, California at an elevation of 7,000 feet. Massive Jeffrey pines tower over the site, providing limited shade. Sagebrush and summer wildflowers dot the area. Robinson Creek is adjacent and offers good rainbow trout fishing. Numerous hiking trails are in the vicinity, including the popular Robinson Creek Trail. Upper and Lower Twin Lakes are just up the road, offering beautiful mountain scenery, boating, canoeing, and fishing for Kokanee salmon, rainbow and brown trout. The rugged and scenic Hoover Wilderness Area can be accessed from…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65214', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65216', 'Lower Twin Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.174600, -119.332400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Lower Twin Lakes Campground is located just 10 miles from Bridgeport, California at an elevation of 7,000 feet. Massive Jeffrey pines tower over the site, offering partial shade. Aspens, sagebrush, and summer wildflowers dot the site. Robinson Creek is adjacent, with good rainbow trout fishing. Numerous hiking trails are in the vicinity, including the popular Robinson Creek Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65216', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65218', 'Crags Campground', 'campground', 38.174600, -119.325400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Crags Campground is partially shaded by Jeffrey pine trees and is near Robinson Creek and Twin Lakes. Fishing in Robinson Creek and Twin Lakes, trails nearby to Yosemite, restaurants, shower and laundry facilities nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65218', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65224', 'San Juan Dispersed Campground', 'campground', 39.120600, -117.272400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Dispersed Campground in an open setting with views of the canyon. Access to Toiyabe Crest National Recreation Trail by the San Juan Trailhead. County Road 21 intersects, and in places follows, the Austin-Grantville Stage Route (1861-1866) The Town of Belmont performs limited maintenance and oversite. Heavy use on 3-day weekends!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65224', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65228', 'East Creek Campground', 'campground', 39.496700, -114.654800, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'East Creek Campground is located high on the slopes of the Schell Creek Range in the middle of an alder, pinyon and juniper forest. East Creek, a perennial stream, runs directly through the picnic area and many birds make it their home during the spring and summer seasons. There are seven campsites, including one tent only camping sites and six RV sites. These sites also have picnic tables and campfire rings. At this campground, recreation activities include mountain biking, backpack/day hiking, and off-highway vehicle riding. S are open.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65228', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6523', 'Trinity River Campground', 'campground', 41.108778, -122.704616, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'The Trinity River campground is located two miles north of the Coffee Creek area on Highway 3, and lies on the banks of the Trinity River. It is approximately 36 miles from Weaverville. It is very popular with travelers as an overnight campground as it is located on Highway 3. This facility has a paved road and spurs, accommodating both trailers and tent campers. Each site has a concrete table and fireplace.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6523', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65244', 'Pine Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.786900, -116.848200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The half-mile Cave trail begins in the campground, with a series of stone steps leading to the rock shelter site. The red, yellow, black and white images (pictographs) here were painted by Native Americans.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65244', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65246', 'Peavine Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.620500, -117.312400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Situated on the eastern side of the Toquima Mountain Range in the Monitor Valley. Fishing in Pine Creek. Access to other sites via Monitor Valley.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65246', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65248', 'Bob Scott Campground', 'campground', 39.455100, -117.001100, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Accessible from U.S. Route 50. In an open setting with pinyon-juniper forest at Bob Scott Summit. Hunting for deer and elk in season. Fishing at Birch Creek, 8 miles from campground. IMPORTANT NOTICE: The Bob Scott Campground will be renovated in Fiscal Year 24. In the meantime, potable water is not available for public consumption at the campground. The District has kept the flush restrooms open and serviceable. Renovations will include improved road access, longer and level RV pads, restroom replacement with vaulted toilet facilities and upgraded public water system. These renovation…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65248', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65250', 'Big Creek Campground', 'campground', 39.346390, -117.136110, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Access to Kingston Canyon and Groves Lake. High clearance vehicle needed. Surrounded by water birch, cottonwood, and Russian olive trees at the mouth of a canyon along a creek. Stream runs through the campground. Currently, road access needs repairs! High clearance vehicles only 2021', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65250', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65252', 'Kingston Campground', 'campground', 39.222900, -117.143200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Located in Peavine Canyon, on the southeastern side of the Toiyabe Mountain Range. Peavine Creek also flows through this site. Hiking north of the campground in Arc Dome Wilderness. Fishing in Peavine Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65252', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65256', 'Lye Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.685200, -117.552900, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Lye Creek Campground is located in the Santa Rosa Mountain Range about 60 miles north of Winnemucca, Nevada. The campground is nestled in a grove of aspen trees along Lye Creek. There are 14 camping sites, including four double sites and one group site. These sites also have picnic tables, campfire rings, and BBQ pedestals. At this campground, recreation activities include river/stream fishing, mountain biking, backpack/day hiking, and off-highway vehicle riding. The Santa Rosa-Paradise Peak Wilderness is not accessible from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65256', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6526', 'Big Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.739200, -123.204600, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This a fee campground with 10 camp units. Can accommodate up to a 22 foot trailer. Open Memorial Day to Labor Day.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6526', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65260', 'Columbine Campground', 'campground', 38.900237, -117.376490, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Primitive sites in an open setting with views of the canyon. Access to Toiyabe Crest National Recreation Trail. County Road 21 intersects, and in places follows, the Austin-Grantville Stage Route (1861-1866)', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65260', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65262', 'Crystal Springs Campground', 'campground', 38.764200, -119.845300, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Quiet sites amidst the shade of Jeffrey and lodgepole pines.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65262', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65264', 'Lookout Campground', 'campground', 39.588610, -120.072779, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Nestled in among the aspens this campground offers a quiet setting to relax in. Rockhounding for crystals at the Crystal Mine (a few miles away on FR 033). Limit for personal use: one 5-lb bucket per week.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65264', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65266', 'Kit Carson Campground', 'campground', 38.776400, -119.896200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Located on the West fork of the Carson River amidst Jeffrey Pines and aspens.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65266', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65268', 'Markleeville Campground', 'campground', 38.697700, -119.776400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Located on Markleeville Creek, in the shade of Jeffrey pines and cottonwood trees.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65268', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6527', 'Burnt Ranch Campground', 'campground', 40.827995, -123.482300, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This facility is a first-come, first-serve facility with 16 units. Can accommodate up to a 25 foot trailer. Please contact the Weaverville Ranger Station at 530-623-2121 for open and close dates.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6527', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65270', 'Bootleg Campground', 'campground', 38.417700, -119.453500, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Bootleg Campground offers solitude and chance to get away from crowds in shaded Jeffrey pines. The campground is across highway from West Walker River which has good fishing opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65270', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65272', 'Buckeye Campground', 'campground', 38.238900, -119.325400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Buckeye Campground provides a quiet camping experience. The campground is on Buckeye Creek and is shaded by Jeffrey and Lodgepole pines. Hiking along Buckeye Creek into the nearby Hoover Wilderness. Hiking on Eagle Creek to the flanks of Eagle Mountain. Buckeye hot spring (140 degrees F) is just east of the campground. The spring comes out above the creek, over a rock overhang, which creates a cave-like area in the pool. Another small spring is upstream. This is a very popular spring year round. Fishing in Buckeye Creek offers different kind of fishing experience to get away from crowds.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65272', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65274', 'Sonora Bridge Campground', 'campground', 38.367400, -119.481800, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Sonora Bridge Campground offers opportunity to get away from crowds amidst shade of Jeffrey pines. Campground is close to fishing on West Walker River. The river is stocked with trout. Nearby picnic area, near Tule Lake, has accessible facilities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65274', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65276', 'Chris Flat Campground', 'campground', 38.394300, -119.456200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Chris Flat Campground is located in Walker Canyon which is a National Scenic Byway. The Walker River is known for fishing opportunities. The Walker River is stocked with trout.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65276', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65278', 'Leavitt Meadows Campground', 'campground', 38.337800, -119.554200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Leavitt Meadows Campground is nestled amidst Jeffrey Pines alongside the West Walker River. Nearby Leavitt Meadows Trailhead is the starting point for a horse or foot trail along the West Walker River into an area of lake-filled basins. Many climbers use this trail to approach Tower Peak, which offers both technical climbs and scrambles. A permit is required for overnight use of the West Walker River area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65278', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65280', 'Toquima Cave Campground', 'campground', 39.187700, -116.790500, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The big attraction here is, of course, the caves. The half-mile Cave trail begins in the campground, with a series of stone steps leading to the rock shelter site. The red, yellow, black and white images (pictographs) here were painted by ancient Shoshones. Projectile points found at this cave date to about 600-1300 CE. On nearby BLM land is Spencers Hot Springs. The water is 192 degrees, and there is a developed tub and a below-ground pool. 2 units NO group.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65280', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65282', 'Obsidian Campground', 'campground', 38.299900, -119.449200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Obsidian Campground offers opportunity to get away from crowds amidst shade of aspens and pines. Campground is close to Molybdenite Creek and Little Walker River. The river is stocked with trout. Area trailheads offer several interesting hikes. The trail from Molybdenite Creek trailhead splits, with one branch heading south into the Hoover Wilderness, and one looping north along Wheeler Creek to connect with the trail along the Little Walker River. This can be hiked as a loop from Burt Canyon trailhead (just west of campground). The Emma Lake trailhead leads to a short but steep hike to Emma…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65282', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65284', 'Desert Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.621390, -119.340000, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Desert Creek Campground is a remote camping experience in Nevada, located on Desert Creek. Partial shade provided in campground by Jeffrey and Lodgepole pines. Fishing in Desert Creek for stocked rainbow, brown and brook trout. ATV users can enjoy miles of backroads in this area. No trash Service -pack out your trash. Fishing, hiking, and off-highway vehicle opportunities. Four wheel drive not needed, but creek crossings not recommended in early or late summer season.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65284', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65286', 'Green Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.106600, -119.273300, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Green Creek Campground is located alongside Green Creek and is noted for excellent fishing opportunities. Aspens and pine trees provide good shade for campsites. Trailhead for the Hoover Wilderness. Trail leads to Green Lake, then south to a number of other alpine lakes. The trail continues on to Yosemite National Park.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65286', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6529', 'Denny Campground', 'campground', 40.933102, -123.393276, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Facility has 5 sites. Can accommodate up to a 22 foot trailer. No potable water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6529', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65292', 'Mahogany Grove Group Campground', 'campground', 36.313600, -115.618200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Access to North Loop Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65292', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6531', 'Hobo Gulch Campground', 'campground', 40.928960, -123.153329, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Facility has 10 sites available on a first-come, first-serve basis. Tent camping only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6531', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65312', 'Galena Creek Visitor Center', 'campground', 39.362800, -119.850600, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The Galena Creek Visitor Center is managed by Washoe County Regional Parks & Open Space under a special use permit from the U.S. Forest Service with a goal of increasing public understanding and appreciation of the many natural, cultural, historical, and recreational resources in the Galena Canyon area and the Mount Rose Scenic Byway. The Great Basin Institute is the interpretive association that operates the Visitor Center, providing staff and volunteers who greet the public, provide travel information, and offer a wide variety of nature-based programming for all ages. Additional highlights…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65312', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65390', 'South Ruby Campground', 'campground', 40.177900, -115.495700, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The campground is is situated above Ruby Lake below the beautiful Ruby Mountains at a 6,000'' elevation, near the Ruby Lake National Wildlife Refuge in Ruby Valley Nevada. Ruby Valley is a surprising wildlife oasis. An expansive marsh is laced with riparian corridors coursing with cool, spring fed waters. Together with lush meadow and shrub-steppe uplands, these habitats support a diversity of wildlife seldom found in the high desert and is one of the most important waterfowl nesting areas in the region. The refuge is either home or a stopover location for over 220 species of birds. Of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65390', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6540', 'Big Slide Campground', 'campground', 40.664584, -123.497489, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This facility has 8 (tent only) camping units and offers access to swimming, fishing and hiking. No potable water. Beach.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6540', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6543', 'Forest Glen Campground', 'campground', 40.377023, -123.326943, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This facility offers 15 camping units that can accommodate up to a 16 foot trailer. Swimming, fishing, hiking. Vault toilets and shade in most sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6543', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6545', 'Hell Gate Campground', 'campground', 40.370691, -123.313568, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Campground offers 17 camping units that can accommodate up to a 16 foot trailer. There is beach access, swimming, fishing, hiking and bird watching.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6545', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6551', 'Philpot Picnic Area', 'campground', 40.465966, -123.190829, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This facility has 6 picnic spots. There is no water system and it is unpaved access to the facility. The facility provides hiking access for the Philpot Interpretive Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6551', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6553', 'Scott Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.366072, -123.309188, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Campground offers 10 campsites that can accommodate up to a 20 foot trailer. Access to facility is unpaved and there is no water system. The trailhead for the South Fork National Recreation Trail is located at this facility. Swimming, fishing, hiking on the South Fork Trinity River National Recreation Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6553', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65534', 'Timber Creek Campground', 'campground', 39.404900, -114.629200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'There are 11 campsites, including five group sites and six RV sites. These sites also have picnic tables, campfire rings, and BBQ pedestals. At this campground, recreation activities include river/stream fishing, backpack/day hiking, horseback riding, off-highway vehicle riding, cross-country skiing, and snowshoeing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65534', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65536', 'Ward Mountain Campground', 'campground', 39.209200, -114.971200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'There are 33 campsites, including nine back-in and three pull-thru RV sites. These sites also have picnic tables, campfire rings, and BBQ pedestals. At this campground, recreation activities include mountain/road biking, backpack/day hiking, off-highway vehicle riding, cross-country skiing, and snowshoeing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65536', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6554', 'Slide Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.668600, -123.503500, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Slide Creek Campground is has 5 tent only camp units. There is no water system.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6554', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65570', 'Thomas Canyon Campground', 'campground', 40.647200, -115.406800, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Thomas Canyon Trail begins at the campground, leading past several waterfalls, through an alpine meadow into a glacial cirque.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65570', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6559', 'Basin Gulch Campground', 'campground', 40.352076, -122.958743, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located in a thickly wooded area within walking distance of Middle Fork Cottonwood Creek, this shady campground is perfect for tents and small trailers 20 feet or shorter. It is a great starting point for your adventures into the National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6559', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65592', 'Pine Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.838200, -115.429100, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', '.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65592', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6560', 'Beegum Gorge Campground', 'campground', 40.313783, -122.933356, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This tiny, tents only campground is located near Beegum Creek. Partially shaded, this is a great home base for your adventures! Be aware - there are vault toilets available, but no water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6560', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6561', 'Deerlick Springs Campground', 'campground', 40.470262, -122.925584, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This campground has 13 sites and vault toilets. Trailers are not recommended. There is no water so please bring enough for your trip.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6561', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65628', 'Big Bend Campground', 'campground', 41.763000, -115.701900, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Very popular with hunters during the hunting seasons. The mining town site of Gold Creek, within the Island Mountain Mining District, is 5 miles south of Big Bend on county road 745. Very little remains of the town as most of it was moved or torn down in the 1920s. A plaque at the town site contains additional information. In an aspen grove surrounded by wide open country, 15 miles northeast of Wildhorse Reservoir.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65628', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65636', 'Jack Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.519200, -116.058200, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Campground is situated in a beautiful, historic area. Sites are in an open cottonwood area. Please pack out all your trash. This campground can fill up during hunting season.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65636', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6564', 'Tomhead Saddle Campground', 'campground', 40.140534, -122.829149, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Some areas in and near the Yolla Bolly-Middle Eel Wilderness have been affected by recent wildfires; for more information, please call the Hayfork Ranger Station (530) 628-5227', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6564', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6565', 'White Rock Campground', 'campground', 40.253188, -123.022863, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'This small campground has 3 sites. There are no water or restroom facilities. Trailers are not recommended.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6565', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6571', 'Castle Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.235667, -122.379005, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : This small primitive campground is nestled in a thick mixed conifer forest approximately &frac14; mile below Castle Lake. There are 6 sites with tables, fire rings and vault toilets. Bring your own water. 3-night limit. No fee. No reservations. Not recommended for large vehicle or trailers. Usually opens around the end of June depending on when the snow melts, and usually is closed by snow around the first of November. Features : Visitors may walk or drive the short distance to the lake. Castle Lake is a pristine glacial cirque lake with granite cliffs and clear water, one of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6571', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6572', 'Gumboot Campground', 'campground', 41.213335, -122.509414, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : The area on the north side of this shallow alpine lake is open for camping from June to October, depending on snow. There are at least 6 undeveloped sites (no tables) with user-created fire rings and a vault toilet. Bring your own water or purify the lake water. Suitable for tents and mid-size RV''s or trailers. No fee. Usually opens around the end of May and closes due to snow by the first of November. Features : This is one of three alpine lakes on the district that can be reached by passenger car. The lake sits in a broad open bowl surrounded by grassy areas and mixed conifer…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6572', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65730', 'Wildhorse Crossing Campground', 'campground', 41.722600, -115.900100, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Adjacent to the Owyhee (Oh-WHY-HEE) River, a trout stream lined with willows and native brushes. Fishing for trout in river is available. Wildhorse Crossing is located in the Owyhee Canyon on the Mountain City Highway north of Wildhorse Reservoir (fishing!) and is right along the Owyhee River (fishing!) and lots of good opportunities for OHV recreation and many two track and dirt roads for mountain biking, hiking; has two double restrooms, 20 sites, no water, and is $5 per night.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65730', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65732', 'Angel Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.025700, -115.055100, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', '.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65732', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65736', 'Angel Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.025600, -115.085400, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'The campground is next to Angel Lake, and flanked by glacial cirques. Non motorized boating (canoeing) in Angel Lake, and fishing for rainbow, brook, and tiger trout. The Smith Lake Trailhead accesses the northern part of the East Humboldt Wilderness from campground, and another trailhead from just southeast of the campground heads south, to Winchell Lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65736', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6574', 'McBride Springs Campground', 'campground', 41.352624, -122.282008, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : Situated on the lower slopes of Mt. Shasta at an elevation of 5000 feet, this popular campground has 12 sites with tables and fire rings, suitable for tents and small RV''s. Vault toilets. 7 day limit. $10 per night. No reservations. Usually opens by Memorial Day weekend and closes near the end of October. Conveniently located on Mt. Shasta and only a few minutes from I-5, services and supplies. A miniature spring-fed seasonal creek flows through the campground, and a hand operated pump provides well water. Special note : In 2009 a root disease was discovered in the campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6574', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6576', 'Panther Meadows Campground', 'campground', 41.355014, -122.201808, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : This is a walk-in campground located near timberline on Mt. Shasta at 7500 feet. There are 15 sites, all within a short walk of your vehicle. Tables, fire-rings, and vault toilet. Bring your own water or purify the creek water nearby. 3 day limit, per person, per year. No fee. No reservations. Self-register on site. Usually opens around July 1st, depending on winter snowpack, and closes November 1st. Features : Highest campground on the mountain with open views and vistas. There are two small sub-alpine heather meadows a short distance from the campground. Because of the fragile…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6576', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6577', 'Sims Flat Campground', 'campground', 41.061803, -122.359367, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : This campground is located alongside the Sacramento River at an elevation of 1600 feet. There are 19 sites with tables and fire-rings. Suitable for tents and mid-sized RVs or trailers. Flush toilets; piped water. 14 day limit. $15 per night. No reservations. Usually opens by last Saturday in April and closes Nov. 15th. Features : Historic location of Civilian Conservation Corps camp in the 1930s. Interpretive signs depict the camp and suspension bridge spanning the river built by the CCC. World renown fishing on a classic trout stream. Train buffs enjoy watching Union Pacific…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6577', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6580', 'AhDiNa Campground', 'campground', 41.109858, -122.097207, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'AhDiNa Recreation Opportunity Guide Description: Located on the Lower McCloud River at an elevation of 2300 feet, this remote campground has 16 sites with tables and fire rings, flush toilets, and drinking water. The dirt access road from Lake McCloud is very rough and rocky. Low clearance vehicles, trailers, and RVs are not advised. 14 day limit. $10 per night. No reservations . Generally open May 01- November 1st. Features : This campground is situated on an historic site used by Native American tribes and various land owners over the years, including the families of Whittier, Fitzhugh, and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6580', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6581', 'Algoma Campground', 'campground', 41.256358, -121.883089, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Algoma Campground OPEN. Description : Located on the Upper McCloud River at an elevation of 3800 feet, this is a small undeveloped camping area with 8 user-created sites and a vault toilet. No drinking water. No fee. 15 day stay limit. Features : Algoma is the terminus of the McCloud River Trail, a distance of 15 miles from Lower Falls. This area receives less traffic than the more popular McCloud River Loop, offering a quieter riverside camping experience.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6581', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6582', 'Cattle Camp Campground', 'campground', 41.259370, -121.939652, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : At an elevation of 3700 feet, this is one of two developed campgrounds on the Upper McCloud River. There are 27 sites with tables and fire rings, vault toilets, and piped drinking water. Suitable for tents and larger RV''s or trailers. Double sites for large families or small groups. 14 day limit. $15 per night. No reservations. Features : The Upper McCloud River is one of the primary attractions in the area. In addition to swimming and fishing, there is 15 miles of river-side trail to explore. Cattle Camp Swimming Hole is a Day Use Area, no Camping. Please do not dam up the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6582', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6583', 'Fowlers Campground', 'campground', 41.244855, -122.023255, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'The most popular campground on the unit. Located on the Upper McCloud River at an elevation of 3400 feet, it has 39 sites with tables, fire-rings, vault toilets, and piped drinking water. Suitable for tents and mid-sized RV''s or trailers. 14 day limit. $15 per night. The CG has been converted mostly to a reservation system (see below) There are only eight sites that are first come first served. Features : This campground is situated near three waterfalls on the river, which adds to its popularity. The McCloud Falls vary in height from 15 to 50 feet. A river-side trail from the campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6583', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6585', 'Harris Spring Campground', 'campground', 41.456563, -121.784720, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : This is an undeveloped camping area located approximately 15 miles north of Highway 89. There are about 15 user-created sites and a vault toilet. Bring your own drinking water. No Fee. 15 day stay limit. Features : This is near the site of an historic guard station. The guard station, which is essentially a cabin, has been restored by the Forest Service, but is no longer part of the Lookouts and Cabins Rental Program. This camp is very popular with hunters in the fall hunting season.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6585', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6591', 'Trout Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.445281, -121.885576, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Description : Trout Creek is one of the few sizable creeks on the McCloud Flats, and is a popular undeveloped camping area. Vault toilets are provided, but there are no tables at these dispersed sites. Bring your own drinking water. There is no trash/garbage service. Please pack out your trash. 15 day stay limit. Features : In recent years, the Forest Service has partnered with other agencies and organizations to restore this area to its traditional habitat with improvements to the hydrology of the creek bed and propagation of native species. There is a protective perimeter fence to keep out…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=6591', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '65914', 'Centerville Flat Dispersed Campground', 'campground', 38.631372, -119.723082, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', '.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=65914', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6600', 'Bertha Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.751020, -149.254970, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'A small loop campground with 12 sites suitable for vehicle camping, small RV''s and tents, located at MP 65.4 of the Seward Highway. $19/night', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6600', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6602', 'Black Bear Campground', 'campground', 60.788611, -148.888611, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'This is a small loop campground with 12 sites suitable for vehicle camping (RVs not recommended) and tents. 12 sites. Vault toilet, hand driven water pump, dumpster, picnic tables, fire rings, bear lockers. Not included: running water, electricity, dump station, or wood. $19/night', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6602', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6603', 'Granite Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.723611, -149.293611, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'Reservations are made though Recreation.gov (1-877-444-6777) and recommended for summer camping. Fees are charged during the summer season. Reservations may be made up to180 days prior to your desired arrival date in the summer season (Memorial Day through Labor Day in September). A small loop campground with 18 sites (most sites are creekside) suitable for vehicle camping, RVs, and tents with 19 sites. Vault toilet, hand driven water pump, dumpster, picnic tables, fire rings, bear lockers. $19/night. A non-refundable service fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6603', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6604', 'Williwaw Campground', 'campground', 60.785556, -148.877500, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'During the off-season there is no water, no trash service, and no fees. Please pack out all garbage. Outhouse/toilet facilities may be unavailable. Reservations are made though Recreation.gov (1-877-444-6777) and recommended for summer camping. Fees are charged during the summer season. Reservations may be made up to180 days prior to your desired arrival date in the summer season (Memorial Day-Labor Day in September). Williwaw is the largest of the two campgrounds in Portage Valley. Located about 1 mile from the popular Begich, Boggs Visitor Center. 60 sites. Can accommodate RV''s. Restroom…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6604', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66050', 'Jackpine Flats Campground', 'campground', 47.685560, -115.646110, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Jackpine Flats campground is located 20 miles south of Trout Creek on Beaver Creek road 152. The campground has 1 site with table and fire ring. This campsite is best suited for tents or a pop up trailer as there is limited space to maneuver an RV. Amenities include a vault toilet. From Hwy 200 follow Beaver Creek road 152 for approximately 9 miles to the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66050', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66051', 'Marten Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.881940, -115.748060, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Marten Creek Campground is located approximately 9 miles north of Trout Creek. The campground has 6 developed sites (4 with shelters) tables and fire rings, and able to accommodate up to a 32'' rv. One of these sites is able to accommodate a group of up to 45 people and the larger shelter has 3 tables underneath the pavilion. Amenities include vault toilets, gravel roads throughout, developed boat launch and dock.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66051', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66081', 'North Shore Campground', 'campground', 47.860830, -115.632220, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The North Shore Campground is located about 4 miles north of Trout Creek off Hwy 200 on North Shore Road. The campground has 16 (3 pull thru''s) sites including one host site, with tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 40'' rv. Campground roads and campsite parking spurs are paved. Amenities include a campground host, potable water, vault toilets and a fully developed boat launch with dock and boat parking. There are 6 picnic sites with picnic tables (2 with covers) near the boat ramp for day use only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66081', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66082', 'Willow Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.870830, -115.310830, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Willow Creek Campground is approximately 19 miles northeast of Trout Creek on road 154. The campground has 6 sites all with tent pads, tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 40'' rv. Campground roads and parking spurs are gravel. Amenities include vault toilets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66082', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66083', 'Triangle Pond', 'campground', 48.020280, -115.840830, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Triangle Pond is located along the Noxon Reservoir and road 2229. This location is a day use site only. Amenities include vault toilets, picnic tables and fire rings, swimming area and beach. There is an undeveloped boat launch nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66083', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66105', 'McGregor Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.031940, -114.902220, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'McGregor Lake Campground is located approximately 53 miles southeast of Libby, Montana, on Highway 2 at the west end of McGregor Lake in Kootenai National Forest. This area is about halfway between Libby and Kalispell in the heart of the Thompson Chain of Lakes, a premier fishing and hunting area. Natural Features: At an elevation of 3,900 feet, the campground is nestled among young pines at the west end of McGregor Lake in the Fisher River Area. The lake spans 1,240 acres, making it the largest lake in the Kootenai National Forest. The Fisher River Area is the watershed formed by the four…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66105', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66106', 'Sylvan Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.915953, -115.279040, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Sylvan Lake Campground is located southeast of Libby on road 154. The campground has 5 sites with tables and fire rings. Campground roads and parking spurs are of native soil. Amenities include a vault toilet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66106', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66107', 'Howard Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.100944, -115.530667, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Howard Lake campground is located south of Libby on road 4779. The campground has 10 sites (3 pull thru''s) including one host site with tables and fire rings. Campground roads and parking spurs are gravel. Amenities include vault toilets and swimming beach. There are 2 day use sites with fire rings and picnic tables near the beach area. The camphost may close the gate to the campground each evening at 10:00 pm and open it again at 7:00 am. The gate closes for the season on December 1st and is opened again when access permits. Howard Lake and Howard Creek were prospected and named after the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=66107', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66155', 'Paragon Dispersed Camping Area', 'campground', 38.048442, -83.395377, null, 'Daniel Boone National Forest', 'Paragon is a primitive camping area with 10 designated campsites, some with lantern posts and fire rings. Chemical toilets and trash pickup available mid-April through November. This dispersed camping area is located on the Cumberland District , Daniel Boone National Forest. It is near Cave Run Lake , widely known for its scenic beauty and varied outdoor recreation opportunities.This 8,270-acre lake is jointly operated and managed by the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers and the U.S. Forest Service. Nearby facilities: Poppin Rock Boat Ramp .r9_alert_banner { background-color: #FFDD85;…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dbnf/recarea/?recid=66155', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66234', 'Moose Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.628420, -114.388920, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Moose Lake Campground has 3 designated campsite and a vault toilet. Drinking water is not provided. Fishing may be enjoyed in the lake. Moose Lake Campsite Moose Lake camp fire ring', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66234', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66250', 'Red Meadow Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.754300, -114.563730, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'At an elevation of 5,500 feet, Red Meadow Campground has 6 campsites near Red Meadow Lake. Bring your own drinking water, a vault toilet is available. Red Meadow Lake Campsite Food Storage', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66250', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66272', 'Tuchuck Campground', 'campground', 48.922730, -114.600440, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Campground has 7 campsites tucked high up and far away in the Whitefish Range. Several trailheads are within hiking and riding distance. Stock facilities are provided for equestrians (feed bunks, hitch rails, vault toilet, and load ramp) Tuchuck Campsite Tuchuck picnic table Food Storage', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66272', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66330', 'Devil Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.110540, -113.696120, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Devil Creek Campground, at 4360-feet elevation, is located 32 miles southeast of West Glacier, Montana, and six miles west of Marias Pass, a high mountain pass located in Glacier National Park. Natural Features: In the heart of the Rocky Mountains, west of the continental divide and just south of the Canadian border, lies the 2.4 million acre Flathead National Forest. Home to lynx, grizzly bear, and bull trout and with numerous lakes streams and rivers to enjoy, the forest is a premiere destination for visitors. The campground lies between East Glacier and West Glacier. Recreation:…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66330', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66336', 'Devil''s Corkscrew Campground', 'campground', 48.110540, -113.696120, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Located on the east side of the Hungry Horse Reservoir, 37 miles from Martin City, Mt. There are 4 campsites. Campsite Boat Access Reservoir view', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66336', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66340', 'Doris Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.305000, -113.981780, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Doris Creek Campground is located on the west side of Hungry Horse Reservoir, high in the Rocky Mountains, west of the Continental Divide and just south of the Canadian border. Spectacular views and ample opportunities for recreation surround the campground. Natural Features: The campground is situated along the massive Hungry Horse Reservoir, which was dammed to provide hydroelectric power and flood control to the area. It is the 10th highest dam in the United States and provides a stunning backdrop. Home to lynx, grizzly bear and bull trout, the forest is a premiere destination for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66340', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66358', 'Emery Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.333960, -113.949390, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Emery Bay Campground is located on the east shore of the Hungry Horse Reservoir off of Road 38. It sits high in the Rocky Mountains, less than 30 miles from the Continental Divide, and is surrounded by towering mountain peaks. Visitors can expect a variety of recreational activities, including fishing, boating, swimming, hiking, exploring and big game hunting. Natural Features: The campground is situated along the massive Hungry Horse Reservoir, which was dammed to provide hydroelectric power and flood control to the area. It is the 10th highest dam in the United States and provides…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66358', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6640', 'Coeur d''Alene Campground', 'campground', 60.849722, -149.533333, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'A small campground with six walk-in tent sites. This campground has limited services - water is not available. There are toilets, fire pits and tables. This site is not recommended for large RVs or trailers. Water is not available at this campground. There are toilets, fire pits, and tables at the site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6640', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66402', 'Lakeview Campground', 'campground', 48.218470, -113.805380, null, 'Flathead National Forest', '3600-foot elevation. 5 sites near the west shore of Hungry Horse Reservoir. Fishing for trout and whitefish in the reservoir; access at Lost Johnny Point boat ramp. Pack it in, pack it out. Lakeview campsite Campsite picnic area Campsite fire-ring', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66402', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6641', 'Cooper Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.483611, -149.886111, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'Large campground with 26 sites, including 3 tent sites. $23 (single)/$33 (double). A non-refundable service fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov Water, toilets, tables, fire pits, and dumpsters. ATTENTION: Campers Using Tents or Soft-sided Trailers Bears have damaged tents and soft-sided trailers within the Campground in the past. For your safety and the safety of others, please store all attractants - food, garbage, hygiene items, and anything with a smell - in a hard-sided vehicle or in the storage locker provided on site. Be aware and advised that bear incidents within…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6641', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66412', 'Lost Johnny Campground', 'campground', 48.306850, -113.969640, null, 'Flathead National Forest', '3600-foot elevation. 5 sites near the west shore of Hungry Horse Reservoir. Fishing for trout and whitefish in the reservoir; water skiing, sailing, and motor boating are also popular. For landlubbers, head 9 miles west into the exceptionally lovely Jewel Basin Hiking Area. Water and garbage services available at the nearby Lost Johnny Point.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66412', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66414', 'Lost Johnny Point Campground', 'campground', 48.310038, -113.963260, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Lost Johnny Point Campground is located at 3600-feet high in the Rocky Mountains, west of the Continental Divide and just south of the Canadian border. Spectacular views and ample opportunities for recreation surround the campground. Natural Features: The campground is situated on the west shore of Hungry Horse Reservoir, which was dammed to provide hydroelectric power and flood control to the area. It is the 10th highest dam in the United States and provides a stunning backdrop. Home to lynx, grizzly bear and bull trout, the forest is a premiere destination for visitors. Recreation:…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66414', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6642', 'Crescent Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.496474, -149.680232, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'During the off-season there is no water, no trash service, and no fees. Please pack out all garbage. Outhouse/toilet facilities may be unavailable. A small campground with 9 sites. $19 (single)/$33 (double)', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6642', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6643', 'Porcupine Campground', 'campground', 60.930663, -149.663254, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'There are 34 campsites $23/night. A non-refundable fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov The Gull Rock Trailhead is accessed from the Hope Highway on the signed road before the entrance to the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6643', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6644', 'Primrose Campground', 'campground', 60.340833, -149.369722, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'This campground includes 8 sites with no hookups. Water, toilets, tables, fire pits, dumpsters, and a boat ramp. This campground is located close to the Primrose Trailhead and is adjacent to Kenai Lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6644', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6645', 'Ptarmigan Campground', 'campground', 60.406111, -149.363333, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'This campground has 16 sites and no hookups. $19/night. A non-refundable service fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov Water, toilets, tables, fire pits, and dumpsters.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6645', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6646', 'Quartz Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.479167, -149.728889, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'During the off-season there is no water, no trash service, and no fees. Please pack out all garbage. Outhouse/toilet facilities may be unavailable. Access to the Boat Launch and Kenai Lake public access are open year-round. Snow plowing is intermittent as weather and road conditions allow. Reservations are made though Recreation.gov (1-877-444-6777) and recommended for summer camping. Fees are charged during the summer season. Reservations may be made up to180 days prior to your desired arrival date in the summer season (Memorial Day through Labor Day in September). This campground has 45…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6646', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6647', 'Russian River Campground', 'campground', 60.482215, -149.971405, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'The Russian River Campground area is closed to all public vehicle and pedestrian traffic. The closure is necessary for public safety due to construction involving extensive heavy machinery use. The campground is scheduled to remain closed until June 3, 2025. A large campground with 83 sites, paved roads and spurs, and no hookups. $23 (single)/$33 (double). A non-refundable service fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov. Amenities include - water, flush toilets, tables, fire pits and dumpsters. ATTENTION: Campers Using Tents or Soft-sided Trailers - Be Bear Aware Bears have…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6647', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6648', 'Tenderfoot Creek Campground', 'campground', 60.636111, -149.497500, null, 'Chugach National Forest', 'Reservations are made though Recreation.gov (1-877-444-6777) and recommended for summer camping. Fees are charged during the summer season. Reservations may be made up to180 days prior to your desired arrival date in the summer season (Memorial Day through Labor Day in September). This campground has 35 sites and no hookups. Water, toilets, tables, dumpsters, fire pits, boat ramp. $23 a night. A non-refundable service fee will be added to each reservation by Recreation.gov', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/chugach/recarea/?recid=6648', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66514', 'Beaver Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.923948, -113.372898, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'This is a free campground located 63 miles south of the town of Hungry Horse on the gravel East Side Reservoir Road #38. The campground is located at an elevation of 4,200 feet and is open from May 15 through November 30. Beaver Creek Campground is situated next to Spotted Bear River just off the Spotted Bear River Road #568. The 4 unit campground is set back from the road and the campsites are less than 100 feet to the river. The site is located in an old growth stand of trees. It is a moderate use site that usually has open campsites during the middle of the week. It often is used as a base…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66514', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66768', 'Peter''s Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.057559, -113.643774, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'This is a free campground located 42 miles south of the town of Hungry Horse on the gravel East Side Reservoir Road #38. The campground is located at an elevation of 3,600 feet and is maintained from May 15 through September 30. Peters Creek Campground is situated next to the Hungry Horse Reservoir just off the East Side Reservoir Road #38. The 6 unit campground is set back from the road and the campsites are less than 100 feet to the reservoir. The site is located in a second growth stand of trees. It is a low use site that usually has open campsites. It often is used as a base for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66768', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66838', 'Spotted Bear Campground', 'campground', 47.927260, -113.525980, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'This is a fee campground for $13 per night/$5 per extra vehicle (no fee 9/30 - 5/15) located 55 miles south of the town of Hungry Horse on the gravel East Side Reservoir Road #38. The campground is located at an elevation of 3,800 feet and is maintained from May 15 through September 30. Spotted Bear Campground is situated next to the Spotted Bear and South Fork Flathead Rivers just off the East Side Reservoir Road #38. The 13 unit campground is set back from the road and most of the campsites are located above the river. The site is located in a second growth stand of trees. It is a high use…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66838', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '66996', 'Holland Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.441130, -113.608480, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview The Holland Lake Campground and Group Site are located on the shores of Holland Lake in the Swan Valley of northwest Montana. Holland Lake Campground is a great place to enjoy the Flathead National Forest. It offers clean campsites with great lake access and ample opportunities for hiking on the scenic Holland Falls National Recreation Trail. Natural Features: At an elevation of 4,050 feet, the campground sits among tamarack, ponderosa pine and Douglas fir trees. There are some sites close to the 416-acre lake; others are further back or higher on the bank. A variety of wildlife make…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=66996', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67016', 'Lindbergh Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.407153, -113.721057, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Lindbergh Lake Campground has 25 designated campsites. Restrooms, fire rings, and food storage boxes are available. Drinking water is not provided; please bring your own source of water. This campground is wheelchair accessible. Fishing, swimming, and boating may be enjoyed on the lake. The maximum recommended trailer length for this area is 20 feet. Please pack out what you pack in-- no trash service is provided. There is a trail from the campground which leads part of the way around the west side of the lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67016', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67054', 'Swan Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.936420, -113.848240, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview This recreation area is located near the village of Swan Lake at the north end of the scenic Swan Valley in northwest Montana, about 17 miles southeast of Big Fork. The campground consists of two loops. Ponderosa Loop offers open, large sites with plenty of space, while sites at Birch Loop are shaded and more clustered together. There is also a reservable group site which accommodates up to 100 people. Natural Features: In the heart of the Rocky Mountains lies the 2.4 million acre Flathead National Forest. Home to lynx, grizzly bear, and bull trout, with numerous lakes, streams and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67054', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67072', 'Ashley Lake North Campground', 'campground', 48.208310, -114.623750, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Ashley Lake North Campground has 6 campsites and a host site. There are picnic tables, fire rings, and SST vault toilet and an informational bulletin board. Stay limit is 5 days.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67074', 'Ashley Lake South Campground', 'campground', 48.212210, -114.568970, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'This is a very small campground with 2 sites, a vault toilet, picnic tables and fire rings. There is a walk down boat launching site for kayaks and canoes. Access road has sharp hairpin corner so RVs are not recommended. Stay limit is 5 days.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67074', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67118', 'Upper Stillwater Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.603220, -114.656840, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Upper Stillwater Lake Campground has 5 designated campsites, restroom, gravel boat launch, and day parking. The area has several hiking trails near by and the Stillwater River borders the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67118', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67122', 'Sylvia Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.344798, -114.818157, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Sylvia Lake Campground has 3 designated campsites. Each site has a picnic table, firering and a vault toilet in the campground. There is a small boat ramp for fishing boats, canoes and kakaks. The lake has native grayling and cuttroat trout.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67122', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67130', 'Tally Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.414320, -114.586130, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Tally Lake Campground is located on the northern shores of its namesake lake, west of Whitefish, Montana. The campground is popular with locals and tourists visiting the Flathead National Forest and offers a variety of recreation facilities and activities for the whole family. Natural Features: The campground is nestled in the highlands of northwestern Montana, adjacent to Tally Lake, the second deepest Lake in Montana 445 feet deep. It sits in a mature forest of Western Larch and Douglas fir trees. Recreation: Hiking, horseback riding and biking trails wind around the Tally Lake…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=67130', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67165', 'White Spar Campground', 'campground', 34.506170, -112.477680, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'White Spar Campground at 5,641 feet in elevation is a short drive of 2.7 miles south of downtown Prescott and east of Hwy 89. Campers will appreciate the mild weather and the cool ponderosa pine forest the campground is nestled in. The campground''s convenient location allows for many opportunities for pursuing recreational activities in the area. Activities include camping, hiking, mountain biking and bird watching. Several connector and loop trails in the area allow for multiple modes of travel. The Tri-City Community comprising Prescott, Chino Valley, and Prescott Valley has events,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67165', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67167', 'Lower Wolf Creek Campground', 'campground', 34.454579, -112.459746, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'Located on the banks of Wolf Creek, Arizona walnut and live-oaks are interspersed among the ponderosa pines in this boulder-strewn campground that was constructed by the Civilian Conservation Corps in the late 1930s. View photos on Flickr Facilities 20 campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings with grills No drinking water Vault toilets Garbage service', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67167', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67171', 'Hazlett Hollow Campground', 'campground', 34.170072, -112.285409, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'This is a relatively small, semi-primitive campground in the southern end of the Bradshaw Mountains in the Horsethief Basin Area. Ponderosa pine is the dominant vegetation type in the area. One of the most attractive and well-developed campgrounds in the southern Bradshaws. Most of the walls and walks throughout the campground were built of stone during the 1930s by the Civil Conservation Corp (CCC). This site may close early or open late, depending on snowfall. History of Hazlett Hollow Campground , researched and compiled by AARCHER, Inc. (1,523 KB PDF) View photos on Flickr Facilities 15…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67171', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67173', 'Mingus Mountain Campground', 'campground', 34.692561, -112.120523, null, 'Prescott National Forest', '***ALERT: Mingus Mountain Campground Electricity Outage!*** Mingus Mountain Campground currently has no electricity due to lightning damage. Prescott National Forest, Verde Ranger District, will continue to work to get the electricity restored. At this point, February of 2024, there is no specific date when we expect to have electricity in the campground restored. We will continue to pursue funding to help repair the electrical issues and apologize for any inconvenience. If you have questions please call the Verde Ranger Station at (928) 567-4121. Site Description: Located in the cool pines…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67173', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67175', 'Potato Patch Campground', 'campground', 34.709387, -112.153723, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'Located in the Mingus Mountain Area in ponderosa pine forest, this campground offers cool summertime temperatures and fairly easy access via a paved and winding mountain road. Nearby are Woodchute Wilderness, Woodchute Trail #102 , and the historic mining town of Jerome lies 8 miles northeast on U.S. Highway 89A. Mingus Mountain Brochure (1.86 MB) NOTE- Brochure Correction: Mingus Mountain Campground and Picnic Site do not have electricity available at this time. View photos on Flickr Facilities 28 campsites with picnic tables, grills, and fire pits (A-Loop) 3 accessible campsites and 2…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67175', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67179', 'Powell Springs Campground', 'campground', 34.578060, -112.067650, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'A historic campground built by the CCC, Powell Springs is flanked by Hackberry Wash, a seasonal creek. Ponderosa pines provide shade in the campground, and riparian vegetation grows along the wash. View photos on Flickr Note: This site closes following especially heavy rain or snow, and when the roads are too icy. If you plan to visit and want to make sure it is open, please contact the Verde Ranger Station: 928-567-4121. When the office is closed, please check the right-hand column under "Alerts and Warnings" to see if there are weather-related closures, and follow the link to see if this…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67179', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67181', 'Lynx Campground', 'campground', 34.516646, -112.388001, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'Located in the Lynx Lake Recreation Area. Lynx Lake is one of the most popular recreation spots in central Arizona on the Bradshaw Ranger District. More than 90,000 people visit each year! Mild weather, the cool ponderosa pine forest, a serene 55-acre lake, trout fishing, boating, hiking, mountain biking, horseback riding, gold panning, archaeological sites, and bird watching attract visitors from throughout Arizona, and bring them back again and again. Lynx Lake Recreation Area Brochure (1,020 KB) View photos on Flickr Facilities 35 campsites with picnic table, fire rings, and grills 4…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67181', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67183', 'Hilltop Campground', 'campground', 34.510991, -112.380488, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'Located in the Lynx Lake Recreation Area. This campground is located in the ponderosa pine forest about 0.5 mile directly south of Lynx Lake. The campsites provided are generally large enough to accommodate most recreational vehicles under 40 feet in length. A host is available to provide information and assist visitors to locate a suitable camping site. Lynx Lake Recreation Area Brochure (1,020 KB) Map of Hilltop Campground (168 KB JPG) View photos on Flickr Facilities 38 campsites with picnic tables, and grills Drinking water 5 vault toilets Garbage service RVs: Maximum vehicle length 40''…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67183', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67185', 'Yavapai Campground', 'campground', 34.602437, -112.540492, null, 'Prescott National Forest', 'This 22-site campground is located in the Granite Basin Recreation Area amidst granite boulders in mixed pinyon-juniper and ponderosa pines. It is convenient to Granite Basin Lake, Granite Mountain Wilderness, and five day-use sites with picnic facilities and trail access. Yavapai Campground photos on Flickr Granite Basin Recreation Area Brochure (1.54 MB) Note: This site closes following especially heavy snow and when the roads are too icy. If you plan to visit and want to make sure it is open, please contact the Bradshaw Ranger Station: 928-443-8000. When the office is closed, please check…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/prescott/recarea/?recid=67185', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6765', 'Outlet at Priest Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.498834, -116.893287, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Outlet campground is located on the southwest shore of Priest Lake near the headwaters of Priest River. Campers come to Outlet for sunshine, fishing, boating, kayaking, and the breathtaking views of the rugged Selkirk Mountains of the Idaho Panhandle National Forests. Natural Features: Outlet campground is situated at an elevation of 2,500 feet on Priest Lake. The lake is one of three largest and most beautiful lakes in the Idaho Panhandle, and reaches 300 feet in depth and covers 25,000 acres. The world''s largest Mackinaw trout was caught here in 1963. Upper Priest Lake is part of the Upper…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6765', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6766', 'Osprey Campground', 'campground', 48.505892, -116.887757, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Campers come to Osprey for sunshine and boating at Priest Lake, and for breathtaking views of the rugged Selkirk Mountains. Fishing is also a big draw, with trout just waiting to be caught. While here, watch for moose, grizzly and black bears, wolves, mountain lions and deer. Osprey, as inferred by the campground name, also inhabit the area. Natural Features: Osprey Campground is perched on the lower western shore of Priest Lake near Outlet Bay. The beautiful 25,000-acre lake is fed by springs trickling down from the Selkirks. The clear, blue lake reaches 300 feet in depth. Recreation :…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6766', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6767', 'Luby Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.549612, -116.923834, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Luby Bay Campground is located near both Lamb Creek and Priest Lake. The campground is densely wooded with nicely secluded sites, and is within easy access to many great views of the Selkirk Mountains. Natural Features: The campground sits at an elevation of 2,500 feet on the western shores of Priest Lake. Campsites are shaded by hemlock and cedar. Priest Lake consists of the main lake where most water recreation takes place. To the north, the lake connects via a narrow channel with Upper Priest Lake. Recreation : Visitors enjoy kayaking, canoeing and power boating up the 3.5-mile…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6767', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6769', 'Reeder Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.625396, -116.894291, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Reeder Bay Campground is a picturesque hideaway for nature immersion and relaxing water sports on Priest Lake. Campsites are shaded by a dense forest of cedar, fir and hemlock. Campers visit Reeder for its incredible beach that slopes down into the refreshing, clear lake. Natural Features : The campground is situated on the western shore of Priest Lake, nestled deep below the crest of the Selkirk Mountains. The lake spans 19 miles in length and reaches a depth of 300 feet. Priest Lake is noteworthy for its incredibly clear waters, fed by streams cascading from the high Selkirk peaks. A…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6769', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6770', 'Beaver Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.735900, -116.860300, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Beaver Creek Campground sits in the Idaho Panhandle National Forests, offering phenomenal views of the Selkirk Mountains across the reflective waters of Priest Lake. Natural Features: The campground is situated on the northwest shore of Priest Lake at an elevation of 2,500 feet, shaded by hemlock and cedar. Priest Lake consists of the main lake, where most water recreation takes place, and the smaller Upper Priest Lake to the north. The two lakes are divided by a narrow channel. Recreation : A local beach is easily accessible for swimming and boating. Visitors enjoy kayaking, canoeing or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6770', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6772', 'Kalispell Island Group Site and other Campgrounds', 'campground', 48.567038, -116.899431, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Kalispell Island Group Site is located on the southeast side of Kalispell Island on Priest Lake. The rustic campsite is part of the Three Pines camping area at site #29. The island, reached only by boat, faces the beautiful Selkirk Mountains. Other Camping: West Shores - 7 camp units, west side of island (vault toilet). Peninsula - 2 camp units, south west side of island (portable toilet required). Schneider - 5 camp units, south west end of island (vault toilet). Silver - 8 camp units, south end of island (vault toilet). Silver Cove - 3 camp units, south end of island (vault toilet). Selkirk…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6772', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6773', 'Bartoo Island Group Site/Campgrounds', 'campground', 48.543949, -116.878938, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Bartoo Island Group Site: This group campsite, also known as Sunrise Group Site, is a rustic group camping area on Bartoo Island, only reachable by boat. Surrounded by the clear waters of Priest Lake, Bartoo Island Group site provides the ideal getaway for groups of 10 to 30 people, looking for a rugged, but highly rewarding camping experience on the peaceful shores of Priest Lake. Natural Features: Priest Lake spans 25,000-acres of incredible beauty, fed primarily by the waters of the Priest River. Named after the historical presence of Jesuit priests who settled in the lake area in the mid…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6773', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6774', 'Plowboy Campground', 'campground', 48.768920, -116.877280, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Plowboy Campground is loacted on the southwest shores of Upper Priest Lake, with majestic views of the Selkirk Crest. Five campsites are furnished with fire rings, picnic tables, and bear-proof storage boxes. Plowboy is easily accessed by boat or by the Navigation Trail. Please note that this campground has a Pack It In, Pack It Out policy on all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6774', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6775', 'Navigation Campground', 'campground', 48.794900, -116.910560, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Navigation Campground is located on the northwest shores of Upper Priest Lake, with majestic views of the Selkirk Crest. Four campsites are furnished with fire rings, picnic tables, and bear-proof storage boxes. Please note that this site has a Pack It In, Pack It Out policy on all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6775', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6776', 'Trapper Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.797780, -116.890690, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Trapper Creek Campground is located on the northeast shore of Upper Priest Lake. It has five sites with beautiful views of Plowboy Mountain, all furnished with fire rings, picnic tables, and bear-proof storage boxes. Please note that this campground has a Pack It In, Pack It Out policy on all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6776', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6777', 'Geisinger Campground', 'campground', 48.770080, -116.863262, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Geisinger Campground is located at the entrance to Upper Priest Lake. It has three sites at the confluence with The Thorofare, all furnished with fire ring, picnic tables, and bear-proof storage boxes. Please note that this campground has a Pack it In, Pack It Out policy on all garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6777', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67820', 'Browns Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.436164, -117.196351, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Newport Ranger District, Browns Lake Campground lies 25 miles northeast of Newport. This lake is nonmotorized, flyfishing only. Located within the campground is a historical cabin believed to have been built by the Civilian Conservation Corps. The trailhead for Browns Lake Trail #320 is located near the boat ramp. Browns Lake Browns Lake Trail #320 Logging in the area may impact accessability.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67820', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67824', 'Edgewater Campground', 'campground', 48.754167, -117.405278, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Situated along the banks of the Pend Oreille River. Popular activities include boating and fishing. Day use area with great river views. Boat launch available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67824', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67834', 'Panhandle Campground', 'campground', 48.510015, -117.271578, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is located 30 miles north of Newport (15 miles north of Usk) adjacent to LeClerc Road (County Road #9325). This small campground, lies next to the Pend Oreille River and is suitable for both tent and RV camping with large RV''s. Most campsites are private and are in walking distance of the river.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67834', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67836', 'Pioneer Park Campground', 'campground', 48.214170, -117.053610, null, 'Colville National Forest', '*Pioneer Boat Launch is open, though erosion damage may make launching difficult. Use at you own risk. (6/21/2023)* Pioneer Park Campground is located in northeast Washington on the Pend Oreille River. Visitors enjoy hiking, fishing, boating and swimming. The campground''s proximity to the city of Newport provides urban entertainment opportunities as well.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67836', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67840', 'South Skookum Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.391667, -117.182778, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'South Skookum Lake is relatively small and is not suitable for boats exceeding 20 feet. The boat ramp is small and unimproved. Two docks, one of which is accessible, are located near the launch area and provide fishing opportunities for campers who do not have boats. South Baldy lookout, which is still staffed during the summer months, is visible from the campground and is a popular day trip.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67840', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67856', 'Deer Creek Forest Camp', 'campground', 48.864722, -118.395000, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Nearby trails are Taylor Ridge Trail #74 and Kettle Crest North Trail #13 . This high elevation fee campground was burned over during the Stickpin fire of 2015. The site has been reconstructed and has numerous young trees including Douglas fir, ponderosa pine, lodgepole pine and aspen. Understory grass, shrubs, and wildflowers are well established. The campground includes a mix of back-in and pull-through campsites and will also offer horse corrals as of late June, 2024. The campground is located on the designated route of the Pacific Northwest National Scenic Trail, is across the street from…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67856', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67866', 'Ferry Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.522778, -118.809722, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Ferry Lake Campground is a 9-unit fee campground located off the beaten path, but easily accessible campground that offers tranquil camping and good lake fishing. Each campsite has a parking spur, table, and fire ring. The campground has a mix of nice tent sites, camper/van sites, and small motorhome/trailer sites. Large RVs are not recommended due to the size of the turn-around at the end of the campground road. There are two outhouses and a boat launch for small watercraft. With its handful of small shaded campsites and a ban on internal combustion engines, the lake is quiet enough to hear…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67866', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67878', 'Long Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.500833, -118.809722, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Long lake has well shaded level campsites that can accommodate anything from tents to larger RVs and trailers. The entrance road is a bit narrow and rough along the eastern shoreline of Fish Lake, so larger RV''s should use caution. Amenities include an old fashion hand pump well that provides the campground with potable water, flat parking spurs, tables, fire grills, and two outhouses. Long Lake is a beautiful, clear, fly fishing only lake that is stocked with cutthroat trout. Internal combustion engines are prohibited. Beautiful views of the 12.8 acre lake can be seen from the 1.5 mile trail…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67878', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67900', 'Swan Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.512778, -118.833611, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Swan Lake Campground is located in a beautiful mixed pine setting approximately 14 miles south and west of Republic, Washington. Access to the campground is via State Route 21 and paved Forest Road 53 (Scatter Creek). The campground 26 campsites with a mix of back-in and pull-through sites that will accommodate everything from the smallest tent to the largest RV. The lakeshore loop will accommodate up to moderate size trailers and RVs and all provide lakeshore views. The non-lakeshore loop include all of the campground''s pull-through sites. Each site is accessed by a paved road, but most…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67900', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67904', 'Ten Mile Campground', 'campground', 48.518056, -118.736944, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Ten Mile Campground includes five campsites in a shady, mixed pine setting. Ten mile creek cuts through the middle of the campground and generally flows from April through June or early July. Each campsite has a level parking spur, table, and fire ring. The campground has a single outhouse and no water or garbage service. The campground is located along State Highway 21 and is located 10 miles south of Republic, Washington. Access to the Sanpoil River for fishing and water play is a short walk across Highway 21 through the day-use picnic area. Ten Mile Trail #25 takes off from the campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67904', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67920', 'East Sullivan Campground', 'campground', 48.838611, -117.279722, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is located on the north end of beautiful Sullivan Lake and offers many recreational opportunities. Campsites are suitable for both tent and RV camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67920', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67936', 'Mill Pond Campground', 'campground', 48.854167, -117.290556, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This lies along Sullivan Creek and offers great opportunities for hiking on a looped trail system and connects to Mill Pond Historic Site. The Sullivan Creek Trail #565 connects the campground with the Mill Pond Flume Trail #520 , Floodplain Trail #523, Elk Creek Trail #560 , and Mill Pond Historic Site .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67936', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67946', 'Noisy Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.790556, -117.282222, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Though the campground is closed for the season, as is the boat launch. Within walking distance to the lake, the campsites in this campground are nice and private. Noisy Creek Trail #588 can be accessed from the campground and the lake provides many wildlife viewing and recreational opportunities. Campsites are suitable for both tent and RV camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67946', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67970', 'West Sullivan Campground', 'campground', 48.839167, -117.284444, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'West Sullivan Campground is located at the north end of beautiful Sullivan Lake. It is suitable for tent, trailers, and small RV''s. Campsites are near the lake. The day use area has picnic spots.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67970', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67976', 'Big Meadow Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.729551, -117.563452, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is equipped with tent/trailer sites, interpretive trails, boat launch, and a nice fishing dock. Some campsites are private and some with a lake view. This campground is good for wildlife viewing especially around the lake. A short paved walk out to a lookout viewing platform affords great views of the lake. Nearby is the Hess Homestead Cabin which is day use only, first come first serve.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67976', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67978', 'Canyon Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.577500, -118.239722, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This pack it in/pack it out campground is a single large circular loop .25 miles from the highway on a dirt road with minimal traffic noise. A few campsites are adjacent to canyon creek which is hidden from view. Convenient for overnight campers it is also a nice location for a few days of relaxed camping. A one mile paved walking trail with three benches traverses along Sherman Creek between the campground and the Sherman Pass Log Flume Heritage Site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67978', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6798', 'Sam Owen Campground', 'campground', 48.219620, -116.286290, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Sam Owen Campground is nestled on the banks of Lake Pend Oreille in an open forest of pine and cedar. Popular activities include hiking, canoeing, swimming, boating, wildlife and bird watching. Natural Features: Sam Owen Campground is situated on a peninsula on the east side of Lake Pend Oreille in the Idaho Panhandle National Forest, at an elevation of 2,000 feet. The lake spans 82,088 acres and has 125 miles of shoreline. The well-loved campground shares a peninsula with the Sam Owen Game Preserve, which provides plenty of opportunities to see wildlife up close. Deer are very easy to spot,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6798', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67980', 'Davis Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.739167, -118.227778, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This small rustic campground provides beautiful views of Davis Lake from each campsite. There is a single lane dirt road which serves as access to the campsites and the small boat launch. Boating is noncombustible motors only and the cutthroat trout fishing is fantastic. In addition there is a 1.2 mile hiking trail # 92 will take you around Davis lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67980', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67986', 'Gillette Campground', 'campground', 48.612500, -117.534167, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'The campsites are nice and big but not private. A covered area with a large tree trunk is an interesting attraction along with access to Rufus and Springboard Trails. Gillette Lake is in walking distance. The Springboard Trail #149 leaves from this campground. The campground and much of the surrounding area is open to licensed OHV use.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67986', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6799', 'Green Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.178042, -116.408599, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'This campground is closed for the summer of 2024 for a complete renovation Green Bay Campground features 11 designated sites with picnic tables and fire rings, vault toilets, and a swimming beach.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6799', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67992', 'Jungle Hill Horse Campground', 'campground', 48.635100, -118.451080, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Jungle Hill is a spacious camping area which offers pack; saddle amenities and access to the 44.6 mile Kettle Crest National Scenic Trail . Non-potable water is located in a nearby creek just a short distance from the campground. A mixture of lodgepole pine, western larch and Douglas fir provides shade and privacy is very good between campsites. Take Sherman Pass Scenic Byway, HWY 20 and turn onto Albian Hill Rd. You will procceed up a steep and windy gravel road for 2 miles to get to the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67992', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '67998', 'Kettle Crest Trailhead (Sherman Pass)', 'campground', 48.608690, -118.475980, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This multiple-use trailhead found on Sherman Pass provides summer and winter access to the Kettle Crest National Recreation Trail (Kettle Crest Trail #13 North and South) and the Pacific Northwest National Scenic Trail. The trailhead includes an outhouse, information board with trail maps, trail user registration boxes, and parking that will accommodate 15-20 vehicles and 5-7 vehicles with trailers. The upper parking is available for passenger vehicles and the lower parking area is for trucks, RVs, and horse trailers. Camping at the trailhead is discouraged. No campfires are allowed. Sherman…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=67998', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6800', 'Maiden Rock Campground', 'campground', 48.099180, -116.510040, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Maiden Rock Picnic Ground is accessible by boat only. It features 4 picnic units, fire rings, a vault toilet, and a swimming beach.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6800', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68004', 'Lake Ellen East Campground', 'campground', 48.502222, -118.246111, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Lake Ellen East Campground is one of two campgrounds located on each end of the 75.5 acre Lake. Access through the campground is a one way, single lane gravel road loop. Campsites have good separation with lots of vegetation for privacy. Access to the lake for fishing and swimming is a short walk. Wildlife viewing is abundant with bald eagles, osprey, loons, beaver and more. This is a popular lake for families with small children because of the large availability for fishing off the bank. Fishing for rainbow trout is good. Many amateur photographers also enjoy the area for its picturesque…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68004', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68006', 'Lake Ellen West Campground', 'campground', 48.496389, -118.263333, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Lake Ellen West Campground is one of two campgrounds located on each end of the 75.5 acre lake. Access to the campground and the boat launch is a single lane gravel road. Campsites have good separation for privacy. There is a boat dock on site and fishing for rainbow trout is good. Wildlife viewing is abundant with bald eagles, osprey, loons, beaver and more. This is a popular lake for families with small children because of the large availability for fishing off the bank. Many amateur photographers also enjoy the area and its picturesque opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68006', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68008', 'Lake Gillette Campground', 'campground', 48.612500, -117.538611, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Camping sites are nice and spacious and close to facilities. Some are very private and others closer together, some have a view of the lake. Day use for trails and beach area are nice with picnic areas and lots of parking. Access to Rufus Trail #148 is near this campground. An amphitheatre is also close and can be reached by one of the many trails. This is a great family campground with plenty of things to do.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68008', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6801', 'Whiskey Rock Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.051205, -116.453859, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Whiskey Rock Bay Campground features 9 camp units with 3 sites on lake. In addition there are 4 picnic sites with fire rings, vault toilets, a dock, and a swimming beach.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6801', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68010', 'Lake Leo Campground', 'campground', 48.649167, -117.496667, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Campsites are nice; some are private with lake views and others closer together.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68010', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68012', 'Lake Thomas Campground', 'campground', 48.623360, -117.535460, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Most sites are tent sites, private and have a view of the lake. This campground is located on a small hillside and overlooks Lake Thomas. Access to Rufus Trail #148 is near this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68012', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68018', 'Little Twin Lakes Campground', 'campground', 48.576410, -117.645630, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Camping sites are big and provide privacy from others. It''s very private and great for wildlife viewing. The day use site is a wildlife viewing areas with a great view.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68018', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68026', 'Old Stage Horse Camp', 'campground', 48.729010, -118.522040, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This is designed as a horse camp. There is a creek for watering your horses. Old Stage Trail #1 head leaves from this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68026', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68032', 'Pierre Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.904444, -118.139444, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'There is one entrance and two ends to Pierre Campground. The north end has six sites for smaller campers. The south end has nine sites and a tight J hook turn around most of these are set up for pick-up campers and tents. 175 foot fishing dock.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68032', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68040', 'Sherman Overlook Campground', 'campground', 48.605000, -118.462778, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This Campground is equipped with picnic areas and 9 tent/trailer sites. Bathrooms are available. Some campsites are private. Connects to the Kettle Crest via the Sherman Pass Tie Trail #96. The campground also provides access to Sherman Overlook Trail #96.A. This is a short paved ADA accessible interpretive trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68040', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68060', 'Trout Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.624381, -118.240521, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This small campground has private tent sites close to the lake with access to a fishing dock. There is a small boat launch and the lake is noncombustible motors only. The campground also hosts the Hoodoo Canyon Trail #17 Trail Head. This is a 4.7-mile hiking trail that also intersects the Emerald Lake #94 hiking trail. Wildlife has been seen frequently at the lake which includes moose and whitetail deer. This area is frequently used by fishermen, hikers, and hunters.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68060', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '68064', 'Wapaloosie Horse Campground', 'campground', 48.663666, -118.439763, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Wapaloosie is a small campground with a circular drive and two pull-thru campsites for trucks with trailers. It is a wonderful (circle the wagons) experience for Pack and Saddle enthusiasts. Amenities such as hitching posts, hayfeeder and a nearby creek make it a destination for equestrian use. The Wapaloosie Trail #15 is a short 2.7 mile ride/hike to access the 44.6 mile Kettle Crest National Scenic Trail. This area and its trails offer panoramic views of the surrounding mountains, abundant wildlife, wildflowers, incredible sunrises and sunsets. This multiple use recreation area also brings…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=68064', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6821', 'Robinson Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.971100, -116.217100, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Robinson Lake Campground features 10 camp units (3 accessible), potable water, handicap accessible vault toilets, a boat ramp, and a day use area with 2 picnic units', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6821', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6822', 'Copper Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.984618, -116.168349, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Copper Creek Campground features 16 camp units (3 accessible), potable water, accessible vault toilets, and a scenic location on the Moyie River. Beautiful Copper Falls viewpoint trail is 1.5 miles east on Copper Falls Road #2517 and there is fishing access to the Moyie River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6822', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6823', 'Meadow Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.819870, -116.147330, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Meadow Creek Campground features 22 camp units, potable water, vault toilets, and access to the scenic Moyie River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6823', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6824', 'Smith Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.778780, -116.264000, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Smith Lake Campground features 7 camp units, potable water, vault toilets, a boat ramp, and a day use area with 3 picnic units.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6824', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6825', 'Solomon Lake Fishing', 'campground', 48.796221, -116.101838, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Solomon Lake offers a developed site in a remote area, with moderate road access. Solomon Lake is locally popular and receives heavy use. Facilities are best suited for single families or groups with a focus on day use. Camping and large group use are common, in addition to short term fishing and picnicking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6825', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6842', 'Mokins Bay Campground', 'campground', 47.784440, -116.665560, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Mokins Bay Campground is located near the eastern shore of Hayden Lake in northwest Idaho. Located in the northwest portion of the Bitterroot Mountain range, known as the Coeur d'' Alene mountains, this campground offers visitors solitude in a forested setting. Natural Features: The small campground is surrounded by a heavy canopy of pines. Wildflowers like trillium and buttercups thrive in the springtime, creating a stunning backdrop for campers. Hayden Lake boasts a 40-mile shoreline with a surface area of 3,800 acres. The lake was formed by the Missoula Floods that occurred nearly 15,000…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6842', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6843', 'Honeysuckle Campground', 'campground', 47.739200, -116.474600, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Honeysuckle Campground, located at the confluence of Deception Creek and the North Fork of the Coeur d''Alene River, is 22 miles from Coeur d''Alene. It was renovated in 1994 and has seven campsites including a host site. Campground roads and campsite parking spurs are paved. Amenities include potable well water with a hand pump and vault toilets. Minimum operating season is Memorial Day through Labor Day.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6844', 'Bumblebee Campground', 'campground', 47.633330, -116.279440, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Bumblebee Campground is located near the Little North Fork Coeur D''Alene River, making it a perfect fishing and seasonal hunting base camp. Swimming and floating the river are popular activities as well. Natural Features: The campground sits next to Bumblebee Creek near the Little North Fork Coeur D''Alene River at an elevation of 2,200 feet. In winter 2021, a wind event uprooted several hundred trees in the campground. Subsequent logging removed the down and damaged trees resulting in very open conditions. Coeur d''Alene National Forest spans 726,819 acres and is one of three forests…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6844', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6846', 'Beauty Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.607000, -116.669000, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Beauty Creek Campground is located a half mile from Lake Coeur d''Alene along the peaceful Beauty Creek. Visitors enjoy breathtaking scenery and convenient access to miles of trails. Natural Features: The campground is nestled in a narrow valley along Beauty Creek in northern Idaho. At an elevation of 2,100 feet, it is a sparsely wooded valley surrounded by heavily wooded hillsides. Beauty Creek sits in the Idaho Panhandle National Forest, between the Cascade Mountains to the west and the Bitterroot Mountains to the east. Recreation: The trailhead for the Caribou Ridge National Recreation…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6846', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6847', 'Bell Bay Campground', 'campground', 47.473028, -116.842142, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Bell Bay Campground is a prime place to set up camp on Coeur d''Alene Lake. The upper camp loop is on a hill overlooking the beautiful lake, while the lower loop sits on a short ridge along the shoreline. Natural Features: Located in the Panhandle of northern Idaho, the campground is surrounded by a forest of Ponderosa and other mixed pines. It lies on the southeast shores of Coeur d''Alene Lake just north of Harrison, Idaho. The lake spans 50 square miles, offering countless recreation opportunities and scenic views for visitors. Recreation: Hikers enjoy the Bell Bay Trail, a foot path that…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6847', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6849', 'Big Hank Campground', 'campground', 47.824640, -116.101060, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Big Hank Campground is located along the North Fork of the Coeur d''Alene River in Idaho Panhandle National Forest. Shore fishing is a large draw, along with local hiking and biking trails. The campground also provides an excellent base camp for hunters during season. Wildlife like mule deer, moose, osprey and calliope hummingbirds are often spotted. Natural Features: Big Hank is located along the banks of the Coeur D'' Alene River and Big Hank Creek. At 2,800 feet elevation, the campground sits on the Big Hank Meadow. Big Hank was logged in 2021 to remove hazard trees. Hazard trees are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6849', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6850', 'Berlin Flats Group Campground', 'campground', 47.793410, -115.952135, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Berlin Flats Group Area is located along Shoshone Creek, near the North Fork Coeur d''Alene River. This area provides a perfect escape for a warm summer weekend. Here, visitors can tent camp or pull out their RVs and trailers. The nearby river provides ample fishing and river floating opportunities. Natural Features: The campground sits among lodgepole and other mixed pines along the river at an elevation of 2,600 feet. The area is located among peaks of the Cascades, about 70 miles from the popular Coeur d''Alene Lake. Wildlife watchers and photographers have the chance to see mule deer,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6850', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6851', 'Devil''s Elbow Campground', 'campground', 47.771414, -116.032749, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Devil''s Elbow Campground is perched on the banks of the North Fork Coeur d''Alene River, providing a perfect escape for a warm summer weekend. Here, visitors can camp in tents or RVs and spend their days fishing or floating the river. Natural Features: The campground sits among lodgepole and other mixed pines along the river at an elevation of 2,600 feet. The area is located in the Coeur d'' Alene mountains 69 miles from popular Coeur d''Alene Lake. Wildlife watchers and photographers have the chance to see mule deer, moose, osprey and calliope hummingbirds. Recreation : Rafting, swimming and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6851', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6852', 'Kit Price Campground', 'campground', 47.739200, -116.474660, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Kit Price is a beautiful campground overlooking the North Fork Coeur ''Alene River. Campers enjoy the benefits of the river by fishing along the banks, swimming and floating. Hiking is also a great way to see mountain views. Kit Price was completely renovated in 2021, including new tables, fire rings, paved parking spurs, and restrooms. All sites are handicapped accessible. Natural Features : The campground is situated along the North Fork Coeur d'' Alene River at an elevation of 2,550 feet. Campsites are very open with smaller trees and brush species dominating the area. Popular Coeur d'' Alene…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6852', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6893', 'Shadowy St. Joe Campground', 'campground', 47.325668, -116.393254, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'The Shadowy St. Joe Campground features 14 fully accessible campsites with electrical hookups, picnic tables, fire rings and vault toilets. Refuse receptacle provided, ample parking, convenient trailer space, potable piped water, boat launch, and a group picnic shelter. The day use picnic shelter has tables that can seat up to 40 people. In 2023, the campground received a complete redesign paid for by the Great American Outdoors Act and with a Recreational Vehicle grant provided by Idaho Department of Parks and Recreation. The redesign included all new accessible facilities, the addition of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6893', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6894', 'Big Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.303600, -116.121100, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', '9 camp units, vault toilets, day use area, Pack it In Pack it Out waste management system. Fishing, National Recreation Trails, hunting, berry picking, hiking, site of former Civilian Conservation Corps camp.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6894', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6895', 'Emerald Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.007884, -116.325836, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Emerald Creek Campground features 18 camp units, potable water, and vault toilets. a short distance from the campground. The Garnet Area is one of our most popular recreation sites where, for a small fee, one can dig for gem quality star garnets. Mosquitos can be prolific throughout the season, consider bringing bug repellent.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6895', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6896', 'Cedar Creek Campground', 'campground', 47.050660, -116.289160, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Cedar Creek Campground features 3 camp units, and vault toilets. There is no developed water so bring your own. Please observe Pack it In Pack it Out for your refuse. Attractions include fishing on the St. Maries River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6896', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6897', 'Camp 3 Campground', 'campground', 47.131100, -116.104100, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Camp 3 Campground features 4 camp units, stock loading ramp, corral, and vault toilets. There is no developed water so bring ample supplies for your use. Please observe the Pack it In Pack it Out policy for your refuse. Attractions include fishing and proximity to a historic cabin.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6897', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6902', 'Telichpah Campground', 'campground', 47.295370, -115.774590, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Telichpah Campground features 5 camp units and vault toilets. Please observe the Pack it In, Pack it Out refuse policy. There is no developed water. Trailers are not recommended. Attractions include fishing on the North Fork St. Joe River, nearby streams. Trailhead to Nelson Peak National Recreation Trail System.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6902', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6903', 'Turner Flat Campground', 'campground', 47.236561, -115.654301, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Turner Flat Campground features 10 camp units, 1 group camping area to accomodate up to 15 people, potable water (June-October), vault toilets, and day use area. Please observe the Pack it In Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include the St. Joe Wild and Scenic River, fishing, and tubing/floating until mid-July.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6903', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6904', 'Tin Can Flat Campground', 'campground', 47.230012, -115.620794, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Tin Can Flat Campground features 11 camp units, potable water (June-October), and vault toilets. Please observe the Pack it In, Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include St. Joe Wild and Scenic River, fishing, floating (until mid-July).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6904', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6905', 'Mammoth Springs Campground', 'campground', 47.103882, -115.630717, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Mammoth Springs Campground features 8 camp units, vault toilets, and potable water (July-September). Please observe the Pack it In Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include Dismal Lake (1 mile). This campground was recently improved through a grant through an Idaho Department of Parks and Recreation.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6905', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6906', 'Conrad Crossing Campground', 'campground', 47.158576, -115.415957, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Conrad Crossing Campground features 8 camp units (2 on the river and 5 above the highway), potable water (June-October), vault toilets, and a day use area. Please observe the Pack it In Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include historic Montana Trail, St. Joe Wild and Scenic River, fishing, and floating until mid June. Raft access.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6906', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6907', 'Fly Flat Campground', 'campground', 47.112623, -115.390098, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Fly Flat Campground features 14 camp units, potable water (June-October), and vault toilets. Please comply with the Pack it In Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include fishing in wild trout waters, St. Joe Wild and Scenic River, and the Fly Creek Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6907', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6908', 'Spruce Tree Campground', 'campground', 47.038082, -115.347865, null, 'Idaho Panhandle National Forests', 'Spruce Tree Campground features 9 camp units, potable water, and vault toilets. Please observe the Pack it In Pack it Out refuse policy. Attractions include fishing in wild trout waters, beginning of wild portion of St. Joe Wild and Scenic River, St. Joe River Trail #48.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ipnf/recarea/?recid=6908', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69486', 'Foster Bar Campground', 'campground', 42.634574, -124.056152, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Foster Bar Campground is located on edge of large meadow next to the mighty Wild and Scenic Rogue River. Just downstream is the "take-out" boat ramp for rafters and fishermen; this portion of the river is world-renowned for its fishing opportunities! This is also a very important historic area, as it''s the location of the last battle fought during the Rogue River Indian Wars. The Lower Rogue River Trail #1168 accesses the Rogue River for fishing. Facilities 8 campsites (4 tent only, 4 tent or trailer) with picnic table, and fire pits Campground host available Drinking water Flushing toilets…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69486', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69528', 'Lobster Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.501496, -124.296024, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Lobster Creek campground is set in the forest on a large gravel bar, fronting the mighty Wild and Scenic Rogue River. Facilities Water 7 campsites (3 tent sites and 4 tent/trailer sites) with picnic tables and fire pits Campground host available Firewood available for purchase at host site Boat launch Gravel bar for day use fishing or picnicking 2 restrooms, with 4 flushing toilets each (2 men/2 women) Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69528', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69536', 'Ludlum Campground', 'campground', 42.035066, -124.110749, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Ludlum Campground is located adjacent to Wheeler Creek and the Winchuck River, just minutes from ocean beaches, and 30 minutes from the redwoods of northern California. There are opportunities to hike; one option is the Chimney Camp Trail #1279 , which is a pleasant hike along Wheeler Creek. Ludlum House Recreation Rental is also adjacent to the campground. Facilities 7 campsites with barrier-free picnic tables and fire pits Drinking water Vault toilets Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69536', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69540', 'Miller Bar Camping and Day Use Area', 'campground', 42.138456, -124.174915, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Miller Bar is operated as a dispersed site, and is located on large river bar on the beautiful Wild and Scenic Chetco River . Enjoy summer fun in the crystal clear waters of this outstanding river! A few shaded spots can be found along the treeline. Tents or small trailers only. Camping on the gravel bar during the winter months is discouraged due to the frequency of high water events. Facilities Camp where you want No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal from Memorial Day through Labor Day', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69540', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69560', 'Nook Bar Camping and Day Use Area', 'campground', 42.146000, -124.155000, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Nook Bar provides dispersed campsites for tents or small trailers on a large river bar by the beautiful Wild and Scenic Chetco River . Enjoy summer fun in the crystal clear waters of this outstanding river! A few shaded spots can be found along the tree line. Camping on the gravel bar during the winter months is discouraged due to the frequency of high water events. Facilities Vault toilet Garbage disposal from Memorial Day through Labor Day', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69560', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69564', 'Oak Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.518739, -124.041930, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This site is located along the Wild and Scenic Illinois River and the Illinois River West Trailhead . For tents and small trailers only. Facilities 15 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No campground host No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69564', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69584', 'Quosatana Campground', 'campground', 42.496082, -124.229627, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'May 2021 Update: Please note that the dump station is temporarily closed until further notice , due to repairs needed to the wastewater system at Quosatana. Thank you for your patience as we work towards fixing this. Quosatana campground is located along the famously mighty Wild and Scenic Rogue River. Boat or shore fish from this beautiful campground, which is spread out over 15 acres on a large river bar. It offers space for everyone to enjoy their time along the river and in the surrounding areas. Myrtlewood groves and large meadows await you! Facilities 43 campsites (3 accessible sites)…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69584', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69618', 'South Fork Camping and Day Use Area', 'campground', 42.187260, -124.131668, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This is a dispersed campsite for tents and small trailers is located at the confluence of South Fork Chetco with the main stem of the Wild and Scenic Chetco River . Enjoy summer fun in the crystal clear waters of this outstanding river. Upper South Fork Camp provides a more secluded location along the South Fork Chetco River. Lower South Fork Camp provides a larger area with access to both the South Fork and main stem Chetco River. Facilities Camp where you want No picnic table No fire pits No campground host No drinking water Portable toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69618', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69654', 'Abbott Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.881337, -122.507586, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Abbott Creek Campground is a remote and picturesque campground in the midst of an old-growth forest and adjacent to Abbott Creek. This campground offers opportunities for fishing, swimming and hiking. There are five OHV friendly campsites within the campground that allow for easy access to Prospect OHV Trail System . The Upper Rogue River Trail may be accessed nearby at Woodruff Bridge Day Use Area. Facilities 25 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits OHV use allowed at sites 1-5 Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69654', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69670', 'Beaver Dam Group Campground', 'campground', 42.304000, -122.367000, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Beaver Dam Group Campground can accomodate group sizes up to 40 and is located along Beaver Creek within an old growth forest. The campground offers opportunity for hiking, swimming, fishing and star gazing. Facilities 4 campsites (3 tent sites, 1 trailer site) with picnic tables, and fire pits No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69670', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69710', 'Daley Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.306536, -122.366584, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Daley Creek Campground is located near the confluence of Beaver Dam and Daley Creeks within an old growth forest. This campground offers opportunity for hiking, fishing and swimming. Facilities 6 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69710', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69716', 'Doe Point Campground & Day Use', 'campground', 42.392738, -122.323024, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This remote and picturesque campground is in the midst of old-growth forest and adjacent to Fish Lake, offering some of the best fishing in the area. A boat launch for Fish Lake (speed limit 10 mph) is located at adjacent Fish Lake Campground , and many amenities are offered at nearby Fish Lake Resort. Numerous hiking trails are within easy access, including the Fish Lake, High Lakes, Brown Mountain, and the famous Pacific Crest Trail, as well as the Sky Lakes Wilderness and Mt. McLaughlin Trail systems. Additional campgrounds nearby include Fish Lake Resort, the adjacent Fish Lake Campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69716', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69720', 'Farewell Bend Campground', 'campground', 42.916240, -122.435330, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Farewell Bend Campground is adjacent to the Rogue River and neighbors Crater Lake National Park . This campground can accommodate most RV''s / trailers and has paved parking pads at each campsite. Snacks and a hot meal are close by at Union Creek Resort . Within the campground are numerous fishing locations and many hiking opportunies, including access to the Rogue Gorge Trail . Facilities 61 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings Children''s Play Area 4 flush toilet restroom facilities Campground Host Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69720', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69728', 'Fish Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.394214, -122.318227, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This picturesque campground is in the midst of old-growth forest and adjacent to Fish Lake. The lake offers opportunity for fishing and swimming. A boat launch for Fish Lake (speed limit 10 mph) is located within the campground, and amenities are offered at nearby Fish Lake Resor t. Numerous hiking trails are within easy access, including the Fish Lake, High Lakes, Brown Mountain, and the Pacific Crest trail. Facilities 17 campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings 3 walk-in tent sites with picnic tables, and fire rings Campground Host Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69728', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69738', 'Fourbit Ford Campground', 'campground', 42.500890, -122.403450, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Fourbit Ford Campground is located along Fourbit Creek. This campground is a short distance from Willow Lake and located on the site of the original supply road (Old Military Road) for Fort Klamath. Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69738', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69812', 'Mill Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.794375, -122.467664, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Mill Creek Campground is adjacent to Mill Creek. The campground has opportunity for fishing and swimming. Facilities 10 campsites with picnic tables and fire pits Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69812', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6982', 'Horseshoe Recreation and Campground Area', 'campground', 39.180240, -79.601810, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Constructed in the 1930s by the Civilian Conservation Corps, Horseshoe is nestled in the mountains of West Virginia along Horseshoe Run. Horseshoe is located approximately 7 miles northeast of St. George, West Virginia, on State Route 7.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6982', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69828', 'Natural Bridge Campground', 'campground', 42.892509, -122.462826, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Natural Bridge Campground stretches along the scenic Upper Rogue River, with majestic conifers creating pleasantly shaded sites and privacy between campsites. This campground offers opportunity for fishing, swimming and hiking. Rogue Gorge Trail and the Uper Rogue Trail are easily accessed from campground. Facilities 17 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69828', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69832', 'North Fork Campground', 'campground', 42.377265, -122.360514, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'North Fork Campground offers scenic views and opportunity for fishing, swimming and hiking. Fish Lake Traihead is just across street from the campground. Facilities 9 campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69832', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6984', 'Big Rock Campground', 'campground', 38.296059, -80.523888, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Small, wooded 5 unit campground adjacent to the Cranberry River. Located on Forest Road 76, approximately 7 miles north of Richwood, WV.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6984', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69858', 'River Bridge Campground', 'campground', 42.821450, -122.493593, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'River Bridge Campground is adjacent to the Rogue River and offers ample opportunity for fishing swimming and hiking. The Upper Rogue Trail is easily accessible from parking lot and the nearby are several sandy areas that offer a place to sit and relax by the river. Prospect OHV trail system is eassily accessed from campground. 9 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits 2 OHV campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Garbage Disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69858', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6986', 'Bishop Knob Campground', 'campground', 38.337760, -80.489680, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'A 60-unit wooded, semi-primitive campground centrally located on a ridge-top between the Cranberry and Williams Rivers. Located off Forest Road 101 in Webster County. Approximately 13 miles from Richwood, WV and 3 miles from Dyer, WV.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6986', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6987', 'Cranberry Campground', 'campground', 38.325180, -80.441710, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'A popular semi-primitive campground adjacent to the Cranberry River. This campground receives very high use during trout stocking from the beginning of spring through the end of June and again in the fall from September through October. During these high use times there are usually more campers waiting than there are sites available. During high use, the centrally located Bishop Knob Campground can usually accommodate campers when no sites are available along the Cranberry or Williams River Corridors. Located on Forest Road 76, 13.5 miles from Richwood, West Virginia, and 7 miles from Dyer,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6987', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6988', 'Cranberry River Sites', 'campground', 38.295470, -80.516070, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Fourteen primitive and separately numbered campsites dispersed along a 5-mile section of the lower Cranberry River. Toilets closed as of November 30. Campsites are number 6-19 along the Cranberry River between Big Rock Campground and Cranberry Campground on Forest Road 76. Double sites available at sites 7 and 12.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6988', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6989', 'Summit Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.248730, -80.444800, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'A 33-unit semi-primitive, wooded campground with paved access roads and parking spurs, located approximately 10 miles from Richwood, WV, adjacent to a popular 43-acre cold water fishing lake. Although the campground closes in winter, the lake is accessible year-round.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6989', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69892', 'South Fork Campground', 'campground', 42.646848, -122.335887, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'South Fork Campground is near the South Fork of the Rogue River within an old growth forest. Facilities 6 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69892', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6991', 'Island Campground', 'campground', 38.579033, -79.703912, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'This primitive campground is a favorite among fisherman for being adjacent to Long Run and the East Fork of the Greenbrier River. For hikers, this campground is located close to the East Fork Trail #365. This is an 8 mile trail with some difficult terrain to traverse. Also close by is the shorter Smoke Camp Trail #324. It is 1.8 miles in length for those looking for more of a day hike. Island Campground is located approximately 5 miles north and east of Bartow, West Virginia.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6991', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69922', 'Union Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.910270, -122.450080, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This picturesque campground in the midst of the Union Creek Historic District, in the middle of an old-growth forest. Union Creek itself flows through the campground and intersects the Rogue River. This campground offers quiet secluded campsites. Snacks and a hot meal are within walking distance at Union Creek Resort . Nearby fishing locations and numerous hiking options are within easy access to the Union Creek and Upper Rogue River Trails. Facilities 74 campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings - (3 of the campsites offer full RV hookups. Located outside of main campground on an ATV dirt…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69922', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6993', 'Laurel Fork Campground', 'campground', 38.740270, -79.692320, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Located along the Laurel Fork River between Laurel Fork North and South Wilderness areas, this primitive campground offers visitors a nice camping opportunity in the Middle Mountain area on the site of an old Civilian Conservation Corps location. D ay hiking and backpacking opportunities are available leaving from this campground as well through the Laurel Fork North and South Wilderness .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6993', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6996', 'Day Run Campground', 'campground', 38.215221, -80.080691, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Located just off the Highland Scenic Highway this small developed campground is a perfect getaway for fisherman and hikers. Many of the 12 camping sites boarder the upper scenic Williams River and the campground is within walking distance of many popular trails. Each site is equipped with a wooden picnic table, lantern post, and fire ring. Several campsites also have a tent pad, although all sites are suitable for tent or trailer camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6996', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6997', 'Pocahontas Campground', 'campground', 38.102949, -79.967280, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'With a convenient location just off State Route 92 this campground is great for families and outdoor enthusiasts. Two Lick Trailhead is located within the campground and providing easy and accessible access. Also each campsite is furnished with a fire ring, picnic table, and lantern ring.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6997', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '69976', 'Whiskey Springs Campground', 'campground', 42.492789, -122.417634, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Whiskey Springs Campground is quiet and secluded and can accomodate most trailers lengths. The campground is a short distance from Willow Lake Recreation Area and numerous hiking trails are within easy access, including the Mt. McLaughlin Trail #3716 . Facilities 34 campsites with picnic tables, and fire rings Garbage disposal', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=69976', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '6998', 'Tea Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.343270, -80.231860, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Tea Creek Campground is a spacious 28-site campground is tucked away at the intersection of the Williams River and Tea Creek. This campground is a recreational hub of the area. There are four trailheads located within the campground and walking distance to most of the T ea Creek Trail System . Each camping site is equipped with a parking spur, picnic table, fire ring with a grill, waste receptacle and a lantern hookup. V isitors are encouraged to use the three bear-proof trash cages located throughout the campground during their visit.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=6998', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7000', 'Big Bend Campground', 'campground', 38.889610, -79.238060, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Big Bend is located in the Smoke Hole Canyon next to the South Branch of the Potomac River at the end of County Route 2. Located 10 miles south west of Petersburg, West Virginia. The river is located 200 feet from campground and is open for fishing and non-motorized boat use. A one mile loop trail is available for hiking at the campground and 60 miles of backcountry trails are located close by in the Seneca Creek Backcountry as well as the trails located in Smoke Hole Canyon .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7000', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70018', 'Buck Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.773848, -123.952864, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This is a campground on the Powers to Glendale Bike Route. It is six miles to the Panther Ridge Trail #1253 , which leads to Hanging Rock. Facilities 2 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70018', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70022', 'Butler Bar Campground', 'campground', 42.725675, -124.270842, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Butler Bar Campground has primitive camping with access to the Wild and Scenic Elk River , and is adjacent to the Copper-Salmon Wilderness and Grassy Knob Wilderness . Planning to ride the Wild Coast Scenic Bikeway ? This is one of the campgrounds along the way! Facilities 7 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70022', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7003', 'Red Creek Campground', 'campground', 39.032260, -79.315940, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Red Creek Campground is a primitive, small campground that sits on top of the Allegheny Plateau and within the Dolly Sods Scenic Area. The climate and plant life here resembles Northern Canada. A stone''s throw from the campground is Dolly Sods Wilderness which offers a unique wilderness hiking opportunity for those looking for adventure. This area features unique scenery and unusual plant communities. Flowering laurel, rhododendron and azaleas highlight this area from May through June. Huckleberry picking is popular during the month of July. And for those looking for wildlife, bird banding is…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7003', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70030', 'Daphne Grove Campground', 'campground', 42.736674, -124.054646, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This site is located along the South Fork of the Coquille River. There is a group shelter for up to 25 people. Facilities 14 RV campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Drinking water (unavailable until further notice) 4 vault toilets Garbage disposal (from Memorial Day to Labor Day only)', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70030', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70032', 'Eden Valley Campground', 'campground', 42.808610, -123.890326, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Sites are along the Glendale-Powers Bicycle Recreation Area , a beautiful way to experience the many waterfalls and sweeping scenery this part of southern Oregon has to offer! Facilities 11 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water 2 vault toilets No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70032', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7004', 'Seneca Shadows Campground', 'campground', 38.822220, -79.387220, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Seneca Shadows Campground overlooks Seneca Rocks and is surrounded by mountains on both the east and west. Hiking and nature study at Seneca Rocks are just a couple of the popular activities in the area. The North Fork South Branch Potomac River is nearby, making fishing a popular pastime. Two local caves beckon ambitious explorers, and the 900-foot high Seneca Rocks can be viewed from most campsites. Seneca Shadows is the newest campground in the Spruce Knob-Seneca Rocks National Recreation Area . Many sites offer outstanding views of the 900 foot Seneca Rocks . This is a modern campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7004', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7005', 'Spruce Knob Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.707380, -79.588260, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Spruce Knob Lake Campground is located west of Spruce Knob , the highest point in West Virginia. Also close by is Spruce Knob - Seneca Creek Backcountry , which holds 60 miles of trails ready to be explored. For individuals looking for group camping located close by is Gatewood Campground . If you enjoy stream or river fishing as well you can head over to Gandy Creek. Fishing is available at Spruce Knob Lake. Built in 1952 for fishing, the 25-acre lake is regularly stocked with trout by the West Virginia Division of Natural Resources. Numerous small but hungry bluegills along the shoreline…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7005', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70058', 'Island Campground', 'campground', 42.723529, -124.041968, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Sites are located along the South Fork of the Coquille River, and offer the cool of shade during the heat of summer. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal from Memorial Day weekend through October', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70058', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70064', 'Laird Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.701271, -124.204612, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Sites are located on the Wild and Scenic Elk River , and along the Wild Rivers Coast Scenic Bikeway ! Facilities 4 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70064', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7007', 'Blue Bend Recreation Area and Campground', 'campground', 37.921209, -80.260670, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Located on State Route 16, near Alvon, West Virginia, Blue Bend is in a rustic and beautiful setting along scenic Anthony Creek. The area serves both campers and daytime visitors, and is popular for fishing, swimming, hiking, and picnicking. Most of these trails were constructed in the 1930''s by the Civilian Conservation Corps. Anthony Creek Trail follows the creek in a narrow valley filled with rhododendron and many flowering forest trees. Blue Bend Loop Trail offers three scenic overlooks and has a trail shelter for overnight use. The South Boundary Trail travels from the beautiful…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7007', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70074', 'Myrtle Grove Campground', 'campground', 42.786000, -124.023000, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This site provides primitive campsites along the South Fork of the Coquille River. Facilities 5 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage Disposal Memorial Day weekend through Labor Day weekend', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70074', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7008', 'Lake Sherwood Recreation Area and Campground', 'campground', 38.008126, -80.011929, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'Lake Sherwood Recreation Area is a complete family destination offering a wide variety of activities and camping options. Standard, tent-only and group camping facilities are perched along Lake Sherwood, the largest lake on Monongahela National Forest. Swimming beaches, a picnic area, boat ramp and several hiking trails are among the features of the area. At an elevation of 2,600 feet, Lake Sherwood spans 156 acres. A variety of animals make their home here, including black bear, coyote, wild turkey, white-tailed deer, red and gray fox, bobcat, fisher, otter and mink.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7008', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70092', 'Rock Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.707618, -124.059048, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Located on the shores of Rock Creek, a tributary of the South Fork Coquille River , this small campground is the perfect place to take shelter under the trees and listen to the sounds of the creek. A quick drive and visitors can venture to the Coquille Falls trailhead and other scenic spots along the Coquille River. Facilities 7 campsites (tent-only) with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal from Memorial Day weekend through October', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70092', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70098', 'Sru Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.730708, -124.006042, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Campsites are located in a mountain lake setting. This site is also close to the Coquille River Falls Research Natural Area. Facilities 6 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Fishing platform No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70098', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70106', 'Sunshine Bar Campground', 'campground', 42.712146, -124.310928, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Lush campsites at Sunshine Bar Campground are located on the Wild and Scenic Elk River, and along the Wild Rivers Coast Scenic Bikeway . Facilities 6 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water 2 vault toilets No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70106', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '7011', 'Highland Scenic Highway', 'campground', 38.306620, -80.096133, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'The Highland Scenic Highway is a designated National Scenic Byway that extends 43 miles from Richwood to US Route 219, north of Marlinton. Four scenic overlooks provide a comfortable rest stop, with panoramic views of the surrounding mountains and valleys. The Highway traverses the mountainous terrain of the Allegheny Highlands and Plateau, and rises from 2,325 feet near Richwood to more than 4,500 feet. The Highway is a paved two-lane road, designated as State Routes 39 and 150. Route 150 is a 23-mile Parkway section that is not maintained in the winter . Winter travel on the road may be…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=7011', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70140', 'Carberry Group Campground', 'campground', 42.025550, -123.165292, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Carberry Group Campground is located along Cougar Creek. The tent site locations vary in size, with the smaller, more intimate sites found adjacent to Cougar Creek. Lake access is found across County Road 777 from the campground, with a trail that leads to Carberry Creek. (When the lake is full, the trail ends at the lake). There is nearby access to Applegate Lake and an OHV trail system. There are wheelchair accessible facilities and trails. DURING THE OFF SEASON: This site is open all year, but is a walk-in site during the off-season, with no service provided during that time. Park at the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70140', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70230', 'Harr Point Campground', 'campground', 42.034920, -123.112792, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Campground is on the east shore of Applegate Lake and is accessible only by the Payette Trail #970 or by boat. Persons accessing this site by boat may find current information about lake levels helpful. This is a semi-primitive site. Facilities 5 campsites (tent-sites) with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70230', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70232', 'Hart-tish Campground', 'campground', 42.052189, -123.129962, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Located in southwest Oregon in the Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest, Hart-Tish Park is surrounded by a variety of landscapes, boasting nearby volcanic peaks, rivers and old-growth forests. Hart-Tish Park offers several acres of beautifully groomed lawn sloping down to the shores of Applegate Lake. Visitors can spot the peaks of the majestic Red Buttes Wilderness while looking south over the lake. Hart-tish offers day use areas for swimmers, and the convenience of a cement boat ramp for those looking to launch their boats! The Applegate Lake borders the campground making the view worth the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70232', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70246', 'Jackson Campground', 'campground', 42.114043, -123.087065, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Jackson Campground sits on the shores of the Applegate River, a popular recreation site located north of the Red Buttes Wilderness Area. Visitors enjoy swimming, cycling, boating, canoeing, fishing and hiking the various trails near the river. Nearby is the inactive Bigfoot trap, built in 1974 by the North American Wildlife Research Team and found along the Collings Mountain Trail. The trap was inspired by a miner who lived near the Applegate River who claimed to have found 18-inch-long, human-like tracks in his garden. The organization operated the trap, keeping it baited with carcasses for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70246', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70358', 'Acorn Woman Lakes Campground', 'campground', 42.035187, -123.025607, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Acorn Woman Lakes is one of more popular areas in the Applegate Recreation Area! If you want to get away from it all and really enjoy the beauty of southwest Oregon, Acorn Woman Lakes is the ideal opportunity for that. The air is clean and the water fresh,and at night, the stars are bright! Hiking and fishing top the list of recreational opportunities at Acorn Woman Lakes Campground. Two mountain lakes, a river and a handful of hiking trails are accessible from the campground. Anglers enjoy the remote location and scenic backdrop of two natural lakes, providing excellent fishing opportunities…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70358', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70388', 'Tipsu Tyee Campground', 'campground', 42.035517, -123.125495, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Tipsu Tyee is located along the shore of Applegate Lake and is accessible only by the Payette Trail #970 or by boat. Persons accessing this site by boat may find current information about lake levels helpful. Facilities 5 campsites (tent-sites) with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70388', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70404', 'Watkins Campground', 'campground', 42.023784, -123.158686, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Sites are located on Applegate Lake. There are wheelchair accessible facilities. Facilities 14 campsites (tent-sites) with picnic tables, and fire pits 1 group campsite (20-50 people) No drinking water Vault toilet Garbage disposal available during operating season Seasonal information: The site is free and open during the off-season as a walk-in site (parking at the gate, and proceeding on foot). No services or water are available during the off-season. Please pack out all trash and remember to Leave No Trace .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70404', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70418', 'Wrangle Campground', 'campground', 42.050258, -122.855920, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'There are several picnic tables and a rustic shelter built by the Civilian Conservation Corps in 1936, and a cabin built by the Soil Conservation Service, also in the 1930s. There is a community kitchen available. Facilities 5 campsites (tent-sites) with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70418', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70446', 'Big Pine Campground', 'campground', 42.458585, -123.676018, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Temporary Closure Order due to hazardous trees. These sites are located in a rustic camp. Campsites are suitable for tents and trailers. This site is home to what was once the world''s tallest ponderosa pine tree--it is now the second tallest! Facilities 12 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Drinking water (hand pump) 3 vault toilets Garbage disposal (during open season)', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70446', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70460', 'Bolan Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.023505, -123.458244, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Bolan Lake Campground sits along the shores of Bolan Lake, a 12-acre lake sitting high above the Illinois Valley. Campsites are in a dispersed camping area, but are equipped with tables and fire pits. Large conifers provide shade in the heat of summer months, and the wildflowers are not to be missed in this area in the early summer. Bolan Lake Trail #1245 , located within the campground, climbs up to the old fire lookout on Bolan Peak. The lookout is available for rent; reservations must be made at www.recreation.gov . Facilities 12 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70460', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70504', 'Chinquapin Group Campground', 'campground', 42.140601, -123.457592, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'The large meadow at the Chinquapin Group Campground makes a great location for group events such as reunions, church camps, school field trips and scouting events. Within a short walking distance there are swimming areas in Grayback Creek and creek side trails with meadows, marshes, spring wildflowers, wildlife and berry picking. Visitors can continue 10 miles east on Highway 46 and visit Oregon Caves National Monument for a tour of one of the few marble caves in the world. Facilities Can accomodate up to 75 people Picnic tables, and fire pits Drinking water No electricity Vault toiled No…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70504', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70546', 'Grayback Campground', 'campground', 42.148460, -123.465396, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This campground is located in a beautiful forested setting, with the Oregon Caves National Momunent located approximately 5 miles further down the road. Several of the campsites are located along Sucker Creek, which also provides cool waters to jump in or just soak your feet in on hot summer days. Revel in the amazing biodiversity that is so unique to the Illinois Valley by venturing out on the 1 mile loop trail suitable for families that leads to Grayback Creek and around the historical Civilian Conservation Corps camp at the Cedar Guard Station. There is a pleasant day use area with a small…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70546', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70562', 'Josephine Campground', 'campground', 42.242380, -123.686259, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'A rustic setting above Josephine Creek and the Illinois River. Facilities 6 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70562', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70584', 'Little Falls Campground', 'campground', 42.240336, -123.675536, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Little Falls Campground is a pleasant little campground, complete with views of the Illinois River and the expansive mountains surrounding the Illinois Valley. Facilities 3 tent campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits Amphitheater with large fire pit No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70584', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70634', 'River Bench Campground', 'campground', 42.295079, -123.740103, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Several walk in campsites along the Illinois River . River Bench Day Use and Campground are located on a lower river terrace, within a forested setting. Must hike down one of two access trails to use. Facilities 8 walk in campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet within walking distance No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70634', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70636', 'Sam Brown Campground', 'campground', 42.443084, -123.688946, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Sam Brown Campground is centered around a large meadow that has a colorful history of the earlier miner and homesteader to the area. Trails are located throughout the area, as well, with options for hiking, mountain biking, horseback riding, and motorcylces, including Elkhorn Mine Jeep Road. Nearby trail opportunities include: Briggs Creek Trail #1132 (the trailhead located in campground) Taylor Creek Trail #1142 Onion Way Trail #1157 Secret Way Trail #1282 Dutchy Creek Trail #1154 The size of this campground, and nature of the landscape, lends itself to large group camping, with 2 picnic…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70636', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70674', 'Sixmile Campground', 'campground', 42.297000, -123.730000, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Campsites are located along the Wild and Scenic Illinois River. There are 2 covered picnic sites across the road from the camping area. Facilities 4 walk-in campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water 2 vault toilets (within walking distance from campsites) No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70674', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70678', 'Spalding Pond Campground', 'campground', 42.347000, -123.702000, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'This primitive camping area is near the historic mill site pond. This pond is stocked with rainbow trout annually by the Oregon Department of Fish and Wildlife. Fishing is best in the spring to early summer. There is an accessible trail and fishing platform. Facilities 4 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water No toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70678', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70680', 'Store Gulch Campground', 'campground', 42.295703, -123.755597, null, 'Rogue River-Siskiyou National Forest', 'Campsites are located along the Wild and Scenic Illinois River . Facilities 4 campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits 2 walk-in campsites with picnic tables, and fire pits No drinking water Vault toilet No garbage disposal - Please pack it out', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/rogue-siskiyou/recarea/?recid=70680', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70778', 'Lambert Creek Horse Camp', 'campground', 48.728680, -118.522970, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This shaded horse camp is located across the road from the Old Stage/Midnight Ridge Trailhead , which offers a great horseback, hiking, or mountain biking loop opportunity. The 6-unit campground offers parking spurs, picnic tables, rock fire rings, creek access for watering stock, and an outhouse. The area is fenced with cattleguards to keep cattle out. There is a 6-foot bypass gate adjacent to the entrance road cattleguard to allow stock users access to the trail system. There are currently no corrals, highlines, or hitching rails at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=70778', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70824', 'Lake Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.039083, -115.490833, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Lake Creek Campground is located approximately 32 miles southwest of Libby off the West Fisher road. The campground has 4 sites all with tent pads, tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 32'' rv. There are also 4 dispersed campsites. Campground roads and parking spurs are gravel or native material. Amenities include potable water and vault toilets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70824', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70846', 'Oscar Miller Camping Area', 'campground', 48.039892, -115.454564, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'This dispersed camp area is within an old homestead and offers a vault toilet, a hitch rail and an unloading/loading ramp for animals.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70846', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70848', 'Loon Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.597386, -115.670853, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Loon Lake campground is approximately 20 miles northwest of Libby on raod 471. The campground has 4 sites (two with tent pads), tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 20'' rv. Campground roads and parking spurs are gravel and native material. Amenities include a vault toilet, an undeveloped access for small boats.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70848', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70849', 'Empire Lake Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.786924, -118.752657, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Empire Lake Sno-park has a large parking area that will accommodate approximately 5 vehicles with trailers and an outhouse. There is an information board with a map showing the groomed snowmobile trail system during the winter and a road map during the summer. The parking area is available for dispersed camping and day-use during the summer months. The last 3 miles of road leading to the sno-park is narrow in places.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=70849', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70854', 'Timberlane Campground', 'campground', 48.488890, -115.525000, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Timberlane Campground is located along a forest creek and in an area thick with towering trees. Several hiking trails exist in the area. The campground may accommodate up to 200 people and is great for reunions and receptions. Its a great place to enjoy the Kootenai National Forest. Natural Features: The campground is located along Pipe Creek in the Kootenai National Forest of northwestern Montana. It lies in a mixed conifer forest at an elevation of about 2,600 feet. A variety of wildlife make its home in the area. The area is historically significant, once a former habitat and hunting…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70854', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70861', 'McGillivray Campground and Group Sites', 'campground', 48.488042, -115.299664, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The McGillivray Campground has 33 total campsites and provides three opportunities for group rental camping. The group shelter will accommodate up to 200 people making it great for reunions and receptions. The two smaller group sites will accommodate up to 25 people each and are both located within the campground. Both group sites are ideal for campers to share an area with friends and family. In addition to the group sites there are 4 other single sites on the reservation list. The sites all provide recreational opportunities such as hiking, fishing, boating and swimming. Campground Map…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70861', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70865', 'Penny Springs Campground', 'campground', 44.711790, -115.694420, null, 'Boise National Forest', 'Penny Spring Campground is a treat for campers who enjoy the great outdoors in a remote area. Near enough to enjoy the Warm Lake area, but also a quiet spot out of the summer crouds, Penny Springs offers plenty of relaxing under the pine forest canopy. In the late summer months, visitors enjoy picking huckleberries and viewing trails covered in wildflowers. Recreation: Catch a fish in the nearby stream, view the wildlife and enjoy a picnic with friends. Don''t forget your Motor Vehicle Use Map of the Cascade Ranger District. It is your guide to open roads and trails designated for hiking,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/boise/recarea/?recid=70865', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70944', 'North Dickey Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.720830, -114.857220, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'North Dickey Lake Campground is a beautiful campground next to scenic Dickey Lake and several hiking and mountain biking trails. It''s conveniently located off the main highway and provides a secluded location for outdoor enjoyment. A day use area is located on the other side of the lake. Natural Features: The campground is located in northwestern Montana on a hillside next to the 800-acre lake. It is nestled in a forest of larch and fir trees at an elevation of about 3,100 feet. In the spring and early summer, the sound of the loon can often be heard from the campground. Recreation : The…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70944', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70947', 'Grave Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.819236, -114.886447, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Grave Creek Campground is located 4 miles north of Fortine on road 7061. The campground has 4 campsites with tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 20'' rv. Amenities include vault toilets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70947', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70951', 'Big Therriault Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.936747, -114.877833, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Big Therriault Lake campground is located 12.5 air miles from Fortine. The campground has 10 campsite, including one host site, with tables, fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 32'' rv. Amenities include potable water, vault toilets, food storage boxes and boat ramp developed for small boats.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=70951', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '70954', 'Fir Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.425460, -115.290830, null, 'Boise National Forest', 'The Fir Creek Campground is located along Forest Service Road 579 near the in beautiful but remote Bear Valley at an elevation of 6,400 feet. It is adjacent to the Frank Church - River of No Return Wilderness and scenic Elk Creek. Situated in a high mountain meadow dotted with Douglas fir and lodgepole pine amid the peaks of the Sawtooth Range, it is a perfect summer retreat. Deer, elk, moose, red squirrels, coyote and lynx all live in the area. The sounds of elk, coyote and wolf are often heard in the summer and fall months. In winter, wildlife enthusiasts can watch carefully for snowshoe…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/boise/recarea/?recid=70954', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71013', 'Ice House Campground', 'campground', 38.829734, -120.365699, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 23 miles east of Placerville on Highway 50 then 11 miles north on Ice House Road (Forest Road 3) then 1.5 miles east on Forest Road 32. Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Ice House Campground Picnicking Fees', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71013', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71027', 'Jones Fork Campground', 'campground', 38.858877, -120.384733, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Jones Fork Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71027', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71029', 'Lone Rock Campground', 'campground', 38.863334, -120.385998, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Bike-in or Walk-in along the Union Valley trail from Jones Fork Campground or Boat in from Union Valley boatramp. Union Valley Bike Trail & Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71029', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71031', 'Sunset Campground', 'campground', 38.868890, -120.399284, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Sunset Campground Picnicking Fees and Passes Union Valley Bike Trail and Campgrounds', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71031', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71056', 'Azalea Cove Campground', 'campground', 38.881372, -120.369814, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Union Valley Bike Trail & Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. This is a walk-in, bike-in or boat-in campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71056', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71058', 'Wench Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.889243, -120.370567, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Wench Creek Campground Wench Group Campgrounds Fees and Passes Union Valley Bike Trail and Campgrounds', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71058', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71059', 'Yellowjacket Campground', 'campground', 38.891074, -120.387840, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Yellowjacket campground will be closed for construction in 2021. Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Yellowjacket Campground Fees and Passes', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71059', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71064', 'Wolf Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.885285, -120.399510, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Campground Group Campground Fee', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71064', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71065', 'Camino Cove Campground', 'campground', 38.878704, -120.428467, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71065', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71066', 'West Point Campground', 'campground', 38.870948, -120.441785, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71066', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71067', 'Fashoda Campground', 'campground', 38.867979, -120.397563, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Fashoda Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Note: Parking for this campground is in the central parking lot. You can drive down to campsite to drop off gear then park in parking area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71067', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71069', 'Loon Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.979985, -120.316854, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 23 miles east of Placerville on Highway 50 and 29 miles north on Ice House Road (Forest Road 3) on the south side of Loon Lake. Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Loon Lake Campground Loon Group Campgrounds Loon Boatramp Camping Fees Desolation Wilderness Picnicking', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71069', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71072', 'Northshore Campground', 'campground', 38.999568, -120.318717, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Northshore Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71075', 'Wentworth Springs Campground', 'campground', 39.011516, -120.325376, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Wentworth Springs Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71075', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71076', 'Pleasant Campground', 'campground', 39.011811, -120.290268, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Small boat or hike in campground on the east shore of Loon Lake campground. Access via the Loon Lake Trailhead or boatramp at Loon Lake Campground. Pleasant Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71076', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71081', 'Gerle Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.975616, -120.392395, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 23 miles east of Placerville on Highway 50 then 24 miles north on Ice House Road (Forest Road 3), and 3 miles north on Forest Road 33 to Gerle Reservoir. Gerle Creek Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71081', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71082', 'Airport Flat Campground', 'campground', 38.985255, -120.380386, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 23 miles east of Placerville on Highway 50 then 24 miles north on Ice House Road (Forest Road 3), and 3 miles north on Forest Road 33. Sites are arranged into pods to accommodate groups of 15 25 people. Airport Flat Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=71082', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71118', 'Little Grass Valley Recreation Area', 'campground', 39.729000, -120.987000, null, 'Plumas National Forest', '8-3-2021 At this time the Black Rock boat dock has been removed from the water and is not available until further notice. The Feather River Ranger District manages 8 family campgrounds around Little Grass Valley Reservoir. There are approximately 323 camping units. Campsites in Red Feather, Running Deer, Little Beaver parts of Loop A & B and the southern half of Wyandotte, and Horse Camp may be reserved through www.recreation.gov (1-877-444-6777) All other campgrounds are available on a first-come, first server basis. Each campground has piped water. Trailer sites are available, as well as…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/plumas/recarea/?recid=71118', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71120', 'Sly Creek Recreation Area', 'campground', 39.591000, -121.108000, null, 'Plumas National Forest', 'Sly Creek Campground has 25 units. Campground has drinking water, rest rooms,and garbage service. Each camping unit has a table and a fire ring.Trailers up to 22 feet can be accommodated, however no hookups are provided. Maximum stay is 14 days. Sly Creek Reservoir usually opens around May 4 through October. Boat ramp open.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/plumas/recarea/?recid=71120', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71212', 'Rocky Gorge Campground', 'campground', 48.652069, -115.311772, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Rocky Gorge Campground is located approximately 26 miles southwest of Eureka off Hwy 37. The campground has 60 campsites including one host site, with tables, fire rings and some with tent pads and able to accommodate up to 32'' rv. Amenities include potable water, vault toilets, dock and a fully developed boat launch.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=71212', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71215', 'Rexford Bench Campground', 'campground', 48.899283, -115.158983, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Rexford Bench Campground is the most highly developed campground within the Kootenai National Forest. It is a popular destination for boating, fishing and swimming on Lake Koocanusa, and hiking in the surrounding forest. Beautiful sandstone formations can be viewed not far from the campground, and osprey and eagles can often be seen fishing in the reservoir. Natural Features: The campground is located on an arm of Lake Koocanusa in northwest Montana near the Canadian border. The 46,500-acre reservoir has over 127 miles of shoreline and is formed by 422'' Libby Dam on the Kootenai River, which…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=71215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71231', 'Eleven Mile Canyon Auto Tour', 'scenic_drive', 38.936000, -105.406036, null, 'Pike-San Isabel National Forests', 'Eleven Mile Canyon Auto Tour is managed by the USDA Forest Service to protect its rich natural resources and historic sites, and to provide public recreation. The focal point along this nine-mile route is the South Platte River which begins high above Fairplay and flows in a southeasternly direction across South Park. Below, Elevenmile Reservoir, the river turns northeast and cuts into the Pikes Peak batholith- a large mass of igneous rock. Originally called "Granite Canyon," the towering walls are composed of Pikes Peak granite that have been polished gray from years of weathering. In places…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/psicc/recarea/?recid=71231', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71233', 'Camp 32', 'campground', 48.835156, -115.194631, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Camp 32 campground is located 15 miles southwest of Eureka off Pinkham Creek road 7182. The campground 8 sites with tables, fire rings. Accommodating up to a 20'' rv. Amenities include potable water, vault toilets and a large open field. Camp 32 was a logging camp established in 1924 by the Bonners Ferry Lumber Company and operated for approximately 2 years. The land was acquired from early homesteader, Margaret Durall. The site included several out buildings. A company store and several small cabins.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=71233', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71234', 'Tobacco River Campground', 'campground', 48.894383, -115.134986, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Tobacco River Campground is located approximately 5 miles west of Eureka off Pidgeon Bridge Road 7277. The campground has 6 sites, tables and fire rings. The access road is able to accommodate up to a 20'' rv. Access and campground roads are gravel. Amenities include a vault toilet and an undeveloped boat ramp for small packable boats.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=71234', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71236', 'Swisher Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.968789, -115.133681, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Swisher Lake Campground is located 8 miles northwest of Eureka on Sophie Bay road 7160. The campground has 4 sites with tables and fire rings. Amenities include a vault toilet, hitching rack and easy access to the lake. The access road to the campground is 0.42 miles long and closed to all motorized traffic. This campground is popular with horsemen and hikers.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=71236', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71252', 'Reservoir C Campground', 'campground', 41.660278, -120.773889, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Close to the boat ramp and right on the water, campsites at Reservoir C are quiet, scenic and partly shaded. A recommended spot for amateur astronomers; light pollution is non-existent.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71252', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71258', 'Blue Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.142778, -120.280000, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Blue Lake Campground Blue Lake Campground is located on a gentle slope above beautiful Blue Lake. Forty-Eight large and well spaced sites offer plenty of shade. A three-mile trail surrounds the lake with a paved section of trail along the east shore between the campground and the boat ramp. Assistance will be required for persons in wheelchairs. Blue Lake Group Site Group site reservations must be made at least one day in advance though Recreation.gov or by calling (877) 444-6777. At least three camp pads should be occupied on the first night. This site is not recommended for gatherings over…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71258', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71260', 'Cave Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.978611, -120.204444, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'The campground at Cave Lake is lightly used and can be the perfect place for a weekend or week long getaway. Deer hunting season, in the fall, is the busiest time of year.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71260', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71262', 'Stough Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 41.562222, -120.254167, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Stough Reservoir Campground is only one mile off Hwy 299 on a gravel road. At 6,200 feet it provides relief from the heat of the valleys on either side. Small trailers and motorhomes will find access and turnarounds manageable. The reservoir is small but is kept stocked by the California Department of Fish and Wildlife. Campsites sit away from the shore with nice views of the reservoir. Stough Reservoir is Number 4 on the Basin & Range Birding Trail. Bring you camera and binoculars and expect to see Prairie Falcons, Rufous Hummingbirds and Wild Turkeys.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71262', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71264', 'Patterson Campground', 'campground', 41.198001, -120.187007, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Patterson Campground is located on the southern end of the South Warner Wilderness area. This is an ideal site to begin one''s hike of the Summit Trail. Patterson is a family camp with only 6 sites for tents and small campers and trailers. Equestrian camping is not advisable in Patterson Campground, consider staying at East Creek Campground instead. Patterson Guard Station Directly adjacent to Patterson Campground is Patterson Guard Station. Built in 1921 and renovated in 2022, this cabin is now available for overnight rentals through Rec.gov Reserve Now', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71264', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71266', 'Mill Creek Falls Campground', 'campground', 41.276667, -120.288056, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Located on the edge of the South Warner Wilderness this campground is nestled in the thick pine forests above Jess Valley at the south end of the Warner Mountains. It''s easy access makes for a perfect weekend get away.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71266', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71270', 'Ash Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.161389, -120.828056, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'The low elevation for the Ash Creek Campground allows it to open earlier in the season than others at higher elevations. Fishing is always good at Ash Creek as it is stocked by the California Department of Fish and Wildlife. There are lots of good spots for fly fishing within walking distance of the campground. Please do not create resource damage by driving on soft roads or saturated soil. Remember the weather can change quickly and you do not want to be unprepared for extreme conditions. There is a boil water advisory. Located just past Ash Creek Campground is the Red Tail Rim Trail south…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71270', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71272', 'Willow Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.013056, -120.828056, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Willow Creek Campground is the best kept secret in northern California. This small campground (8 sites) is easy to find, easy to navigate in and out with small trailers and motor homes and never full. A tiny creek runs between the campground and the day use picnic area. Lots of shade trees muffle the sounds of the highway. No water available!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71272', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71274', 'Lower Rush Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.293333, -120.878056, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Shady campsites and a creek running along side make Lower Rush Creek Campground a great getaway destination. Trailers larger than 22 feet are not recommended. No potable water is available at this campground. In the winter months roads may become soft or impassable. Please do not create resource damage by driving on soft roads or saturated soil. Remember the weather can change quickly and you do not want to be unprepared for extreme conditions.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71274', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71276', 'Howard''s Gulch Campground', 'campground', 41.485833, -120.968889, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Set back off the highway in a tree lined gulch this campground is a very quiet and pleasant place to spend the weekend or your entire vacation. A short hiking trail is available for nature viewing as this is one of the several Basin and Range Birding Trail stops within the Modoc National Forest. A recent dedication of the Highway 139 Auto Tour and Howard''s Gulch Interpretive Sites brings an added benefit to this area. The Auto Tour is just south of the campground on the Howard''s Gulch Frontage Road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71276', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71280', 'Medicine Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 41.585840, -121.585570, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'The popular Medicine Lake Recreation Area and adjacent Medicine Lake are located in the Medicine Lake Highlands in northeastern California. The Recreation Area is located in the Modoc National Forest at an elevation of 6,770 feet. See also Little Medicine Lake Picnic Area Natural Features: Medicine Lake Recreation Area is nestled along Medicine Lake and mostly sheltered by mature lodgepole pine trees but can be windy at times. The Recreation Area lies adjacent to the Medicine Lake Lava Flow which is accessible by a short hike. The Glass Mtn. and Burnt Lava Flow Geologic Areas are located…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71280', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71286', 'Payne Springs Campground', 'campground', 41.554722, -121.560833, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Located in the scenic Medicine Lake Highlands, Payne Springs is surrounded by many attractions. This campground is adjacent to the Modoc Volcanic Scenic Byway and the Lava Beds National Monument is located near by. It is a great place to visit and learn about the local geology and history. There is no drinking water. There are picnic tables and fire pits at each site with fair road conditions getting to the sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71286', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71288', 'Emerson Campground', 'campground', 41.263889, -120.137778, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Located on the east side of the South Warner Wilderness, this campground and picnic area also serve as the staging area for the Emerson Trail into the wilderness. This free campground is fairly secluded due to the narrow, steep, rough, dirt access road. Campsites are mostly shady and set back from the parking area in the trees. There is no water at Emerson Campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71288', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71290', 'Reservoir F Campground', 'campground', 41.579444, -120.873611, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'The campsites at Reservoir F are spacious and close to the shoreline. The early morning sun greets campers from across the lake as the afternoons are shaded by the tall pines.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71290', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71292', 'Big Sage Campground', 'campground', 41.578889, -120.628056, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Big Sage Reservoir and campground are surrounded by juniper woodland and sagebrush. The reservoir is several thousand acres and the campground lies on the shore near the boat ramp.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71292', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71294', 'Lassen Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.826111, -120.295000, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Lassen Creek Campground is a lovely little campground near the obsidian collection areas. This campground has picnic tables and fire rings.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71294', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71296', 'Pepperdine Campground', 'campground', 41.450278, -120.240833, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Formerly used as a family camp and a horse camp, the horse corrals are now located at the Pepperdine Equestrian Campground. The family campsites are mostly shaded and enjoy serene surroundings for an enjoyable camping experience. The Summit Trail begins here and heads south into the South Warner Wilderness . No wilderness permits are required however, if you plan to use a camp or backpack stove or charcoal barbeque or have a campfire outside the developed campground, you will need a current California Campfire Permit .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71296', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71300', 'Jane''s Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 41.879811, -120.764000, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'This campground, located some 30 miles north of Alturas along Crowder Flat Road should be known for it''s true beauty and solitude. The campground circles the south-eastern section of the lake. A dirt boat-ramp is located just to the north of the entrance road. No drinking water is supplied at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71300', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71302', 'Blanche Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.557331, -121.570219, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Blanche Lake and Campground are located a few miles southeast of Medicine Lake and offer campers a little more seclusion than that of the larger lake area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71302', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71304', 'Red Tail Rim Trail South Trailhead', 'campground', 41.167467, -120.829722, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'The Red Tail Rim Trail South Trailhead is the staging area for riding, hiking or mountain biking the Red Tail Rim Trail. There are hitching posts but no corrals. This trail is not a loop. The opposite trailhead is located at Red Tail Rim Trail North, about 8 miles north of Adin along Hwy 299/139. Ash Creek Campground is located south of this trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71304', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71328', 'Doorknob Warming Hut Snowpark', 'snow_area', 41.671667, -121.561944, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'Part of the Tri-Forest Snowmobile trails system, Doorknob offers access to over 250 miles of snowmobile trails on the Modoc, Shasta Trinity and Klamath National Forests. In the summer the area is a popular picnic and day hiking spot. Door Knob has a warming shelter open to all snow enthusiasts. There is a wood stove inside and firewood in the covered area outside. For snowmobile trail conditions please see: https://www.fs.usda.gov/detail/klamath/recreation/?cid=stelprdb5110665', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71328', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71382', 'Schonchin Springs Campground', 'campground', 41.591944, -121.616667, null, 'Modoc National Forest', 'This little campground is approximately 1 mile from the Headquarters Campground and gets most of its use when the four other Medicine Lake Campgrounds are full. If you are looking for close proximity to the lake but would prefer a quiet, more secluded environment, try Schonchin Springs Campground. Map of the campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/modoc/recarea/?recid=71382', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71417', 'Middle Piney Entrance Winter Trailhead', 'snow_area', 42.608086, -110.479350, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Middle Piney Entrance Winter Trailhead is located at the Forest Boundary and the Middle Piney Road, WY-350. From this trailhead, snowmobilers can head south to Snider Basin and the Tri-Basin Divide, or north to North and South Cottonwood and McDougal Gap.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71417', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71421', 'Middle Piney Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.602966, -110.565440, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Middle Piney Lake Campground is located on beautiful Middle Piney Lake, and is a no fee camp site. There is a vault toilet that is cleaned and maintained regularly, but no trash or water services. This is a pack-in/pack-out site. Enjoy a spectacular view of the lake and great fishing. There is a boat ramp at the lake, but Wyoming Game and Fish regulations allow non-motorized and electric powered boats on the lake. The trailhead to access the Wyoming Range National Recreation Trail and Wyoming Peak are located at this campground; and visitors are a short drive away from the North Piney Lake…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71421', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71427', 'North Horse Creek SnowmobileTrailhead', 'snow_area', 42.949849, -110.382670, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The North Horse Creek Winter Trailhead provides access to some of the best snowmobiling in the country. From the trailhead riders can jump on the Blind Bull/North Horse Creek Snowmobile trail and head to the top of the Wyoming Range and down into the Grey''s River. For more adventurous off trail riders the North Horse Creek area offers open powder fields and challenging climbs. Check with local Avalanche forecasters before you go to check on snow conditions.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71427', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71437', 'Sacajawea Campground', 'campground', 42.618471, -110.531080, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Sacajawea Campground is located on the Middle Piney Road just east of Middle Piney Lake. The campground is in a cool shaded area, surrounded by trees, located on Middle Piney Creek. The campground has toilets, water and trash service, there are sites large enough to accommodate trailers, but has not trailer hookups. A campground host is present typically July 1 - Labor Day. Sacajawea Campground puts visitors in the heart of the Big Piney Ranger District with quick access to the Wyoming Range National Recreation Trail, Middle Piney Lake, North Piney Lake ATV trail and the historic Lander…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71437', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71479', 'Hatchet Campground', 'campground', 43.824725, -110.355198, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Located along Highway 26, the Hatchet campground offers a great place to stop for the night when travelling the scenic highway between Jackson and Dubois, Wyoming. Opportunities for fishing designated wild and scenic rivers are available nearby. During the fall hunting season, this campground offers a popular staging area. This site is equipped with 9 campsites, accessibility to bear boxes, access to water, a single-unit vault toilet, campfire rings, and a dumpster.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71479', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71493', 'Pacific Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.939366, -110.442942, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Pacific Creek Campground is located next to the Teton Wilderness boundary at the north end of Pacific Creek Road, approximately 9.5 miles from the Moran entrance station. The campground is equipped with 7 standard campsites and 1 pull through site. There are corrals and hitching posts for horses, a stock tank, two double vault toilets, three game storage poles, and accessibility to bear boxes. Please be aware that there is no water provided, plan accordingly. Visitors can access the Pacific Creek Trailhead which is a popular route into Hawk''s Rest and the Thorofare. Campground closes…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71493', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71503', 'Sheffield Campground', 'campground', 44.098103, -110.668122, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Sheffield Campground is located in the northeast corner of the Buffalo Ranger District, just outside of the John D. Rockefeller Parkway. Heading north on Highway 191 to Yellowstone, take a right onto the Forest Service dirt road before you get to the Snake River Bridge just before Flagg Ranch. The campground sits just outside of the Teton Wilderness. This location is equipped with 5 campsites, a single-unit vault toilet, access to bear boxes, and campfire rings. Nearby, visitors can access the wilderness via Sheffield Trailhead which provides access to the historic Huckleberry Lookout.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71503', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71517', 'Turpin Meadow Campground', 'campground', 43.857148, -110.268730, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Turpin Meadow Campground is located 17-miles East of Moran Junction on the Buffalo Valley Road. It is outfitted with 14 standard campsites, 4 pull through sites, 2 double-unit vault restrooms, and 1 single-unit vault restroom. It is also equipped with corrals, hitching posts, water access, a stock tank, accessibility to bear boxes, dumpsters, and a game storage pole. There are corrals and designated places to tether stock.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71517', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71527', 'Allred Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.485220, -110.961605, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Allred Flat Campground is located approximately 20 miles south of Afton, Wyoming on the south side of Salt River Pass. The campground is adjacent to Little White Creek, with beaver ponds and bird-watching opportunities. Pine and aspen trees offer partial shade and summer wildflowers are abundant. Hiking, mountain biking, and horseback riding trails aren''t far away, ranging from easy 1/2-mile long paths to challenging 14-mile trails into the backcountry. Nearby Smiths Fork Road offers many miles of scenic driving, especially fun with side-by-side vehicles, with beautiful views of the Wyoming…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71527', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71545', 'Cottonwood Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.638650, -110.818263, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Cottonwood Lake Campground is located next to Cottonwood Lake in the Salt River Mountains at an elevation of 7,000 feet, approximately 13 miles southeast of Afton, Wyoming. North Fork Creek runs near this site where pines and aspens offer partial shade. The lake offers great boating for smaller craft (there is no ramp available) and fishing for brook and cutthroat trout. Trails for hiking, biking, horseback riding, and ATVs begin within the site. This campground offers 18 campsites total. On the west loop, 6 sites have hitching rails for horses, and three small pipe-rail horse corrals are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71545', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71555', 'Forest Park Campground', 'campground', 42.831170, -110.691685, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Forest Park Campground is located 34 miles from the north end of the Greys River Road, shaded under tall pines. 13 campsites share a hand pump; vault toilets are available at both ends of the large loop. Sites accommodate trailers up to 30 feet long. Many nearby trails and forest roads are available for exploration, including a number of roads well suited for side-by-side trail vehicles. Free Motor Vehicle Use Maps help visitors know more about those opportunities. They are are available at Forest Service Offices or for download from our website. This web page also includes info about a free…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71555', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71559', 'Greys River Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 43.155642, -111.003369, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Large parking area accommodates many trucks and trailers; toilet on site. Groomed snowmobile trailhead is closed to wheeled vehicles from Dec. 1 through May 1.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71559', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71577', 'Moose Flat Campground', 'campground', 42.971707, -110.768736, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Moose Flat Campground is located along the Greys River, 22 miles from the north end of the Greys River Road. Ten campsites accommodate trailers up to 30 feet long; visitors are limited to a 14 day stay. Pearson Creek Trailhead, which begins with a river ford, is adjacent to campground. Potable water via a hand pump and vault toilets are both available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71577', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71579', 'Murphy Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.073667, -110.836057, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Murphy Creek Campground is located 14 miles up from the north end of the Greys River Road at Alpine. Ten campsites are available and there is a 14 day stay limit. Sites accommodate trailers up to 30 feet with one 70'' pull-through. Water is available as well as a vault toilet; no hookups are provided. Free Motor Vehicle Use Maps help visitors know more about those kinds of opportunities and are available at Forest Service Offices or for download from our website. This webpage also includes info about a free map app for smartphones.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71579', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71605', 'Smiths Fork Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 42.528433, -110.897940, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The parking area is just alongside Hwy 89 on the east side of the road. This trailhead is the southern terminus of Trail A, with connections to Trails L and H. Snowmobilers can reserve LaBarge or Cazier Guard Stations; safety shelters are available at Poker Hollow and Poison Meadows.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71605', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71613', 'Swift Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.725167, -110.906586, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', '*** This site is closed until further notice due to erosion and the need for public safety *** Seven shady campsites are nestled at the base of the Salt River Range right along the musical Swift Creek just outside Afton, Wyoming. A single faucet is available at site 1, and an accessible toilet is provided in the center of the campground. Large picnic tables welcome family groups for meals.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71613', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71623', 'Atherton Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.638548, -110.522141, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Atherton Creek Campground is located on Lower Slide Lake. This is a beautiful and quiet camping location where you can quickly and easily get away from the hustle and bustle of Grand Teton National Park and Jackson, but still access those places in less than 30 minutes if you wish. The road access is paved up to the campground and winds through aspen stands with gorgeous views of the Gros Ventre River. Boat and fishing access are excellent for Lower Slide Lake, allowing for great trout fishing and peaceful evenings floating around looking for wildlife.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71623', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71627', 'Crystal Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.610451, -110.431422, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Crystal Creek Campground is located along the Gros Ventre River and Crystal Creek, both designated Wild and Scenic Rivers for the spectacular surrounding scenery and excellent fishing opportunities. This is a small and peaceful campground that has several nearby options for hiking, biking and OHV riding. Sites 1 - 3 are accessible, while sites 4 - 6 are damaged by river erosion and are unusable. Overflow campground across road is Open and usable as well. Caution advised when recreating near river bank.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71627', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71629', 'Curtis Canyon Campground', 'campground', 43.513818, -110.661172, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Curtis Canyon Campground is a great place to camp if you want to be close to town but still off the beaten path. This wooded campground is located above the National Elk Refuge and a quick walk from your campsite will reward you with amazing views of the Refuge and the Teton mountain range. Hiking and horseback riding are all easy to achieve just minutes from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71629', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71631', 'East Table Campground', 'campground', 43.212844, -110.807709, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'East Table Campground is located along the designated Wild and Scenic Snake River. The campground offers excellent views of the surrounding mountains and the river, and is nicely wooded to shelter visitors from the highway. For general information about the Snake River Canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71631', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71637', 'Granite Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.359580, -110.446633, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Granite Creek Campgound is a large wooded campground nestled in the valley between high mountain peaks very near to the Gros Ventre Wilderness. The campground is located next to designated Wild and Scenic Granite Creek, offering excellent fishing opportunities right next to the campground. Nearby is the popular Granite Creek Hot Springs which is great fun for all ages for soaking in the water and the view after a hard day of recreating. Multiple trails are available very close to the campground and throughout the Granite Creek corridor for hiking, horseback riding and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71637', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71649', 'Hoback Campground', 'campground', 43.281511, -110.593578, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Hoback Campground is situated along the designated Wild and Scenic Hoback River. This is a small but pretty campground that offers excellent fishing just a few minutes walk from your campsite. If you want to visit the hustle and bustle of the Snake River or Jackson but wish to camp where things are quiet this is a great place to stop and rest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71649', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71657', 'Kozy Campground', 'campground', 43.270271, -110.517082, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Kozy Campground is located along the Hoback River, allowing for excellent fishing in an area of the Hoback that has less visitors. This campground is located far enough away from the hustle and bustle of the Snake River and Hoback Junction, that is makes for a quiet and peaceful spot to camp out and enjoy the outdoors.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71657', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71671', 'Station Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.205052, -110.834564, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Station Creek Campground is located along the designated Wild and Scenic Snake River. Plenty of trees make this campground cozy and quiet, making it a great place to enjoy the outdoors with your family and friends in between rafting the Snake River. This is a very busy campground so get there early to make sure you get a site as only the group sites are reserveable. General information on the Snake River Canyon .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71671', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71681', 'Wolf Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.198505, -110.903378, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Wolf Creek Campground offers great views of the Snake River Canyon. This is the largest campground in the Snake River Canyon with many sites available and it rarely fills, so if you are arriving late in the day this might be your campground. This campground also offers for folks looking to boat on the designated wild and scenic Snake River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71681', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71701', 'Hams Fork Campground', 'campground', 42.251600, -110.730435, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Hams Fork Campground is located on the Big Spring Scenic Backway or Hams Fork Road, Forest Road #10062, north of Kemmerer. The Campground has 13 sites, 2 vault toilets, potable water, and trash service in the summer. The Hams Fork Campground is a good base camp for recreating on the south end of the Kemmerer Ranger District with just a short drive to Big Spring for a picnic, a nice long scenic drive up Hobble Creek, a variety of hiking trails, and fantastic fishing in the Hams Fork River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71701', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71707', 'Hobble Creek Campground', 'campground', 42.397983, -110.783954, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Hobble Creek Campground is a beautiful and remote campsite on the Kemmerer Ranger District. The Hobble Creek Campground is located at the trailhead to Lake Alice and offers 18 campsites, toilet, trash and potable water in the summer on fish-filled Hobble Creek. Corrals are available for stock. Lake Alice, is a short 1.5 mile hike east from the campground. Trailers longer than 30 feet are not recomended. The Hobble Creek Campground is also located close to the Hobble Creek Trailhead where visitors and continue along Hobble Creek and eventually connect in to the historic Lander Cutoff of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71707', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71739', 'Big Sandy Campground', 'campground', 42.687767, -109.270787, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'This campground is located at the north end of the Big Sandy Opening, along Big Sandy Creek approximately 60 miles southeast of Pinedale, Wyoming. It is a smaller campground, with 4 sites in the main loop and additional site near the Stock Trailhead for those visitors with horses. The campground is located next to Big Sandy Trailhead, which leads some of the most popular destinations in the Bridger Wilderness. Popular activities in the area include hiking, fishing, hunting, horseback riding, and photography. This is a primitive campground, there is no drinking water and you are required to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71739', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71745', 'Boulder Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.856726, -109.617295, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Boulder Lake Campground is location 25 miles southeast of Pinedale, Wyoming. This campground sits on the east end of Boulder Lake, near Boulder Creek. There are 15 sites available, each are equipped with a picnic table, fire ring and a lantern holder. Recreational activities include backpacking, day hiking, fishing (creek and lake), nature photography and swimming. There is no drinking water available onsite and proper food storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71745', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71755', 'Fremont Lake Campground and Group Campground', 'campground', 42.946390, -109.791940, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Fremont Lake Campground is located on the east shore of pristine Fremont Lake at an elevation of 7,400 feet, just 7 miles northeast of Pinedale, Wyoming, the nearest full-service community. Water sports and fishing are popular activities on the scenic lake. Natural Features : Fremont Lake sits at the foot of the rugged Wind River Range, known for its craggy granite peaks and sparkling glacial lakes. The campground is situated on a forested hillside above the lake. Aspen, Douglas fir, juniper and a dense understory provide shade and privacy between campsites. Recreation : The lake provides…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71755', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71759', 'Green River Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.315574, -109.863173, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Green River Lakes Campground is located near the shores of beautiful Lower Green River Lake, at an elevation of 8,000 feet. Visitors enjoy hiking and backpacking into the adjacent Bridger Wilderness, as well as fishing and canoeing on the lake. Square Top Mountain towers over scenic Green River Lakes. This unique peak is part of the Wind River Range and tops out at an elevation of 11,581 feet. Most campsites afford scenic views of the peak and the lake below. Lodgepole pines dot the campground, offering very limited shade. Wildlife and summer wildflowers are abundant in the area. The access…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71759', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71769', 'Half Moon Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.936513, -109.759356, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Half Moon Lake Campground is situated just off the northeast shore of Half Moon Lake. Heavy willow stands provide excellent privacy between sites and an Aspen over-story provide shade among the 17 sites. Visitors enjoy water sports such as boating, swimming, canoeing and paddle boarding right from the beach within the campground. Two miles down the gravel road is an excellent hiking trail for users of all abilities. This is a primitive campground, the access road is not paved, drinking water is not available, and proper Food Storage is Required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71769', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71789', 'The Narrows Campground', 'campground', 43.104826, -109.942607, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The Narrows Campground is located next to scenic New Fork Lake, at the edge of the Wind River Range in northwestern Wyoming. The campground is situated in a dense grove of aspens, at an elevation of 7,800 feet. Shade is plentiful and most sites afford scenic lake views. Visitors enjoy hiking and horseback riding into the adjacent Bridger Wilderness, as well as boating and fishing on the lake. The access road to the campground is not paved, drinking water is not available, and proper Food Storage is Required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71789', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71791', 'New Fork Group Campground', 'campground', 43.082116, -109.970341, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'Located just 24 miles north of Pinedale, this group site campground includes large picnic tables, BBQ stands, a fire ring, and a double vault toilet for your large party needs. Just a short hike away is New Fork Lake, which offers great boating, canoeing and swimming. Anglers fish for kokanee salmon, brook, lake and rainbow trout. A boat ramp is located approximately 1 mile from the group site. There is no drinking water available and proper Food Storage is Required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71791', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71795', 'New Fork Lake Campground', 'campground', 43.081104, -109.967952, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'New Fork Lake Campground is located right on the lake shore of New Fork Lake, among a grove of aspens. This site has a great day use beach adjacent to the campground, with a sandy beach providing fun for the whole family. The 1,070-acre New Fork Lake offers great boating, canoeing and swimming. Anglers fish for kokanee salmon and brook, lake and rainbow trout. A boat ramp is located a mile and a half from the campground, at the lake''s northwestern shore. This is a primitive campground, the access road is not paved, drinking water is not available, and proper Food Storage is Required. Fish…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71795', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71825', 'Whiskey Grove Campground', 'campground', 43.253887, -110.018556, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'This campground is located in the Upper Green River valley, situated right on the Green River. Conifer trees dominate the over-story in this smaller campground of 9 sites. Each site provides a picnic table, fire ring and a Food Storage Box. Drinking water is provided in the form of a hand-pump near the entrance of the campground. Campers enjoy fishing the river, scenic day trips, hunting, and nature photography. Access to this campground is via a dirt road approximately 4 miles from the end of the pavement.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71825', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71829', 'Willow Lake Campground', 'campground', 42.991111, -109.900264, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'This campground is located on the south shore of Willow Lake, 14 miles north of Pinedale on a dirt road. This is an undeveloped campground and receives minimal levels of maintenance. Few sites within the camp area provide picnic tables and fire rings. A boat launch and a vault toilet service the entire dispersed area. This lake has great views of the Wind River Range and is popular for its boating and fishing. Please remember proper Food Storage is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=71829', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71836', 'Pine Valley Recreation Area', 'campground', 37.379658, -113.475060, null, 'Dixie National Forest', 'Pine Valley Recreation Area is situated in a beautiful valley surrounded by the Pine Valley Mountains. There are several compgrounds with sites for single families, large groups, motorhomes, and horses. See the list of campgrounds below in the camping and campgrounds tab to find the type of site that best suits your needs. Map of Pine Valley Recreation Area. Trails in the area include: Brown''s Point Trail Equestrian Trail Whipple Trail Pine Valley Canal Trail Gardner Peak Trail', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dixie/recarea/?recid=71836', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71882', 'Dean Gardner Campground', 'campground', 37.377191, -113.477391, null, 'Dixie National Forest', 'Located near Pine Valley Wilderness and adjacent to Pine Valley Reservoir , this new campground offers campsites that are shaded by large Ponderosa pine trees. Horse riding, fishing, and hiking are popular in this area. Bike riding opportunities and horse trails are nearby. Several trails including the Whipple , Brown''s Point , and Gardner Peak lead into the Pine Valley Wilderness area. Facilities 21 single campsites (up to 8 people) with picnic tables, fire pits, and tent pads 3 double sites (up to 16 people) with picnic tables, fire pits, and tent pads Drinking water (Memorial Day-Labor…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dixie/recarea/?recid=71882', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '71884', 'Mitt Moody Campground', 'campground', 37.375567, -113.457035, null, 'Dixie National Forest', 'The Mitt Moody sites range from being tucked away in the hillside to one that overlooks a nearby stream. All items need to be packed in by foot via a short walking trail. Parking is limited to one vehicle per site. The trailhead for the Pine Valley Canal Trail and the Santa Clara River Trail begin from this loop. The Mitt Moody loop offers a more secluded primitive camping experience compared to the other loops in the Pine Valley Recreation Area. Facilities 2 single walk-in tent sites (up to 8 people) 1 double site (up to 16 persons) Drinking water (Memorial Day-Labor Day) Vault toilets No…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dixie/recarea/?recid=71884', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72084', 'Haystack West Shore Campground and Day Use Area', 'campground', 44.493824, -121.160494, null, 'Ochoco National Forest', 'This scenic, high desert campground and day use area is located on the western shore of Haystack Reservoir . There is one fully accessible campsite as well as easy access from the Day Use parking area to the boat ramp. This site is managed by Crook County Parks and Recreation District. For more information on the site and to make reservations, visit: https://ccprd.org/camping/haystack-reservoir/ View a map of Haystack Reservoir West Shore Campground . Also, see Haystack Reservoir Campground and Day Use Area and the Haystack Reservoir South Shore Group Campground .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ochoco/recarea/?recid=72084', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72088', 'Haystack South Shore Group Campground', 'campground', 44.489755, -121.152296, null, 'Ochoco National Forest', 'Haystack South Shore Group Campground is the only group campground on Haystack Reservoir . This facility contains two group campsites, each of which holds up to 75 people, making it ideal for large events such as family reunions, or groups of rock climbers visiting the nearby Smith Rock State Park . The facility is operated by Crook County Parks and Recreation District. For more information on how to reserve sites, visit: https://ccprd.org/camping/haystack-reservoir/ View a map of the Haystack South Shore Group Campground . Also, see the Haystack Reservoir Campground and Day Use Area and the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ochoco/recarea/?recid=72088', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72141', 'Antelope Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.965687, -109.554436, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Antelope Flat Campground lies on the shores of the beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir at an elevation of 6,000 feet, on the Ashley National Forest within the Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area. Visitors love Antelope Flat for its easy access to boating, water skiing and fishing. Nearly every site within the campground offers scenic reservoir and mountain views. Russian olive trees and cottonwoods dot the rolling, sagebrush-covered landscape. Shade is limited, and temperatures range from warm days to cool nights. Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area is known not only for its beautiful red…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72141', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72143', 'Lodgepole Campground', 'campground', 40.813799, -109.466344, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Lodgepole Campground is settled near beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir just 26 miles north of Vernal, Utah, at an elevation of 8,000 feet. Visitors enjoy exploring local trails and day-tripping to the reservoir, only 10 miles away. A scenic aspen forest dotted with pines covers the campground, offering pleasant shade and pretty fall color. Summer wildflowers are abundant in this shady, secluded campground. Don''t Move Firewood: Help prevent the spread of tree-killing pests in our national forests by obtaining firewood near your destination and burning it on-site. Firewood is available for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72143', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72147', 'Pole Creek Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.679047, -110.056923, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Pole Creek Campground is located atop Pole Creek Mountain in a scenic lodgepole pine and Engelmann spruce forest, elevation 10,000 feet. Pole Creek Lake is a five-minute walk from the campground, offering pretty views and rainbow trout fishing. Trailheads for both hikers and ATVs are nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72147', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72149', 'Lucerne Campground', 'campground', 40.986871, -109.592120, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Lucerne Campground is located on the shore of Flaming Gorge Reservoir at an elevation of 6,100 feet. The campground is situated in a high desert landscape with sagebrush and a few scattered trees. Natural shade is minimal. Fishing, boating, canoeing, water skiing and swimming are popular activities on the lake. Campers are offered the convenience of an adjacent boat ramp, marina and fish cleaning station. Lucerne Marina has boat rentals, fuel, slips, fishing licenses, bait and groceries. Showers are available throughout the campground. A dump station is located on-site. The amphitheater…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72149', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72151', 'Buckboard Crossing Campground', 'campground', 41.249050, -109.597078, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Buckboard Crossing Campground is located on the far northwest shore of Flaming Gorge Reservoir. The campground is situated in a high desert landscape with sagebrush and a few scattered trees. Natural shade is minimal. Campers are offered the convenience of an adjacent boat ramp, marina and fish cleaning station. Buckboard Marina has a boat ramp, boat rentals, fuel, slips, fishing licenses, bait and groceries. Non-campers can use the shower facilities for a small fee. A dump station and trash collection is located on-site. Don''t Move Firewood: Help prevent the spread of tree-killing pests in…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72151', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72153', 'Mustang Ridge Campground', 'campground', 40.928266, -109.443542, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Mustang Ridge Campground is located on a high desert bluff above beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir. The reservoir can be accessed within a half-mile of the campground. The campground is situated among a dense pinyon pine and juniper forest dotted with sagebrush. The vegetation provides privacy between campsites but only partial shade. The outer loop campsites are on the edge of the ridge and offer expansive views of the reservoir. A boat ramp is adjacent to the campground, offering great access to boating, water skiing and fishing on the reservoir. Sunny Cove Day Use Area is within a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72153', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72155', 'Red Canyon Campground', 'campground', 40.893333, -109.558333, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Red Canyon Campground is located in a grassy meadow high above Flaming Gorge Reservoir, along Red Canyon Road. Visitors enjoy exploring the Red Canyon Rim Trail and canoeing and fishing at Greens Lake. The campground lies close to beautiful cliffs overlooking Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Lodgepole and ponderosa pines dot the campground, providing limited shade. Summer wildflowers are plentiful. Nearby Greens Lake offers great canoeing and fishing for rainbow and brook trout. Red Canyon Lodge sits on the shore. Canoe and bike rentals, horseback riding, a restaurant and gift shop are available. Red…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72155', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72157', 'Iron Mine Campground', 'campground', 40.554995, -110.887337, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Iron Mine Campground in nestled in the scenic North Fork Drainage off Highway 35, about 18 miles from Tabiona, Utah. The North Fork Drainage lies on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains in northeastern Utah. Visitors enjoy fly-fishing and exploring many local trails. Natural Features: The campground is situated in an aspen forest dotted with subalpine fir, lodgepole pine and spruce near the North Fork Duchesne River at an elevation of 7,400 feet. The campground affords beautiful scenic views of the surrounding canyon and summer wildflowers are plentiful. Recreation: Fishing for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72157', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72159', 'Dripping Springs Campground', 'campground', 40.923371, -109.356505, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Dripping Springs Campground is situated in the rolling high desert terrain near Flaming Gorge Reservoir. The campground is part of the Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. Campers frequent Dripping Springs for its close proximity to the Green River and Little Hole, both of which offer excellent rafting and world-class fishing opportunities. Nearly every site within the campground offers scenic reservoir and mountain views. Russian olive trees and cottonwoods dot the rolling, sagebrush-covered landscape and shade is limited. Dripping Springs is surrounded by…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72159', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72161', 'Hades Campground', 'campground', 40.534008, -110.872058, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Hades Campground is nestled in the scenic North Fork Drainage off Highway 35, about 17 miles from Tabiona, Utah. The North Fork Drainage lies on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains in northeastern Utah. Visitors enjoy fly-fishing and exploring the many local trails. Natural Features: The campground is situated in forest of aspen, subalpine fir, lodgepole pine and spruce just above the North Fork Duchesne River at an elevation of 7,400 feet. The campground affords beautiful scenic views of the surrounding canyon and summer wildflowers are plentiful. Recreation: Fishing for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72161', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72163', 'Yellowpine Campground', 'campground', 40.535378, -110.641552, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Yellowpine Campground is located next to Rock Creek in the Rock Creek Drainage on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains. Visitors enjoy fishing and exploring the popular Rock Creek Trail. This is Yellowpine Campground in Rock Creek Canyon; it is not on the Mirror Lake Highway near Kamas, Utah. Natural Features: This shaded campground is situated among towering Ponderosa pines at an elevation of 7,200 feet. Aspens and summer wildflowers dot the landscape. Rock Creek flows alongside the campground. Evenings in this area are cool. Recreation: Rock Creek offers fishing for brown,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72163', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72165', 'Aspen Campground', 'campground', 40.495710, -110.844271, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Aspen Campground is nestled in the scenic North Fork Drainage just off Highway 35, about 13 miles from Tabiona, Utah. The North Fork Drainage lies on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains in northeastern Utah. Visitors enjoy fly-fishing and exploring the many local trails. Natural Features: The campground is situated in a forest of aspen, subalpine fir, lodgepole pine and spruce just above the North Fork Duchesne River at an elevation of 7,200 feet. The campground affords beautiful views of the surrounding canyon and summer wildflowers are plentiful. Recreation: Fishing for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72165', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72167', 'Greendale Campground', 'campground', 40.882089, -109.458533, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Greendale Campground is located in the beautiful Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. Flaming Gorge Reservoir is nearby, offering exciting recreational activities like boating, fishing and swimming. This is a small and quiet campground. A forest of ponderosa pines towers over Greendale, offering partial shade. Beneath the trees, grasses and plentiful summer wildflowers cover the campground. Trash collection is provided. Dump stations do have a fee and are located at Antelope Flat, Deer Run, Firefighters, and Lodgepole Campgrounds. Showers are located at Deer…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72167', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72169', 'Firefighters Memorial Campground', 'campground', 40.891018, -109.457322, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Firefighters Campground is just 3 miles from beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir, within the Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. The campground serves as a memorial to three firefighters who lost their lives in the 1977 Cart Creek Fire. Visitors enjoy boating, fishing, swimming and hiking. The campground is situated on a gently-sloping hillside dotted with shady ponderosa pines and juniper. A dump station and trash collection are available. Public showers are available 2.5 miles away at Deer Run Campground for campers with proof of camping registration.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72169', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72171', 'Avintaquin Campground', 'campground', 39.882823, -110.775604, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Avintaquin Campground is located atop scenic Indian Canyon, just off Highway 191 between Duchesne and Helper, Utah. Visitors come to the area for its scenic beauty, birding and wildlife viewing opportunities and to explore the Reservation Ridge Scenic Backway. Natural Features: The campground is situated among towering Douglas fir trees at an elevation of 9,000 feet. You can see a variety of wildlife in the area, including mule deer and elk. Recreation: Reservation Ridge Scenic Backway accesses the campground. This dirt road is open to off-road vehicles, mountain biking and hiking. It offers…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72171', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72173', 'Deer Run Campground', 'campground', 40.908702, -109.446739, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Deer Run Campground is a small campground that is located in the beautiful Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. Deer Run is situated among juniper, pinyon pine and sagebrush above Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Shade is limited and the reservoir is not visible from the campground. A resident deer herd gives this site its name. A dump station and marina are located in the immediate area at Cedar Springs. Other dump stations are located at Antelope Flat, Firefighters, and Lodgepole Campgrounds. There is a fee for the use of the dump stations. Trash collection is…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72173', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72175', 'Cedar Springs Campground', 'campground', 40.908688, -109.446741, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Cedar Springs Campground is a small campground located in the beautiful Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. Flaming Gorge Reservoir and Cedar Springs Marina are less than a mile from the campground. Exciting recreational activities abound, including boating, water skiing and fishing. Cedar Springs is situated among juniper, pinyon pine and sagebrush on a hillside above Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Shade is limited but the vegetation provides good privacy between sites, many of which have scenic views of the reservoir below. A dump station, trash collection and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72175', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72177', 'Skull Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.862726, -109.527022, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Skull Creek Campground is located about 35 miles north of Vernal, Utah near Flaming Gorge Reservoir. The campground is partially shaded. Visitors enjoy hiking and biking on local trails and boating, fishing and swimming on the reservoir. Skull Creek lies in a hillside forested with ponderosa pines and aspens near Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Summer wildflowers dot the landscape. Garbage dumpster is available. There is NO WATER available at this campground. There is a fee to use the dump stations that are located at Antelope Flat, Deer Run, Firefighters, and Lodgepole. Showers are located at Deer…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72177', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72179', 'Greens Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.868616, -109.541865, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Greens Lake Campground is located next to its scenic namesake along Red Canyon Road. Visitors enjoy canoeing and fishing on the lake and exploring the Red Canyon Rim Trail. The campground lies on the shore of Greens Lake, about 1 mile from beautiful cliffs overlooking Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Lodgepole and ponderosa pines and aspens dot the campground, providing partial shade. Summer wildflowers and grasses are plentiful. Dump stations are located at Antelope Flat, Deer Run, Firefighters, and Lodgepole and available to use for a small fee. Trash Collection is available. Showers are located at…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72179', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72181', 'Canyon Rim Campground', 'campground', 40.882511, -109.549664, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Canyon Rim Campground is located in a grassy meadow high above Flaming Gorge Reservoir, along Red Canyon Road. Visitors enjoy exploring the Red Canyon Rim Trail and canoeing and fishing at Greens Lake. The campground lies about 1 mile from beautiful cliffs overlooking Flaming Gorge Reservoir. Lodgepole and ponderosa pines dot the campground, providing limited shade. Summer wildflowers are plentiful. Garbage dumpster is available. Dump stations are located at Antelope Flat, Deer Run, Firefighters, and Lodgepole Campgrounds to use for a small fee. Showers are located at Deer Run and Mustang…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72181', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72183', 'Upper Stillwater Campground', 'campground', 40.554590, -110.698597, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Upper Stillwater Campground is located below its namesake reservoir in the Rock Creek Drainage on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains. Visitors enjoy fishing and exploring the popular Stillwater Trail. Natural Features: The campground is situated just below the Upper Stillwater Dam at an elevation of 8,000 feet. The concrete dam is visible from the campground. A forest of Ponderosa pine, lodgepole pine and aspen trees provides only sparse shade. Summer wildflowers are abundant. Recreation: The Stillwater Trail begins just outside the campground and provides access to the High…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72183', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72185', 'Browne Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.860316, -109.817411, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Browne Lake Campground is located next to a small lake on the north side of the Uinta mountains. The campground is accessed via a well-maintained dirt road. Browne Lake offers boating and fishing in Browne Lake. Check fishing season information and regulations. The campground is partially shaded by pines and aspens and sunny sagebrush meadows. Summer wildflowers dot the surrounding grassy meadows. The lake is visible from most of the sites and a short trail leads to its shore. Only group sites are reservable. Water at the campground is not potable. Gravel, narrow road that can get rough and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72185', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72187', 'Hideout Boat-In Campground', 'campground', 40.914129, -109.646455, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Hideout Boat-In Campground is located on beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir, 2 miles from the nearest road. The campground is surrounded by scenic cliffs. The campground is forested with pinyon pine and juniper, which offer only limited shade. This popular campground gets its name from a hiding spot used by Butch Cassidy and his gang. Most sites afford partial views of the reservoir. Boating, water skiing, canoeing, fishing and swimming are popular activities right out your front door. The campground is only accessible to visitors who boat or hike-in to the location. Most patrons boat to the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72187', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72189', 'Jarvies Canyon Boat-In Campground', 'campground', 40.929511, -109.478727, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Jarvies Boat-In Campground is located on beautiful Flaming Gorge Reservoir in Jarvies Canyon. Campers must boat-in to the facility , and the nearest boat ramps are located at Cedar Springs and Mustang Ridge Marinas, both 20 minutes across the water. The campground is situated among dense stands of juniper and pinyon pine on a hillside overlooking the reservoir. The vegetation offers good privacy between campsites but limited shade. Most sites have partial views of the reservoir and its surrounding red cliffs. Water and garbage service are not available. Campers are to carry out all garbage.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72189', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72191', 'Firehole Campground', 'campground', 41.347193, -109.442212, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Firehole Canyon Campground is located on the far northeastern shore of Flaming Gorge Reservoir within the Flaming Gorge Recreation Area on the Ashley National Forest. Rock Springs, Wyoming, is just 29 miles away. The campground lies in a high desert environment. Russian olive trees and sagebrush are scattered throughout the site. Shade is minimal. The site affords scenic views of the reservoir and surrounding bluffs and red rock formations. Fishing, boating, canoeing, water skiing and swimming are popular activities on the lake. Campers are offered the convenience of an adjacent boat ramp and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72191', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72193', 'Bootleg River Camp', 'campground', 40.544534, -109.174172, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Bootleg is on the north side of river on a small sandy bench 8.42 miles below the dam and 1.22 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, two tent pads, portable toilet screen and two benches. Site has natural shade. Capacity: 6 people. Hike in from Little Hole or boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses Reservations may be made for this site by calling 1-877-444-6777 or go online at…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72193', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72195', 'Cats Paw River Camp', 'campground', 40.544910, -109.173377, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Cats Paw Camp is a boat-in campsite along the north side of the Green River, located about 1.3 miles below Little Hole Boat Ramp. This area is typical of a high desert environment, with shady junipers, cottonwoods, Ponderosa pines, and summer wildflowers. This site can accommodate 6-8 people. Reservations may be made for six sites (Bootleg, Cats Paw, Cottonwood, Big Pine I, Big Pine II, and Trail''s End) by calling 1-877-444-6777 or go online at "http://www.recreation.gov". All other sites are first come, first served. Registration for campsite use must be made the day of use at Little Hole on…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72195', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72197', 'Cottonwood River Camp', 'campground', 40.544914, -109.172791, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Cottonwood is on the north side of the river 8.75 miles below the dam and 1.55 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, two tent pads, portable toilet screen and two benches. Site has natural shade. Capacity: 10 people Hike in from Little Hole or boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses Reservations may be by calling 1-877-444-6777 or reserve online at Recreation.gov . All other sites are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72197', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72201', 'Big Pine I River Camp', 'campground', 40.544207, -109.160130, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Big Pine is on north the side of river 10.5 miles below dam and 3.3 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, two tent pads, portable toilet screen and two benches. Site has natural shade. Capacity: 8 people Boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses All campers are required to have a portable toilet system. There are no garbage facilities. Please pack out your garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72201', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72203', 'Big Pine II River Camp', 'campground', 40.911669, -109.266617, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Big Pine II is on the north side of river 10.5 miles below dam and 3.3 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, four tent pads, portable toilet screen and four benches. Site has natural shade. Capacity: 12 people Boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses All campers are required to have a portable toilet system. There are no garbage facilities. Please pack out your garbage.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72203', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72205', 'Stateline Cove Campground', 'campground', 40.999793, -109.606444, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Dispersed beach camping on the sandy shore of Flaming Gorge. Located six (6) miles East of Manila, Utah on the Utah/Wyoming border. Campground has four portable and three vault toilets, some picnic tables. Terrain is high desert with no trees and sandy beaches. All sites are on a first come, first serve basis', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72205', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72207', 'Manns Campground', 'campground', 40.923387, -109.714093, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Up to 10 people can camp in each single site and up to 20 people in each double site. The campground is next to Sheep Creek. If you want to fish the creek, check the fishing regulations, there are season dates that fishing is permitted. The campground is located in flat terrain with lots of trees and bushes throughout the campground. Some sites are shaded. Children should be closely supervised while playing in or around water. No potable water​.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72207', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72209', 'Willows Campground', 'campground', 40.923333, -109.713333, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground is ran by a concessionaire. Garbage service is available. No Water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72209', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72213', 'Grizzly Ridge Meadow', 'campground', 40.753053, -109.484341, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is dispersed camping area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72213', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72215', 'North Fork Camping Area', 'campground', 40.740578, -109.681501, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'North Fork Camping Area is for dispersed camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72217', 'Kane Hollow', 'campground', 40.712203, -109.533100, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is a dispersed camping area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72217', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72219', 'South Fork Camping Area', 'campground', 40.735646, -109.738788, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This camping area has 6 sites on the South Fork of Rock Creek, near the south shore of Upper Stillwater Reservoir. There is a trail that starts from the campground area and goes north into the High Uintas Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72219', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72221', 'Windy Park Camping Area', 'campground', 40.759872, -109.639753, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is a dispersed camping area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72221', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72223', 'Range Study Area', 'campground', 40.715885, -109.476176, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is a dispersed camping area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72223', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72225', 'Massey Meadow Camping Area', 'campground', 40.624942, -109.786187, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is a dispersed camping area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72225', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72227', 'North Iron Springs', 'campground', 40.703558, -109.556134, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This is a dispersed camping area that has 2 group areas that can accomodate up to 100 campers each. Maximum RV length 25 feet. After September 10 there is no water. Please pack out your trash.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72227', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72229', 'Rock Spring Camping Area', 'campground', 40.548786, -110.696723, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Rock Spring Camping Area', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72229', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72231', 'Jackson Camping Area', 'campground', 40.011064, -110.959504, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Jackson Camping Area', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72231', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72233', 'Mill Flat Camping Area', 'campground', 40.559192, -110.887906, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Mill Flat Camping Area', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72233', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72237', 'East Park Campground', 'campground', 40.780982, -109.553209, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'There are 21 campsites on the shore of East Park Reservoir where you can fish for rainbow trout. There is a trailhead at north end of the lake that leads east to US 191, and another one at the south end that leads west to Oaks Park Lake. This is a fantastic waterfowl hunting area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72237', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72239', 'Kaler Hollow Campground', 'campground', 40.702305, -109.615406, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'There are 4 tent sites at the north end of the Taylor Mountain Plateau. The Old Carter Military Trail passes by the campground. Consult the forest map for details about specific hikes. OHV use is permitted in the area north and south of the campground. The Forest Service offers a free detailed map of the areas open to unrestricted use. Please contact the Forest Service for information about exploring the Big Brush Creek Cave.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72239', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72241', 'Oaks Park Campground', 'campground', 40.742166, -109.623593, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'There are 11 campsites on the south shore of large and lovely Oaks Park Reservoir. There is a pump handle well on the west shore of the reservoir. Trails lead north from the lake, and the area is open to OHV use. A trail leads south from the campground to the Big Brush Creek Cave. If you are interested in caving, please contact the Forest Service.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72241', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72243', 'Paradise Park Campground', 'campground', 40.394441, -109.543840, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'There are 15 campsites on the shores of Paradise Park Lake where you can fish for rainbow trout. You can take Forest Road 296 (a jeep trail) to its end and hike to a number of isolated and lovely little lakes which dot the area to the northeast of Paradise Park. The Deadman Lake Trail is open to hiking and horses and is 8.5 miles long. Drinking water is not provided. Enjoy mountain biking on nearby roads and trails (but not on wilderness trails!). The area north and east of Paradise Park is open to OHV use only on designated routes; the area south and west is fairly unrestricted. Pick up a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72243', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72245', 'Whiterocks Campground', 'campground', 40.620558, -109.941708, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground has been recently remodeled with native rock and restored to a primitive state, and does not include water. The off season is from late November to early May, depending on conditions. The campground is at approximately 7500 foot elevation, with 21 campsites, and a maximum RV length of 30 feet. Attractions include fishing in the Whiterocks River, and scenic views of Whiterocks Canyon dramatic cliff formations. The surrounding area is open to restricted OHV use, only on designated Forest Service trails. Please contact the Ashley National Forest Flaming Gorge-Vernal Ranger…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72245', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72247', 'Uinta Canyon Campground', 'campground', 40.624040, -110.139742, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground is located along the Uinta River. Fishing in the Uinta River for brown, rainbow, and cutthroat trout is a popular activity in this area. The High Uintas Wilderness trailhead is nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72247', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72249', 'Moon Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.568500, -110.508094, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Moon Lake Campground is located on the shores of the scenic two mile long Moon Lake on the southern slope of the 13,000 foot peaked Uinta Mountains. Visitors come to Moon Lake to enjoy cool mountain air, fishing, canoeing and motor boating, scenic vistas, hiking trails and horse rides. The campground include single and double sites. Natural Features: The campground is situated on the lake shore at an elevation of 8,100 feet where lodgepole pine, aspen and Douglas fir provide some shade away from the lake. Wildlife and flowers both flourish in the canyon. Recreation: Moon Lake offers great…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72249', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72251', 'Swift Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.601351, -110.348150, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'The Swift Creek Campground sits at just over 8000 feet elevation near the confluence of Swift Creek and the Yellowstone River. A lovely waterfall is nearby. The campground is near the boundary of the High Uintas Wilderness, and the trailhead from the campground leads to a number of alpine lakes. Fishing for brook, brown and rainbow trout is possible in the Yellowstone River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72251', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72253', 'Riverview Campground', 'campground', 40.590156, -110.336313, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'The Riverview Campground sits at an elevation of just under 8000 feet. Fishing in the Yellowstone River for rainbow, cutthroat, and brown trout is popular. There is trailhead access to the High Uintas Wilderness at the end of Forest Road #124 at the Swift Creek Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72253', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72255', 'Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 40.575962, -110.325200, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'The Reservoir Campground sits at an elevation of 7900 feet near the Yellowstone Reservoir and the Yellowstone River. Trailhead access to the High Uintas Wilderness is at the end of Forest Road #124 at the Swift Creek Trailhead.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72255', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72257', 'Bridge Campground', 'campground', 40.545981, -110.334212, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'The Bridge Campground is at over 7600 feet adjacent to the Yellowstone River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72257', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72259', 'Yellowstone Campground', 'campground', 40.542890, -110.336328, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Yellowstone Campground lies along its pretty namesake river on the southern slope of the Uinta Mountains, about 40 miles from Duchesne, Utah. Visitors come to the area to enjoy its extensive off-road trail system and great fishing opportunities. Natural Features: The campground sits on the banks of the Yellowstone River at an elevation of 7700 feet. A forest of aspen, maple and Ponderosa pine covers the area. Wildlife and summer wildflowers are abundant. Recreation: The Yellowstone River offers fishing for rainbow, brown, brook and cutthroat trout. The Yellowstone ATV Trail System is…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72259', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72261', 'Kingfisher Island Boat-in Campground', 'campground', 40.940367, -109.639838, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground has 8 boat-in only tent camping sites on the east shore of Kingfisher Island, a large island in the southwest arm of Flaming Gorge Reservoir. This campground has new docks and offers gorgeous views. Visitors enjoy fishing in Flaming Gorge Reservoir for mackinaw (lake trout), Utah chub, rainbow trout, channel catfish, and smallmouth bass. Nearby Activities The Green River below the dam is one of the best trout streams in the country, and is also popular among rafters and kayakers. There are over 220 miles of trails in the Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area. Sheep Canyon…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72261', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72263', 'Deep Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.854956, -109.729402, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground is at the northern edge of the Uinta Mountains. There is no water or garbage service . Nearby Activities: Elk Park Trail leads south into the mountains. There is a shorter trail that goes northwest to Summit Springs. Fishing for rainbow trout in Deep Creek is popular in this area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72263', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72265', 'Carmel Campground', 'campground', 40.930773, -109.732556, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This developed campground has interpretive displays which help you appreciate the magic of the surrounding area. Nearby Activities: Sheep Canyon Geological Area, just west of the Flaming Gorge National Recreation Area, features stunning scenic panoramas, framed by colorfully-striated cliffs.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72265', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72267', 'Spirit Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.837474, -109.999488, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'The campground is tucked into a mix of conifers and is located beside Spirit Lake. No water or garbage service is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72267', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72269', 'Stonefly I River Camp', 'campground', 40.543921, -109.175003, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Stonefly I River Camp is on the north side of river 8.2 miles below dam and 1.0 miles below Little Hole. This site has one table, one fire ring, two tent pads, a portable toilet screen and one bench. Capacity: 6-8 people Campers can hike in from Little Hole or boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses. Reservations may be made for six sites (Bootleg, Cats Paw, Cottonwood, Big Pine I, Big Pine II, and Trail''s…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72269', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72271', 'Stonefly II River Camp', 'campground', 40.543988, -109.174817, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Stonefly II is on the north side of river 8.2 miles below dam and 1.0 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, two tent pads, a portable toilet screen and one bench. Capacity: 6-8 people Hike in from Little Hole or boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses. Reservations may be made for six sites (Bootleg, Cats Paw, Cottonwood, Big Pine I, Big Pine II, and Trail''s End) by calling…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72271', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72273', 'Sand River Camp', 'campground', 40.544325, -109.174429, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Sand is on the north side of the river 8.3 miles below dam and 1.1 miles below Little Hole. Site has one table, one fire ring, three tent pads (fits up to four or five tents), portable toilet screen and two benches. Site has natural shade. Capacity: 8-10 people. Campers can hike in from Little Hole or boat in from the Spillway or Little Hole. Sites are along the banks of the Green River on Section B, downstream from Little Hole. Vegetation is Pinyon pine, juniper, sagebrush, Ponderosa pine and river bottom shrubs and grasses. Reservations may be made for six sites (Bootleg, Cats Paw,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72273', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72277', 'Sheep Creek Bay Campground', 'campground', 40.921216, -109.674832, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground is convenient to boat ramp with four sites on asphalt.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72277', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72289', 'Rock Creek Group Campground', 'campground', 40.529941, -110.611522, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Rock Creek Group Campground is located next to Rock Creek in the Rock Creek Drainage at an elevation of 7200 feet. The drainage sits on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains. Visitors enjoy fishing and exploring the popular Stillwater Trail. Natural Features: This shaded campground is set back off the main road for privacy. Dense stands of aspen and pine trees shade the campground, while sagebrush and wildflowers dot the landscape. Evenings in this area are cool. Recreation: Rock Creek offers fishing for brown, brook and rainbow trout. Whitewater rafting and kayaking…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72289', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72293', 'Miners Gulch Group Campground', 'campground', 40.533636, -110.623324, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Miners Gulch Campground is located next to Rock Creek in the Rock Creek Drainage at an elevation of 7,500 feet. The drainage sits on the southern slope of the beautiful Uinta Mountains. Visitors enjoy fishing and exploring the popular Rock Creek Trail. Natural Features: This shaded campground is set back off the main road for privacy. Dense stands of aspens shade the campground. Pines, sagebrush and wildflowers dot the landscape. Evenings in this area are cool. Recreation: Rock Creek offers fishing for brown, brook and rainbow trout. Whitewater rafting and kayaking opportunities are available…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72293', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72303', 'South Iron Springs Group Site', 'campground', 40.703388, -109.555803, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Iron Springs Group Campground is located approximately five miles off US Highway 191 along meandering Red Cloud Loop Scenic Backway next to a grassy meadow bordered by shady pines and aspens. Sagebrush and summer wildflowers dot the meadow, and ATV trails crisscross the area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72303', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72313', 'Sheep Creek Scenic Byway Interpretive Site', 'scenic_drive', 40.928458, -109.720832, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Sheep Creek Scenic Byway Interpretive Site', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72313', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72315', 'Antelope Scenic Byway Interpretive Site', 'scenic_drive', 40.966565, -109.466755, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This overlook gazes upon the Flaming Gorge.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72315', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72403', 'Greendale Overlook Interpretive Site', 'scenic_drive', 40.872391, -109.496014, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This overlook is part of the Flaming Gorge-Uintas Scenic Byway and overlooks the Greendale valley.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72403', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72407', 'Sheep Creek Bay Overlook Interpretive Area', 'scenic_drive', 40.906999, -109.699129, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Sheep Creek Bay Overlook', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=72407', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72842', 'Devils Canyon Campground', 'campground', 37.739015, -109.406265, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Devils Canyon Campground is located just 13 miles south of Monticello, Utah at an elevation of 7,400 feet. Ponderosa pines, pinyon pines, and junipers cover the area offering limited shade. Summer temperatures are warm in the day and cool in the evening. Popular attractions in the area include Canyonlands, Arches, and Mesa Verde National Parks, Dark Canyon Wilderness, and Edge of the Cedars State Park. Evening programs may be available at the Edge of the Cedars Museum in Blanding. This campground contains 42 single-family sites with picnic tables and fire rings. Vault toliets and drinking…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72842', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72848', 'Foy Lake Fishing/Camping Site', 'campground', 37.902468, -109.509941, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The Foy Lake Fishing and Camping Site is located next to Foy Lake, a 4.2 acre lake located about 1.0 miles off FH 49 Loop/Harts Draw down Spring Lake Road #100. The Department of Wildlife Resources of Utah (DWR) stocks this reservoir with Rainbow Trout.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72848', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72854', 'Harts Draw Highway', 'scenic_drive', 37.869100, -109.382700, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The Harts Draw Highway travels across the northeastern flank of the Abajo Mountains and SR-211 near Newspaper Rock. The Harts Draw-Canyonlands Overlook is about 10 miles from Monticello, with vistas of the La Sal Mountains, Shay Mountain, and the Needles District of Canyonlands National Park. In autumn, aspens and maples are blazing flags along the drive. In winter, the road is plowed from Monticello to the winter recreation area where you can find trails for skiing, snowshoeing, and snowmobiling. For a brochure on winter activities for the Moab and Monticello Ranger Districts, click here.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72854', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72878', 'Nizhoni Campground', 'campground', 37.781045, -109.538970, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Nizhoni Campground is located approximately 12 miles north of Blanding, Utah at the foot of the Abajo mountains at an elevation of 7,800 feet. Towering ponderosa pines forest the site, offering partial shade and gambel oaks and sagebrush dot the landscape. Summer temperatures range from 80-90 degrees during the day and 55-65 degrees at night. Mule deer, wild turkeys, Abert''s squirrels, and the occasional black bear may be seen in the area. Popular activities include biking, hiking, wildlife viewing, and touring the mountains. There are 21 single sites and two group areas that can accomodate…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72878', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72932', 'Buckeye Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.440238, -109.044868, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Buckeye Recreation Area sits at an elevation of 7600 ft on the east side of the La Sal Mountains surrounded by ponderosa pine trees. It is most easily accessible from the town of Paradox, CO and is a popular fishing and camping location in the mountains. The Buckeye Recreation Area is located adjacent to Buckeye Reservoir . The recreation area is spread out around the reservoir and consists of the Pioneer Campground (30 single family reservable campsites and one reservable group site), a boat ramp for small fishing boats (5 HP motor limit and wakeless speed, a day-use picnic area, and 18 less…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72932', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '72970', 'Elk Ridge State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 37.930900, -109.747300, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Elk Ridge Road seems to be on top of the world. From here travelers see stunning views of Monument Valley, the Bears Ears National Monument, Canyonlands National Park and scenery nearly 200 miles in the distance. The backway follows the Elk Ridge spine at nearly 9,000 feet (often as a single lane) with panoramic views of red rock canyons and Canyonlands National Park. Near the start of the route, the road passes through the Bears Ears buttes on the northern section of the Shash Jaa unit of Bears Ears National Monument. These twin buttes stand over 8700 feet in elevation and are sacred places…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=72970', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73062', 'Ferron Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 39.143500, -111.455200, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Ferron Reservoir Campground is located just below the ridgeline of the Wasatch Plateau at an elevation of ~9,500 feet. The campground is set in a scenic alpine basin among spruce, fir, and aspen trees, which provide partial shade for campers. The campground is adjacent to Ferron Reservoir and offers amazing scenery, including seasonal wildflowers and autumn leaves which put on quite a show in the surrounding area. Activities offered at this campground include wildlife watching, canoeing, boating (small craft only) and fishing for rainbow and cutthroat trout. Numerous off-highway vehicle (OHV)…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73062', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73082', 'Willow Lake Campground', 'campground', 39.135446, -111.380508, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Willow Lake Campground is located on the east shore of scenic Willow Lake, at an elevation of 9,640 feet. The small lake sits in an alpine basin high on the Wasatch Plateau. Spruce, fir and aspen trees dot the open landscape, providing partial shade in the campground. Wildlife and summer wildflowers are plentiful, and autumn leaves put on quite a show in the surrounding area. This campground contains 10 single-family sites with picnic table and campfire rings. Most sites have lake views, though none have direct lake access. A footpath leads to the shore from the campground. Vault toilets are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73082', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73096', 'Cleveland Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 39.579910, -111.242972, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Cleveland Reservoir Campground is located along Utah''s scenic Energy Loop on top of the Wasatch Plateau off Hwy 31 approximately 18 miles east of Fairview, Utah. Cleveland Reservoir Campground sits at an approximate elevation of 9,000 feet and is located next to Cleveland Reservoir, a 135.8 acre reservoir located in Huntington Canyon off UT-31. Vault toilets are provided, but there is no water, electricity, sewer hookups, or garbage service. This is a "pack it in, pack it out" site, so all trash must be removed upon departure. This campground sits on the north end of the Arapeen OHV trail…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73096', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73098', 'Forks Of Huntington Campground', 'campground', 39.501400, -111.162200, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Forks of Huntington Campground is located in beautiful Huntington Canyon along the Huntington and Eccles Canyons National Scenic Byway on Utah Highway 31. At an elevation of 7,600 feet, the campground is located in thick stands of pines with the Left Fork of Huntington Creek running through the campground. The 6-mile Left Fork of the Huntington National Recreation Trail, for hiking and horses, begins in the campground, and the 10-mile Fish Creek National Recreation Trail, for hiking, biking, and horses is nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73098', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73110', 'Little Rock Campground', 'campground', 39.544254, -111.163992, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Little Rock Campground is a primitive campsite nestled in a shaded spruce stand located in beautiful Huntington Canyon along the Huntington Canyon National Scenic Byway. It sits at an elevation of approximately 8,000 feet. Many recreational activities are available, including hiking, biking and fishing. This campsite provides a graveled parking spur, picnic table, and fire ring. There is no water or vault toilet on site but water and a flush restroom can be accessed &frac12; south of Little Rock Campground at Old Folks Flat Campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73110', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73112', 'Lower Little Bear Campground', 'campground', 39.443436, -111.136376, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Lower Little Bear Campground is a primitive campground nestled in a partially shaded area alongside Huntington Creek. This campground is located in beautiful Huntington Canyon along the Huntington Canyon National Scenic Byway on Utah Highway 31. It sits at an elevation of approximately 7,100 feet. Many recreational activities are available, including hiking, biking and fishing. This campground provides a double site, group site (accommodate 40 people), graveled parking spur, picnic table, and fire ring. There is no water or a vault toilet on site but a restroom can be accessed &frac14; north…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73112', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73124', 'The Energy Loop: Huntington & Eccles Canyons NSB', 'scenic_drive', 39.409645, -111.115789, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Whatever the season, the views are breathtaking on The Energy Loop - the Huntington and Eccles Canyons National Scenic Byway (NSB). The route is rich with the history of mining and energy production. Outstanding recreation opportunities abound. There are numerous interpretive sites along the byway, including the recovery site of a 9,500 year-old mammoth skeleton. The National Scenic Byway can be accessed from SR-10 at Huntington, US-89 at Fairview, and US-6 at Colton.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73124', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73126', 'Joes Valley Campground', 'campground', 39.295100, -111.291800, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Joes Valley Reservoir Campground is located in a high mountain valley adjacent to and just above Joes Valley Reservoir at an elevation of ~7,000 feet. Juniper, pinyon pine and sagebrush cover the area, and aspen and pine dot the surrounding hillsides. Several sites provide nice views of the reservoir, and some sites are shaded. The campground contains several single- and double-family campsites, all of which are accessible. Vault toilets and drinking water are provided. Roads and parking spurs are paved. A boat ramp is located within the campground. The reservoir offers good fishing for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73126', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73136', 'Joes Valley Overlook', 'scenic_drive', 39.300021, -111.272164, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Overlook site at Joes Valley Reservoir. The Joes Valley Overlook provides an expansive view of the sparkling waters of Joes Valley Reservoir. The site is nestled among a smattering of sagebrush and juniper trees, just above the shoreline of the reservoir. This is an ideal spot to stretch your legs and take a break from driving.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73136', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73174', 'La Sal Mountain Loop State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 38.457400, -109.368000, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The Central Federal Lands Highway Division (CFLHD) of the Federal Highway Administration, in cooperation with the US Forest Service (FS), the Bureau of Land Management (BLM), and San Juan County is proposing to rehabilitate and widen 2 segments of road, totaling 12.12 miles along La Sal Mountain Loop Road. This project is scheduled for construction beginning in the spring of 2024 to fall of 2025. Construction has started as of May 20, 2024, get the latest updates and access information here: https://highways.dot.gov/federal-lands/projects/ut/la-sal From the alpine ridges of the La Sal…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73174', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73176', 'Mason Draw Campground', 'campground', 38.542901, -109.303070, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Mason Draw Campground offers 5 first come/first serve campsites that are available for $10/night. It is located just off the La Sal Loop Road near the Castle Valley Overlook. This is a basic campground with vault toliets, campfire rings, and picnic tables. There is no water available. For more information, please contact the Moab Ranger District, 435-259-7155.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73176', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73192', 'Oowah Campground', 'campground', 38.502800, -109.272400, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Oowah Lake Campground sits at 8800 ft. elevation in the spectacular La Sal mountains. There are 11 tent-only, first come/ first serve campsites next to the small but scenic Oowah Lake. Trailhead access from the campground includes the Clarks Lake, Boren Mesa, Moonlight Meadows, and Warner Lake trails. Hike a short distance for spectacular vistas of the Canyonlands region. There is also a day-use area with three large picnic tables. Fishing is also popular at this mountain lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73192', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73218', 'Warner Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.519956, -109.276604, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Warner Lake campground is at an elevation of 9,400 feet among dense aspen trees with Warner Lake close by. There are 19 camp sites with picnic tables and campfire rings. A group area can accommodate up to 50 campers and a small cabin nearby sleeps up to 4 people. Views of the surrounding La Sal mountain peaks are stunning with Haystack mountain visible from a few of the campsites. Activities nearby include fishing for rainbow trout in the lake and hiking on the extensive trail system accessed from trailheads a short walk away. No powerboats are allowed on Warner Lake but canoeing and kayaking…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73218', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73228', 'Abajo Loop State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 37.918200, -109.450800, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The Abajo Loop leads from the desert floor and red rock canyons to steep mountains over 11,000 feet high, with overlooks and panoramic views. The backway travels Forest Road 105 west from Monticello to the junction of Forest Road-079 where it heads south through North Canyon, northwest of the shadow of Horsehead Peak. The tour concludes in Blanding. Although suitable for passenger vehicles during late spring or summer through fall, this route is not recommended for large RVs or trailers. North Creek pass does close in winter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73228', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73242', 'Buckboard Campground', 'campground', 37.880691, -109.449271, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The campground offers several single-family sites, as well as two group sites than can each accommodate up to 50 guests. Firewood may be collected in and around the campground. Forest Road 105 to the campground is paved, while parking spurs and the roads within the campground are graveled. There are two vault toilets and the campground has water available (seasonally.) There is a 14 day stay limit at this campground. Aspens and Gambel oaks surround the site, offering partial shade. The campground sits at an elevation of 8,900 feet, and summer temperatures range from 75-85 degrees during the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73242', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73250', 'Dalton Springs Campground', 'campground', 37.874158, -109.433441, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'There are sixteen first come/ first serve campsites in an aspen and gambel oak grove at 8200 ft elevation. There are multiple trails and roads nearby offering recreation opportunities for biking, hiking, motorized activities, and equestrian use. Mule deer, black bears, and other wildlife may be seen nearby. Newspaper Rock, the Needles District of Canyonlands National Park, and Edge of the Cedars State Park Museum are nice day trips from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73250', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73258', 'Big Drift Staging Area', 'snow_area', 39.614941, -111.303042, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'This is a parking/staging area for both snow machines and ATVs that use the nearby trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73258', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73278', 'Ephraim to Orangeville Road', 'scenic_drive', 39.337600, -111.522600, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'This is a two part experience: from Skyline Drive to Joes Valley and Orangeville, and from Ephraim to Skyline Drive. The drive to Orangeville will take you from high meadows at the skyline, through stands of aspen and conifer, past Joes Valley Reservoir and to the broad open plain of Castle Valley. Driving from Ephraim to Skyline Drive, you will climb 5000 feet in 15 miles. Along the way are interpretive displays explaining the unique scientific work that began in Ephraim Canyon and continues today at the Great Basin Experiemental Range.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73278', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73316', 'Lake Canyon Campground', 'campground', 39.579034, -111.250237, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Lake Canyon Recreation Area is located along Utah''s scenic Energy Loop on top of the Wasatch Plateau off Hwy 31 approximately 18 miles east of Fairview, Utah. Situated between Huntington and Cleveland Reservoirs at an approximate elevation of 9,000 feet, this area is a fishing and ATV paradise. Vault toilets are provided, but there is no water, electricity, sewer hookups, or garbage service. This is a "pack it in, pack it out" site, so all trash must be removed upon departure. This area has five reservable group sites, and four reservable double sites(#11, 17, 24 & 41). If sites are not…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73316', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73340', 'Potters Pond Campground', 'campground', 39.451100, -111.268600, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Potters Pond Campground is located in a high mountain valley in Upper Joes Valley. It is next to two sparkling ponds at an elevation of 9,000 feet. Grasses and pine trees cover the area, and aspen trees dot the surrounding mountainsides. This campground offers a variety of campsites, including single, double and equestrian sites. Some sites have views of the ponds and most sites are shaded. The campsites are equipped with tables and campfire rings with grills. Vault toilets are provided, but there is no water, electricity or trash collection available within the campground. Visitors will need…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73340', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73352', 'River Bend Campground', 'campground', 39.434940, -111.132156, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'River Bend Campground is a primitive campsite nestled in a shaded area alongside Huntington Creek. This campground is located in beautiful Huntington Canyon along the Huntington Canyon National Scenic Byway on Utah Highway 31. It sits at an elevation of approximately 7,100 feet. Many recreational activities are available, including hiking, biking and fishing. This campsite provides a double site (accommodate 12 people), graveled parking, picnic table, and fire ring. There is no water or a vault toilet on site but a restroom can be accessed &frac12; north of River Bend at Little Bear…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73352', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73382', 'Upper Joes Valley Dispersed Site', 'campground', 39.347300, -111.269700, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Upper Joes Valley is located at ~7340'' elevation, just south of the intersection of Millers Flat Road and Lowry Water Road. The trees offer shade for most campers and provide spectacular autumn color. Many people enjoy the solitude and primitive experience of camping away from developed campgrounds and other campers. "Dispersed camping" is the term used for camping anywhere in the National Forest outside of a designated campground, and is generally allowed anywhere unless posted otherwise. Many people drive out on Forest Service roads into the woods and find spots that meet the needs for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73382', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73400', 'North Skyline Drive State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 39.923000, -111.232100, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'North Skyline Drive, a gravel road, climbs to the Wasatch Plateau from US-6 and undulates south for 27 miles to SR-31. This section is located in the Spanish Fork - Scofield Recreation Area on the Ferron/Price Ranger District in the Manti-La Sal National Forest. This backway provides scenic views into Lake Fork and Fish Creek drainages and access to prime fall hunting areas. It is a groomed snowmobile trail in winter. The road is suitable for passenger cars, but is closed in the winter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73400', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73404', 'South Skyline Drive State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 39.617329, -111.311043, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Your journey begins on SR-31 and continues 55 miles south to the Fishlake National Forest boundary. Stunning views of nearby mountain ranges are on constant display, complimented by vivid wildflower displays in mid to late summer. This route is the backbone of the Arapeen OHV trail system.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73404', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73424', 'Ferron to Mayfield State Scenic Backway', 'scenic_drive', 39.142800, -111.417800, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Winding up 12-Mile Canyon from Mayfield, this backway begins and ends in pinyon-juniper country, but climbs to well over 10,000 feet while passing through stands of aspen and conifer. There are angler destinations along the way. This gravel route is accessible to passenger cars during summer and fall, then becomes a snowmobiler''s haven during the winter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73424', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73434', 'Lake Hill Campground', 'campground', 39.327949, -111.497555, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Lake Hill Campground is situated next to pretty Lake Hill Reservoir just five miles from Ephraim, Utah, elevation 8,400 feet. A mixed forest of spruce, fir, and aspen covers the area, offering partial shade in most sites. Some are more exposed than others. Summer wildflowers and wildlife are abundant. Canoeing and rainbow trout fishing are popular activities on the small man-made reservoir. This campground contains two group sites: #1 can accommodate up to 30 people and eight vehicles, with one large picnic table, serving table, utility table, fire ring, and potable water spigot; #2 can…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73434', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73436', 'Manti Community Campground', 'campground', 39.253470, -111.542073, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The Manti Community Campground is just seven miles from Manti, Utah next to Yearns Reservoir at an elevation of 7,400 feet. A mixed forest of spruce, pinyon, juniper, fir, and aspen covers the area, offering partial shade. Summer wildflowers and wildlife are abundant. Canoeing and fishing for cutthroat trout are popular on the small man-made lake. This campground contains one group site that can accommodate up to 30 people and six vehicles, with large picnic tables, a utility table, and a fire ring with benches. Single-family sites are available as well, with picnic tables and fire rings.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73436', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73452', 'Twelve Mile Flat Campground', 'campground', 39.123080, -111.487970, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Twelve Mile Flat Campground is located beneath the shadow of Mt. Baldy near the top of the Wasatch Plateau in an open wildflower-filled meadow surrounded by spruce and pines, elevation 10,120 feet. ATV trails are abundant in the area, providing exciting riding for all skill levels. Skyline Drive passes outside the campground. A short, but steep drive over the ridge leads to Ferron Reservoir for canoeing and rainbow and cutthroat trout fishing. This campground contains two group sites that can accommodate up to 50 people and eight vehicles each, with large picnic tables and fire rings with…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73452', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73454', 'Twin Lake Campground', 'campground', 39.118846, -111.604935, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Twin Lake Campground, at 8,100 feet, is located in Twelve Mile Canyon. ATV trails are abundant in the area, providing exciting riding for all skill levels. No water at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73454', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73458', 'Upper Six Mile Ponds Campground', 'campground', 39.188400, -111.540500, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Upper Six Mile Ponds Campground is just ten miles from Sterling, Utah at an elevation of 8,400 feet. A mixed forest of spruce, pinyon, juniper, fir, and aspen covers the area, offering partial shade. Summer wildflowers and wildlife are abundant. Canoeing and fishing for trout are popular at the ponds. Many people enjoy the solitude and primitive experience of camping away from developed campgrounds and other campers. "Dispersed camping" is the term used for camping anywhere in the National Forest outside of a designated campground, and is generally allowed anywhere unless posted otherwise.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73458', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73462', 'Chicken Creek Campground', 'campground', 39.530252, -111.773480, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Elevation 6200 feet. 8 shady sites, set among pines in Chicken Creek Canyon. Fishing is good in Chicken Creek. Pets must be leashed in campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73462', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73474', 'Maple Canyon Campground', 'campground', 39.556822, -111.687184, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Maple Canyon Campground is nestled among thick groves of maples below beautiful towering rock walls, just 3 miles from Freedom, Utah. Rock climbing is the campground''s main draw, attracting climbers from all over the world with its numerous routes for beginners and experts alike. This campground contains one group site that can accommodate up to 25 people, several single family sites, and four walk-to tent sites, sites 1-16 have picnic tables and fire rings. Sites 2, 3, 4, and 12 must be accessed by carrying your gear a short distance from the parking area and sites A-G only have fire rings.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73474', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73494', 'Flat Canyon Campground', 'campground', 39.645500, -111.260100, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Located in the Spanish Fork - Scofield Recration Area on the Ferron/Price Ranger District of the Manti-La Sal National Forest, Flat Canyon Campground is great for family fun, its an easy to get to campground never having to leave pavement. If you love ﬁshing there is an angler''s trail leads from the campground to nearby Boulger Reservoir. Electric Lake is approximately one mile away. Boating, fishing, hiking, biking, and scenic driving are popular activities in the area. This campground contains one group site that can accommodate up to 50 people as well as several single-family campsites.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73494', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73496', 'Gooseberry Campground', 'campground', 39.686800, -111.297200, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Gooseberry Campground is located in the Spanish Fork - Scofield Recreation Area on the Manti-La Sal National Forest''s Ferron/Price Ranger District. This campground is on an aspen-covered hillside in a beautiful mountain valley above Gooseberry Reservoir at an elevation of 8,500 feet. Sagebrush and mature fir trees dot the area. Gooseberry Reservoir, which is visible from several sites, offers good cutthroat and rainbow trout fishing, as well as canoeing. The Great Western Trail runs nearby, offering excellent opportunities for hiking, biking, and ATVs/OHVs. This campground has vault toilets…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73496', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73500', 'Gooseberry Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 39.711528, -111.293828, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'Gooseberry Reservoir Campground is located in the Spanish Fork-Scofield Recreation Area on the Manti-La Sal National Forest''s Ferron/Price Ranger District. This campgound is located in a beautiful mountain valley in an open sagebrush meadow next to Gooseberry Reservoir at an elevation of 8,400 feet. The surrounding mountains are dotted with aspens, fir trees and sagebrush. The reservoir is visible from all sites and offers good cutthroat and rainbow trout fishing, as well as canoeing. No boat ramp is available, and reservoir is open to non-motorized watercraft only. This campground has vault…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73500', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73512', 'North Skyline Winter Staging Snowpark', 'snow_area', 39.678632, -111.312792, null, 'Manti-La Sal National Forest', 'The North Skyline Winter Staging Snowpark is located in the Spanish Fork - Scofield Recration Area on the Ferron/Price Ranger District of the Manti-La Sal National Forest. This staging area can be used by those snowboarding in the Fairview Snowboarding area as well as for snowmobiles at the head of Fairview Canyon as it provides access to North Skyline and Fish Creek motorized winter sports area. For seasonal information about this site, please contact the Price Ranger District: 435-636-3500.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mantilasal/recarea/?recid=73512', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73579', 'Beartree Recreation Area', 'campground', 36.666943, -81.681660, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Due to Hurrican Helene impacts, Bever Flats, Chipmunk Circle, and group camping are closed for the 2025 season. Picnicking and day use are available beginning 5/16.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73579', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73595', 'Blowing Springs Campground', 'campground', 38.068890, -79.883610, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Offering both sunny and shaded camping sites, visitors to Blowing Springs Campground will be amazed by the phenomenon for which this site is named. A unique geological feature creates a duct that blows air out of the rocks at a constant 58 degrees, which may feel warm or cool depending on the season. Direct access to trails leading to swimming holes, and a stream stocked with trout are a few of the many reasons to visit this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73595', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73617', 'Brandywine Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.595276, -79.199720, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Located on the 10-acre Brandywine Lake, this wooded recreation area affords access to multiple hiking and mountain biking trails, a swimming beach, and a campground with an onsite host.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73617', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73633', 'Camp Roosevelt Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.733055, -78.517220, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Camp Roosevelt Campground is the site of the first Civilian Conservation Corps Camp in the Nation. Follow the path through the CCC camp and view the foundations where the actual buildings once stood. Proud and lofty oak trees create the perfect atmosphere for enjoying a simple picnic or camping out with friends or family.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73633', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73635', 'Camp Run Campground', 'campground', 38.746666, -79.108055, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Nestled along a Shenandoah Mountain drainage in Pendleton County, WV, Camp Run provides an opportunity for primitive 1950''s style camping that is popular with hunters.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73635', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73637', 'Cane Patch Campground', 'campground', 37.101944, -82.678890, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Cane Patch Campground is within walking distance of Phillips Creek Day Use Area. The campground has 35 campsites, 7 of which have electric hookups.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73637', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73641', 'Cave Mountain Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 37.574444, -79.534450, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Nestled in the Blue Ridge Mountains of Virginia, the Cave Mountain Lake Recreation Area welcomes generations of families who enjoy the rustic beauty and peacefulness of the area. Easy access from I-81, close proximity to historic Lexington, and access to Natural Bridge make Cave Mountain Lake a perfect travel destination.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73641', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73661', 'Comers Rock Recreation Area', 'campground', 36.763050, -81.224910, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Located on top of Iron Mountain at 3800 feet, a small primitive campground and historic picnic area await the true outdoor enthusiast. The log picnic shelter with large stone fireplace was built by the Civilian Conservation Corps. Within walking distance of the campground are long distance hikes in Little Dry Run Wilderness, 360 degree views from Comers Rock Overlook and former fire tower, and the Unaka Nature Trail. Less than 2 miles away is Hale Lake for fishing, hiking, and canoeing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73661', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73723', 'Greenwood Point Campground', 'campground', 37.959167, -79.964720, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Greenwood Point Campground at Lake Moomaw offers the solitude of an isolated and remote location. With no road access, the adventure is just getting there! Strap on that pack and take a hike, paddle, or canoe directly to the shores of the campground. Wooded campsites encircle an open and grassy common area, and lakeside views make this a popular private and quiet camping destination.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73723', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73725', 'Grindstone Recreation Area', 'campground', 36.687500, -81.541664, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Partial Closure All camping loops are closed for the 2025 season due to impacts from Hurricane Helene. Overnight Parking is available from 4/1 to 12/2, but will be closed during construction. Escape the summer heat at 3,800 feet in elevation. Hike from your campsite to the top of Mount Rogers or stay and enjoy one of the best birding sites in the region. Enjoy watching a campfire, splashing in the creek, or exploring the playground and the Whispering Waters Nature Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73725', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73739', 'Hawk Recreation Area', 'campground', 39.116390, -78.499170, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Hawk Campground sits nestled in the Alleghany Mountains surround by a spectacular nature setting. Experience an exciting hiking experience with easy access to the Tuscarora Trail right from the campground. In the fall, this inviting location offers hunters a secluded environment to stay overnight. Fall asleep to the mellow sounds of the trees gently swaying overhead and the simple harmony of nearby crickets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73739', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73743', 'Hidden Valley Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.099167, -79.821945, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'With vast fields of wildflowers that attract countless butterflies, birds, and other wildlife, the Hidden Valley Recreation Area is appropriately named due to its secluded and hidden feeling. Drawing visitors for hundreds of years, the valley is a historic location with an antebellum-era mansion which is now run as a Bed and Breakfast. Camping is available at the campground. Stocked with trout, the Jackson River flows through the valley, and movie buffs will recognize the area as the setting for the movie Somersby .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73743', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73755', 'High Knob Recreation Area', 'campground', 36.889720, -82.621666, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'The High Knob Recreation Area was built by the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC) in the late 1930''s. This remote and private location offers cooler summer temperatures due to its higher mountain elevation. The area offers a campground and day use and picnic area along a scenic mountain lake. Many of the original CCC structures are still in use here today.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73755', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73759', 'Hone Quarry Campground', 'campground', 38.460000, -79.134720, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Hone Quarry Campground is within one mile of Hone Quarry Reservoir. Nearby trailheads lead to popular rock climbing areas. Highlights of the campground include a picturesque stream, a hike to a nearby 15-foot waterfall and an adjacent group picnic shelter that is non-fee and is available first-come first-served.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73759', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73763', 'Hopper Creek Group Campground', 'campground', 37.560000, -79.509160, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Hopper Creek Group Campground offers a shaded and rustic atmosphere for group tent camping with an open area for activities and a large campfire ring for evening gatherings. Because only one group can reserve the area at a time, it offers a great opportunity for privacy and solitude.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73763', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73771', 'Hurricane Campground', 'campground', 36.722500, -81.490555, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Located along a rushing mountain stream under the shade of hemlock and rhododendron, this campground offers a peaceful setting for quiet evenings around the campfire. While only 2 miles off State Highway 16, the setting feels much more remote. Hikers can walk from their campsite to the Appalachian Trail and many other nearby trails. This site is not recommended for large RVs.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73771', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73807', 'Little Fort Campground', 'campground', 38.866943, -78.444440, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Little Fort is a first-come-first-serve minimally developed recreation area located near the meadow that was once a rest stop for a stagecoach line. Enjoy the thrill of riding the largest OHV system in the state of Virginia with easy access right from the campground to the Peters Mill Run/Taskers Gap OHV trail system.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73807', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73829', 'McClintic Point Campground', 'campground', 38.015419, -79.921141, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'McClintic Point at Lake Moomaw sits on the northern end of the lake. Enjoy the easygoing, peaceful vibe of McClintic Point''s rustic campground set among scattered trees and open fields. This angler''s paradise provides plentiful shoreline fishing and some lakefront campsites. Boating, canoeing, water skiing and and fishing are popular activities on the lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73829', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73843', 'Morris Hill Campground', 'campground', 37.931110, -79.971110, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Morris Hill at Lake Moomaw offers a peaceful, rustic campground. The campground offers scenic views from its perch on a ridge above the southern end of Lake Moomaw. Located just a half-mile from the lakeshore, this campground provides easy access to sandy swim beaches, a fishing pier, boat ramp, and hiking and biking trails. Hikers enjoy the nearby Morris Hill Bike Trail and Fortney Loop Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73857', 'North Creek Campground', 'campground', 37.541390, -79.584724, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Located along the edge of North Creek, this campground offers shady campsites and a relaxed atmosphere. Prop your feet up and listen to the stream as it gurgles past, or take advantage of the fishing at your door.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73857', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73869', 'North River Campground', 'campground', 38.339443, -79.207220, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'This open area campground was originally constructed as a CCC camp. Evidence of the original sites and logging trails still remain today. North River Gorge is a popular hiking, biking, and fishing area with a swinging bridge spanning the North River. Close proximity to Wild Oak National Recreation Trail, Stanton Dam Day Use Area and Elkhorn Lake provide multiple recreational options that are easily accessible within a few miles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73869', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73905', 'Raccoon Branch Campground', 'campground', 36.746387, -81.425835, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Only 11 miles from I-81 via State Route 16, this beautiful little campground is nestled at the base of Dickey Knob and adjacent to Raccoon Branch Wilderness. Raccoon Branch campground offers scenic mountain views, hiking from your campsite, and cold mountain streams. Popular for trout fishing, summer vacations, and fall foliage viewing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73905', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73909', 'Raven Cliff Recreation Area', 'campground', 36.836113, -81.070000, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'From the 200 foot sandstone Raven Cliff to the 1810 iron ore furnace, this recreation area is off the beaten path but worth the effort. With a small primitive campground, picnic area, and large day use area, visitors can spend a few hours or few days. Cripple Creek runs through the picnic area and is popular for fishing, wading, and tubing. Large open fields are great for sports and picnics.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73909', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73959', 'Sherando Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 37.919724, -79.010000, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Sherando Lake Recreation Area is known locally as the jewel of the Blue Ridge Mountains. Families enjoy picnicking in this shaded and woody area, while relaxing on the sandy beach of a 25-acre spring-fed lake. Access to multiple trailheads and rustic architecture provide numerous points of interest for families to enjoy.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73959', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73971', 'Steel Bridge Campground', 'campground', 37.600834, -80.218890, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Enjoy splashing or fishing in the cool water of Potts Creek, a stocked trout stream adjacent to this rustic campground and day use area. The campground has three unpaved and well-shaded campsites situated along a single dirt road that parallels the creek. A parking area is available for day-use visitors. Historic Paint Bank, Virginia is a scenic three mile drive from here.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73971', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73977', 'Stony Fork Campground', 'campground', 37.010000, -81.190000, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Stony Fork is located in a natural forest setting at the foot of Big Walker Mountain and adjacent to the Big Walker Scenic Byway. A short drive from I-77 and I-81, the campground is popular with RVers and tent campers. The East Fork of Stony Fork Creek winds through the campground and provides water play and trout fishing. A one mile nature trail will take campers through stands of pine and hardwoods, while the campground loop road itself is popular with walkers. For the more experienced hiker, Seven Sisters Trail leads from the campground to the top of Little Walker Mountain and back to the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73977', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73987', 'The Pines Campground', 'campground', 37.605000, -80.076670, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'The Pines is a rustic campground in a wooded setting, located adjacent to Barbour''s Creek, a stocked trout stream. Most of the campsites are designed for tents, but small recreation vehicles can be accommodated. Jeep enthusiasts can experience some of the most challenging 4-wheeling in Virginia at nearby Potts Mountain Jeep Road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73987', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73991', 'Todd Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.365555, -79.211390, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Visitors to Todd Lake Recreation Area enjoy a historic campground complete with a wheelchair accessible beach. A children''s playground, plenty of open fields, grills, and picnic tables make this location an ideal place to spend a relaxing summer afternoon. Explore multiple trails from this location popular among mountain biking, backpacking, and hiking enthusiasts.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73991', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '73999', 'Trout Pond Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.952500, -78.733890, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Trout Pond Recreation Area boasts two beautiful lakes: Rock Cliff Lake and Trout Pond. Relax on a sandy mountain beach or fish for stocked trout while kids splash in the cool waters of Rock Cliff Lake. Trout Pond, home to native Brook trout, is the only natural lake in West Virginia. A designated swimming area, and easy lakeside trails make this a perfect family destination.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=73999', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74007', 'Walnut Flats Campground', 'campground', 37.198055, -80.886390, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'This small, primitive campground is well suited for tent camping but also accommodates small recreation vehicles. It has shaded sites clustered around a grassy opening surrounded by forest. Flat Top Mountain Trail System, the Appalachian Trail, Dismal Creek (a stocked trout stream), and the Falls of Dismal are close by.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=74007', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74023', 'White Rocks Campground', 'campground', 37.430000, -80.492226, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'White Rocks Campground is in a secluded forest setting with cool summertime temperatures and great wildlife watching opportunities. A small creek meanders through several campsites and a nature trail traverses through the woods. Area highlights include Mountain Lake Wilderness, Mountain Lake, Glen Alton Day Use Area, Hanging Rock Raptor Observatory, Potts Rail Trail, Appalachian Trail, and multiple hiking opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=74023', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74043', 'Wolf Gap Recreation Area', 'campground', 38.924545, -78.689090, null, 'George Washington & Jefferson National Forest', 'Wolf Gap Recreation Area was once the site of a 1930''s African American Civilian Conservation Corps Camp. This recreation area has many hiking opportunities nearby. From here begin your hike to the popular Big Schloss Overlook with scenic views of Virginia and West Virginia mountains. Stay at one of our charming campsites and enjoy falling asleep to the peaceful symphony of nearby crickets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gwj/recarea/?recid=74043', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74380', 'Oak Creek Canyon Scenic Drive', 'scenic_drive', 35.028030, -111.734110, null, 'Coconino National Forest Recreation', 'Get your camera ready for this one, and don''t forget your swimsuit, hiking shoes, and fishing pole. Just south of Flagstaff, Arizona State Route 89A descends a breathtaking series of switchbacks into a scenic, smaller cousin of the Grand Canyon. Known for colorful rocks and unique formations, Oak Creek Canyon is famous the world around for its spectacular scenery. Before you drive into the canyon you''ll want to stop at Oak Creek Canyon Vista . Here you can get a bird''s eye view of what awaits you down the road and, at the same time, shop for Native American jewelry and other craft items from…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coconino/recarea/?recid=74380', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74388', 'Chirpchatter Campground', 'campground', 40.868733, -122.119749, null, 'Shasta-Trinity National Forest', 'Located east of Shasta Lake, these remote campsites offer the perfect spot to relax. Forested and shady, this is a perfect home base for your OHV adventures! Be aware, Fenders Ferry is a rough, unimproved dirt road. There is no lake access from this facility. This campground is very popular in the fall during hunting season. For more information and directions click this link', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stnf/recarea/?recid=74388', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74437', 'Crocker Pond Campground', 'campground', 44.310311, -70.823472, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'This secluded, 7 site campground is located on the edge of Crocker Pond under a towering white pine forest. Crocker Pond along with several other nearby fishing ponds have boat launches for non-motorized boats.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74437', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74443', 'Dolly Copp Campground', 'campground', 44.332581, -71.219284, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​Located along the Peabody River, this site has ample opportunity for small family picnics or large group gatherings. The large picnic pavilion, originally constructed by the Civilian Conservation Corps in 1936, was rebuilt in 1996 using many of the original timbers, along with trees planted by the same 1936 CCC crew.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74443', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74463', 'Hastings Campground', 'campground', 44.351990, -70.984154, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Picture yourself living in the heart of a logging camp back in the late 1800s while you relax at your campsite or fish for brook trout in the nearby Evans Brook. Constructed on the site of the old town of Hastings this campground is in a young forest with ample open area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74463', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74507', 'Rattle River Shelter', 'campground', 44.379987, -71.107488, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Rattle River Shelter is reached by hiking 1.7 miles up the gradual grade of the Rattle River Trail. In addition to the shelter, 3 designated tent sites provide for overflow camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74507', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74549', 'Wild River Campground', 'campground', 44.305408, -71.064590, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Wild River Campground will be closed for the season due to storm damage. Visitors can enjoy a variety of recreation opportunities around the campground, including fishing in the Wild River, strolling along the easy grade of the Wild River Trail, or exploring the rugged Wild River Wilderness.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74549', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74577', 'Big Rock Campground', 'campground', 44.048676, -71.561005, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​This campground is named after one of the many large boulders dropped from the glaciers that shaped this region. Big Rock Campground has 28 wooded campsites and is a short distance from a number of nearby attractions including Otter Rocks, the Lincoln Woods Visitor Center, and many popular hiking trails along the Kancamagus Highway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74577', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74587', 'Campton Campground', 'campground', 43.873447, -71.626717, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Campton Campground is one of the first National Forest campgrounds visitors encounter when driving north on Interstate 93. Only a short distance east of exit 28, this location has 58 sites scattered amongst ancient white pine trees.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74587', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74649', 'Hancock Campground', 'campground', 44.063690, -71.594207, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​Located at the western end of the scenic Kancamagus Highway, this campground serves as an excellent place to start your White Mountain adventure. The nearby Lincoln Woods Visitor Center is the jumping off point for numerous hiking trails leading into the Pemigewasset Wilderness; the Kancamagus Highway is an extremely popular scenic byway with numerous hiking, picnic, and swimming spots; and the town of Lincoln offers many amenities. Hancock Campground has 56 wooded sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74649', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74717', 'Russell Pond Campground', 'campground', 44.008744, -71.648928, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​Campground''s 86 campsites are tucked into the hillside overlooking Russell Pond, a popular boating and fishing site (due in part to regular fish stocking by the State Fish and Game Department). This campground has flush toilets, hot showers, both RV and tent sites, and features a beautiful amphitheater with free interpretive nature programs on summer Saturday evenings.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74717', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74731', 'Sugarloaf I Campground', 'campground', 44.260410, -71.504662, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​This campground''s 29 sites are in a quiet setting in close proximity to the Zealand River and the many Zealand Valley hiking opportunities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74731', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74733', 'Sugarloaf II Campground', 'campground', 44.258091, -71.503937, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​Sugarloaf II is as pleasant as nearby Sugarloaf I, with the addition of a nice grassy field, perfect for lounging or a ball game on a sunny day. It has 32 sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74733', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74765', 'Waterville Campground', 'campground', 43.941860, -71.509170, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​This campground is located in the heart of Waterville Valley and serves as a wonderful basecamp for exlporing the numerous hiking trails located in this area.It has 27 campsites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74765', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74775', 'Wildwood Campground', 'campground', 44.075100, -71.793678, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Wildwood Campground is located in the western most reaches of the National Forest, and serves as a quiet retreat for those seeking a rustic camping experience. It has 26 campsites. A Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC) picnic pavilion is directly across the road. Drive West on Route 112 for excellent views of Mount Moosilauke and frequent moose sightings.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74775', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74779', 'Zealand Campground', 'campground', 44.264568, -71.500595, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', '​Conveniently located along NH Rte 302, this small 11 site campground offers open and partially wooded camping along the Ammonoosuc River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74779', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74795', 'Basin Campground', 'campground', 44.267448, -71.022850, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Basin Campground is temporarily closed for plumbing and electrical work. The anticipated re-opening date is to be determined. Basin Campground is named for nearby Basin Pond. Offering a boat launch (non-motorized boats only), fishing and hiking, as well as picnic tables, this is a great place to stay and explore the eastern reaches of the Forest. 13 of the campgrounds 21 sites are reservable.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74795', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74803', 'Blackberry Crossing Campground', 'campground', 44.006805, -71.244965, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Blackberry Crossing is unique in that is was a CCC (Civilian Conservation Corps) Camp during the 1930''s. There is a self-guided tour of the old camp within the campground. The campground has 26 sites that are available on a first come, first served basis. There are hand pumps for water and vault toilets. A short walk from the campground is the Albany Covered Bridge, The Nanamocomuck Ski Trail, and the Boulder Loop hiking trail. There are coin operated showers six miles west on the Kancamagus Highway (Rt 112).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74803', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74821', 'Cold River Campground', 'campground', 44.264469, -71.013329, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Just a short distance from the Cold River and beautiful Basin Pond, this site is popular with fishermen and hikers looking to explore the eastern reaches of the National Forest. This campground has 14 sites, 8 of which are reservable from Memorial Day through Columbus Day. It has vault toilests, a hand pump for water, and a picnic pavillion.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74821', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74825', 'Covered Bridge Campground', 'campground', 44.003151, -71.232193, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Stop and take a picture of the covered bridge as you enter this campground. Located along the Kancamagus Scenic Byway this 49 site campground awaits you. There is a 7'' 9" height restriction through the Covered Bridge so larger RVs can access the campground via Passaconaway Road from West Side Road in Conway. The Boulder Loop Trail, a three mile loop hike, and the Swift River are just short walks away.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74825', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74865', 'Jigger Johnson Campground', 'campground', 43.997879, -71.333931, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Named after Jigger Johnson, an almost legendary north country woods boss during the regions colorful logging era, this campground is located along the Kancamagus Scenic Byway. The Swift River flows behind the campground and a short trail connects to the Russell-Colbath Historic Site. Its central location makes it ideal for hiking, biking, and other recreational activities in the National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74865', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74905', 'Passaconaway Campground', 'campground', 43.997640, -71.370967, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'This heavily wooded campground has 33 sites with the Swift River a short distance away. Across the highway from the campground is the trailhead for the UNH Trail to Mt. Hedghog, the Downes Brook Trail, and the Mt. Potash Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74905', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74933', 'Sawyer River Road Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 44.086156, -71.352175, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'This trailhead accesses Sawyer River Road which serves as a snowmobile trail in winter (shown as Sawyer River Trail on snowmobile maps). It also connects to the Meadowbrook Trail and Bear Notch Road to make a large 25 - 30 mile loop. Multiple hiking trails such as Signal Ridge and Sawyer Pond Trails can also be accessed from this trailhead in winter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74933', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74955', 'White Ledge Campground', 'campground', 43.954365, -71.213893, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'White Ledge campground has 28 sites. Two hiking trails leave the campground: the White Ledge Trail is a moderate 4 mile loop and the Carter Ledge Trail is a strenuous 4.5 mile hike to the summit of Mt. Chocorua, one of the most popular mountains in the National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=74955', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74968', 'Milsap Bar Campground', 'campground', 39.706000, -121.268000, null, 'Plumas National Forest', 'This location is closed (Affected reservations have been cancelled and refunds have been issued.) Local managers are committed to the health and safety of recreational visitors and our staff. We are following the guidelines from our department and the CDC regarding COVID-19, closely monitoring the situation and responding to current conditions. 12 sites available; this campground lies on the south shore of the Middle Fork Feather River on Forest route 22N62 at the confluence of the Little North Fork of the Middle Fork Feather River and South Branch Feather River. Access is via Brush Creek or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/plumas/recarea/?recid=74968', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74986', 'Swift Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.728214, -121.657684, null, 'Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest', 'Swift Creek Campground (formerly Baker Lake Resort) is located about halfway up on Baker Lake across the road from Park Creek. The cabins are no longer there, but the area has been upgraded with about 50 private campsites that accommodate either tents or RVs. The campground includes a day-use area by the lakeshore with picnic tables, one shelter and grills, a paved boat ramp suitable for larger boats and a 20-slip dock.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbs/recarea/?recid=74986', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74989', 'Rogers Cow Camp', 'campground', 39.768000, -121.310000, null, 'Plumas National Forest', 'Recently redeveloped, this campground is located off 23N15 road, northwest of the Oro-Quincy Highway (Highway 162). The campground features 6 sites, a hand pump drinking water well, vault toilet, picnic tables, and fire rings. Popular motorcycle staging area. Single Track trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/plumas/recarea/?recid=74989', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '74991', 'Sand Flat Campground (4wd only)', 'campground', 38.404000, -119.788000, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', '4 x 4 drive to six sites with picnic tables, campfire rings. Near the North Fork of the Stanislaus River. Wooded area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=74991', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75147', 'Dairy Springs Campground', 'campground', 34.955960, -111.482080, null, 'Coconino National Forest Recreation', '/* http://www.dynamicdrive.com */ var mygallery=new fadeSlideShow({ wrapperid: "fadeshow1", dimensions: [500, 200], imagearray: [ ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384356.jpg", "/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384358.jpg", "_new", "Sign at the entrance to Dairy Springs Recreation Area."], ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384362.jpg", "/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384365.jpg", "_new ", "Campground Entrance."], ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384369.jpg", "/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384370.jpg", "_new ", "Informational Kiosk."], ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5384373.jpg",…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coconino/recarea/?recid=75147', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75414', 'Aspen Campground - East Fork Black River', 'campground', 33.807371, -109.314331, null, 'Apache-Sitgreaves National Forest', 'Aspen Campground on the East Fork of the Black River is a small campground shaded by Ponderosa pines and hardwood trees located streamside at a bend of the East Fork of the Black River. The East Fork meanders through the forested valley shaded by tall ponderosa pines and bordered by grasses, alders, and streamside hardwoods. Campsites are located a few steps from the stream to protect the Black River''s unique riparian zone, but access to the river is easy as the undergrowth serves more to enhance the river''s picturesque nature than to obstruct easy passage. Sites are small and only a few can…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/asnf/recarea/?recid=75414', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75464', 'Coyote Canyon Camping Area', 'campground', 36.072044, -106.630238, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Coyote Canyon Camping Area is a primitive campsite and picnic area next to Coyote Creek. Uses: picnicking, camping Facilities: One picnic table, two fire rings, and one portable toilet. No potable water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75464', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75498', 'Resumidero Camping Area', 'campground', 36.114451, -106.746919, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Resumidero is a popular primitive camping area. Located in a large alpine meadow, Resumidero is a local favorite and used by numerous recreationists for camping, picnicking, and group gatherings. Uses: Picnicking, camping, and parking for access to San Pedro Parks Wilderness through Vega Redonda trail 43 and Corralitos Trail 452 (on the west side of the meadow). Facilities: portable toilets during summer months only, picnic tables, fire rings. Special Instructions: The existing "acequia" (irrigation ditch) is utilized by residents for irrigation of farmland. PLEASE DO NOT POLLUTE THE WATER IN…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75498', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75502', 'Rio Chama Campground', 'campground', 36.355135, -106.672734, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Located on the Rio Chama Wild & Scenic River. Ten individual campsites each include a picnic table and a campfire ring. RV''s up to 20 feet can be accommodated in only a few sites. No potable water, or hookups.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75502', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75508', 'Rio Puerco Campground', 'campground', 36.099851, -106.724516, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Rio Puerco is a remote primitive campground. There are no fees and reservations are not accepted. Uses: camping, fishing, and picnicking. Facilities: picnic tables and 1 portable toilet during summer months only. There are no fire rings. Special Instructions: Can accommodate up to 20-foot RV''s. No potable water or hookups.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75508', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75530', 'Clear Creek Campground', 'campground', 35.998709, -106.828067, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Elk and deer in the surrounding forest, fish in the Rio de las Vacas and proximity to San Pedro Parks Wilderness make this campground at 8,500'' in elevation a veritable spring, summer and fall paradise.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75530', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75560', 'Rio De Las Vacas Campground', 'campground', 35.996940, -106.806110, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Tall Ponderosa Pines and meadows frame the Rio de las Vacas Campground. The Rio de las Vacas stream runs alongside the east boundary of the campground and offers fishing adjacent to camping sites. The campground is located approximately one mile past the Clear Creek Campground. May to October, picnicking in the open meadows, fishing the river or hunting the forests make this campground popular throughout the season.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75560', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75576', 'Aspen Basin Campground', 'campground', 35.794459, -105.805837, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'The Aspen Basin Campground is located adjacent to the very large parking area at Santa Fe Ski Basin. There are 10 units, Picnic tables, and fire rings. There is a vaulted toilet at the far west end of the parking lot. This campground is less developed than most, and primarily serves those who use it for an overnight stay before embarking on a backpack into the Pecos. There is ample space for trailer/RV camping, but no dump station is available. There is no potable water and no Campground Host. The entire area is very scenic, and NM 475 is also designated as the Santa Fe Scenic Byway. Because…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75576', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75602', 'Big Tesuque Campground', 'campground', 35.769170, -105.808610, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Big Tesuque is a travel-in campground not conducive to trailer or RV camping. There are 10 units, picnic tables and grills, and vaulted toilets in the parking lot. There is no potable water and no campground host. The entire area is very scenic, and NM 475 is designated as the Santa Fe Scenic Byway. Because of the large stands of aspen, the area is very busy, especially in the fall aspen viewing season. both above and below Big Tesuque Campground, including hiking, biking, and picnic areas. Winter activities include both nordic and alpine skiing. Tesuque is pronounced "tes-sue-kay"', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75602', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75604', 'Black Canyon Campground', 'campground', 35.725589, -105.839878, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Black Canyon Campground is one of the more popular campgrounds on the Santa Fe National Forest and offers the most amenities of any of the campgrounds in the Espanola Ranger District. Some sites are single- and double-family camping sites. Six are tent-camping only and visitors must park and travel to the campsite. A few are available on a first-come, first-serve basis. There are 36 units for cars and RVs. There are picnic tables and grills, a campground host on-site, vaulted toilets, and several double sites to accommodate a maximum of 16 people. There is a very nice hiking trail that leaves…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75604', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75608', 'Borrego Mesa Campground', 'campground', 35.977238, -105.771693, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'The Borrego Mesa Campground is located close to several trailheads leading into the north half of the Pecos Wilderness. Amenities include picnic tables, firepits, and small corrals at each site suitable for one or two horses. The vaulted toilet is currently not in service. Adjacent to and south of the campground is the Rio Medio Trailhead, one of the major trailheads into the Pecos Wilderness. The campground is rather primitive and little used, and is much less developed than most. The campground is rather primitive and receives little use; it is much less developed than most. It is primarily…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75608', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75776', 'Jemez Falls Campground', 'campground', 35.824533, -106.608470, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'The campground is located in a stunning Ponderosa Pine and forest meadow environment in proximity to the East Fork Jemez River. Come prepared for warm summer days and cooler nights. Jemez Falls, largest waterfall in the Jemez Mountains, is close by. The Valles Caldera National Preserve and Bandelier National Monument are within a short driving distance. Uses: Overnight camping, hiking and nearby fishing Facilities: Campground has 52 camp sites with picnic table and fire ring. Paved access which allows trailers and RV''s up to 40 feet. Vault toilets, no dump station available. Drinking water,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75776', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75798', 'Paliza Family Campground', 'campground', 35.704467, -106.626979, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Campground is situated in a beautiful Ponderosa Pine forest. Located in Lower Paliza Canyon, the campground has original CCC shelters in some sites. At 6,700 feet please come prepared for warm days and cool nights. Uses: Overnight camping, hiking Facilities: 30 camp sites; five sites have shade shelters. Vault toilets; no dump station available. There is no drinking water available at the campground. Special Instructions: This campground is designated as a reduced impact and recycle campground. Users are required pack out trash during the off-season. Cutting live vegetation is prohibited.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75798', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75806', 'Redondo Campground', 'campground', 35.861390, -106.626725, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'The Redondo Campground is situated in a stand of Ponderosa Pine interspersed with grass and wildflower meadows within the Jemez National Recreation Area. The campground is approximately 8,200 feet in elevation and you can plan for warm days and cool nights. The Valles Caldera and Bandelier National Monument are within driving distance, both are accessed via the Jemez Mountains Trail National Scenic Byway (NM State Highway 4). Uses: Overnight camping, hiking and fishing Facilities: Campground has 62 camp sites; each with a picnic table and fire ring. Vault toilets are available; there are not…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75806', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75816', 'San Antonio Group Campground', 'campground', 35.886374, -106.646273, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'The San Antonio Group Campground is located in the San Antonio Campground. This area has towering ponderosa pines, open forest meadows, and has the San Antonio River running alongside it. Visitors can access the paved walking trail found in the campground. There are 11 parking spaces for the nine campsites in the group area. Facilities: Group site with nine walk-in camp sites and a pavilion which accommodates up to people. The campground has vault toilets and drinking water spigots. No dump station is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75816', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75836', 'Vista Linda Campground', 'campground', 35.715519, -106.721545, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'This popular campground is open year round. The campground is located in the scenic San Diego Canyon, with spectacular red rock canyon and mesa views. Come prepared for warm days and cool nights during the summer months and cold winter temperatures. The Jemez River, adjacent to the campground, offers excellent fishing opportunities (valid State fishing license required) and wildlife viewing. Uses: Overnight camping, hiking and fishing. Facilities: The campground has 13 units with grills. Host is present on-site. Amenities include drinking water, paved access and vault toilets. No hook-ups or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75836', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75860', 'Cowles Campground', 'campground', 35.812683, -105.664353, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Cowles Campground sits at the base of the Winsor Canyon where it meets the Pecos Canyon and is near Cowles Ponds, Winsor Creek, Pecos River, and Winsor Ridge Trailhead. Note: campground shelters are currently closed while safety assessments are performed. Uses: tent camping, picnicking, fishing, & hiking. Facilities: 1 vault toilet, 9 camping units with tables, fire rings, grills, 2 covered three-sided shelters with fireplaces, and trash bins. No potable water, utility hook-ups, dump stations or showers. Special Instructions: Users are encouraged to recycle and pack out trash. Please visit…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75860', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75864', 'Winsor Ridge Trailhead', 'campground', 35.812604, -105.659773, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Located 20 miles north of Pecos on NM 63, the Winsor Ridge Trailhead is the access point for Winsor Ridge Trail #271 and the trail to Panchuela Campground and Trailhead. Uses: Hiking, Backpacking, Horseback Riding. Facilities: vaulted toilet, trash bins, trailhead kiosk, parking for passenger vehicles & trailers. Special Considerations: Users are encouraged to recycle and pack out trash. Please visit the Leave No Trace website for more information about frontcountry and backcountry outdoor ethics www.lnt.org .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75864', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75870', 'El Porvenir Campground', 'campground', 35.710318, -105.412239, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Beautifully situated in a mixed conifer forest next to Beaver Creek near the base of Hermit''s Peak. Some suggested uses: tent and RV camping, picnicking, fishing, hiking. Facilities: 13 camping units with picnic tables, fire rings/grills, 2 vault toilets, and bear proof trash bins. No utility hookups, dump stations or showers. Special Instructions: Users are encouraged to recycle and pack out trash. Please visit the Leave No Trace website for more information about frontcounty and backcountry outdoor ethics .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75870', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75872', 'E.V. Long Campground', 'campground', 35.698367, -105.421959, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Situated next to Gallinas Creek among big Ponderosa Pines and mixed conifers, E.V. Long Campground provides a rustic-type camping experience. Uses: tent and RV camping, picnicking, hiking and fishing. Facilities: 3 vault toilets, tables, fire rings, grills, and trash bins. A total of 14 camping units exist (first-come, first- serve basis). No hook-ups, dump stations, or showers available. Special Instructions: Users are encouraged to recycle and pack out trash. Please visit the Leave No Trace website for more information about frontcountry and backcountry outdoor ethics.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75872', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75874', 'Field Tract Campground', 'campground', 35.686703, -105.693073, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Situated on the Pecos River, Field Tract Campground provides an inviting forested setting. The Sangre De Cristo Mountains surround the Pecos Canyon and provide magnificent opportunities for wildlife viewing. This campground offers tent and small-RV campsites, vault toilets, drinking water, picnic tables and grills. Six of the 15 units have three-sided shelters. Campsites are suitable for trailers up to 22 feet in length.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75874', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75894', 'Holy Ghost Campground', 'campground', 35.769466, -105.700164, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'This 23 site Campground is situated in a beautiful steep canyon right along Holy Ghost Creek, 16 miles north of Pecos on NM 63 and FR 122. Facilities: vaulted toilets, trash bins, tables and grills. Caution: Holy Ghost Road is very narrow and is not suitable for large trailers. Avoid driving off the pavement on the high bank (uphill side) of the road to protect endangered plant habitat. Take only photos of flowers, do not pick them . Leaving them provides for pollinators (butterflies and bees) and seeds for next year''s flowers. Please remove mud, seeds, vegetation and debris from everything…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75894', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75902', 'Iron Gate Campground', 'campground', 35.839949, -105.620315, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Important Note: The campground is OPEN to the public but visitors may encounter a closed gate on Forest Road 223 before the campground. This gate is for livestock management. Please feel free to enter through the gate but close it again once you pass through. Thank you for your cooperation. Located above 9,000 feet, Iron Gate Campground is an excellent spot to access the Pecos Wilderness for day hiking and horseback riding. This campground features 14 indivdual units, vaulted toilets, trash bin, tables, fire pit/grill, 4 horse corrals. Maximum recommended length for vehicle and horse trailer…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75902', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75906', 'Jacks Creek Campground', 'campground', 35.838930, -105.655774, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Bring Your Own Water No drinking water provided. Please bring your own potable water for the duration of your trip. New water systems are anticipated to be installed in 2025. Located in the Sangre de Cristo Mountains this 39 site campground is near the Pecos Wilderness Area, which features 160,000 acres of majestic mountain scenery, high mountain lakes and the Pecos River, and is forested with fir trees intermixed with aspens, which shimmer with golden foliage in the fall. A variety of wildlife, such as elk, mule deer, migratory birds, and other raptors inhabit the nearby Forest. Hikers find…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75906', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75926', 'Links Tract Campground', 'campground', 35.756697, -105.661353, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Primitive dispersed camping located 16 miles north of Pecos on NM 63, then 1 mile on FR 646. Uses: Camping. Facilities: Pit toilet, tables, and few fire pits. No water is available. Special Instructions: Users are encouraged to recycle and pack out trash. There are no fees.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75926', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '75950', 'Panchuela Campground', 'campground', 35.829844, -105.664173, null, 'Santa Fe National Forest', 'Panchuela campground is nestled at the edge of the Pecos Wilderness with Panchuela Creek running along the eastern side of the campground. The campground has potable water. At a little over 8,300 feet visitors to this campground escape from the warmer temperatures of the city and enjoy the moderate temperatures of the Sangre de Cristo Mountains. There are 6 sites inside the campground and are within walking distance of the parking lot. With the nearby Pecos Wilderness Area, this campground makes for the perfect base camp for those looking take day hikes into the Wilderness Area. The campsites…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/santafe/recarea/?recid=75950', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76026', 'Iron Lake Campground', 'campground', 44.905457, -114.193174, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Eight campsites with picnic tables and fire rings are along the shores of this high alpine lake. the campground has piped drinking water and vault toilets but no garbage services are available. The trail from campground leads to more lake fishing, at the Hat Lakes to the south. Carry-down access for non motorized boats to the lakes. The drive in along Salmon River Mountain Road, offers spectacular views of craggy peaks and deep pine forests.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76026', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76028', 'Lost Spring Campground', 'campground', 45.850244, -114.465607, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '6 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings are along Silver Creek offer a quiet setting in the forest. This primitive campsite has a vault toilet, no drinking water, and no garbage services and is popular with hunters in the fall.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76028', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76032', 'Mill Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.472647, -114.440978, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This small, but popular campground is near Challis and along the Custer Motorway. Nearby access for rainbow trout fishing in Mill Creek. The motorized trail to the east of the campground heads south to Bayhorse Lake campground and trail system. Eight camping units contain picnic tables and fire rings, with an additional larger site that fits group camping. The campground amenities include a vault toilet and hand pump for drinking water. No garbage collection service is available. ATV use on Forest Roads only - no riding within campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76032', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76034', 'Mosquito Flat Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 44.517942, -114.433556, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This recreation site has 11 campsites and a day use picnic area along the shore of Mosquito Flat Reservoir near Challis. Nearby, the Yankee Fork Trail (#147) provides access to the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness. Each campsite is equipped with picnic tables and fire rings. The campground accommodates motorhomes and trailers up to 32-foot long. There are vault toilets on site, but no drinking water or garbage services within the site. Fish Your National Forests: This site can be accessed by Passenger Car; Fish available include: Trout; Types of fishing available include: Wade,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76034', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76036', 'Morse Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.630881, -113.790783, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Three primitive campsites with picnic tables and fire rings along Morse Creek. The campground amenities include a vault toilet. No garbage service or drinking water are on site. Nearby activities include fishing for trout and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76036', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76038', 'Big Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.441573, -113.599379, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Three primitive campsites at the confluence of the North and South Forks of Big Creek. Each site is equipped with a picnic table and fire ring. The campground has a vault toilet and there is no drinking water or garbage service on site. Horse/Hiker and motorized trails from the campground follow each creek for several miles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76038', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76042', 'Iron Bog Campground', 'campground', 43.650000, -113.765108, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground has 21 campsites with a maximum length trailer size of 35 foot. Seven sites are located along Iron Bog creek and the rest are out in the open sage-brush. There is one hand pump (during summer months) and two accessible restrooms. Four campsites have shade-awnings. Non-reservable campground with a $10.00/night fee. Hitching rail available outside of the campground, no horses are allowed in the campground. One group campsite with 25 person capacity. Nearby Iron Bog Lake, Brockie Lake and Fishpole Lake. Smiley Mountain looms overhead. Use is light, with the exception of holiday…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76042', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76044', 'Phi Kappa Campground', 'campground', 43.860000, -114.217000, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'The campground has 21 campsites in a beautiful wooded setting. Amenities include one handpump to provide potable water (the natural color of which is rusty), and two vault toilets. Water is only available during the summer months. Non-reservable campground with $10/night fee. Nearby areas of Interest are Kane Lake, Big Fall Creek Lake, Sun Valley/Ketchum Area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76044', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76046', 'Park Creek Campground', 'campground', 43.836538, -114.258507, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'The Park Creek Campground has 12 units in a wooded setting. There is one handpump that provides potable water, and one vault toilet. Water is available in summer months only. Nearby areas of interest include Summit Creek Trail, Big and Little Fall Creek, and Sun Valley/Ketchum.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76046', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76048', 'Star Hope Campground', 'campground', 43.745000, -113.941000, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'The Starhope Campground has 21 units in a beautiful wooded setting with Starhope Creek flowing through it. There are two handpumps to provide potable water, three vault toilets are available, and several hitching rails. The hitching rails are located outside of the campground. Horses are not allowed in the campground. Water is available during summer months only. Nearby areas of interest include Broad Canyon, Starhope Canyon and Bear Creek Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76048', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76050', 'Timber Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.397965, -113.409405, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '**SUMMER 2024- THERE WILL BE NO WATER AT TIMBER CREEK CAMPGROUND** The Timber Creek Campground has 12 camp units in a wooded setting, with two creeks flowing on either side of it. Two faucets provide potable water in the summer months. There is also one accessible vault toilet, a horse hitch rail and unloading ramp. Nearby areas of interest include Mill Creek Lake, and Timber Creek ATV trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76050', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76052', 'Wildhorse Campground', 'campground', 43.824055, -114.095199, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'The Wildhorse campground has 13 sites in a heavily wooded setting. There are two handpumps that provide water in the summer months, and two accessible vault toilets. Nearby areas of interest include Boulder Creek Lake, Waterfall Trail, and the head of Wildhorse canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76052', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76062', 'Boundary Creek Campground Complex', 'campground', 44.529281, -115.292166, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Boundary Creek Campground is located within the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness, adjacent to the boat launch for the Middle Fork of the Salmon River in Idaho. It has 15 units containing fire rings, picnic tables, and parking spurs. There is a comfort station and drinking water available at four hydrants throughout the campground. Generally, the site provides overnight camping for boaters awaiting the next days launch on the Middle Fork of the Salmon River. Five units are now reservable through Recreation.gov . Fish Your National Forests: This site can be accessed by Passenger Car;…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76062', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76064', 'West Fork Morgan Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.702731, -114.315206, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'One site with picnic table and fire ring, near trail access to Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness. Camp area amenities include a vault toilet. No drinking water or garbage service is on site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76064', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76068', 'Dagger Falls Campground', 'campground', 44.528440, -115.285582, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Eight sites are located along the Middle Fork of the Salmon River away from the busy Boundary Creek launch area. Each site has a picnic table and fire ring. The campground amenities include a vault toilet and drinking water. There are no garbage services available. The water falls are magnificent and the fishing terrific.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76068', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76072', 'Meadow Lake Campground', 'campground', 44.434780, -113.317560, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Updated August 29, 2022 The water system has been shut down for the season. Meadow Lake Campground is located on the Leadore Ranger District of the Salmon-Challis National Forest. This high alpine campground sits at an elevation of 9,160 feet in the Lemhi Mountain Range, 22 miles from Leadore, Idaho. Natural Features: Meadow Lake Campground is located at the base of the 10,720-foot Meadow Lake Peak and along the banks of the 13.3-acre Meadow Lake. The high elevation campground is dotted with lodge pole pine and white bark pine trees and is frequented by deer and mountain goats. Recreation :…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76080', 'Corn Creek Boat Ramp & Campground', 'campground', 45.369220, -114.684075, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '2900-foot elevation. 18 campsites on the Salmon River. Put-in for floating the Salmon Wild & Scenic River, Class III-IV rapids. Hiking and horse riding trail from campground loops south to Butt Creek Point, then north to Horse Creek Campground, also on the Salmon. Fishing in the river for cutthroat and rainbow trout, steelhead and whitefish. Picnic facilities are accessible. Boat ramp used by jet boaters and river floaters.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76080', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76082', 'Horse Creek Hot Spring & Campground', 'campground', 45.503868, -114.459951, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '6200-foot elevation. Disperse camping near the border of the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness and Montana''s Bitterroot National Forest - restroom facilites, but no picnic tables or fire-rings. Trout fishing in Woods Creek. No trailheads from campground, but a number of trails branch in all directions from the trailhead 4 miles west on Forest Road 065.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76082', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76084', 'Ebenezer Campground', 'campground', 45.305770, -114.515733, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '11 campsites on the Wild & Scenic Salmon River. Fishing in the river for cutthroat and rainbow trout, steelhead and whitefish. Trailheads to the west and north of the campground access extensive trail systems, and loop trips can be planned, heading north and west or south and east.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76084', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76086', 'Spring Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.392022, -114.254310, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '5 developed campsites and numerous undeveloped sites on the Wild and Scenic Salmon River, upstream from its confluence with the Wild and Scenic Middle Fork. The area is easy to explore-- it''s webbed with dirt roads, jeep trails, and single track trails. Fishing in the river for cutthroat and rainbow trout, steelhead and whitefish. Put-in for a 10 mile run with Class III rapids at the popular day use area. Take-out at Cove Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76086', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76090', 'Bighorn Crags Campground', 'campground', 45.103372, -114.526745, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '14 campsites with picnic tables and fire grates near the main trailhead for the Bighorn Crags in the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness. Separate area for horse camping with corrals and water troughs. Campground has piped drinking water, vault toilets but no garbage collection services on site. This is an area of rugged mountains, lakes, and hoodoos. Trails climb up into a highly popular region of the wilderness, winding past numerous lakes and fascinating geologic formations.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76090', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76092', 'Williams Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.019026, -113.989044, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '4500-foot elevation. Picnic area on Williams Lake, with the trailhead to 2 walk-in or boat-in campsites. The picic area and fishing area are both fully accessible. Five tables with connecting walkways overlook scenic vistas of the lake and surrounding mountains. Fishing for rainbow trout in the lake, and fantastic fly fishing in the inlet. Trailhead for Thunder Mountain National Historic Trail at the end of FR 028. Ice fishing in the winter. Full-service resort on south shore of the lake includes a tackle shop and restaurant.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76092', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76094', 'Cougar Point Campground', 'campground', 45.083168, -114.054661, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '6600-foot elevation. 18 campsites in the Salmon River Mountains. Big game hunting in season. Short trails run north, south and west from the campground. The area is heavily timbered with mixed conifers.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76094', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76096', 'Wallace Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.247307, -114.007289, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '12 campsites on Wallace Lake with picnic tables and fire rings. Within the campground are vault toilets and drinking water. Fishing in the lake. Primitive boat launch can be used for non-motorized canoes or rowboats on the lake. The drive on Salmon River Mountain Road offers fantastic views of the Salmon River Range and of deep pine forests.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76096', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76104', 'Deep Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.124877, -114.216551, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '4800-foot elevation. 3 campsites along Deep Creek Ridge. Short trail to Leacock Point.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76104', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76106', 'Mcdonald Flat Campground', 'campground', 45.034126, -114.298237, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '5400-foot elevation. 6 campsites along Panther Creek. Fishing for wily trout in Panther Creek. 20-foot maximum trailer length.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76106', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76108', 'Yellowjacket Lake Campground', 'campground', 45.066400, -114.551500, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '8000-foot elevation. 7 campsites on Yellowjacket Lake, near the border of the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness. Sugarloaf Rock provides a fascinating and stunning backdrop for the lake. Trails from the campground go throughout the Yellowjacket Mountains and into the wilderness. Nearby trailside attractions are Hoodoo Meadows, McEleny Peak, and Yellowjacket Creek. Most area trails, except those in the wilderness, are open to multiple use. Fishing in the lake or in Yellowjacket Creek. Carry-down access for non-motorized boats to the lake. FR 113 is narrow with few turnouts. Not…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76108', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76110', 'Twin Creek Campground & Group Picnic', 'campground', 45.608646, -113.967219, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', '5100-foot elevation. 40 campsites near the North Fork of the Salmon River. Fishing in the river and in Twin Creek. Loop hike on trails #108 & #109. Historical monument marks the Lewis and Clark National Historical Trail. There are no garbage services at the campground or pavilion.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76110', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76112', 'Bench Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.319298, -115.235834, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'A nice small campground in the trees along Bench Creek near Highway 21. Fishing in the stream and nearby Bull Trout Lake. Trail adjacent to the campground, heading southeast to Stanley Lake. Each of the 5 sites have picnic tables and fire rings with cooking grills. Amenities within the campground include a vault toilet. No drinking water is provided on site, and this small campground accommodates smaller trailers and motorhomes up to 30 feet long.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76112', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76114', 'Banner Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.353392, -115.214479, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'A nice campground along Highway 21 in the trees with a small creek running through. Campground has 5 campsites with picnic tables and fire rings with cooking grills. The campground amemities include a vault toilet. No drinking water is available and the campground is limited to trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet long; there are no hookups within the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76114', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76116', 'Thatcher Campground', 'campground', 44.368177, -115.145376, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground is just off Highway 21, and tucked back into the trees, overlooking beautiful Capehorn meadows. Walk across the street to overlook a marshy wetland, a hangout for breakfasting moose, elk, and a variety of birds. Each of the 5 sites is equipped with picnic tables and fire rings with cooking grills. The campground accommodates trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet and has vault toilets and hand pumps for drinking water. No full hookups.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76116', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76118', 'Pole Flat Campground', 'campground', 44.303789, -114.719457, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground is away from the main road and up the hill overlooking the river and the dredge ponds. Campsites include picnic tables tent pads fire rings with cooking grills. Campground amenities include a vault toilet and drinking water. Sites accommodate trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet long.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76118', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76120', 'Custer #1 Campground', 'campground', 44.399185, -114.663981, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground is along the Custer Motorway just above the townsite of Custer, a boom town during the late 1800''s. Visit the museum, open 9 - 5 Memorial Day through Labor Day. Facilities include 6 sites with picnic tables and fire rings with cooking grills. Campground has a vault toilet and can accommodate trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet long.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76120', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76122', 'Lola Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.407383, -115.180017, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Lola Creek Campground sits adjacent to Marsh Creek. Marsh Creek Trailhead is a short distance away as is the trailhead to Lola Lakes. Each of the 21 campsites is equipped with picnic tables and fire rings with cooking grills. The campground amenities include vault toilets, trash removal services and handpumps for drinking water. The campground accommodates trailers and motorhomes up to 35 feet long. There are no hookups and the stay limit is 14 days. The trail along Marsh Creek heads into the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness and to the Middle Fork of the Salmon River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76122', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76126', 'Flat Rock Campground', 'campground', 44.290182, -114.718574, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground offers camping adjacent to the Yankee Fork of the Salmon River. Fishing for rainbow trout in the river, and interpretive and historical tours is available nearby. Facilities at each of the 6 sites include picnic tables, fire pits with cooking grills. Campground amenities include a vault toilet, hand pump for drinking water but no full hookups. Sites accommodate trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet long.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76126', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76128', 'Beaver Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.415531, -115.146280, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Beautiful setting along Beaver Creek, this campground is close to access for the Frank Church River of No Return Wilderness. Fishing for trout in Beaver Creek, in nearby Cape Horn lakes, and in the many alpine lakes found along the trail in the wilderness. Trail #4021 leaves the campground to go north into the wilderness. Horse corrals with feeding stations are across the road, at the trailhead. Facilities at each of the 8 campsites include tables and fire rings with cooking grills. Within the campground amenities include hand pump for well water and newer vault toilets. While there are no…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76128', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76130', 'Blind Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.281334, -114.732761, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This campground is the first of several campsites along the canyon formed by the Yankee Fork of the Salmon River. Fishing for rainbow trout in the river, and interpretive and historical tours available nearby. Each site has picnic tables, fire rings with cooking grills. There is a Vault toilet. The sites accommodate trailers and motorhomes up to 32 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76130', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76132', 'Flat Rock Extension Campground', 'campground', 44.293039, -114.716074, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Just upriver from Flat Rock Campground, this little campground is a favorite. Shaded sites sit along the road and the Yankee Fork River is across the road. Three campsite facilities include picnic tables, tent pads and fire rings with cooking grills. The campground has a vault toilet and accommodates trailers and motorhomes up to 16 feet. There are no hookups, drinking water is only available from nearby Flat Rock Campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76132', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76170', 'Mill Creek Trailhead & Campground', 'campground', 44.366961, -113.362762, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'Mill Creek Campground and Trailhead consists six camp sites available in a wooded setting along scenic Mill Creek. There is one accessible vault toilet, hitching rail, and unloading ramp. No Water is available. Nearby areas of interest include Mill Creek Lake National Recreation Trail, Mill Creek Lake and Firebox Meadows.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76170', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76192', 'Lake Creek Trailhead & Campground', 'campground', 43.767935, -113.903099, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This area has four camping units in an open sage brush area adjacent to Lake Creek with one vault toilet. Hitching rails and loading ramp are available outside of the campground. Horses are not allowed in the campground. Drinking water is available during the summer months. Nearby attractions are the Lake Creek ATV trail, Green Lake Trail, and Muldoon Canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76192', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76194', 'Mt. Borah Trailhead and Camping Area', 'campground', 44.133601, -113.837293, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This area serves as a base camp for climbing the tallest mountain in Idaho. It has 5 campsites, accessible vault toilet, No drinking water, safety and informational signs. Nearby areas of interest include Earthquake site and Mackay Reservoir.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76194', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '76244', 'Banner Summit Rest Stop', 'scenic_drive', 44.305873, -115.231716, null, 'Salmon-Challis National Forest', 'This rest stop also has two picnic tables for travelers to enjoy a picnic.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/scnf/recarea/?recid=76244', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77510', 'Herb Martyr Campground', 'campground', 31.872500, -109.234400, null, 'Coronado National Forest', 'The Herb Martyr trailhead, located near Herb Martyr campgound, is one of the popular birdwatching and overall hiking areas in Cave Creek Canyon. Though South Fork is known for its trogons, there are plenty of other interesting and rare creatures to encounter here. Over 300 species of birds have been sighted in the Chiricahua Mountains, including the magnificent hummingbird, blue-throated hummingbird and Montezuma quail. Other interesting types of wildlife frequently sighted here include Apache fox squirrels, coatimundis and Coues white-tailed deer. The scenery is quite impressive in this…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coronado/recarea/?recid=77510', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77553', 'Great Meadow Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 42.396832, -122.196154, null, 'Fremont-Winema National Forest', 'The Great Meadows Sno-Park is for summer and winter recreation. In the winter, you''ll find over 165 miles of groomed trails for snowmobiling, cross-country skiing, and snowshoeing. Food and lodging are available at Lake of the Woods and Fish Lake resorts. From the Sno-Park, there are scenic views of Mt. McLoughlin to the north. Great Meadows Sno-Park is located 35 minutes west of Klamath Falls, Oregon. It was specifically designed as a Sno-Park with land from a construction phase in the 1940s. Today the expansive 1.5 acre parking lot accommodates up to 50 vehicles with trailers in the winter,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/fremont-winema/recarea/?recid=77553', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77573', 'Murray Bay Campground', 'campground', 48.265960, -113.815070, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Overview Murray Bay Campground is located high in the Rocky Mountains, less than 30 miles from the Continental Divide, surrounded by towering mountain peaks. Visitors can expect a variety of recreational activities, including, fishing, boating, swimming, hiking, exploring and big game hunting. The campground is 22 miles south of Martin City on the east shore of Hungry Horse Reservoir. This campground has a 16 day stay limit. Pets must be on a leash at all times while visiting campgrounds. Natural Features: The campground is situated along the massive Hungry Horse Reservoir, which was dammed…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=77573', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77576', 'Lid Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.285880, -113.909540, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Lid Creek Campground is a 23-site campground with picnic tables, vault toilets, & fire grates. There is no water available. There is a native boat ramp- only small watercraft are recommended for launching. The campground is 15 miles south of Hungry Horse on the west shore of Hungry Horse Reservoir. This campground has a 16 day stay limit. Pets must be on a leash at all times while visiting campgrounds. Overview Lid Creek Campground lies in the heart of the Rocky Mountains, west of the Continental Divide and just south of the Canadian border. Spectacular views and ample opportunities for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=77576', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77578', 'Big Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.599800, -114.162100, null, 'Flathead National Forest', 'Big Creek Campground feature a hosted, 22-site campground with picnic tables, vault toilets, fire grates, and potable water. There is a boat ramp for river launching. The campground is 20 miles north of Columbia Falls on the North Fork Road. This is bear-country; proper food storage is required. This campground has a 14-day stay limit. Pets must be on a leash at all times while visiting campgrounds. Campground Map Big Creek Campsite / Big Creek Boat Ramp / River View at Big Creek', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/flathead/recarea/?recid=77578', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77588', 'Mann Creek Campground', 'campground', 44.412308, -116.909779, null, 'Payette National Forest', 'Located on Bureau of Reclamation land and operated by the Payette National Forest, Mann Creek Campground offers 13 sites, several of which are accessible for people with disabilities. Picnic tables, some of which are covered, and fire rings, vault toilets and drinking water are provided. Roads and spurs are gravel. No hook-ups are provided. This area is hot and dry in the summer, and shade is limited. The typical season of use is mid-April to late-September. Exact opening dates depend on snow levels.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/payette/recarea/?recid=77588', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77616', 'Diamond Fork', 'campground', 40.071848, -111.430550, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Winter recreation area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=77616', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77623', 'Dru Barner Campground', 'campground', 38.942930, -120.764091, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'The campground is ideal for equestrian use, with four water troughs, several pull through spaces, and access to trails. The park provides day-use facilities for staging non-motorized trails recreation. Location: 7.5 miles east of Georgetown on Wentworth Springs Road (Forest Road 1), then 1 mile north east on Forest Road 13N16 and 0.5 miles northwest on Forest Road 13N58. Dru Barner Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contain information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77623', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77626', 'Stumpy Meadows Campground', 'campground', 38.904586, -120.591024, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 17 miles east of Georgetown on Wentworth Springs Road. Stumpy Meadows Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77626', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77632', 'Hell Hole Campground', 'campground', 39.070476, -120.416609, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 22 miles east of Georgetown on Wentworth Springs Road, and 29 miles northeast on Forest Highway 2 (Eleven Pines road) to just before Hell Hole Reservoir. Hell Hole Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77632', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77633', 'Upper Hole Campground', 'campground', 39.081898, -120.357878, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'This facility is only accessible by boat or trail. Location: 22 miles east of Georgetown on Wentworth Springs Road, and 29 miles northeast on Forest Highway 2 (Eleven Pines road) to Hell Hole Reservoir, then 3 miles southeast by boat or hiking trail. Upper Hell Hole Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77633', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77634', 'Big Meadows Campground', 'campground', 39.074505, -120.427383, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Location: 22 miles east of Georgetown on Wentworth Springs Road and 27 miles northeast on Forest Highway 2. Big Meadows Campground Recreation Opportunity Guide (ROG) - This guide contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77634', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77636', 'Wrights Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.844582, -120.236676, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Wrights Lake Campground Wrights Equestrian Camping Fees and Passes Picnicking Desolation Wilderness Desolation Wilderness web site', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77636', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77646', 'Dead Horse Campground', 'campground', 41.033706, -110.366206, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Dead Horse Campground. This campground does not have water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=77646', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77736', 'Chestatee Overlook', 'scenic_drive', 34.664960, -83.982860, null, 'Chattahoochee-Oconee National Forest', 'The Chestatee Overlook gives you a wide-angle view of the watershed that gives rise to the Chestatee River. In the foreground lies the Dockery Lake Campground and in the distance is the Blood Mountain Wilderness. This is a great photo opportunity.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/conf/recarea/?recid=77736', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77811', 'Cerro Alto Campground', 'campground', 35.424400, -120.741100, null, 'Los Padres National Forest', 'The campground sits at 1,000 above sea level in a verdant canyon pass astride a semiannual creek. Cerro Alto Peak (2,624 ) is the destination of Hikers, Bikers and Equestrians with its 360 view encompassing the Central California Coast and Inland Valley. The campground has 22 units, 12 of which are handicapped accessible. Each site has a picnic table, fire ring and most have a pedestal grill. Several of the sites are walk-in sites. Cerro Alto Campground is located at the base of Cerro Alto Peak. The Forest Service maintained a fire lookout tower at the top of Cerro Alto Peak until 1973. At an…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lpnf/recarea/?recid=77811', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77817', 'Osceola Vista Campground/Group Campground', 'campground', 43.972535, -71.518785, null, 'White Mountain National Forest', 'Osceola Vista is a popular spot for group camping and is located near a host of outdoor activities, including hiking, mountain biking, canoeing and golfing. Just minutes away, hiking enthusiasts will find the Sandwich Range Wilderness and 80 miles of the White Mountain National Forest''s prime hiking trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whitemountain/recarea/?recid=77817', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '77826', 'Sand Flat Campground', 'campground', 38.763837, -120.324530, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Sand Flat Campground Fees and Passes Hiking/Biking Trails', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=77826', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78502', 'Lovers Leap Campground', 'campground', 38.799416, -120.141112, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Lovers Leap Campground Fees', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78502', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78504', 'China Flat Campground', 'campground', 38.755033, -120.267988, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. China Flat Campground Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78504', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
