  ('usfs', '78514', 'Pipi Campground', 'campground', 38.567305, -120.439261, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Pipi Campground Picnicking Fees and Passes Gold Note OHV Trail System', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78514', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78515', 'Middle Fork Cosumnes Campground', 'campground', 38.584286, -120.300105, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Middle Fork Cosumnes Campground Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78515', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78517', 'Sugar Pine Point Campground', 'campground', 38.547154, -120.240428, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Sugar Pine Point Campground Fees and Passes', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78517', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78518', 'Pardoes Point Campground', 'campground', 38.535995, -120.238214, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Pardoes Point Campground Picnicking Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78518', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78519', 'South Shore Campground', 'campground', 38.535420, -120.244792, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. South Shore Campground Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78519', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78522', 'Silver Lake Campground East', 'campground', 38.672243, -120.119797, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Silver Lake Campground Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails Mokelumne Wilderness', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78522', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78523', 'Silver Lake Campground West', 'campground', 38.672243, -120.119797, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'This facility is owned and operated by El Dorado Irrigation District. www.eid.org/recreation/silver-lake', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78523', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78524', 'Caples Lake Campground', 'campground', 38.704164, -120.052795, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Caples Lake Campground Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails Mokelumne Wilderness', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78524', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78527', 'Kirkwood Campground', 'campground', 38.707073, -120.087194, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Kirkwood Campground Picnicking Fees and Passes Non-motorized Trails Mokelumne Wilderness', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78527', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78531', 'Mokelumne Campground', 'campground', 38.478592, -120.271143, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. Mokelumne Campground Non-motorized Trails Mokelumne Wilderness Mokelumne Wilderness web site', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78531', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78532', 'White Azalea Campground', 'campground', 38.485128, -120.262261, null, 'Eldorado National Forest', 'Recreation Opportunity Guides (ROG) - These guides contains information, maps, and directions to assist you in enjoying your trip to the Eldorado National Forest. White Azalea Campground Non-motorized Trails Mokelumne Wilderness Mokelumne Wilderness web site', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/eldorado/recarea/?recid=78532', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78570', 'Rucker Lake Campground', 'campground', 39.357732, -120.652105, null, 'Tahoe National Forest', 'This is a PG&E lake/campground on the Tahoe National Forest. Car-top launch for kayaks and boats. There is no boat ramp at the lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tahoe/recarea/?recid=78570', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78658', 'Windfall Harbor Shelter', 'campground', 57.837500, -134.316670, null, 'Tongass National Forest', '12'' x 10'' 3-sided CCC Adirondack-style shelter with dirt floor', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78658', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78669', 'Eagles Nest Campground', 'campground', 55.706667, -132.851667, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Eagle''s Nest Campground is nestled in the forest above the scenic Balls Lake. The campground provides 12 camping sites, including ten drive-in sites and two walk-in locations along the lake side. One centrally located, two-stall outhouse is provided. Eagle''s Nest is perfect for families traveling through Prince of Wales Island that want to stop and rest at a beautiful, well-cared for campground in the center of the Island. Eagle''s Nest also offers an accessible Interpretive Trail that describes the salmon cycle in the stream, as well as longer hiking trail. Special Features: Eagle''s Nest…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78669', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78675', 'Harris River Campground', 'campground', 55.466917, -132.862194, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Harris River Campground has 14 drive-in campsites, with space for a small to medium-sized RV, picnic tables, and fire rings. Two outhouses are available. A short trail leads visitors through a muskeg and its unique vegetation. Reserve campsites or pay with fee envelope at site. Stay limit is 14 days. Special Features: The Harris River Campground offers quiet, peaceful campsites. Across the road is the Twentymile Spur Trail that follows the Harris River through its steep valley. Visitors should bring their salmon rod as there is great fishing right beside the campground in the lower Harris…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78675', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78679', 'Horseshoe Hole Campground', 'campground', 55.814417, -133.129694, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Horseshoe Hole dispersed camping area is situated at the end of a timber road in the Staney Creek watershed and offers two campsites. It is only a quick walk through the woods to Horseshoe Hole on Staney Creek from either of the two campsites. Each site has a hardened tent site, a fire ring, and a picnic table. No outhouses are available. The area provides visitors with miles of roads, excellent fishing on the creek and its tributaries, hunting opportunities, and great berry picking. There are lots of opportunities to view wildlife at Horseshoe Hole. The site has no fee and is first-come,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78679', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78686', 'Lake No. 3 Campground', 'campground', 55.653056, -132.584417, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Lake No. 3 dispersed camping area is named for the lake that one of the sites overlooks. This small camping area has 2 hardened campsites, fire rings and picnic tables available for visitors looking for a more secluded camping area. Special Features: Lake No. 3 dispersed campsite is a nice, small site without a lot of amenities. It is within a mile of the Salt Chuck Trail , which brings hikers to an interesting abandoned copper mine site. The campsite is also close to Lake Ellen and No. 3 Lake. Many visitors hike down to these lakes to swim or fish for trout and Dolly Varden. The second…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78686', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78700', 'Staney Bridge Campground', 'campground', 55.806917, -133.122500, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Staney Bridge dispersed camping area is located just west of the Staney Creek crossing on Forest Service Road 2050. The dispersed camping area offers two sites, each with a hardened tent site, a fire ring and a picnic table. The Staney Bridge camping sites are within walking distance from Staney Creek and excellent fishing. This area provides visitors with miles of roads, excellent fishing on the creek and its tributaries, hunting opportunities, and great berry picking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78700', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78742', 'Road 85784', 'scenic_drive', 57.938000, -135.610000, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Closed Road 85784.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78742', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78743', 'Road 85785', 'scenic_drive', 57.914000, -135.575000, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Closed Road 85785.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78743', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78744', 'Road 85786', 'scenic_drive', 57.912000, -135.561000, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Closed Road 85786.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78744', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78750', 'Auk Village Campground', 'campground', 58.375108, -134.729376, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Near a scenic beach, the campground was once a village site for the Auk Tlingit Natives. There are 11 camping sites and each campsite has a picnic table and fire ring; most meet accessibility standards. There are water faucets and one accessible vault toilet in the campground. It is 15 miles Northwest of Juneau on Glacier Highway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78750', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78790', 'Mendenhall Lake Campground', 'campground', 58.413342, -134.592905, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'This campground is on Mendenhall Lake, with a view of the Mendenhall Glacier, and is about 13 miles from downtown Juneau. Sites include: 9 full-service RV sites with electricity, water and sewer hook-ups; 9 partial-service RV sites with electricity and water hook-ups; 51 basic-service sites; 7 sites in a separate walk-in backpacker area with covered shelter for cooking; 48 sites that accommodate camping units larger than 30 feet. All of the sites have tent pads, picnic tables and fire grills that meet accessibility standards. Water faucets and vault toilets are dispersed throughout the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78790', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78833', 'Anchor Pass Buoy', 'campground', 55.973210, -131.397310, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'This buoy is white with blue and white reflective tape. It is available on a first come, first serve basis and is intended for use by small to medium watercraft. The buoy is located in 30-80 feet of water and has a 7/8 inch chain. This buoy provides a means of access to the Anchor Bay cabin maintained by the Forest Service.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78833', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78854', 'Last Chance Campground', 'campground', 55.423333, -131.560000, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'ALERT: 05/25/18 NO potable water at this time . Please check back for updates. This campground has 19 drive-in camping units (17 of these are fully accessible to people in wheelchairs) available with paved road access. Facilities include fire rings, garbage cans, vault toilets, and hand pump water - no hookups. Last Chance Campground was reconstructed in 1995 and is designed to be barrier free. All unreserved sites are available on a first-come-first-serve basis.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78854', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78893', 'Icehouse Cove Buoy Camping Area', 'campground', 55.298430, -131.470050, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'This buoy is available on a first come; first serve basis and is intended for use by small and medium watercraft. The buoy is located in 30-80 feet of water and has a 7/8 inch chain. Look for a white buoy with blue reflective tape. This buoy provides access to the Black Mountain trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78893', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78904', 'Signal Creek Campground', 'campground', 55.409167, -131.697778, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Signal Creek Campground is a drive-in campground with 24 units. Stay in stunning campsites surrounded by giant spruce, hemlock, and cedar trees. This area is adjacent to Ward Lake, hiking trails, and an abundance of fishing areas. All unreserved sites are available on a first-come-first-serve basis.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78904', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '78962', 'Three C''s Group Use Campground', 'campground', 55.411111, -131.694167, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'This campground has 4 drive-in camping units available with paved road access. Facilities include fire rings, garbage cans, vault toilets, and hand pump water - no hookups. This site is available for group use and is only available to single users if other campgrounds (Signal Creek, Last Chance) are full.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=78962', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79014', 'Ohmer Creek Campground', 'campground', 56.577300, -132.740000, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Ohmer Creek Campground is on a minimal maintenance schedule due to budget constraints. Please pack in/pack out your trash and use restroom facilities at neighboring Forest Service recreation areas if a waste containment system is not available on your camping unit.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79014', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79124', 'Sawmill Creek Campground', 'campground', 57.061406, -135.209458, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Primitive campground with 4 overnight sites and 1 day use covered picnic shelter', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79124', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79135', 'Starrigavan Rec Area - Campsites', 'campground', 57.132887, -135.366274, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Starrigavan Recreation Area - 34 primitive campsites located in 3 loops; fully ADA accessible.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79135', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79188', 'Lower Salamander Creek Campground', 'campground', 56.348333, -132.190556, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Site is located next to Salamander Creek. There are 3 separate covered picnic shelters each with a picnic table and fire ring. A small sandy beach is located next to the shelter closest to the creek and swimming opportunities exist at higher water levels.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79188', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79197', 'Nemo Campsites Entry & Info Site', 'campground', 56.305833, -132.347778, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Entry and Information site for the Nemo Campsites on Wrangell Island. Site is occupied by Wrangell Island Host Volunteers, and used for evening campground programs in the summer months. Available for camping when not occupied by island hosts. Information boards provide posted information for the public.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79197', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79201', 'North Wrangell Pond Shelter', 'campground', 56.458690, -132.296650, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The North Wrangell Pond Shelter on Wrangell Island is a 3-sided shelter accessible via a 0.4 mile spur off the North Wrangell Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79201', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79209', 'Thoms Creek Crossing Campsite', 'campground', 56.188056, -132.162500, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Thoms Creek Crossing Campsite is a fully accessible, single occupancy campsite on the south end of Wrangell Island. Access is via a short footpath from the parking area at the bridge to the site on the shore of Thom''s Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79209', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79211', 'Three Sisters Overlook Campsite', 'campground', 56.295278, -132.343306, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Three Sisters Overlook Campsite is a fully accessible, single occupancy site on the Nemo-Skip Loop Road on Wrangell Island. Site overlooks Zimovia Strait, with spectacular views of the "three sister peaks" (Virginia, Bessie, and Helen) on Etolin Island.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79211', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79212', 'Turn Island Beach Campsite', 'campground', 56.252194, -132.334167, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'Located on the west shore of Wrangell Island, Turn Island Beach Campsite includes two tent platforms for camping and picnicking with a shared outhouse facility. The site is on saltwater, and can be accessed either by boat or on foot via the Nemo Saltwater Access Trail on Wrangell Island.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79212', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79215', 'Upper Salamander Creek Campsite', 'campground', 56.315278, -132.036667, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Upper Salamander Creek campsite is a fully accessible, single occupancy site on Wrangell Island. Access to site is via a 700 foot gravel path from the parking area on the road to the site overlooking Salamander Creek.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79217', 'Yunshookuh Loop Campground', 'campground', 56.308889, -132.336083, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'The Yunshookuh Loop Campsite is a fully accessible campground with options for RV or tent camping (no hookups). Space for three groups, with shared outhouse between sites. A 12'' x 16'' covered picnic shelter is located at the middle site. The site provides for scenic views of Zimovia Straight. Site is popular for winter sledding on roadway when snow limits access to ATV, snow machine, or skis/snowshoes.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79217', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79234', 'Yakutat Beach Campsite 2', 'campground', 59.501246, -139.752283, null, 'Tongass National Forest', 'This is the middle of three tent platforms along the beach bluff to the North West of the Cannons at Cannon Beach. This site consists of a tent platform that can be covered with a tarp, a picnic table and a fire ring. It is located on the bluff and accesses the beach. This site is used by people beachcombing, walking, picnicking, surfing, and camping.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tongass/recarea/?recid=79234', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79237', 'Columbine Corrals Campground', 'campground', 32.706429, -109.913457, null, 'Coronado National Forest', 'This campground, nestled in mixed-conifer forest at 9,440 feet, has six sites with picnic tables and fire pits. There are vault toilets, bear-proof trash cans, and public corrals. There is also drinking water at this site. Ash Creek Trail #307 and Web Peak Trail #345 start from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coronado/recarea/?recid=79237', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79271', 'Bagby Campground', 'campground', 44.954175, -122.168917, null, 'Mt. Hood National Forest', 'Bagby Hot Springs Campground is situated along the Hot Springs fork of the Collawash River. The campground is set among towering cedar and old-growth Douglas fir. The site is a wonderful base to experience Bagby Hot Springs and access primitive trails in the Bull of the Woods Wilderness . Bagby Campground provides camping with picnic tables, fire rings and vault toilets. Site capacity: 6 people and 2 vehicles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mthood/recarea/?recid=79271', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79307', 'Double Springs Campground', 'campground', 34.942380, -111.493580, null, 'Coconino National Forest Recreation', '/* http://www.dynamicdrive.com */ var mygallery=new fadeSlideShow({wrapperid: "fadeshow1", dimensions: [500, 200], imagearray: [["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382082.jpg", " /Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382083.jpg", "_new", "Welcome to Double Springs Campground."], ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382084.jpg", " /Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382085.jpg", "_new", "We’ll keep you informed when things change. "], ["/Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382086.jpg", " /Internet/FSE_MEDIA/stelprdb5382087.jpg", "_new", "Water is available at several locations – bring your jug!"],…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coconino/recarea/?recid=79307', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79401', 'Haynes Canyon Vista', 'scenic_drive', 32.931194, -105.761564, null, 'Lincoln National Forest', 'Located about 1 mile south of the NM6563 and NM130 turnoff, this viewing area (vista in spanish) makes for a wonderful photo opportunity.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lincoln/recarea/?recid=79401', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79452', 'Buffalo Gap Campground', 'campground', 46.954980, -103.673706, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', '#slider{border:0} $(window).load(function(){$("#slider").nivoSlider({effect:"fade",animSpeed:700,pauseTime:8000,randomStart:true,directionNav:true,controlNav:false})}); Buffalo Gap Campground features many amenities for an enjoyable camping experience. A camp host is on site from Memorial Day to Labor Day.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79452', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79454', 'CCC Campground', 'campground', 47.587142, -103.276520, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'This newly remodeled campground is a favorite among Maah Daah Hey Trail users.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79454', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79455', 'Summit Campground', 'campground', 47.539961, -103.241504, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'There are two walk-in tent sites with picnic tables and fire grates. There are also two picnic areas with shelters and pull through camping units for RV''s and other vehicles. The campground has a handicap accessible vault toilet. A 100-yd hiking trail leading west from the campground provides visitors with a scenic view of the underlying valley. Summit trailhead is in the north end of the campground on the west side of the road. The campground has sufficient parking space that can also be used as a meeting point for Summit Trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79455', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79456', 'Sather Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 47.672293, -103.807874, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Enjoy the lake view from your spacious campsite, or enjoy fishing for Bass, Crappie, or Trout off the floating pier located in the day use loop.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79456', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79457', 'Burning Coal Vein Campground', 'campground', 46.597678, -103.443906, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Enjoy the scenic lookout from the Columnar Juniper area or the Ponderosa Pines just south and west of the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79457', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79459', 'Bennett Campground', 'campground', 47.490278, -103.348667, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Enjoy the peaceful serenity offered at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79459', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79460', 'Magpie Campground', 'campground', 47.308585, -103.473584, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'This campground has plenty of shaded areas during the heat of summer. A perfect assembly point for folks who plan to travel to Devil''s Pass for the amazing view. The Ice Caves are just a short hike away from this campground as well! A Maah Daah Hey trailhead is located at this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79460', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79461', 'Elkhorn Campground', 'campground', 47.228405, -103.669277, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Enjoy the breathtaking view of a scenic canyon from this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79461', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79463', 'Wannagan Campground', 'campground', 47.055184, -103.587853, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'A great meeting area for the north end of the Buffalo Gap Trail. The switchbacks located on the Maah Daah Hey Trail offer a sweeping vista of the region, including a scenic view of many large buttes.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79463', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79464', 'Whitetail Picnic Area', 'campground', 47.197931, -103.303293, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Whitetail Picnic Area is a 10-unit picnic ground nestled in the densely wooded area of Whitetail Creek Drainage. Fire grates are available and a vault toilet. There is ample parking space available for most sizes of vehicle. Be aware that the road to the picnic area crosses Whitetail Creek via a low water crossing that may be impassable during periods of high runoff.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79464', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79476', 'Hankinson Hills Campground', 'campground', 46.119940, -96.967818, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Enjoy a night under the stars on the prairie at Hankinson Hills Campground, located three miles northwest of Hankinson, North Dakota. Click here for a map of the Hankinson Hills Campground and Trail. Hankinson Hills Campground has two camping loops. One camping loop, with six campsites, allows campers to have horses and the other camping loop, with nine campsites, is designated for campers without horses. There are a total of 15 campsites, each with a picnic table and fire ring. There is a large picnic shelter for day use and group events, as well as a large group fire ring with benches. The…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=79476', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79489', 'Soapstone Campground', 'campground', 40.578955, -111.028283, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Local popular recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. This campground is equipped with picnic tables.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=79489', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79503', 'Eshom Campground', 'campground', 36.689100, -118.950400, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located in the Giant Sequoia National Monument at 4,800 feet in elevation, this facility is nestled among ponderosa pine, cedar, Sequoia and other conifers. This Forest Service campground is part of the Hume Lake Ranger District in Sequoia National Forest. It is located approximately 80 miles northeast of Fresno, CA, near Kings Canyon and Sequoia National Parks. Natural Features: The Sequoia National Forest is located at the southern end of the Sierra Nevada in central California. The forest is divided into three districts that comprise 1.1 million acres. The Hume Lake Ranger District, in…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79503', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79508', 'Green Cabin Flat Campground', 'campground', 36.859586, -119.102523, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '1,000-foot elevation. Undeveloped camping area on the wild and scenic Kings River. This area is secluded and requires significant travel time to visit Giant sequoia trees. Whitewater rafting down to Pine Flat Reservoir, with up to Class III rapids. Food storage rules apply in black bear country. Check current fire restrictions before venturing out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79508', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79514', 'Hume Lake Campground', 'campground', 36.793783, -118.908090, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'The campground is within minutes of a walk to Hume Lake and groceries, public phone, boat rentals and other concessions including gasoline are also within a half-mile walk from most campsites. There are 74 campsites available on reservation. Great spot for fishing and other non-motorized water sports! ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit ExplorUS - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com ) or call their home office at 559-335-5385.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79514', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79520', 'Princess Campground', 'campground', 36.803000, -118.938000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'This spectacular site has three campground loops - Shining Cloud, Yellow Moon, and Morning Star. It has the greatest number of huge, old Sequoia tree stumps and young Sequoia trees along with a pleasant variety of conifers. Shade is good throughout the campground; privacy between camp sites is fair to good. Princess Campground is in the middle of Indian Basin Grove next to Indian Basin Meadow and Creek. 90 sites. Multi-family group sites. Dump station. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79520', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79533', 'Stony Creek Campground', 'campground', 36.665000, -118.833000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Stony Creek offers nearly 50 campsites on reservations, spread out along the creek. Vault toilets, drinking water and an amphitheater are available at the campground. Public phone, public showers, groceries, restaurant, and gasoline are available 1/2 mile away at the Stony Creek Resort. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit ExplorUS - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) or call their home office at (559)335-5385.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79533', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79537', 'Tenmile Campground', 'campground', 36.754000, -118.893500, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '5800-foot elevation. 13 campsites on Tenmile Creek. Hiking and mountain biking in two nearby sequoia groves. This campground is within the Giant Sequoia National Monument. Trails in the monument, open to hikers, horses, and bikes (outside the wilderness areas), wind through giant sequoia groves, up mountains, and alongside wild rivers. Compacted dirt surfaces, no drinking water Maximum RV length 22 feet. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit ExplorUS - Hospitality Management…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79537', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79539', 'Upper Stony Creek Campground', 'campground', 36.666000, -118.832500, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Upper Stony Creek campground is 14 miles SE of Grant Grove via Generals Highway. Upper Stony Creek offers 23 family units; units are mix of recreation vehicle and single car spurs. Vault toilets, picnic area, and drinking water are provided. Upper Stony Creeks campground elevation is 6,400 feet. Hiking into the Jennie Lakes Wilderness and mountain biking outside the wilderness are an attraction. Public phone, public showers, groceries, restaurant, and gasoline are available 1/2 mile away at the Stony Creek Resort. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79539', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79548', 'Landslide Campground', 'campground', 36.765000, -118.882000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '5800-foot elevation. Nine campsites, including six tent-only sites, with hiking in two nearby groves of giant sequoias. This campground is within the Giant Sequoia National Monument. Trails in the monument, open to hikers, horses, and bikes (outside the wilderness areas), wind through giant sequoia groves, up mountains, and alongside wild rivers. Compacted dirt surfaces, fee required Maximum RV length 16 feet. Special food storage rule in effect because this is black bear country! Check current fire restrictions before venturing out. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79548', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79554', 'Mill Flat Campground', 'campground', 36.856500, -119.097000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Mill Flat Campground is situated at 1,100 feet elevation with five campsites on the Kings Wild and Scenic River. Rafting is popular in the river, with up to Class III rapids in the river. This campground is within Giant Sequoia National Monument. Trails in the monument are open to hikers, horses, and bikes (outside the wilderness areas). Unsuitable for trailers, no drinking water. Special food storage rule in effect in black bear country. Check current fire restrictions before venturing out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79554', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79581', 'Big Meadow Campground', 'campground', 36.718140, -118.833060, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'This campground, at an elevation of 7,500 feet, is located near vast meadows and high granite mountains. There are 30 single units and 8 double units. Natural Features: An open meadow that is surrounded by a variety of pines, including lodgepole, Jeffery and red fir. A creek runs through the meadow. A trailhead nearby leads into the Jennie Lakes Wilderness. Buck Rock Lookout, perched at an elevation of 8,500 feet, is a short drive away. Hume Lake is approximately 15 miles from the campground. Recreation: Hiking into the Jennie Lakes Wilderness and fly fishing in Big Meadows Creek are popular…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79581', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79589', 'Buck Rock Campground', 'campground', 36.722725, -118.850537, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'This campground sits at 7,600 ft elevation. It is nearby to Big Meadow Creek, Buck Rock Lookout, and trails into Jennie Lakes wilderness. Natural Features: The Sequoia National Forest is located at the southern end of the Sierra Nevada in central California. The forest is divided into three districts that comprise 1.1 million acres. The Hume Lake Ranger District, in which this campground is located, has elevations range from about 1,000 along the Kings River near Pine Flat Reservoir and to 11,000 feet, the peak of Mt Harrington. This land scape is home to 13 Sequoia Groves and the majestic…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79589', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79592', 'Camp 4 Campground', 'campground', 36.857014, -119.106942, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located at 1,000-feet elevation, Camp 4 campground offers five campsites near the Wild and Scenic Kings River with a table, fire ring, and a vault toilet. Rafting is popular here, with up to Class III rapids in the river. Supplies may be obtained in Piedra. No drinking water is available. Unsuitable for trailers.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79592', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79597', 'Convict Flat Campground', 'campground', 36.819000, -118.833000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located in Kings Canyon, 19 miles NE of Grant Grove via Hwy 180. Campground (5 units), vault toilet and suitable for small - midsize trailers. Elevation 3,000 feet. No water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79597', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79605', 'Paradise Cove Campground', 'campground', 35.650502, -118.424729, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Paradise Cove offers beach type camping near the shore of Lake Isabella with 58 family units and 80 RV sites. Fish cleaning stations. Flush and vault toilets available. Great site for fishing on Lake Isabella. Dump station available with at fee of $20 per use. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79605', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79608', 'Pioneer Point Campground', 'campground', 35.650890, -118.485924, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Pioneer Point is located on the west side of Hwy 155 near Lake Isabella and offers 78 family unit sites. 30'' RV length. Fish cleaning station, Playground, bathrooms, picnic table, and fire ring with grill. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79608', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79618', 'Sandy Flat Campground', 'campground', 35.582717, -118.524584, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Sandy Flat Campground offers 35 family campsites along the lower Kern River south west from Lake Isabella. Includes 6 walk-in sites, water, and bathrooms. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79618', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79632', 'Auxiliary Dam Campground', 'campground', 35.643190, -118.462890, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located on the southern end of Lake Isabella off Highway 178 near the town of Lake Isabella, this facility offers flush toilets, drinking water, trash service, a dump station and some campsites with stoves and picnic tables above the high water mark. Below the high-water mark, visitors can drive their vehicles to the shoreline and camp at the water''s edge. Below the high-water mark portable toilets and trash receptacles are provided for visitor convenience during the summer. ExplorUS All developed campground areas in the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUs. For…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79632', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79654', 'Boulder Gulch Campground', 'campground', 35.672621, -118.468762, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Boulder Gulch Campground is 2650 ft elevation. Amenities include 78 camping sites, potable water, flush toilets, a fish cleaning station and a playground. This is a popular fishing area. Maximum RV Length is 45 ft. Campfire permits are required for campfires, barbeques, and camp stoves. Permits are available at your local Ranger Station or online at preventwildfireca.org This site can be reserved by calling Toll Free 1-877-444-6777 (International 518-885-3639 or TDD 877-833-6777) or on-line at Boulder Gulch, Sequoia National Forest - Recreation.gov . ExplorUS All developed campground areas on…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79654', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79656', 'Breckenridge Campground', 'campground', 35.467343, -118.580825, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Breckenridge Campground is the only campground on Breckenridge mountain that offers picnic tables and vault restrooms. This campground is unsuitable for trailers, but offers a rustic experience for camping, hunting, or just exploring. No Water available; Pack out all trash Campfire permits are required for campfires, barbeques, and camp stoves. Permits are available at your local Ranger Station or online at readyforwildfire.org', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79656', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79660', 'Brush Creek Dispersed Camping', 'campground', 35.964361, -118.478222, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Brush Creek is a dispersed camping or day use site open year round. There are vault toilets available and seasonal trash bins. This is where the Brush Creek meets the Upper Kern River and is a good spot for fishing. Effective July 30, 2022 through September 30, 2024 No camping within 50 feet of the Brush Creek water''s edge, between the intersection of Brush Creek with the Kern River and points 0.5 miles east of the Kern River along both branches of Brush Creek, in the Brush Creek Dispersed Camping Area. Campfire permits are required for campfires, barbeques, and camp stoves. During fire…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79660', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79664', 'Camp 3 Campground', 'campground', 35.806670, -118.452780, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Camp Three Campground is set amidst oak and locust trees at an elevation of 2,800 feet on the Upper Kern River, offering countless recreational opportunities for visitors. Natural Features: The Sequoia National Forest, located at the southern end of the Sierra Nevada in central California, takes its name from the giant sequoia, the world''s largest tree, which grows in more than 30 groves on the Forest''s lower slopes. The Forest comprises about 1.1 million acres, and elevations range from about 1,000 to 12,000 feet, creating precipitous canyons and mountain streams with spectacular waterfalls,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79664', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79668', 'Camp 9 Recreation Area Campground', 'campground', 35.690657, -118.425226, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Camp 9, rests on the shores of Lake Isabella, a high desert reservoir (elevation 2,600 feet). In the spring and early summer, the breeze can come up in the afternoons, but the mornings are quiet and calm. Camp 9 is popular with RVs and there is lots of parking available to accommodate trailers and motorized watercraft. Dump station fee is $20 per use (there is NO free dumping! ie: free dumping with 4 or more days reserved). For watercraft a courtesy dock for launching located within the day use portion of the site if water levels are accommodating. Shade is limited so plan on bringing…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79668', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79673', 'Cedar Creek Campground', 'campground', 35.749030, -118.582388, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Cedar Creek Campground is currently closed due to damage from the 2016 Cedar Fire. 4800-foot elevation. 11 campsites, with fishing on Cedar Creek. This high elevation campground is a more rustic and mountainous area. The campground offers picnic tables and restrooms. Unsuitable for trailers. Cedar Creek runs the entire length of the campground on both the north and south sides of Hwy 155.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79673', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79676', 'Chico Flat Dispersed Camping', 'campground', 35.823500, -118.462000, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Dispersed Camping on Upper Kern River approximately 4 to 5 miles north from Kernville. Ther is no water available at this location. Portable toilets and trash receptacles are available during summer months. See Larger Picture Here . Dispersed Camping Rules, Regulations, and Tips', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79676', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79695', 'Evans Flat Campground', 'campground', 35.642740, -118.588983, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '6100-foot elevation. 20 campsites with fenced pastures and corrals for horses. A network of roads and trails covers the area. Access from Rancheria Road in the Greenhorn Mountains. Fenced pasture, 4 equestrian sites, no drinking water, Maximum RV length 20 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79695', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79696', 'Fairview Campground', 'campground', 35.928843, -118.490455, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Scenic campground along the North Fork of the Kern River 3500 foot elevation. 55 camp units. Maximum RV length is 45 feet. Vault toilets available. This is available through the reservation system. Accessible campsites available. ExplorUs All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79696', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79697', 'Fish Creek Campground', 'campground', 36.066813, -118.217443, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '54 miles northeast of Kernville via Mtn. 99 and Sherman Pass Rd. (22S05), or 32 miles west of Hwy. 395 via Nine Mile Canyon Rd. (J41). Paved roads; 40 units including 12 suitable for RV''s up to 24''; restrooms; piped well water. There is no trash collection. Elev. 7,400 feet. Open Jun. to Nov. Fee -$17 per night.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79697', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79703', 'Goldledge Campground', 'campground', 35.873727, -118.455981, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Camping along the North Fork of the Kern River 10 miles north of Kernville. 37 campsites. Trailers up to 30 feet. Reservable. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79703', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79712', 'Headquarters Campground', 'campground', 35.797109, -118.449839, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Headquarters Campground is 4 miles north from Kernville via Mountain Hwy 99 along the North Fork of the Kern River. Paved access roads. 44 individual family units including 1 accessible family unit. Trailers up to 27 feet; toilets, and water available. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit ExplorUS - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) or call their home office at (559) 335-5385.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79712', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79713', 'Hobo Campground', 'campground', 35.574459, -118.528778, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Hobo Campground is on the Lower Kern River southwest of Lake Isabella. It has 23 individual family sites. Maximum of 22 foot RV length, but is unsuitable for trailers. Vault toilets available onsite. No water available. This campground in by reservation only', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79713', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79717', 'Horse Meadow Campground', 'campground', 35.902012, -118.371251, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'PLEASE NOTE: There is no water available at this campground. Please come prepared. 7600-foot elevation. 41 campsites. Near Cherry Hill Road 22S12/23S10. Maximum RV length 22 feet. Special food storage rule in effect because this is black bear country! Check current fire restrictions before venturing out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79717', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79719', 'Hospital Flat Campground', 'campground', 35.828762, -118.458043, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'At 3,000 foot elevation along the North Fork of the Kern River, Hospital Flat Campground offers 40 individual family units, and 1 accessible group unit with ramp. Maximum 30 foot RV and trailer length. Paved access roads. Bathrooms and water available. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79719', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79720', 'Hungry Gulch Campground', 'campground', 35.672485, -118.471542, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'At an elevation of 2,700 feet, the Hungry Gulch Campground offers 78 individual family campsites near Lake Isabella. 30'' max RV and trailer length. Water, and bathrooms available. Picnic tables, fire rings with grills, playground. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with EXplorUS. For additional information, please visit ExplorUS - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79720', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79737', 'Limestone Campground', 'campground', 35.963457, -118.478307, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Offering 22 campsites on the Wild and Scenic Kern River, Limestone sits at 3800-foot elevation. Whitewater rafting and fishing in the river. Hiking, mountain biking in the area. No drinking water available Maximum RV length 30 feet. Please pack out your trash. For Kern River Ranger District recreation information, please call 760-376-3781. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79737', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79744', 'Live Oak North Campground', 'campground', 35.702462, -118.460339, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Elevation: 2700'', Sites: 60 Open holiday weekends, fee required Maximum RV length 30 feet. Reservable through www.recreation.gov. ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661) 702-1420, or their Lake Isabella office at 760-376-1269.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79744', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79746', 'Live Oak South Campground', 'campground', 35.701952, -118.461340, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '2700 feet. 90 campsites. 30'' maximum RV length. Reservable through www.recreation.gov.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79746', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79763', 'Old Isabella', 'campground', 35.652472, -118.456888, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located off Highway 178 on the southern side of Lake Isabella, this facility offers visitors a vault toilet, trash service, a visitor information station, and campsites above the high-water mark. Below the high-water mark, visitors can drive their vehicles to the shoreline and camp at the water''s edge. Below the high-water mark, portable toilets and trash receptacles are provided for visitor convenience during the summer. Adjacent to the camping site there is a public boat launch and courtesy dock with a large, paved parking area for vehicles and boat trailers, flush toilets, and drinking…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79763', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79812', 'Quaking Aspen Campground', 'campground', 36.120813, -118.545005, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located along the Western Divide Highway a quarter of a mile past the end of State Highway 190 (27 miles east of Springville). The campground was named for the quaking aspen trees that grow in the area. The trees are a shimmering brilliant green in the spring and deep russet-gold in the fall. Hiking is available on the many trails near the campground. The campground has 32 single family units, two of which are accessible, including a vault toilet. Some units can accommodate recreational vehicles up to a maximum length of 24 feet. Sanitary facilities, potable water, tables, and BBQ stoves are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79812', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79816', 'Redwood Meadow Campground', 'campground', 35.977780, -118.591670, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'This USFS campground is located about 50 miles east of Springville, CA, in the Tule Ranger District of the Sequoia National Forest. There are fishing and hiking opportunities nearby. Trail of 100 Giants is nearby. Approximate season dates are May 17 to October 13. 58 miles SE of Porterville via Hwy 190 and Western Divide Highway . Suitable for RV''s 16'' long; 15 family units; toilets; water; elevation 6,500 feet; open May to October; supplies at Ponderosa Lodge and R-Ranch; campground adjacent to the Trail of 100 Giants. Reservations available. Campfire permits are required for campfires,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79816', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79829', 'Upper Peppermint Dispersed Area', 'campground', 36.082888, -118.525166, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '7100-foot elevation. Undeveloped dispersed camping area within the Giant Sequoia National Monument. Fishing available in nearby Peppermint creek, check with the Department of Fish and Wildlife for regulations. No services, no fee. Dispersed Camping Rules, Regulations, and Tips', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79829', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79831', 'White River Campground', 'campground', 35.845830, -118.634720, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'The White River Campground sits in a stand of mature cedar along the banks of the White River at an altitude of 4,000 feet. The campgrounds are approximately 8 miles from the popular California Hot Springs. Natural Features: The Sequoia National Forest, located at the southern end of the Sierra Nevada in central California, takes its name from the giant sequoia, the world''s largest tree, which grows in more than 30 groves on the Forest''s lower slopes. The Forest comprises about 1.1 million acres, and elevations range from about 1,000 to 12,000 feet, creating precipitous canyons and mountain…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79831', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79837', 'Holey Meadow Campground', 'campground', 35.953618, -118.618590, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '60 miles SE of Porterville. Suitable for RV''s 16'' long; paved and narrow dirt road; toilet; No water; elevation 6,400 feet. Open May to October. Supplies available at Ponderosa Lodge and R-Ranch. Campfire permits are required for campfires, barbeques, and camp stoves. Permits are available at your local Ranger Station or online at Campfire Permit - Ready for Wildfire . ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79837', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79843', 'Leavis Flat Campground', 'campground', 35.879715, -118.676201, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Operated by volunteers from the Giant Sequoia National Monument Association. 3000 feet elevation. 9 campsites. 16 foot max RV length. No water, no reservations. ​ALERT: Incidence of human-bear conflicts have been occurring in this area during the 2024 season. Bears that successfully obtain human food can become easily habituated. Please help protect yourself, other visitors, and bears by using bear resistant food storage canisters while visiting the area', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79857', 'South Fork Rec Campground', 'campground', 35.658567, -118.436891, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located off Highway 178 on the southern side of Lake Isabella, this facility offers flush toilets, trash service, drinking water, a visitor information station, and campsites with stoves and picnic tables above the high-water mark. Below the high-water mark, visitors can drive their vehicles to the shoreline and camp at the water''s edge. Below the high-water mark portable toilets and trash receptacles are provided for visitor convenience during the summer. The site also offers a public boat launch and courtesy dock. ExplorUS For additional information, please visit About Explorus -…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79857', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79870', 'Tillie Creek Campground', 'campground', 35.701458, -118.456155, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Tillie Creek offers 159 family campsites for tents or RV''s campsites. 45'' RV limit. Fish cleaning stations, Playground, bathrooms, picnic tables, and fire rings with grills. Campfire permits are required for campfires, barbeques, and camp stoves. Permits are available at your local Ranger Station or online at Campfire Permit - Ready for Wildfire . ExplorUS All developed campground areas on the Forest operate under a concessionaire permit with ExplorUS. For additional information, please visit About Explorus - Hospitality Management (goexplorus.com) , or call their home office at (661)…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79870', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79874', 'Troy Meadow Campground', 'campground', 36.066813, -118.235298, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', '53 miles northeast of Kernville via Mtn. 99 and Sherman Pass Rd. (22S05), or 34 miles west of Hwy. 395 via Nine Mile Canyon Rd. (J41). Paved roads; 73 units including RV''s with no trailer length limit; restrooms. There is no trash collection. Elev. 7,800 feet. Open Jun. to Nov. Fee -$17 per night. Non-potable water at this time. Connects to OHV trails. This campground offers high elevation forest camping. Including; bear boxes, paved parking spurs.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79874', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79889', 'Belknap Campground', 'campground', 36.141559, -118.747020, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located 19 miles east of Springville , California , take State Highway 190 to the community of Camp Nelson . Turn onto Nelson Drive and follow the signs through town. Elevation is 4,800 feet. Open from April 15 - October 31 depending on weather conditions. The campground has 15 single family units. No trailers or RVs allowed. Vault toilets, potable water, tables, and BBQ stoves are provided. Nearby hiking trails pass through giant sequoia groves. Belknap Creek runs through the campground and the Middle Fork of the Tule River is within walking distance. Fishing is available year around in the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79889', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '79897', 'Coy Flat Campground', 'campground', 36.129309, -118.618694, null, 'Sequoia National Forest', 'Located 20 miles east of Springville, CA, near Camp Nelson via State Highway 190. The campground has 19 single family units and 1 double family unit. Some units can accommodate recreational vehicles up to maximum length of 24 feet. Sanitary facilities, potable water, tables, and BBQ stoves are provided. Open from April 12 through October 27 dependent upon weather conditions. Elevation is 5,000 feet. Hiking trails pass through nearby giant sequoia groves. The Middle Fork of the Tule River and Bear Creek are within a short walking or driving distance. Fishing is available year around on the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sequoia/recarea/?recid=79897', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80034', 'Monjeau Lookout', 'campground', 33.430786, -105.731610, null, 'Lincoln National Forest', 'Monjeau Lookout is a famous landmark on the Smokey Bear Ranger District built originally in 1936 and then reconstructed in 1940 as part of a Civilian Conservation Corps project. This site is a wonderful and adventurous place to visit. Roads leading up to the site are dirt and can be steep in places. Visit during the summer months as the road leading to it closes during the winter with the advent of snow. Monjeau Lookout is listed on the National Register of Historic Places (NRHP).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lincoln/recarea/?recid=80034', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80045', 'Weitas Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.637561, -115.433064, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Weitas Campground is a very popular, no fee campground that''s located about 35 miles northeast of Pierce, just off Forest Service road [FSR] 250. Much of the campground''s appeal comes from its location along the shady banks of Weitas Creek, just south of the North Fork of the Clearwater River (you cross a bridge to reach the campground.) There are only six campsites, so Weitas Campground tends to fill quickly during the height of the summer recreation season. Trail #20 runs south, and then east, out of the campground, providing miles of first-class bank fishing opportunities. The trail…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80045', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80046', 'Washington Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.701869, -115.555933, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Crossing the bridge over to Washington Creek Campground, visitors gain a splendid view overlooking the North Fork of the Clearwater River. This campground offers one host site and 23 campsites (including one group site). Each site contains a gravel parking pad, picnic table and fire ring, with access to 5 restrooms and 3 water spigots which are distributed around the loop for visitors'' convenience. Washington Ridge Trail departs from the campground, offering visitors quick access to higher elevation perspective. The trail is open to hikers, stock users, bicyclists and motorcycles. With river…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80046', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80049', 'Noe Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.684883, -115.366381, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'This six unit campground has an almost park-like aesthetic and is nestled in groves of fir and larch with views of the North Fork River. Whether coming for the day to fish or to stay for a couple nights with your family, Noe Creek Campground is a nice choice if you''re looking for a quiet and peaceful spot to get away.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80049', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80050', 'Kelly Forks Campground', 'campground', 46.717084, -115.254688, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Tucked away in a heavily wooded, streamside location at the confluence of Kelly Creek and the North Fork of the Clearwater River in Northwest Idaho, is Kelly Forks Campground. With 14 campground sites, a group area, campground host and a hiking trail going directly up to Flat Mountain from the site, horseback riding trails in the vicinity, swimming and an abundant watchable wildlife, Kelly Forks has a little of everything. Also, for the all the anglers out there, Kelly Forks boasts a Blue Ribbon cutthroat trout stream (catch and release).', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80050', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80054', 'Hidden Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.831724, -115.179114, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Tucked away in groves of old growth cedar trees and adjacent to the stunning North Fork of the Clearwater River in northwest Idaho, rests a hidden gem: Hidden Creek Campground. With 13 sites, one group tent camping pad, many fishing opportunities and nearby hiking trails, Hidden Creek Campground has proved to be a favorite for many visitors looking to camp out in a place that truely feels encased in nature and her many delights.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80054', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80062', 'Cedars Campground', 'campground', 46.872587, -115.076850, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Cedars campground has five developed campsites situated alongside the North Fork of the Clearwater River and Long Creek. A loop of the Idaho Centennial Trail passes by the campground, and other hiking/horse riding trails are nearby. Anglers will also love this spot as trout are abundant.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80062', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80070', 'Aquarius Campground and Purple Beach Group Site', 'campground', 46.841620, -115.618899, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Aquarius Campground boasts 9 developed sites and 2 group campsites (Purple Beach) on the bank of the scenic North Fork of the Clearwater River. Swimming, fly fishing, tubing and whitewater rafting (May and June) are just a few of the many water sports visitors can enjoy here. Hunters, anglers, and families looking for a quiet spot to take a dip and get away with the kids can all find respite here. Hiking trails near the campground take hikers and backpackers alike into the Mallard Larkins Pioneer Area and to the Black Mountain summit, one of the few remaining places in Idaho where Mountain…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80070', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80077', 'Partridge Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.784423, -116.149056, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Northeast of the Elk Creek Reservoir, located in Elk River, Idaho, the Partridge Creek Campground offers 13 primitive campsites, access to the 3.5 mile Patridge Creek ATV Trail, and an opportunity to drive our scenic Elk River Backcountry Byway!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80077', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80080', 'Little Boulder Campground', 'campground', 46.771233, -116.458522, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Located only 40 miles east of the town of Moscow, Idaho, Little Boulder Campground rests next to the Potlatch River in a heavily forested and richly vegetated and peaceful location. Great for RVs and tents, 17 developed sites, a campground host and all with ample parking and an overflow lot--It''s easy to see why the Little Boulder Campground is a local favorite.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80080', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80081', 'Laird Park Campground', 'campground', 46.943872, -116.645914, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Laird Park Campground, located in the northwest Idaho town of Potlatch and named in memory of A.W. Laird, a lumberman and early leader in the Potlatch Lumber Co., is a fantastic location to bring your family, friends or maybe even your boy or girl scout troupe for some outdoor fun and swimming. The recreation area has a sandy beach (a result of a swimming beach dam built by the Civilian Conservation Corps in 1933), 2 group picnic areas as well a half-mile interpretive trail. Fishing is a popular passtime here too, with abundant opportunities for rainbow and brown trout from the Palouse River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80081', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80125', 'Shaw House', 'campground', 31.931275, -109.961692, null, 'Coronado National Forest', 'This historic 3-bedroom rock house is located in east Cochise Stronghold, within the homeland of the famed Chiricahua Apache chief. Set in the spectacularly scenic Dragoon Mountains, guests enjoy views of Rockfellow Dome, and the house is close to excellent hiking, mountain biking, and horseback riding opportunities. View Photos', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coronado/recarea/?recid=80125', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80130', 'Elk Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.783300, -116.170278, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Less than a mile from the quiet town of Elk River in the mountains of north central Idaho, the Elk Creek Campground is found in a picturesque setting of mature pine forests and next to the tinkling waters of Elk Creek. Only minutes from the largest waterfall in Idaho and the largest and oldest cedar tree east of the cascade range, and a favorite for berry pickers everywhere, this 24 site campground with host and a group shelter is an ideal place for your next family getaway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80130', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80159', 'White Sand Campground', 'campground', 46.508111, -114.686167, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', '59 miles southwest of Missoula, Montana, White Sand Campground is found between the Elk Summit Road and Lochsa River adjacent to White Sand Pond. The campground is underneath a stand of mixed conifers and shrubs. The campground consists of one loop with seven sites and offers picnic tables and fire rings. A day use area located adjacent to the pond is popular for fishing and picnicking. The Campground will accomodate 30-ft. RV''s.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80159', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80161', 'Powell Campground', 'campground', 46.512472, -114.720167, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Adjacent to the Wild and Scenic Lochsa River, 60 miles southwest of Missoula, MT and 88 miles northeast of Kooskia, ID, the Powell Campground has 3 paved loops and sits in a mature stand of mixed-conifers and shrubs, providing nice shade for all of the campsites.It offers water, picnic tables, fire rings, and toilets. A popular destination for visitors from Montana, as well as travelers along Highway 12, it is often used for family reunions, weddings and large group gatherings, and is the only campground in this prospectus to offer electrical hook-ups. The campground is walking distance to…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80161', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80170', 'Treasure Park – Group Use Areas', 'campground', 32.661667, -109.871111, null, 'Coronado National Forest', 'Treasure Park North sits along the scenic Swift Trail in southern Arizona. The picturesque mountain meadow setting provides an escape from the desert heat and opportunities for viewing wildlife and wildflowers, as well as group camping, hiking, mountain biking and picnicking. The location boasts an interesting history. Legend has it that a treasure of stolen gold and silver was buried here by a band of outlaws in the 1850s. They reportedly marked the site with a triangle formed by three colored granite stones, though no buried treasure was ever found.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coronado/recarea/?recid=80170', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80175', 'Glade Creek Group Campground', 'campground', 42.222593, -115.529702, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'A popular spot with the locals, the quaint Glade Creek Group Campground has five sites and is peacefully tucked away on about four acres, alongside a rolling river and under a canopy of mixed-age conifers and low-growing shrubs. The vegetation provides privacy for each site as well as shade in the summer, and due to its position along a large bend in the river, and private beach access, this area is popular with groups of rafters and family gatherings. The campground is located thirty-one miles east of Kooskia and about eight miles east of Lowell, Idaho. Gas, groceries, and other services are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80175', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80229', 'No Name Road TH #705', 'scenic_drive', 39.465818, -106.345682, null, 'White River National Forest', 'This dirt road starts at Hwy 24 and ends at Hwy 24 again further to the south: This road is flat for the first 1/2 mile before steadily climbing switchbacks through forest for another 2 miles or so before reaching a ridge with outstanding views of the Homestake Valley and Camp Hale. It then climbs quickly into the forest and continues winding south for a total of 20 miles over the Continental Divide and ending up back at Hwy 24.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/whiteriver/recarea/?recid=80229', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80252', 'Knife Edge Campground and River Access', 'campground', 46.229620, -115.475088, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Located along the breathtaking Wild and Scenic Lochsa River, about fifteen minutes east of Lowell, ID, families, campers, anglers, kayakers, floaters and boaters may enjoy this five unit, two acre, free-use campground and Lochsa river/boat access site. Picnic tables, fire rings, a changing room, and a single vault restroom is also provided. The Campground will accomodate 40-ft. RV''s.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80252', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80290', 'TeleLi puLaya (Black Oak) Campground', 'campground', 38.193622, -120.052676, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'var $j = jQuery;$j.noConflict();$j(window).load(function() {$j(''#slider'').nivoSlider( {effect: ''fade'',startSlide: 0,animSpeed: 750,pauseTime: 8000});}); TeleLi puLaya Campground is a new campground, which opened in 2014 and provides spectacular views of the Stanislaus River Canyon. Turn left at the Beardsley Dam sign on Highway 108, 5 miles east of the Summit Ranger Station on Highway 108. There are a total of 22 sites, two are group sites. The main road and parking pads are paved. Restrooms are vault toilets. Each site has a table and metal fire ring. Potable water is available; each hydrant…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=80290', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80328', 'Howard Meadows Campground', 'campground', 39.878490, -122.991874, null, 'Mendocino National Forest', 'Has 6 developed sites and 1 vault toilet. No water. A high-clearance vehicle is needed to cross one section of the road into the campground. This campground has a variety of oak and conifer tree species within and around the campground. The campground experienced fire damage from the 2020 August Complex. Howard Lake is just down the road from Howard Meadow Campground, where lake fishing is possible.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mendocino/recarea/?recid=80328', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80483', 'Spring Drive RV Campground', 'campground', 45.114100, -121.517400, null, 'Mt. Hood National Forest', 'This site is easily accessible from Highway 216. Spring Drive RV Campground is a popular camping spot with access to a variety of recreational activities. It offers full hookups and 8 spacious campsites amid a forest of towering trees. The campground is an ideal destination for families that enjoy the great outdoors in the beautiful Pacific Northwest. It is not far from some great wilderness spots, including mountain lakes & streams, trails, and historic sites.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mthood/recarea/?recid=80483', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80545', 'North Timp Snowmobile Route #152', 'snow_area', 36.712815, -112.217131, null, 'Kaibab National Forest', 'The route to Timp and North Timp Viewpoints is a beautiful drive through a ponderosa pine forest. Both points offer a panoramic view of the Grand Canyon and its tributary canyons. Timp Point is the only known, easily accessible point on the Kaibab Plateau where it is possible,with binoculars, to see Thunder River as it emerges from the north wall of Tapeats Canyon. Cool, summer camping is available here with an excellent opportunity to view wildlife, particularly the Kaibab squirrel, deer, fox, turkey, hawks, eagles and a number of songbird species.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kaibab/recarea/?recid=80545', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80550', 'Wendover Campground', 'campground', 45.506646, -114.789682, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Wendover Campground is situated on stretch of land along the Wild and Scenic Lochsa River off the Northwest Passage Scenic Byway and All American Road (US Highway 12) at mile post 158.2. With 27 campsites all positioned within a mature, moss covered pine forest and centered around a small stream, this campground offers a serene spot for camping, picnicking, fishing, hiking, nature viewing and most importantly, relaxing. Hosts are provided when campground is open. The Campground will accomodate RV''s up to 40-ft.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80550', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80551', 'Whitehouse Campground', 'campground', 46.508517, -114.770525, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Approximately an hour west of Lolo, MT at mile post 158.5 of the famous Northwest Passage Scenic Byway and All American Road (US Highway 12), directly across from the Lochsa Wild and Scenic River, rests the Whitehouse Campground. This riverside campground has 11 sites and due to its close proximity to the Lewis and Clark Trail, has much more to offer than just camping. It''s an ideal location for fishing, hiking, back packing, nature viewing or as a place to stop and have a picnic while enjoying a scenic drive down highway 12. The Campground will accomodate 30-ft. RV''s.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80551', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80553', 'Elk Summit Campground', 'campground', 46.328489, -114.644519, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'This sweet destination of a campground rests a short distance from the 1.34 million acre Selway-Bitterroot Wilderness. Located just 24 miles south of Highway 12, you''ll have available to you 15 campsites, stock facilities, stunning scenery, and access to some of the nation''s wildest country including many remote alpine lakes and mountain peaks. Hoodoo Lake is just a short stroll from the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80553', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80567', 'Slide Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.503300, -115.153700, null, 'Humboldt-Toiyabe National Forest', 'Slide Creek Campground is located at the trailhead for Slide Creek which accesses the Jarbidge Wilderness (hiking, horse trips, hunting, backpacking), has one single restroom, horse corrals (no horses allowed in the campground), 5 sites, no water, and is free. Not reservable.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/htnf/recarea/?recid=80567', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80593', 'Cache la Poudre North Park Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 40.696301, -105.273039, null, 'Arapaho & Roosevelt National Forests Pawnee NG', 'This scenic byway is located along the Cache la Poudre River, Colorado''s only wild and scenic river! You can find more information on the Colorado Department of Transportation website .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/arp/recarea/?recid=80593', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80606', 'Lolo Creek Campground', 'campground', 46.294514, -115.751433, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Lolo Creek Campground consists of 9 camping units and is located 21 miles northeast of Kamiah, Idaho along the shores of Lolo and Eldorado Creek. This campground is a fantastic location for a rustic camping trip if you enjoy hiking, ohv trail riding, fishing, huckleberry picking or just watching the scenery while relaxing to the sounds of running water. With 9 camping units situated alongside both the Lolo and Eldorado Creeks, and only minutes from the Lewis & Clark Trail (#25) and the Musselshell OHV Trail System, the Lolo Creek Campground offers a wide variety of unique recreation…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80606', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80672', 'Green River Camps', 'campground', 40.911781, -109.313792, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'Take a step back in time and traverse the same waters that explorers such as John Wesley Powell and William Ashley once explored. Navigate the waters and cast a rod in an adventure the whole family can enjoy. The Green River provides spectacular fishing and river-running opportunities, as well as unique geology, outlaw history and Native American rock art. The Green River Float-In campsites contain 17 sites for river goers to float and camp along the mighty Green River. Some of these sites can be reached on foot but most of these sites can only be reached by boat.The campsites are nestled…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=80672', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80724', 'Wild Goose Campground', 'campground', 46.135869, -115.621975, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Situated along the middle fork of the Clearwater River at milepost 98 on scenic Highway 12, Wild Goose Campground offers a superb location to feel the sand between your toes while deciding on which river adventure you want to enjoy. Tubing, swimming and whitewater kayaking are just a few of the water sports you and your family can choose from, and guided trips and equipment rental are available in the nearby towns of Syringa and Lowel, Idaho. With eight campsites, two toilets and gravel parking, this site could be the perfect spot for your next outdoor water sport adventure. The Campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80724', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80725', 'Wilderness Gateway Campground', 'campground', 46.337958, -115.310728, null, 'Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forests', 'Wilderness Gateway Campground is one of the Nez Perce-Clearwater National Forest''s premier campgrounds. Located at milepost 122.5 along the Northwest Passage Scenic Byway (US Highway 12), the campground offers 91 sites consisting of RV and tent camping, group camping, stock camping and facilities. The recreation area boasts its very own bird-watching trail, large trailhead parking for access into the Selway-Bitterroot Wilderness, dump station, large picnic shelter and flush toilets, too.It also has picnic tables, fire rings, and toilets.. The Wilderness Gateway Campground has something for…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/nezperceclearwater/recarea/?recid=80725', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80784', 'Blueberry Patch Campground', 'campground', 42.484169, -76.798981, null, 'Green Mountain & Finger Lakes National Forests', 'Blueberry Patch Campground is a small, semi-primitive campground located along Picnic Area Road (County Route 2), next to the large blueberry patch it received its name from. This is a popular spot to gather berries when they are in season. The berry patch features the high bush as well as low bush blueberries. There are nine campsites available. Each has a fire pit, a tent pad, a picnic table, and parking for up to two cars. This campground is designed for tents or small campers under 24 feet long. Some of the picnic tables are handicap accessible. There are two handicap accessible vault…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gmfl/recarea/?recid=80784', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80822', 'Historic Route 66 Auto Tour-Williams to Flagstaff', 'scenic_drive', 35.256228, -112.246914, null, 'Kaibab National Forest', 'The Route 66 Auto Tour is part of an ongoing effort to make places of historic interest available for you to enjoy on your national forest, truly a land of many uses. While you''re enjoying this ride into the past, don''t forget to notice the present. Watch for evidence of stock grazing, timber sales and reforestation, hunters, woodcutters, hikers, and bikers. All are here just as you, to make use of some feature of this diverse and productive land. You can do your part to take care of your national forest by keeping it free of litter. Remember to leave historic sites, artifacts, and all…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kaibab/recarea/?recid=80822', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '80932', 'Blanchard Springs Campgrounds', 'campground', 35.972806, -92.177561, null, 'Ozark-St. Francis National Forests', '4/7/25: Closed until further notice due to flood and tornado damage. Seventeen individual campsites and two group sites available. Water available. Sewage dump station available. Sites suitable for smaller RV''s and tents. No electricity or other hook ups. Blanchard Springs Recreation Area Guide Campground and Day-Use Area Rules Blanchard Springs Recreation Area Guide - Spanish', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/osfnf/recarea/?recid=80932', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81072', 'Bingham Springs Campground', 'campground', 44.514457, -120.529419, null, 'Ochoco National Forest', 'This tiny and rustic campground is located adjacent to a meadow and a small pond in the northwestern portion of the Ochoco National Forest. The campground is also adjacent to the Twin Pillars North Trailhead which provides access into Mill Creek Wilderness . The campground is bordered by ponderosa and lodgepole pines, and the open meadow makes for some gorgeous stargazing on warm summer nights.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ochoco/recarea/?recid=81072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81102', 'Pleasant Valley Campground', 'campground', 48.041956, -115.290964, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'The Pleasant Valley Campground is located approximately 32 miles southwest of Libby on Highway 2. The campground has 7 sites tables and fire rings and able to accommodate up to a 32'' rv. There is also 2 stock campsites with feed bins and a corrals. Campground roads and parking spurs are gravel or native material. Amenities include vault toilets.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=81102', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81173', 'Lower Fairy Lake Trailhead/Sno-park', 'snow_area', 45.895697, -110.900365, null, 'Custer Gallatin National Forest', 'Lower trailhead and parking area for Sno-park providing winter access to the Bridger Range.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/custergallatin/recarea/?recid=81173', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81211', 'Trinity Snow-parking area', 'snow_area', 43.606570, -115.276530, null, 'Boise National Forest', 'Snow-parking area. Call the Mountain Home Ranger District for information. 208-587-7961', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/boise/recarea/?recid=81211', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81213', 'Trinity Warming Hut', 'snow_area', 43.659280, -115.405990, null, 'Boise National Forest', 'Small hut where you can get warm when it is really cold outside!', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/boise/recarea/?recid=81213', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81240', 'Scott Trailhead', 'scenic_drive', 44.213100, -121.878000, null, 'Willamette National Forest', 'This trailhead provides access to: Scott Trail #3531 Obsidian Tie Trail Obsidian Trail #3528 Pacific Crest Trail #2000 See trail pages for more information.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/willamette/recarea/?recid=81240', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81561', 'Mumford Bar Campground', 'campground', 39.125500, -120.421000, null, 'Tahoe National Forest', 'Located 17 Miles northeast of Foresthill on Foresthill Divide Road. This small campground is located at the roadside, near the Mumford Bar Trailhead. Mumford Bar Trail offers hiking, mountain biking, or equestrian access to the North Fork of the American River. Featuring 4 campsites (Ok for equestrian use), hitching posts, and vault toilet. No trash service so please pack-in, pack-out. And no potable water so be sure to bring plenty for yourselves.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/tahoe/recarea/?recid=81561', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81571', 'Legacy Campground', 'campground', 40.216420, -121.191175, null, 'Lassen National Forest', 'Legacy is a developed campground near Lake Almanor with 14 sites; maximum of 8 people is allowed per single site; 16 people maximum are allowed per double site. Water and electrical hookups are provided at each site, two sets of hook ups are provided at double site 11. An RV pay per use dump station is located next to the campground. A fee of $30/night is required at this site, fee must be paid upon arrival and before each night of camping. This campground is non-reservable, holding sites in advance of camping is prohibited.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lassen/recarea/?recid=81571', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81603', 'Almanor RV Dump Station', 'campground', 40.217814, -121.189998, null, 'Lassen National Forest', 'The Almanor RV Dump Station is temporarily closed for repairs, please call the Almanor Ranger District for updates (530)258-2141. The Almanor RV Dump Station is open to all visitors, and allows four RVs at a time.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lassen/recarea/?recid=81603', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81713', 'South Ridge Road', 'scenic_drive', 33.737338, -116.706893, null, 'San Bernardino National Forest', 'South Ridge Road 5S11, is a 1.5 mile steep road that leads to South Ridge Trailhead, and 3 Yellow Post Sites. Each site is limited to a maximum of 8 persons at any one time. There is limited parking at these sites for 2 vehicles. Amenities includes 1 picnic table and 1 fire ring. There are no restroom facilities. There is no drinking water. No other camping on this road, campers must be at a yellow post site. Campfire permits are required for any type of fire use - campfires, or stoves. Campfires may not be allowed certain times of the year. Click here for current fire restriction…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sbnf/recarea/?recid=81713', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81714', 'Santa Rosa Road (7S02)', 'scenic_drive', 33.567709, -116.511724, null, 'San Bernardino National Forest', 'Santa Rosa Rd (7S02), sometimes locally referred to as the Santa Rosa Truck Trail, is an 11 miles road accessed from Hwy 74. It begins in chaparral and winds its way up to pines and cedars below Santa Rosa and Toro peaks. The road is usually closed each winter if snow and ice create dangerous conditions.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/sbnf/recarea/?recid=81714', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81760', 'West Lake Marie', 'scenic_drive', 41.331438, -106.325433, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'This scenic trailhead parking area provides access to trails ranging from easy to difficult, beautiful views of alpine lakes, wildlife, and Medicine Bow Peak, and a place to stretch your legs with easy access to Medicine Bow Peak Trail , Tipple Trail , Lakes Trail , and Lake Marie Falls. The Lake Marie Trail is a paved, accessible trail that connects to Mirror Lake Picnic and Fishing Site . This parking area provides a perfect basecamp for exploring trails or making a quick stop along the Snowy Range Highway, with two vault toilets. Recently, a small picnic area with 3 tables with fire rings…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=81760', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81825', 'Jorgen''s Hollow Campground', 'campground', 46.524634, -97.201452, null, 'Dakota Prairie Grasslands', 'Jorgen''s Hollow Campground is located forty miles southwest of Fargo, North Dakota. Click here for a map of the Jorgen''s Hollow Campground and Trails. Jorgen''s Hollow Campground has 14 primitive campsites nestled within the oak savanna. Seven of those sites allow campers to have horses and seven sites are designated for campers without horses. Each campsite has a graveled pad, with a picnic table and fire ring. While at the campground, you can enjoy the area by hiking the Oak Leaf or North Country National Scenic Trail , viewing wildlife, birding, identifying wildflowers, and many other…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/dpg/recarea/?recid=81825', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81828', 'Kennedy Meadows Campground', 'campground', 36.051800, -118.130468, null, 'Inyo National Forest', 'Located on the Pacific Crest Trail near the South Fork of the Kern River, Kennedy Meadows campground is surrounded by the South Sierra, Golden Trout, and Domeland wildernesses. Some of the 37 sites are shaded by juniper and pinion. Maximum vehicle length is 30ft.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/inyo/recarea/?recid=81828', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81868', 'Paradise Campground', 'campground', 35.152900, -120.144600, null, 'Los Padres National Forest', 'Large oak shaded camp, Beautiful scenic views. Area amenities: Tent camping, Picnic tables, Fire rings. High clearance vehicles recommended to get to campground. Pit toilets. No water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lpnf/recarea/?recid=81868', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81875', 'Colson Campground', 'campground', 34.939800, -120.169800, null, 'Los Padres National Forest', 'Colson Campground closed permanently in April 2021. Please contact the Santa Lucia Ranger District for more information about the closure. The following campgrounds are open and can be accessed off Hwy 166: Bates Campground, Miranda Pine, Rock Front OHV Area (Buck Springs Campground, Paradise and Baja Campground), Horseshoe and Brookshire.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lpnf/recarea/?recid=81875', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81939', 'Archie Knowles Campground', 'campground', 44.021210, -123.803130, null, 'Siuslaw National Forest', 'Archie Knowles campground is located beside Highway 126 among Douglas fir, spruce and huckleberry. Knowles Creek flows gently beside the campgrounds.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/siuslaw/recarea/?recid=81939', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81980', 'Hagerman Pass', 'scenic_drive', 39.264941, -106.484945, null, 'Pike-San Isabel National Forests', 'Hagerman Pass offers spectacular views of Turquoise Lake and three surrounding Wilderness areas: Mount Massive , Hunter-Fryingpan and Holy Cross . The road is very rough and high clearance four wheel drive vehicles are recomended. In the 1880''s, the Denver & Rio Grande Railroad and Colorado Midland Railroad competed to see which railroad would reach Aspen from Leadville first. The Colorado Midland railroad crossed the Continental Divide initially through the Hagerman Tunnel and then later the Busk-Ivanhoe Tunnel which now is used as a water diversion tunnel from Ivanhoe Lake on the west side…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/psicc/recarea/?recid=81980', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81981', 'Weston Pass', 'scenic_drive', 39.131198, -106.182278, null, 'Pike-San Isabel National Forests', 'Weston Pass road is not maintained for low clearance vehicles on the Leadville side of pass which can be very rough in places with a few steep pitches. This scenic route travels along the South Fork of the South Platte River and climbs into a high alpine valley above tree line. Weston Peak can be seen to the north and the Buffalo Peaks Wilderness Area to the south.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/psicc/recarea/?recid=81981', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '81993', 'Utica Reservoir Campgrounds', 'campground', 38.424872, -120.013114, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'var $j = jQuery;$j.noConflict();$j(window).load(function() {$j(''#slider3'').nivoSlider( {effect: ''fade'',startSlide: 0,animSpeed: 750,pauseTime: 8000});}); Utica Reservoir is set in a granite basin surrounded by red fir and lodgepole pine forest. The reservoir has lots of islands and is kept mostly full. Granite slabs along the shore extend into the water. There are two campgrounds adjacent to each other, Sandy Flat and Rocky Point. Elevation is 6,800 feet.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=81993', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82076', 'Fourche Mountain Recreation Area', 'campground', 34.897491, -93.390703, null, 'Ouachita National Forest', 'Small campground with a scenic view from the mountaintop. Additional information available here.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ouachita/recarea/?recid=82076', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82078', 'Buckhorn Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 44.149000, -104.084000, null, 'Black Hills National Forest', 'Buckhorn Snowmobile Trailhead provides direct access to snowmobile Trail 3. This is the closest trailhead for riders coming from Newcastle, Wyoming. The trail is 6.5 miles from Four Corners, WY and provides access to trails that spread across eastern Wyoming and western South Dakota. The trailhead is privately owned so respect private property by remaining on roads, parking lots, and trails, and packing out what you packed in. Access Buckhorn Snowmobile Trailhead from Newcastle, Wyoming via US Highway 85 North for 23.3 miles to the Buckhorn Trailhead. The trailhead is on the south (right)…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/blackhills/recarea/?recid=82078', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82080', 'Custer Peak Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 44.253000, -103.701000, null, 'Black Hills National Forest', 'The Custer Peak Snowmobile Trailhead is approximately 11 miles south of Deadwood off of US Highway 385. The trailhead provides direct access to snowmobile Trail 7 and is a gateway to 350 miles of snowmobile trails in the Black Hills. Access the Custer Peak Snowmobile Trailhead from Deadwood via US 385 traveling south for 9.7 miles. At Custer Peak Road turn west (right). Proceed on Custer Peak Road for approximately 0.1 miles to the trailhead parking lot on the north (right) side of the road. If following a GPS, navigate to Mystic Hills Hideaway or the coordinates below. The trailhead is on…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/blackhills/recarea/?recid=82080', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82088', 'Trailshead Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 44.201000, -104.025000, null, 'Black Hills National Forest', 'The Trailshead Snowmobile Trailhead is the epicenter of snowmobiling in the Black Hills. There are nearly ten trails to choose from within a few miles of the trailhead. Those trails extend west into Wyoming, north to Deadwood, and south to Bear Mountain - providing an incredible amount of variety to riders. The trailhead is privately owned so respect private property by remaining on roads, parking lots, and trails, and packing out what you packed in. Access Trailshead Snowmobile Trailhead from Newcastle, Wyoming via US Highway 85 North for 28.9 miles. The trailhead is on the south (right)…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/blackhills/recarea/?recid=82088', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82355', 'North Fisherman Creek Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 43.156017, -110.302017, null, 'Bridger-Teton National Forest', 'The North Fork Fisherman Creek Snowmobile Trailhead offers access to miles upon miles of ungroomed challenging snowmobile experiences. From this trailhead users can explore the Hoback Basin at the foot of the Gros Ventre Range.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/btnf/recarea/?recid=82355', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82459', 'Longhouse National Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 41.858215, -78.961976, null, 'Allegheny National Forest', 'Longhouse Scenic Byway is a 36-mile loop byway that runs through the Allegheny National Forest. Visitors will often feel as if they are driving through a tunnel as they drive through the northern hardwoods of the Allegheny, surrounded by oak and black cherry. The byway circles the Kinzua Creek arm of the Allegheny Reservoir and there are several campgrounds and picnic areas along the byway, including Jakes Rocks Overlook . The byway begins at the intersection of Route 321 and Longhouse Drive. As you begin your drive you will pass Red Bridge Recreation Area, a campground and bank fishing area.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/allegheny/recarea/?recid=82459', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82479', 'Cosmic Campground International Dark Sky Sanctuary', 'campground', 33.479946, -108.922867, null, 'Gila National Forest', 'Cosmic Campground International Dark Sky Sanctuary (CCIDSS) is the first International Dark Sky Sanctuary located on National Forest System lands and also in North America. It is also one of only 14 certified IDA Sanctuaries in the world. International Dark Sky Sanctuaries are lands possessing an exceptional or distinguished quality of starry nights. For more information on dark skies, light pollution, or the International Dark Sky Association . The CCIDSS offers a 360-degree, unobstructed view of the night sky for exceptional stargazing opportunities. This site is situated where there…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gila/recarea/?recid=82479', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82705', '#SNO151 Martin Creek Snowmobile Trailhead', 'snow_area', 47.881000, -115.751000, null, 'Kootenai National Forest', 'Martin Creek Snowmobile Trail #SNO151 starts at Martin Creek Bay and follws FSR 151, 2213, 2244, 2710, 149, 2229, 2214 for over 40 miles of groomed snowmobile trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/kootenai/recarea/?recid=82705', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82840', 'Sheep Creek Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.888453, -109.849481, null, 'Ashley National Forest', 'This campground offers primitive camping near Sheep Creek Lake. There is an unpaved boat launch. No other facilities are available in this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/ashley/recarea/?recid=82840', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82970', 'Carr. 191 North - La Mina Recreational Area', 'scenic_drive', 18.339870, -65.759878, null, 'El Yunque National Forest', 'Most of the recreation facilities on the El Yunque National Forest are on Road 191 North in Rio Grande. The road and most of the recreation sites and trails were constructed during the 1940s by the Civil Conservation Corps. There are numerous trailheads, observation points, and historic sites along the Corridor. Please Note: Winding Road- Drive Carefully Speed Limit 20 mph. __________________________________________________ La mayor a de las reas recreativas en el Bosque Nacional El Yunque se encuentran en la carretera 191 norte en R o Grande. El camino y la mayor a de los sitios de recreaci…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/elyunque/recarea/?recid=82970', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82971', 'Carr. 186 - El Toro Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 18.339427, -65.825215, null, 'El Yunque National Forest', 'The Road 186 Corridor is a 600-meter band of the historic PR Route 186 that was declared a Scenic Byway by the Puerto Rican government. It is the home of R o Esp ritu Santo Watershed and the center of El Yunque Silviculture, Preservation and Research. Please Note: Poor Road Conditions. Drive Carefully. View Map __________________________________________________ El Corredor de la Carretera 186 es una banda de 600 metros que fue declarada una Ruta Esc nica por el gobierno puertorrique o. Es el hogar de la Cuenca del R o Esp ritu Santo y el centro de Silvicultura, Conservaci n e Investigaci n de…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/elyunque/recarea/?recid=82971', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '82972', 'Carr. 191 South - Naguabo', 'scenic_drive', 18.267429, -65.795014, null, 'El Yunque National Forest', 'Recreation areas located on 191 South may be accessed through the municipality of Naguabo. It is not accessible from the north side of the Forest due to a major landslide that occurred in the mid-1970s. The south side of the forest is less traveled than the northern part and offers spectacular scenery, hiking and waterplay. Please Note: Winding Road- Drive Carefully Speed Limit 20 mph __________________________________________________ Se puede acceder a las reas recreativas ubicadas en Carr. 191 Sur a trav s del municipio de Naguabo. No es accesible desde el lado norte del bosque debido a un…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/elyunque/recarea/?recid=82972', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83012', 'Ross Campground', 'campground', 39.735030, -120.749990, null, 'Plumas National Forest', 'Ross Campground has three rustic campsites tucked off of the beaten path. It is located next to Jamison Creek in a conifer forest of predominantly red fir trees.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/plumas/recarea/?recid=83012', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83070', 'Lake Alpine Campground (West Shore)', 'campground', 38.477393, -120.007519, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'Lake Alpine Campground is one of five campgrounds within the Lake Alpine Recreation Area that are situated in mature conifer forest on the shores of Lake Alpine. Lake Alpine Campground has 25 sites; there is RV camping but no hookups or electric. Reservations required via Recreation.gov For more information on the recreation area and links to the other campground pages, visit the Lake Alpine Recreation Area page.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83070', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83083', 'Spicer Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 38.406393, -119.999141, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'Timbered setting near the shore of Spicer Reservoir. Spicer Reservoir Campground is operated by Royal Elk Park Management; Royal Elk Park Management - Camping, Campgrounds, Campsite', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83083', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83090', 'Silvertip Campground', 'campground', 38.481589, -120.017784, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'Silvertip Campground is in red fir and lodgepole pine forest in the Lake Alpine Recreation Area . Campground is one mile from the lake. Reservations required via Recreation.gov', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83090', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83103', 'Union East Campground', 'campground', 38.428128, -119.992264, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'var $j = jQuery;$j.noConflict();$j(window).load(function() {$j(''#slider3'').nivoSlider( {effect: ''fade'',startSlide: 0,animSpeed: 750,pauseTime: 8000});}); Union Reservoir is set in a granite basin with expansive mountain views. The reservoir has lots of small islands and is kept mostly full. The campground is adjacent to the reservoir, nestled in red fir and lodgepole pine forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83103', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83104', 'Union West Campground', 'campground', 38.426475, -119.998524, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'var $j = jQuery;$j.noConflict();$j(window).load(function() {$j(''#slider3'').nivoSlider( {effect: ''fade'',startSlide: 0,animSpeed: 750,pauseTime: 8000});}); Union Reservoir is set in a granite basin with expansive mountain views. The reservoir has lots of small islands and is kept mostly full. The campground is adjacent to the reservoir, nestled in red fir and lodgepole pine forest.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83104', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83139', 'Shadow Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.202505, -123.068856, null, 'Klamath National Forest', 'Shadow Creek Campground is located along the East Fork of the South Fork Salmon River at approximately 3,000 ft. elevation. Access is by paved County Rd. 1C02 (Callahan - Cecilville Rd). There are six campsites, some with RV access, vault toilets, but no potable water.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/klamath/recarea/?recid=83139', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83202', 'Moore Creek Campground', 'campground', 38.479910, -120.266299, null, 'Stanislaus National Forest', 'Campground on the Mokelumne River.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/stanislaus/recarea/?recid=83202', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83246', 'Beth Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.860152, -118.985076, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground has 15 sites in 2 small loops. There are boat launches on either end of the campground. The southern launch accesses Beaver Lake, while the northern launch accesses Beth Lake. An earthen dam is near the northern boat launch. The Beth Lake Trail #316 can be accessed near the earthen dam. There are 2 pit toilets, 2 double vault toilets, and 1 vault toilet. There is a garbage dumpster for campground users only. Water is available in the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83246', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83247', 'Bonaparte Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.793063, -119.057666, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is a popular site on Bonaparte Lake. A boat launch, wheelchair-accessible fishing dock, and day-use/swimming area are also popular amenities. Water and garbage dumpsters are available. Five double toilets as well as a flush toilet service the campground. The campground also has a seasonal Camp Host.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83247', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83249', 'Crawfish Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.484862, -119.215063, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Crawfish Lake is adjacent to this 19 site campground (15 single and 4 double sites), which also has a boat launch. Two toilet facilities service the campground. Each site has a picnic table, fire ring, and parking for small trailers or vehicles. Eleven sites border the lakeshore. The Common Loon has been heard and seen on the lake. No water or garbage facilities available. Please pack garbage out.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83249', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83250', 'Kerr Campground', 'campground', 48.611621, -119.788512, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is located next to the North Fork Salmon Creek. There are two loops in this campground with a total of 11 single campsites and one double site. Each campsite has a picnic table, fire ring, and parking spaces. Two toilet facilities service the campground. No water is available. Garbage service is located in Oriole campground to the south.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83250', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83252', 'Lost Lake Campground', 'campground', 48.853011, -119.049809, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This Campground was developed in the 1930s and 40s by the Civilian Conservation Corps. The old Guard Station at the entrance was built in 1941 which adds to the character of the campground. The campground is located next to Lost Lake which hosts a pair of Common Loons and Canada geese. There are 18 campsites, (14 single sites, and 4 doubles) with picnic tables and fire rings. A day use Picnic site, swim beach, ampitheater, and boat launch are also available. Water and garbage service are available as well. Three toilet facilities service the campground. Two organization camps border the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83252', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83253', 'Oriole Campground', 'campground', 48.594584, -119.770721, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground borders the North Fork Salmon Creek with 10 campsites (7 single and 3 double sites). Each campsite has picnic tables, fire rings, and tent pads. One toilet facility is available. No water is available. Garbage service is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83253', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83254', 'Salmon Meadows Campground', 'campground', 48.657704, -119.841831, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground was originally established in 1937 by the Civilian Conservation Corps and boasts a picnic gazebo built by the CCC as well as an old registration booth. Fourteen campsites will accommodate tents or trailers. Two sites have horse corrals. Each campsite has a picnic table and fire ring.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83254', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83255', 'Sugarloaf Campground', 'campground', 48.594700, -119.697000, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground is adjacent to Sugarloaf Lake. There are 4 single campsites available with picnic tables and fire rings. A vault toilet facility is available. No water or garbage service on site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83255', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83256', 'Tiffany Springs Campground', 'campground', 48.700110, -119.954202, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This campground has 6 single campsites with picnic tables and fire rings. One toilet facility services the site. No water or garbage service is available, please pack out garbage. A nice camping area, although this campground was burned over in the Tripod Fire of 2006, so the site is mainly open with some blackened trees. The Tiffany Lake Trail #373 begins across the Forest Service Road #39 from the Campground. This road has not been graded recently and is not recommended for passanger vehicles. Trailers are prohibited.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83256', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83305', 'Bonaparte Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.792465, -119.057419, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Forest Service Road 3200 and 3200-30. Plowed road leading to a 2 acre parking area suitable for up to 6 vehicles with trailer. Washington State Park Sno-Park Permit required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83305', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83308', 'Crawfish Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.489356, -119.222917, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This Sno-Park is open to mainly snowmobile traffic in the winter season. No toilet facility is available, although the Crawfish Lake Campground is .4 mile down the Forest Service #3000-100 road which does have toilet facilities. A Washington State Sno Park Permit is required.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83308', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83322', 'Kerr Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.611740, -119.788820, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'The Kerr Sno-Park is located across from the Kerr Campground and consists of a toilet facility and a snow shelter. Numerous groomed snowmobile trails into the National Forest are accessed from this Sno Park.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83322', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83413', 'Albian Hill Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.632428, -118.446983, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Three Rivers Ranger District off of Albian road on Sherman Pass.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83413', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83414', 'Flodelle/Tacoma Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.544411, -117.578681, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Three Rivers Ranger District.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83414', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83415', 'Mill Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.611170, -117.551700, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Three Rivers Ranger District', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83415', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83416', 'Ninebark Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.292500, -117.343330, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Newport-Sullivan Ranger Districts. This is down a narrow road with parking provided on one side of the street.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83416', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83417', 'Kings Lake Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.386666, -117.205833, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This is our largest Sno-Park on the Colville National Forest and is found on the Newport-Sullivan Lake Ranger Districts. Parking lot capacity is up to 60 vehicles and trailers. The looped trail system covers over 134 miles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83417', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83418', 'Flowery Trailhead Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.308120, -117.569878, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Located on the Newport-Sullivan Lake Ranger Districts near 49 Degrees North Ski and Snowboard Resort. Located adjacent to the Flowery Trail road.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83418', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83426', 'TIC''s Snowmobile Parking Lot', 'snow_area', 41.039530, -106.160330, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'Parking lot used primarily for snowmobile parking in the winter. This site is not regularly maintained, including the restrooms. It is located in the Snowy Range off of Highway 230 and is managed by the Laramie Ranger District. In the summer there is a day use fee of $5/day/vehicle. It is about 60 yards wide and 150 yards long, and can fit 60-70 trucks and trailers. It is hard packed gravel and is not maintained by the Forest Service in the winter. There is no water but there is a vault restroom (it is recommended that you bring your own toilet paper). The T-South snowmobile trail begins in…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=83426', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83447', 'Little Joe Campground - Lolo NF', 'campground', 47.271237, -115.137062, null, 'Lolo National Forest', 'A small campground along Little Joe Creek several miles south of St. Regis, Montana. It is currently a group of undeveloped, dispersed campsites. It is being planned for further campground development, which will include more amenities and associated campsite fees. If you want to camp at Little Joe, please call the Superior Ranger District at 406-822-4233 to find out the current status of the site.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lolo/recarea/?recid=83447', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83455', 'Bighorn Campground', 'campground', 46.384921, -113.658933, null, 'Lolo National Forest', 'May 2023: Reconstruction work is planned for the Bighorn Campground this summer (2023). Once work begins, the campground will be closed. Upgrades will include vault toilets, new campsites, fire rings, and picnic tables. Reconstruction work is funded by the Great American Outdoors Act. Located in the Rock Creek drainage, this campground is situated right on Rock Creek in an old growth Ponderosa Pine and Douglas Fir forest. This area is known for its blue ribbon trout stream and rugged canyon environment. The campground is open year-round, weather dependent. There are no amenities from October…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lolo/recarea/?recid=83455', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83485', 'North Fork Chewelah Creek Sno-Park', 'snow_area', 48.344790, -117.607000, null, 'Colville National Forest', '67 miles of groomed trails start at the North Fork Chewelah Creek camping area. It is a large open area with immediate access to the non-wheeled vehicles only area. There is a vault toilet and one picnic table found at the far side of the recreation area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83485', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83540', 'Ocean Pond Campground', 'campground', 30.248200, -82.440100, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Ocean Pond Campground''s two-mile wide lake with its shallow, sandy beach provides an escape from everyday life for more than 100,000 visitors each year. The site is about an hour from the First Coast Atlantic beaches and only 30 minutes to multiple state parks, local springs and caves. Backpacking The Great Florida Birding Trail and the Florida National Scenic Trail pass through the campground. Boating, Fishing and Waterskiing This area is a favorite for boaters and water-skiers, anglers and hikers. Facilities includes restrooms, fire rings and picnic tables. A public boat launch and a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83540', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83547', 'Alexander Springs Campground', 'campground', 29.079300, -81.578300, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'At Alexander Springs Recreation Area, enjoy a shaded campground within an easy walk of the springs swimming and picnic area. This 67-unit campground can accommodate tents and recreation vehicles (up to 35-feet long). The concessionaire sells a variety of snacks, souvenirs, ice, charcoal, firewood, beach items and personal items. (Please note: No food is cooked on site by the concessionaire). ** NOTE: Limited internet may affect operations. Please come prepared to make purchases with cash. Camping The 67-unit campground can accomodate tents and recreation vehicles up to 35-feet long. Expect…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83547', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83548', 'Clearwater Lake Campground', 'campground', 28.978919, -81.553600, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'This 42-space campground provides breezy lakefront sites along Clearwater Lake. It accommodates both trailers and tents, and has bathhouses with warm showers. Campers can swim, grill, walk around the lake on the nature trail, mountain bike on the Paisley Woods Bicycle Trail, hike on the Florida Trail, or just drift across the water in a kayak, trailing a line and waiting for a nibble. Boating Paddle your canoe or kayak across the placid waters of Clearwater Lake in search of a quiet spot along the reedy shoreline. It''s slightly more than a mile circuit around the edge of the lake. Camping…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83548', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83549', 'Davenport Landing', 'campground', 29.472300, -81.773700, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Deep in the floodplain forest along the Ocklawaha River, Davenport Landing is a former steamboat stop along this twisting, winding waterway. Three primitive campsites provide a stop for paddlers working their way along the river. Boating Paddle your canoe or kayak across the beautiful waters of Davenport Lading in search of a quiet spot along the shoreline. Fishing Sitting along the Ocklawaha River, this is the perfect location to cast a line from the shallows for a chance to catch that big one. Just keep an eye out for any alligators that may be roaming the area. Hiking The Davenport Landing…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83549', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83575', 'Apalachee Savannahs Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 30.105631, -85.060109, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'The Apalachicola Savannahs, home to the Apalachee Savannahs Scenic Byway, are sub-tropical grasslands scattered with longleaf pine trees and covered with drought-resistant undergrowth. It''s an open landscape where wiregrass, or sometimes palmetto, covers the forest floor. Swamps and savannahs are commonly interspersed with the longleaf community. Wildflowers such as orchids, pitcher plants and sundews flourish. These savannahs are some of the most botanically rich areas in the country. Often holding water all year long, the savannahs host a stunning display of pitcher plants, sundews, wild…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83575', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83590', 'Big Bend Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 30.074700, -84.432900, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Whether you visit the Forest Trail rich in pine forests, hardwood hammocks, savannahs, streams and rivers, or the Coastal Trail of salt marshes, bays, sand dunes and beaches, the state designated Florida Big Bend Scenic Byway is the natural place to be. Starting right outside the Apalachicola National Forest at the Tallahassee International Airport, the scenic byway offers over 200 miles of wonderland inhabited by birds, butterflies, animals and wildflowers. Trace the footsteps of the Apalachee and the Creek, Spanish Conquistadors, British and American troops, pioneers, cowhunters, cotton and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83590', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83607', 'Camel Lake Recreation Area', 'campground', 30.277150, -84.986600, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Surrounding one of the few crystal-clear lakes in the Apalachicola National Forest, Camel Lake Recreation Area provides a quiet place to relax and take in the beauty of the longleaf pine forest. Seepage slopes in the forest create pitcher plant bogs, easily visited along the Florida National Scenic Trail headed west to Memory Island. Boating Electric trolling motors and paddle boats are welcome on the lake. Camping Above the lake''s rim, the focal points of this recreation area are the well-shaded, 10-site campground, suitable for RVs or tents. Picnicking The day-use area has both picnic…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83607', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83642', 'Wright Lake', 'campground', 29.999430, -85.001801, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Wright Lake is a quiet scenic lakefront recreation area that offers a host of amenities and activities for campers and day-trippers. The area around the clear, spring-fed lake offers both a day-use area for swimming, picnicking hiking, and a campground in a beautiful forest setting along one portion of the lakeshore. It is perfect for fishing and boating. Swimmers can also enjoy the white sand beach, and a nearby bathhouse includes flush toilets and hot showers. Picnic tables and grills are scattered among trees with views of the lake. Boating Electric trolling motors or paddle boats are…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83642', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83665', 'Rainy Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.336340, -113.593156, null, 'Lolo National Forest', 'This is a small 6-site campground on Rainy Lake north of Seeley Lake. Sites 2-6 are walk-in only, and site 1 is an accessible RV site. Vehicles must stay on roads, and all sites are first come, first served. Rainy Lake, one of the Clearwater Chain of Lakes, offers fishing and space to canoe or kayak. Hiking is also available nearby.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lolo/recarea/?recid=83665', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83666', 'Hidden Lake Campground', 'campground', 47.143222, -113.570316, null, 'Lolo National Forest', 'Hidden Lake Campground is a 5-site campground southwest of Seeley Lake, Montana. The lake is a 33-acre kettle lake on the west edge of the Clearwater Valley, and is stocked with westslope cuthroat trout. Non-motorized boating is welcome.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/lolo/recarea/?recid=83666', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83671', 'Florida Black Bear Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 29.168400, -81.642600, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Providing more than 60 miles of exploration by car, the Florida Black Bear Scenic Byway - a National Scenic Byway- is a network of scenic roads between Silver Springs and Ormond Beach, including SR 40 through the heart of the Ocala National Forest. The Byway traverses some of Florida''s most pristine ecosystems. Included within the corridor are many public lands such as Juniper Springs Wilderness Area, Silver Springs State Park, the Cross Florida Greenway, Florida National Scenic Trail and the Tiger Bay State Forest. The route also crosses several waterways, which have received special…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83671', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83673', 'Hopkins Prairie Campground', 'campground', 29.269600, -81.686700, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'An island of shade amid a broad, winding grassland, the Hopkins Prairie Campground is a seasonal destination for campers looking to get off the beaten path. An unsung gem, Hopkins Prairie is a rambling incursion of interconnected wet and dry prairie landscape surrounded by sand pine and oak scrub. Boating Depending on water levels in the prairie, you may be able to launch your canoe or jon boat to drift across the deeper spots in this vast ecosystem. Camping Hopkins Prairie is a designated camping area with minimal facilities, open seasonally. Expect full recreation sites during weekends.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83673', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83683', 'Lake Dorr Recreation Area', 'campground', 29.012500, -81.639900, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'A massive patch of blue in a sea of green - that''s Lake Dorr, one of the prettiest big lakes in the Ocala National Forest. Experience outdoor recreation at either the Lake Dorr Recreation Area - campground or day use - or by renting the cabin for your family or group. Along the northwest shore of the lake, the recreation area is set under the deep shade of an oak hammock. Offering RV camping, we also have a boat ramp and picnic area overlooking the view. Camping Bring the family out and get back to nature in this picturesque setting. with campsites for tents, campers and RVs. Reservations may…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83683', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83687', 'Fore Lake Campground', 'campground', 29.270200, -81.918400, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'With 31 sites tucked in the shade of oaks and pines along shimmering Fore Lake, the Fore Lake Campground is a quiet spot for camping on the western edge of the Ocala National Forest in the Fore Lake Recreation Area . Boating -- Non-motorized No gasoline powered engines. Canoes welcome. Boating in the National Forests in Florida is regulated by the state of Florida. Please visit our boating web page before you grab your personal floatation device and head out onto the water. Camping Tents and travel trailers are welcome. Maximum stay limit of 14 consecutive days in a 30-day period. Amenities…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83687', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83710', 'Lake Eaton Campground', 'campground', 29.253300, -81.865500, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'A large, shallow lake cradled by the Big Scrub, Lake Eaton offers many distinctive faces. As a seasonal access area, the Lake Eaton Campground has only 14 sites. At the end of the road, the Lake Eaton Boat Launch and Pier offers opportunities for boating and fishing. Boating Access to Lake Eaton for anglers and birders at the end of the entrance road for the Lake Eaton Campground. You do not need to be camping to enjoy lake access, which is open year-round. Camping Open seasonally, the Lake Eaton Campground provides access for campers and day use visitors to Lake Eaton via a boat ramp and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83710', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83716', 'Big Bass Campground', 'campground', 28.986583, -81.785657, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Spend your next short- or long-term camping trip at Big Bass. With the occasional black bear sighting, this the perfect location to escape the hustle of the city and get back to nature. We offer both tent and RV camping on the south edge of the Ocala National Forest, not far from the Ocklawaha River. Camping Big Bass is a seasonal campground in the southern part of the Ocala National Forest, not far from Doe Lake Recreation Area. Small Game Hunting Enjoy the hunting season as you get deeper in the woods to find your game.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83716', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83720', 'Lake Delancy East Campground', 'campground', 29.430736, -81.786439, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Shaded by stately oaks and tall pines, Lake Delancey is a beautifully rustic location for anyone trying to get out of the city and is a favorite amongst locals. Lake Delancy East is hosts 29 campsites along the eastern shore of the lake. Camping The Delancy East campground offers 29 which includes campsites, picnic tables and grill. Sorry, not ATVs are permitted. Heads up: Bears do frequent this area. You are required to store your food in a bear-proof container or in your vehicle. Fishing We provide access to the lakeshore marshes for fishing. Perfect for tossing one on the fire for dinner…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83720', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83737', 'Porter Lake', 'campground', 30.177200, -84.677200, null, 'National Forests in Florida', 'Primitive camping and day use with fishing on Porter Lake and access for paddlers into winding channels through the floodplain forest of the Ochlockonee River basin. Backpacking Trailhead along the Florida National Scenic Trail . East to Smith Creek and Bradwell Bay, west to Vilas and Camel Lake. Hunting/Camping Used as a hunt camp during general gun season. Camping is allowed to non-hunters during general gun season. Be aware of hunting environment.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/florida/recarea/?recid=83737', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83770', 'Gwynn Tank Campground', 'campground', 33.537580, -108.531898, null, 'Gila National Forest', 'The Gwynn Tank Campground is a flat site in an open ponderosa meadow. Additionally, Gwynn Tank Campground is located adjacent to its namesake Gwynn Tank pond. The pond is historically stocked for recreational fishing and is popular for recreational fishing.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gila/recarea/?recid=83770', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83771', 'Silver Creek Campground', 'campground', 48.905705, -117.518769, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small campground allowing access to North Fork Silver Creek Trail #119 .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83771', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83957', 'Bulldog Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.848958, -118.344608, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This pull off along Boulder Creek Road does not provide access for day-use parking. The stagging area is designed for pick up and drop offs only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83957', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83958', 'E-W Branch Le Clerc Creek Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.534900, -117.282900, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This small stagging area is designed for pick up and drop offs only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83958', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83959', 'Paupac Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.764900, -117.296500, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This large staging area provides ample parking for both motorized and non motorized recreation. Sno-Play is available as conditions allow.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83959', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83961', 'Quartz Ridge Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.593500, -118.640400, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small staging area off Hall Creek Road. The stagging area is designed for pick up and drop offs only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83961', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83962', 'West Fork Trout Creek Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.749300, -118.747500, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small staging area. The stagging area is designed for pick up and drop offs only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83962', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83963', 'Scatter Creek Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.549290, -118.749220, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small parking area at USFS Rd 53/Scatter Creek Road. Winter Wildlife closure areas are found in this area. These are not open to snowmobiles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83963', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83964', 'Konz/Boise Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.599800, -118.740100, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small parking area. Winter Wildlife closure areas are found in this area. These are not open to snowmobiles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83964', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83965', 'Golden Harvest Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.606300, -118.842200, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small parking area at Swan Lake Road/County Road 217 and Golden Harvest Road. Winter Wildlife closure areas are found in this area. These are not open to snowmobiles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83965', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83966', 'Sweat Creek Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.680600, -118.908300, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'Small parking area off of State Route 20. Winter Wildlife closure areas are found in this area. These are not open to snowmobiles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83966', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83967', 'Mt Annie / Sutton Meadows Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.699600, -118.985330, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This is a small turn around staging area. Designed for pick up and drop offs only. Winter Wildlife closure areas are found in this area. These are not open to snowmobiles.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83967', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83968', 'Myers Creek Staging Area', 'snow_area', 48.879500, -119.060600, null, 'Colville National Forest', 'This is a small turn around staging area. Designed for pick up and drop offs only.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/colville/recarea/?recid=83968', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '83970', 'Elkhorn South Winter Trailhead', 'snow_area', 40.871194, -106.939419, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'Columbine Winter Parking and Winter Recreation Area Map North Routt County Winter Recreation Trails Map Elkhorn South is recommended for motorized use and trailer parking and is located approximately one mile northeast up the 550 Road from the Quarry parking area near Columbine and before Little Red Park. The road and lot are plowed in the winter, and 4WD or AWD vehicles are recommended. No wheeled vehicular access is allowed beyond Elkhorn South on the 550 Road. It is open to over-the-snow vehicles only during the winter.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=83970', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84169', 'Stop 9: Panorama', 'scenic_drive', 36.664791, -92.744599, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'Panorama is a very small pull-off along the Glade Top National Scenic Byway. From here you can see panoramic views of the glades and valley below. In February 1905, all federal forest administration was consolidated under the Department of Agriculture''s Bureau of Forestry. These lands were previously administered by the General Land Office (GLO) and United States Geological Survey (USGS) under the Department of Interior. The Forest Service was established on July 1, 1905, replacing the Bureau of Forestry. On March 1, 1911, President William Howard Taft signed the Weeks Act. The Weeks Act…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84169', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84170', 'Stop 2: Smoke Tree Scene', 'scenic_drive', 36.794359, -92.718187, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'American Smoke Tree (Cotinus obovatus) is found is central Texas, eastern Oklahoma, northwest Arkansas, southwest Missouri, Kentucky, Tennessee, Alabama and Georgia. In Missouri it occurs on the Ava/Cassville/Willow Springs Ranger District in Douglas, Ozark, Stone and Taney Counties. American smoke trees thrive in dolomite glade habitats. Missouri''s largest concentration of dolomite glades occurs on the Ava and Cassville Units, which makes this a particularly special tree to the Mark Twain National Forest and especially the Ava/Cassville/Willow Springs Ranger District. American smoke trees…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84170', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84171', 'Stop 10: McClurg Glade', 'scenic_drive', 36.781552, -92.751924, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'Welcome to McClurg Glade! This is a small pull-off where visitors can view the glades. There is an old trail/road you can walk down to get a closer view of the flowers. Before you is a prime example of dolomite/limestone glade in the White River Hills region. The definition of glade is an open, rocky area dominated by drought-adapted wildflowers, warm-season grasses and specialized wildlife. Glades resemble deserts in that they are extremely hot in the summer. They are found on south and west facing slopes where the sun shines most of the day, and soils are shallow and do not hold moisture.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84171', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84173', 'Stop 3: Arkansas View', 'scenic_drive', 36.781361, -92.724342, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'As you look out to the south and into Arkansas, the furthest range of mountains lined against the sky are the Boston Mountains. While the view to the Boston Mountains has always been a prominent feature of this site, Forest conditions have changed considerably since the area was described and surveyed in the 1840s. In 1848, the Government Land Office (GLO) sent surveyors to this area to lay out Township Range and Section lines, mapping the state for the sale of land. Surveyors marked Township/Range/Section corners with metal or rock markers, and blazed witness trees as references to each…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84173', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84174', 'Stop 8: Big Creek Basin', 'scenic_drive', 36.675664, -92.805222, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'This is a very small site located on a sharp curve, please be aware of your surroundings and passing traffic if you pull off. What you see in front of you is oak woodland habitat which surrounds glades and is very important to wildlife and wildflowers that reside in Missouri. Woodlands may have covered a third of Missouri prior to European settlement. Early explorer Henry Rowe Schoolcraft noted the openness of the woods and the abundant grasses and wildflowers growing under the oaks. While settlement was progressing throughout the state, trees in woodlands were harvested and in some cases…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84174', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84175', 'Stop 4: Watershed Divide', 'scenic_drive', 36.757160, -92.746461, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'Watershed Divide is the location where rainwater flows north or south into streams in the glade top area. Everything south of the divide flows into Big Creek. Everything north of the divide flows into Beaver Creek. The Glade in front of you became encroached with Eastern Red Cedar due to exclusion of fire. This photo was taken before restoration activities began. In 2013, it was covered in Eastern Red Cedar (Juniperus virginiana). These trees are native to Missouri, but is a prolific invader of open lands. Because of the amount of Eastern Red Cedar found on glades today, glades are often…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84175', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84208', 'Stop 1: Haden Park', 'scenic_drive', 36.806559, -92.703516, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'Haden Park is the northern most stop along the Glade Top Trail National Forest Scenic Byway. The lands upon which Haden Park are situated were purchased from Mr. Michael Ryan on June 24, 1935, under authority of the Weeks Act. It is not known if Ryan established a home in the area; his name does not appear on the Rolls of the United States Population Census of 1930 for this region of Douglas County, Missouri, though he may have resided elsewhere in the general vicinity. While remnants of a homestead have not been identified nearby, a number of archaeological features have been recorded in the…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84208', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84247', 'Timothy Lake - Stone Creek Campground', 'campground', 45.106389, -121.786389, null, 'Mt. Hood National Forest', 'Stone Creek Campground is located on the shores of Timothy Lake in the shadow of Mt. Hood. The surrounding forest setting offers views of Mt. Hood, several trails for exploration, and abundant fishing. There is a day use parking area on the lakeshore with a small boat launch intended for non-motorized boats such as kayaks or canoes. Stone Creek Campground has 21 tent sites and 22 RV-sized (non-electric) sites in separate loops. The campground has barrier-free sites and amenities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mthood/recarea/?recid=84247', array['RV', 'Car', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84299', 'Paddy Creek Campground', 'campground', 37.553462, -92.040290, null, 'Mark Twain National Forest', 'This campground is near the Paddy Creek Wilderenss Area. It is just a short drive or walk from the Paddy Creek Recreation Area''s picnic and day use site. At the day-use site, there is a trailhead to enter into the Paddy Creek Wilderness Area. The campground is usually open from April 1 through December 1 each year. This area is perfectly located one hour southwest of Rolla and only an hour drive from Ft. Leonard Wood, Missouri, Paddy Creek Campground is nestled in a hollow along Paddy Creek, a major tributary to Big Piney River, just a few miles away. Paddy Creek flows year-round and is a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mtnf/recarea/?recid=84299', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84423', 'Polallie Campground', 'campground', 45.417791, -121.570042, null, 'Mt. Hood National Forest', 'Formerly a designated dispersed campsite, this campground is adjacent to Polallie Trailhead .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mthood/recarea/?recid=84423', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84424', 'Underhill Campground', 'campground', 45.396543, -121.415918, null, 'Mt. Hood National Forest', 'Formerly a designated dispersed campsite, this campground is located near a creek and is adjacent to Underhill Trail .', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mthood/recarea/?recid=84424', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84551', 'Bear Island Campground', 'campground', 44.633020, -83.894322, null, 'Huron-Manistee National Forests', 'A small quiet campground with few amenities. This site is primarily used by river paddlers. Three campsites. Brochure with map : This brochure is set to print on 11 x 17 paper, landscape (wide) orientation. To print on 8 1/2 x 11 paper set the print area to "shrink to printable area," this will make the text on the page smaller. Flickr Photo Album', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/hmnf/recarea/?recid=84551', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84658', 'Red Dirt Winter Trailhead', 'snow_area', 40.145403, -106.548135, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'This area provides winter parking for multiple vehicles and trailers. Open year round. Snowmobile Info Snowmobile Area Map Please Note : There are no groomed or marked winter trails in the Gore Pass area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=84658', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84659', 'Gore Pass Summit', 'snow_area', 40.077630, -106.558160, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'Located at around 9500 feet, this area provides a plowed pulloff and parking area for vehicles and trailers during winter months. Snowmobile Info Snowmobile Area Map Please Note : There are no groomed or marked winter trails in the Gore Pass area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=84659', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84660', 'Gore Pass Winter Trailhead', 'snow_area', 40.078460, -106.635740, null, 'Medicine Bow-Routt NFs and Thunder Basin NG', 'This area provides parking for multiple vehicles and trailers. Open year round. Snowmobile Info Snowmobile Area Map Please Note : There are no groomed or marked winter trails in the Gore Pass area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mbr/recarea/?recid=84660', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84682', 'West Turkey Creek', 'scenic_drive', 31.866563, -109.359038, null, 'Coronado National Forest', 'Perennial water flows through this wooded canyon, supporting a riparian forest and creating a lush year-round recreation destination on the edge of the Chiricahua Wilderness. A HUB FOR HIKING Six trails start from FR 41 along West Turkey Creek and connect with the network of trails that traverse the Chiricahua Mountains. Trails follow drainages and ridges and vary in length and difficulty, but are constant in their beauty, both in the natural features found along the trail and the incredible vistas in all directions. Out-and-back, thru-hikes, and loop options are available. Turkey Pen #262 ,…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/coronado/recarea/?recid=84682', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '84721', 'South Fork Campground', 'campground', 33.528630, -108.586200, null, 'Gila National Forest', 'South Fork Campground is located on the Reserve Ranger District on the south side of Forest Road 141 (Reserve - Beaverhead Rd). The campground has seven campsites with picnic tables and fire pits with grills - most sites can accomodate trailers up to 32 feet in length. The campground also has one picnic site that is designated for day use.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/gila/recarea/?recid=84721', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '8995', 'Tanners Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.571978, -111.700600, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The campground is set among a forest of shady pine, aspen, oak and maple trees. Vivid summer wildflowers are abundant, and autumn leaves put on quite a show. Little Cottonwood Creek runs along the edge of the campground. Dogs, horses, and other domestic animals are prohibited in protected watersheds because their waste can end up in the drinking water, so pets are not allowed in Little Cottonwood Canyon and Tanners Flat campground. This campground has an amphitheater. A per-day, per-vehicle fee will be collected on site for extra vehicles Off-road vehicles are not permitted This campground…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=8995', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9003', 'Anderson Cove Campground', 'campground', 41.249750, -111.786150, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Anderson Cove is located 10 miles east of Ogden, Utah, on the banks of Pineview Reservoir in scenic Ogden Valley. It is a high standard campground, marina, group camping, and day-use beach. It has paved roads and spurs with a high level of security. Everyone must enter the campground past the entry station where a site is assigned or reservation voucher is checked. Hosts are on-site. Its manicured lawns are lined with a variety of shade trees. Temperatures are warm during the day. A cafe/gas station is 1/2 mile from the campground. There are some convenience items are for sale at the cabin.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9003', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9022', 'Bear River Campground', 'campground', 40.910075, -110.830017, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is equipped with picnic tables. Recreation activities within 5 miles from the campground include hiking, fishing, backpacking, and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9022', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9032', 'Beaver View Campground', 'campground', 40.825493, -110.862823, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is located within a popular area for hiking, fishing, backpacking, and mountain biking. This campground is equipped with picnic tables.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9032', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9065', 'Botts Campground', 'campground', 41.277174, -111.658159, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This small campground is located about six miles east of Huntsville, Utah on a curve along the South Fork of the Ogden River. A host is not on-site but can be found at Magpie Campground (west) or South Fork Campground (east). It has been a popular camping spot since the pioneers came to Utah. Although the trees are not thick, they are big and very old. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, hiking, swimming, and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a life jacket is required for all tubers). Nearby Attractions Causey Reservoir is located approximately five miles east. This…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9065', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9068', 'Bountiful Peak Campground', 'campground', 40.980817, -111.804383, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Bountiful Peak Campground is set in an alpine basin high in the Wasatch Mountains at an elevation of 7,500 feet. Farmington, Utah, is 9 miles away. Visitors enjoy exploring local trails on foot, bike and off-road vehicles. Leashed pets are permitted in this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9068', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9072', 'Box Elder Campground', 'campground', 41.495767, -111.948861, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Box Elder Campground is situated next to the town of Mantua and Mantua Reservoir in a pretty mountain valley just 5 miles from Brigham City, Utah. Visitors enjoy boating, fishing and exploring area trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9072', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9075', 'Boy Scout Campground', 'campground', 40.494317, -112.578933, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Leashed pets are permitted in the campground. This campground is near a trailhead and wilderness access. It has 7 single sites, 1 double site and 1 group site that can accommodate up to 35 people. There is no water system in this campground will need to bring your own.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9075', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9082', 'Bridger Campground', 'campground', 41.748231, -111.733631, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Bridger Campground is situated next to the Logan River just 6 miles east of Logan, Utah. The campground sits at an elevation of 5,000 feet in scenic Logan Canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9082', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9084', 'Bridger Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.963175, -110.389447, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered campground is popular for the local fishing and is close to the lake with a boat ramp.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9084', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9103', 'Butterfly Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.720648, -110.866996, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 14 miles away. Local popular recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. This campground is equipped with picnic tables.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9103', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9126', 'China Meadows Campground', 'campground', 40.931282, -110.403451, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered area is popular for its fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9126', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9129', 'Christmas Meadows Campground', 'campground', 40.824961, -110.801983, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Campsite amenities also include picnic tables. Local popular recreational activities include hiking, fishing, backpacking and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9129', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9140', 'Cobblerest Campground', 'campground', 40.595014, -110.975567, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 17 miles. Local popular recreation activities include river fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9140', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9151', 'Cottonwood Campground - SLRD', 'campground', 40.501878, -112.559611, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Cottonwood Campground is located southwest of Grantsville, Utah, in South Willow Canyon at an elevation of 6,080 feet. It''s located in the Stansbury Range where visitors enjoy exploring local trails. Leashed pets are permitted in this primitive campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9151', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9214', 'East Fork Bear River', 'campground', 40.858900, -110.753800, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Dispersed camping is available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9214', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9215', 'East Fork Bear River Campground', 'campground', 40.911892, -110.829319, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground has picnic tables. Local popular recreation activities include hiking, fishing, backpacking, and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9215', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9217', 'East Fork Bear Snow Machine', 'snow_area', 40.913400, -110.828800, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Dogs are allowed. USGS: Christmas Meadows and Red Knob. This is a highly developed snowmobile trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9217', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9257', 'Friendship Campground', 'campground', 41.661292, -111.665347, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Friendship Campground is located about 15 miles from Hyrum, Utah, in the mountains of Blacksmith Fork Canyon at an elevation of 5,600 feet. Visitors enjoy hiking, fishing and exploring off-road trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9257', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9319', 'Green Canyon Picnic Area', 'campground', 41.770164, -111.765436, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'No water or other services are available at this time.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9319', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9323', 'Guinavah- Malibu Campground', 'campground', 41.762200, -111.701000, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Guinavah contains three group sites that accommodate 100 people. Numerous single and double-family sites are available as well. A large amphitheater with bleacher seating is located near Group Site C. Flush toilets and drinking water are provided. The roads are paved while the parking spurs are not.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9323', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9324', 'Guinavah Amphitheater', 'campground', 41.762297, -111.702439, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Conservation Corp built this amphitheater The Gunavah-Malibu campground is closed for the 2023 season for re-construction.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9324', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9328', 'Hayden Fork Campground', 'campground', 40.830388, -110.853735, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is equipped with picnic tables. Recreation activities within 5 miles from the campground include hiking, fishing, backpacking, and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9328', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9348', 'High Creek Campground', 'campground', 41.976489, -111.735244, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'There are no fees for this campground under current conditions. There are no restroom facilities or services. This campground is located North of Logan Canyon.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9348', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9359', 'Hoop Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.925876, -110.123262, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered campground is popular for the local fishing and is close to the lake. This campground has no water available', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9359', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9369', 'Intake Campground', 'campground', 40.498006, -112.571064, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Intake Campground is located southwest of Grantsville, Utah, in South Willow Canyon at an elevation of 6,320 feet. It''s located in the Stansbury Range where visitors enjoy exploring local trails. Leashed pets are permitted in this campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9369', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9383', 'Jordan Pines Group Campground', 'campground', 40.646522, -111.648139, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This group campground is a perfect location for family reunions, church outings and company picnics. It offers four overnight campsites and one day-use picnic site, all of which contain picnic tables, campfire rings and grills. Vault toilets and drinking water are provided. A volleyball court and horseshoe pit are available, but campers must bring their own net, ball and horseshoes. Roads and parking spurs are paved. Dogs, horses, and other domestic animals are prohibited in protected watersheds because their waste can end up in the drinking water, so pets are not allowed in Big Cottonwood…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9383', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9416', 'Ledgefork Campground', 'campground', 40.742364, -111.099350, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 14 miles away. Local popular recreation activities inlcude fishing at Smith Morehouse Reservoir and hiking. This campground has no water, so please bring your own', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9416', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9420', 'Lewis M. Turner Campground', 'campground', 41.885144, -111.571436, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Lewis M. Turner Campground is about 22 miles northeast of Logan, Utah, at an elevation of 5,900 feet. This scenic area is known for its vivid summer wildflowers and excellent trails. The campground is set back off the highway in the aspens.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9420', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9428', 'Lilly Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.680551, -110.938565, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 25 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. Motorized boats are prohibited on Lilly Lake', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9428', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9441', 'Little Lyman Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.934792, -110.612283, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is equipped with picnic tables. Recreation activities within 5 miles from the campground include fishing and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9441', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9443', 'Lodge Campground', 'campground', 41.777858, -111.620144, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The campground is well shaded and off the beaten path with the Right Hand Fork of the Logan River nearby. This is a pretty, rustic campground with sounds of the river heard throughout the area. Because of the heavy understory and middlestory, camping sites enjoy good privacy.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9443', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9444', 'Lodgepole Campground', 'campground', 40.309913, -111.260618, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Lodgepole Campground is located in scenic Daniels Canyon just a short drive from Heber, Utah, and Strawberry Reservoir at an elevation of 7,800 feet. Campers enjoy fishing and hiking in the canyon and day-tripping to Strawberry.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9444', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9453', 'Loop Campground', 'campground', 40.487897, -112.603181, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The desert canyon is forested with oak, maple and juniper trees, which offer partial shade. Willow Creek runs alongside the site. Leashed pets are permitted in the campground. It has 12 single sites and 1 double site. There is no water system in this campground will need to bring your own.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9453', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9457', 'Lost Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.681642, -110.934389, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 25 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. Operating a boat with anything other than an electric motor on Lost Creek Lake is prohibited', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9457', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9460', 'Lower Meadows Campground', 'campground', 41.286623, -111.643195, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is located on the far side of the river from Highway 39. The entrance is the same as Upper Meadows, but instead of turning left, stay on the road, cross the bridge and turn to the right at the top of the hill. This campground is one of the most spacious with the individual sites quite far apart. The grass is usually tall and thick. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, hiking, swimming and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a life jacket is required for all tubers). Causey Reservoir, a scenic mountain lake, is four miles east.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9460', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9461', 'Lower Narrows Campground', 'campground', 40.492036, -112.592022, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Leashed pets are permitted in the campground. It has 3 single sites. There is no water system in this campground will need to bring your own.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9461', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9462', 'Lower Provo River Campground', 'campground', 40.593483, -111.118394, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'There are no hook-ups in this campground. The nearest phone is 9 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include river fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9462', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9467', 'Magpie Campground', 'campground', 41.270264, -111.667206, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is heavily wooded with mostly cottonwood trees and other river-bottom types of vegetation. The South Fork of Ogden River flows adjacent to the campground. Firewood is available from the on-site Host. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, hiking, swimming and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a life jacket is required for all tubers). Causey Reservoir, a scenic mountain lake, is five miles east.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9467', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9477', 'Maples Campground', 'campground', 41.227872, -111.865505, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'There is no longer a Maples campground north of the Snowbasin Ski Resort. All picnic tables, firerings and restrooms have been removed. The public may still camp in the area, but must camp away from the trail that goes through the site. All access is walk-ins/bicycles/horses only, no motor vehicles, it is approximately 1/2 mile from the gate. The gate just off the pavement at the lower Snowbasin parking lot is the gravel trail/road to the area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9477', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9479', 'Marsh Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.951900, -110.396600, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered campground is popular for the local fishing and is close to the lake.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9479', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9490', 'Meeks Cabin Campground', 'campground', 41.005205, -110.583369, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Popular recreation activities within 5 miles of the campground include fishing and mountain biking. This campground is located outside the Mirror Lake Area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9490', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9510', 'Mirror Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.700867, -110.885514, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground with no hook-ups. The campground is near an access to the High Uintas Wilderness. The nearest phone is 16 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. Campsites 65-79 are equipped for equestrian use (horses, mules, lamas) hitching rails and feeding boxes', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9510', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9519', 'Monte Cristo Campground', 'campground', 41.463678, -111.497479, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Monte Cristo Campground is located 30 miles east of Huntsville, Utah. ​This campground is at the highest elevation in the Ogden District at 9,000 feet. Individual campsites are surrounded by spruce and Douglas fir stands, adding their fresh scent to the clear, cool air. Visitors enjoy exploring the local trails via hiking, biking, horseback riding and off-road vehicle riding. (Horses are not allowed within the campground and you must trailer your ATV one mile or more). The drive along scenic Highway 39 through wildflower-filled meadows and beautiful forests is spectacular. Summer wildflowers…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9519', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9522', 'Moosehorn Campground', 'campground', 40.693801, -110.892150, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 17 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking. Operating a motorized boat on Moosehorn Lake is prohibited.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9522', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9573', 'Perception Park Family Campground', 'campground', 41.289719, -111.640667, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Perception Park Family Campground is located on the banks of the South Fork Ogden River at. Campers love the park for its shade and great river access. This scenic campground is situated among shady cottonwoods and willow. Moose and deer wander through the campground on occasion. It was built for the use of the physically challenged in the mid 1980''s. This qualifies Perception Park Family as a higher standard campground. Concrete platforms with benches have been placed in several locations along the river for the enjoyment of the handicapped. Although the campground was built for the use of…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9573', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9588', 'Pioneer Campground', 'campground', 41.628894, -111.693017, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Pioneer campground is located on the banks of the Blacksmith Fork River about 9 miles from Hyrum, Utah at an elevation of 5,600 feet. This little campground has many nicely secluded sites tucked under Black Willow and Box Elder trees.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9588', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9598', 'Preston Valley Campground', 'campground', 41.773639, -111.654881, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Preston Valley is a riverside location where the sounds of the river provide a pleasant background to an enjoyable, relaxing stay. This scenic area appeals to fly fishing enthusiasts and birdwatchers. Other activities include wildlife viewing, hiking area trails, scenic driving the canyon road, and mountain biking on designated trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9598', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9609', 'Red Banks Campground', 'campground', 41.898469, -111.564394, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Red Banks Campground, located 23 miles northeast of Logan, Utah, sits on the banks of Logan River. The aspen and willows on the campground offer partial shade to some campsites, and the heavy grasses and shrubs offer privacy from fellow campers.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9609', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9616', 'Redman Campground-SLRD', 'campground', 40.616369, -111.588711, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The campground is set among a forest of shady spruce and pine trees. Vivid summer wildflowers are abundant and autumn leaves put on quite a show. Hiking and mountain biking are popular activities on area trails, including the Donut Falls Trail, which begins nearby. Fly-fishermen enjoy casting on Big Cottonwood Creek. Dogs, horses, and other domestic animals are prohibited in protected watersheds because their waste can end up in the drinking water, so pets are not allowed in Big Cottonwood Canyon and Redman campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9616', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9630', 'Rock Canyon Campground', 'campground', 40.270000, -111.590000, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is close to the trailhead and is located in a timbered setting. This campground has no water available and is reservation only', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9630', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9650', 'Shady Dell Campground', 'campground', 40.590114, -111.015751, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered campground is popular for its fishing and stream.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9650', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9657', 'Shingle Creek ATV Campground', 'campground', 40.614961, -111.129753, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 8 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include ATV trail riding, stream fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9657', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9677', 'Smithfield Campground', 'campground', 41.870342, -111.754164, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground offers access to hiking and biking trails. Two miles up the road is the Smithfield Canyon trailhead, which leads into the Mount Naomi Wilderness. There is a stock loading ramp at the trailhead parking lot. Trail 007 leads to Tony Grove Lake, on the other side of the wilderness. Activities include fishing, hiking, mountain biking, and horse riding.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9677', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9680', 'Smith-Morehouse Campground', 'campground', 40.769276, -111.107381, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. The nearest phone is 13 miles away. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9680', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9691', 'South Fork Campground', 'campground', 41.282989, -111.653808, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'South Fork Campground is located adjacent to the South Fork of the Ogden River approximately 7 miles east from Huntsville, Utah. This scenic campground is situated among cottonwoods and willow. Moose and deer occasionally wander through the campground. This campground has gravel spurs and roads, cement table pads, fire rings. An on-site Campground Host is in site 21 near the entrance. Firewood is available for purchase from the host. Campers love this area for its great river access. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, swimming, and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9691', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9699', 'Spring Campground', 'campground', 41.662097, -111.654081, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Spring Campground is located on the Left Hand Fork of the Blacksmith Fork River. It is about 12 miles from Hyrum, Utah, in the mountains of Blacksmith Fork Canyon at an elevation of 6,000 feet. Visitors enjoy hiking, fishing and exploring off-road trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9699', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9702', 'Spring Hollow Campground', 'campground', 41.753750, -111.716692, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Spring Hollow Campground is situated next to the Logan River just 4 miles east of Logan, Utah, in scenic Logan Canyon. Visitors enjoy fishing, canoeing and exploring local trails. A forest of oak, maple, box elder and cottonwood trees covers the area, providing ample shade and beautiful fall color. Summer wildflowers and wild roses are abundant. The Logan River flows past the campground and a large pond is located at the campground''s edge.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9702', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9705', 'Spruces Campground', 'campground', 40.642872, -111.636972, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Redman Campground set among a forest of shady spruce and pine trees is located in scenic Big Cottonwood Canyon at an elevation of 8,300 feet. Salt Lake City is conveniently close. Visitors enjoy hiking, biking and fishing. Dogs, horses, and other domestic animals are prohibited in protected watersheds because their waste can end up in the drinking water, so pets are not allowed in Big Cottonwood Canyon and Spruces campground. The campground contains two group sites and numerous single, double, and triple-family sites, all with picnic tables and campfire rings. Flush toilets and drinking water…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9705', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9709', 'Stateline Campground', 'campground', 40.981750, -110.385556, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered campground is popular for the local fishing and is close to the lake with boat ramp. The closest dump station is the Bear River Dump station, which is located just outside of Evanston, Wyoming. Visitors are more than welcome to come and fill up with water at our station before heading up to the desired campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9709', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9713', 'Stillwater Campground', 'campground', 40.868300, -110.834500, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is equipped with picnic tables. Popular recreation activities within 5 miles of the campground include hiking, fishing, backpacking and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9713', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9720', 'Sulphur Campground', 'campground', 40.790600, -110.883600, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The campground is equipped with picnic tables. Local popular recreation activities include hiking, fishing, backpacking and mountain biking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9720', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9721', 'Sunrise Campground', 'campground', 41.921408, -111.460883, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Sunrise Campground is close to Bear Lake Summit, just 6 miles west of Garden City and Bear Lake, Utah, at an elevation of 7,800 feet. Visitors to the Bear Lake area are treated to a wide range of outdoor recreational opportunities, including boating, water skiing, hiking and scenic driving.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9721', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9751', 'Tony Grove Lake Campground', 'campground', 41.893892, -111.639697, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Tony Grove Campground is situated on the mountainside above beautiful Tony Grove Lake, about 19 miles east of Logan, Utah, at an elevation of 8,100 feet. This scenic area is known for its vivid summer wildflowers and excellent trails.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9751', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9756', 'Trial Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.844908, -110.953839, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is a paved campground with no hook-ups. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9756', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9767', 'Upper Meadows Campground', 'campground', 41.290907, -111.635696, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Upper Meadows Campground is a small campground located adjacent to the South Fork of the Ogden River. This campground has gravel spurs and roads, cement table pads, fire rings. A Campground Host is in Lower Meadows just west of the entrance. Firewood can be purchased from the Host. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, hiking, swimming and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a life jacket is required for all tubers). Causey Reservoir, a scenic mountain lake, is three miles east. Site Details and Accessible Features', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9767', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9768', 'Upper Narrows Campground', 'campground', 40.491861, -112.594575, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This primitive campground is dispersed over a mile-long stretch of road. One walk-to group site, ideal for family reunions or church groups, is available for up to 50 people. A footbridge must be crossed to access the site from the parking area. Picnic tables and campfire rings are provided, as are vault toilets. Roads and parking spurs are dirt. Leashed pets are permitted in the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9768', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9781', 'Washington Lake Campground', 'campground', 40.675286, -110.960622, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground with no hook-ups. Popular local recreation activities include lake fishing and hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9781', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9813', 'Whitney Snow Machine', 'snow_area', 40.853114, -110.867200, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Dogs are allowed. USGS Quad: Whitney Reservoir. This is a highly developed snow trail.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9813', array['Snowmobile']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['snowmobile']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9820', 'Willows Campground', 'campground', 41.292013, -111.634697, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Willows Campground is located adjacent to the South Fork of the Ogden River. This campground has gravel spurs and roads, cement table pads, fire rings. An on-site Campground Host is in site 5 near the entrance. Firewood can be purchased from the Host. Popular local recreation activities include fishing, hiking, swimming, and tubing down the South Fork Ogden River (a life jacket is required for all tubers). Causey Reservoir, a scenic mountain lake, is two miles east. Site Details and Accessible Features', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9820', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9835', 'Wood Camp Campground', 'campground', 41.773639, -111.654881, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground provides access to biking, climbing, hiking, fishing, horse riding, and more in the Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest. The Old Juniper Trailhead, located just outside the campground, leads to the Jardine Juniper, which at 1500 years old is thought to be the oldest tree in the Rocky Mountains.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9835', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9840', 'Yellow Pine Campground', 'campground', 40.629563, -111.175069, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This is an unpaved campground and has no water available. Popular local recreation activities include hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9840', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9843', 'Maple Bench Campground', 'campground', 39.963000, -111.692399, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered-setting campground is located in a Canyon. Enjoy the scenic drive to the campground.Facilities have not been modified. Popular local activities include lake fishing, lake floating, rafting, kayaking, and hiking. Facilities not Modified.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9843', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9844', 'Payson Lakes Campground', 'campground', 39.933472, -111.634336, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Payson Lakes Campground is situated in stands of aspen and fir trees. There is a lake within the campground where you can boat, fish, and swim. An asphalt walkway goes around the lake. There are also nearby hiking trails and open areas where recreation activities can occur. The campground is just off a National Scenic Byway, about 12 miles from Payson, a full-service community. The campground has no hook-ups or phone service. Popular local activities inlcude river and lake fishing, lake floating, rafting, kayaking, swimming, and day-hiking.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9844', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9845', 'Balsam Campground', 'campground', 40.198533, -111.402186, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Balsam Campground is located in Hobble Creek Canyon. Vegetation is fir, maple and cottonwood trees. Hobble Creek runs next to the campground. There are concrete pads under the tables. Popular activities include fishing Hobble Creek, playing volleyball or hiking Dry Canyon or Wardsworth Trail (both of which leave Hobble Creek Road within one mile of campground). Maple, fir and cottonwood trees forest the area, providing partial shade, beautiful fall color and some privacy between campsites. Hobble Creek runs through the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9845', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9846', 'Cherry Campground', 'campground', 40.168725, -111.477139, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This timbered-setting campground is located in a stand of maple and cottonwood trees, next to Hobble Creek. Roads and spurs are paved. There are cement pads under the tables, and fire pits. Other amenities include grills horshoe pit, picnic tables, volleyball court. Popular activities include fishing, hiking nearby trails, wildlife viewing, and golfing at a local course. It is about six miles from a full service community. The water source in the campground isn’t passing and folks should bring their own water as they have in the past.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9846', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9847', 'Blackhawk Campground', 'campground', 39.897519, -111.630178, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is closed due to fire damage Some sites in the campground are open with fees, no water and on a first-come first-serve basis This timbered-setting campground sits just off the Nebo Loop, a National Scenic Byway. Visitors enjoy the campground for its beautiful panoramic views and great trail opportunities. The dominant vegetation consists of fir, pine, aspen, and Gambel oak trees, which provide partial shade and nice fall color. Broad grassy meadows cover the areas around the trees. Summer wildflowers and wildlife are abundant.. 5 miles away is Payson Lake, a fifteen acre…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9847', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9849', 'Bear Canyon Campground', 'campground', 39.785994, -111.729153, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Bear Canyon Campground is just off the Nebo Loop National Scenic Byway. The dominant vegetation consists of fir trees, aspen, open grass meadows and gamble oak. The campground is situated at the base of Mt. Nebo Wilderness with picnic tables, nearby hiking trails and open areas for group activities. Wildlife viewing is another popular activity in this area. There is no water available at this campground. Each campsite within Bear Canyon offers beautiful views of the surrounding Wasatch Range. Aspen and fir trees line the edges of the campground, which sits in a large grassy meadow. Few trees…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9849', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9850', 'Whiting Campground', 'campground', 40.131725, -111.527696, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Whiting Campground has a very pleasant setting in maple and cottonwood trees. There are mountainous horse trails, hiking trails, wildlife viewing and fishing opportunities. Firewood, grills, picnic tables are some of the amenities the campground has to offer.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9850', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9852', 'Vernon Reservoir Campground', 'campground', 39.988300, -112.384600, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Open setting with no modified facilities. Lake fishing is the main recreational activity for this area. There is no water available at this campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9852', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9853', 'Ponderosa Campground', 'campground', 39.768536, -111.713992, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This Ponderosa is near Spanish Fork. It is not on the Mirror Lake Highway or in the Dixie National Forest near St. George. Is this the campground you''re requesting? Located ten miles from Nephi, this timbered-setting campground is situated in a ponderosa pine forest area, near Salt Creek. There is good privacy between units. Campground is within 1.5 miles of the Mt. Nebo Wilderness and close fishing streams, access to hiking trails, national scenic byway (Nebo Loop) and six miles from Devil''s Kitchen Geological Area. Firewood, grills, picnic tables are all part of the improved amenities.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9853', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9854', 'Tinney Flat Campground', 'campground', 39.900669, -111.728521, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Tinney Flat Campground sits just off of the Nebo Loop National Scenic Byway. The Santaquin Canyon road is paved, but very steep and narrow. There are hiking, bird watching, river fishing and wildlife viewing opportunities. Firewood, grills, picnic tables are amenities are available.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9854', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9855', 'Diamond Campground', 'campground', 40.072897, -111.430669, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is an open-setting, with access to trailheads, waterfalls, and canyons. River fishing and hiking are a couple of the recreation activities that are popular in this area.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9855', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9856', 'Maple Lake Campground', 'campground', 39.955631, -111.691253, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Timbered setting with limited accessibility. Lake fishing and floating, rafting, kayaking, swimming, and hiking are popular recreation activities for this area. There is no water available at this campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9856', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9857', 'Cottonwood Campground', 'campground', 39.780538, -111.723068, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is surrounded by Cottonwoods and Maples and located next to a stream. Gravel roads and spurs. Site Details and Accessibility Features', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9857', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9886', 'Aspen Grove Campground', 'campground', 40.124869, -111.036114, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Aspen Grove Campground is located in a mountainous area near Soldier Creek Dam above the Soldier Creek section of beautiful Strawberry Reservoir. Improvements include paved roads and spurs, cement pads, tables and fire circles. There is no phone service. You must stay on the site you reserve; no site swapping is allowed. Strawberry Reservoir offers excellent boating, water skiing and canoeing. Anglers fish for rainbow trout, cutthroat trout and Kokanee salmon. Aspen Grove Day Use Area is less than 1/4 mile below the campground. A boat ramp, boat rentals, slips, a fish cleaning station and…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9886', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9887', 'Currant Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.331775, -111.066949, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Currant Creek Campground is situated next to Currant Creek Reservoir. Aspen, fir and lodgepole pine are the dominant tree species. Rainbow and cutthroat trout are the principal fish species in the reservoir. There is a campground host on site. Facilities and improvements include paved roads & parking spurs, dump station, boat ramp, fire rings, firewood, grills, picnic tables, handicap accessible fishing pier and playground. Popular activities include hiking, wildlife viewing, fishing and boating.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9887', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9888', 'Mill Hollow Campground', 'campground', 40.491626, -111.103599, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Mill Hollow reservoir is adjacent to the campground. Beautiful aspen fir and lodgepole pines surround the campground. Improvements include gravel roads and parking spurs, picnic tables, fire rings, and a grill at each site. Popular activities include hiking, bird watching, horseshoe pitching, snowshoeing, wildlife viewing and fishing. No power or telephones.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9888', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9889', 'Renegade Campground', 'campground', 40.121370, -111.158348, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'The campground is located on Strawberry Reservoir. Setting is rolling sage brush hills & valleys. Sites are equipped with picnic tables, fire rings, and grills. No power or telephones. Improvements included paved roads, boat launch ramp, fish cleaning station, and garbage service. Popular activities include fishing, boating, canoeing, jet skiing, water skiing and wildlife viewing. Trails available outside campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9889', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9890', 'Soldier Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.154914, -111.055181, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Located adjacent to Strawberry Reservoir with dump station and boat ramps provided. Roads are paved. Each site has picnic table and fire ring. There are panoramic views of Strawberry Reservoir and valley. Camping spurs are between 50-75 feet apart. Marina and store are close. Popular activities include fishing, boating, water skiing, hiking, biking and interpretive programs. There is horseback riding outside the campground. Campground loops are adjacent to marina and boat launch. Boat rentals, slip rentals, fuel, groceries, fish cleaning station and supplies are available. Fish Your National…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9890', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9891', 'Strawberry Bay Campground', 'campground', 40.180382, -111.172886, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Strawberry Bay Campground is located adjacent to Strawberry Reservoir. The campground is in a setting of rolling hills covered with sagebrush. ATVs are allowed in designated routes outside the campground. Roads are paved. Popular activities include boating, canoeing, water skiing, hiking, biking, horseback riding and fishing for rainbow trout, cutthroat trout & kokanee salmon. Leashed pets are permitted.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9891', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9892', 'Wolf Creek Campground', 'campground', 40.482378, -111.031978, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Wolf Creek Campground sits at an elevation of 9,400 feet in stands of aspen and fir trees. This campground is subject to early winters and late springs and can close earlier or open later than expected.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9892', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9899', 'Hope Campground', 'campground', 40.300000, -111.620000, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'This campground is located in maple, scrub oak, and some fir. Road is paved from Provo Canyon. Grills and picnic tables are a couple of the improved amenities that are available at this campground. While you are here enjoy some fabulous hiking. There is no water available in this campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9899', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9900', 'Altamont Group Campground', 'campground', 40.435650, -111.635714, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Altamont Campground is located along the beautiful Alpine Loop Scenic Byway high in the Wasatch Mountains. The Mount Timpanogos Wilderness Area is adjacent. Visitors enjoy hiking the nearby Timpooneke Trail to the summit of Mount Timpanogos. The campground lies among dense, shady stands of aspen, fir and spruce trees at an elevation of 7,400 feet. Wildlife and summer wildflowers are abundant and autumn leaves put on quite a show. The rough, dirt Timpooneke Road also begins across the road, nearly circumnavigates Mount Timpanogos and offers excellent mountain biking and birding opportunities.…', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9900', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9901', 'Granite Flat Campground', 'campground', 40.490000, -111.650000, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Granite Flat Campground is located in aspen, douglas fir, spruce and pine trees and is close to Lone Peak Wilderness. Tibble Fork and Silver Flat Reservoirs are close and offer good fishing. The nearest telephone is five miles away. Popular activities include hiking, fishing, rafting, kayaking, visiting Timpanogos Cave and viewing wildlife. Amenities with facility includes a baseball field, firewood, grills, and picnic tables. This campground is popular for hiking, horshoe pitching, and wildlife viewing. There is no water available in the campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9901', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9902', 'Little Mill Campground', 'campground', 40.448628, -111.676181, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Little Mill Campground is located in American Fork Canyon and is situated next to the American Fork River. Popular activities include hiking, fishing, and wildlife viewing. This campground is 1-1/2 miles from Timpanogos Cave National Monument. Facility amenities include firewood, grills, and picnic tables. Please bring all the water you will need for your stay. There is no water available on site.`', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9902', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9903', 'Mount Timpanogos Campground', 'campground', 40.405528, -111.606186, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Mt. Timpanogos Campground is surrounded by aspen and fir trees. This campground is situated next to the Mt. Timpanogos Wilderness. Hiking opportunities are nearby. Campground roads and spurs are paved. There is no water available at the campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9903', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9904', 'Theater-in-the-Pines Campground', 'campground', 40.404472, -111.603425, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Mount Timpanogos Trailhead is nearby and accesses hiking trails to the 11,700 foot Mount Timpanogos. Please check-in with host at Mt. Timpanogos Campground to gain access to Theater in the Pines. Firewood, grills and picnic tables are some of the improved amenities for this campground. Take some time to enjoy some wildlife viewing, river fishing, caving, and viewing the the waterfalls. There is no water available at the campground.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9904', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9906', 'Timpooneke Campground', 'campground', 40.432181, -111.643475, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Timponeeke Campground is located in a mountainous area next to the Mt. Timpanogos Wilderness. Aspen, spruces and fir trees are the dominant tree species. Hiking, horseback riding, and wildlife viewing are popular activities in this area. Site amenities include firewood, grills and picnic tables. There is no water available at the campground', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9906', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9908', 'Mirror Lake Scenic Byway', 'scenic_drive', 40.700800, -110.884800, null, 'Uinta-Wasatch-Cache National Forest', 'Heading east from Kamas through the national forest, Mirror Lake Highway is one of the most popular mountain routes in the state. The road winds through farm and ranch lands and rises to heavily forested, mountain terrain, accented by meadows and rugged peaks. There are numerous access points into the High Uinta Wilderness along this byway.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/uwcnf/recarea/?recid=9908', array['Motorcycle', 'Car', 'RV']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[]),
  ('usfs', '9913', 'Cranberry Glades Botanical Area', 'campground', 38.203147, -80.265797, null, 'Monongahela National Forest', 'The Cranberry Glades Botanical Area protects the largest area of bogs in West Virginia. Bogs are acidic wetlands more commonly found in the northern areas of this country and in Canada. The ground in a bog is spongy and consists largely of partially-decayed plant material known as peat. Because of its unique conditions, some unusual plants grow in bogs, including carnivorous or insect-eating plants. The Botanical Area encompasses 750 acres.', 'https://www.fs.usda.gov/recarea/mnf/recarea/?recid=9913', array['Car', 'RV', 'Motorcycle']::text[], 'public domain', 'US Forest Service', array['road_trip', 'motorcycle']::text[])
